{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance","id":52328,"title":"Tell me what you want: re: Solar Performance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-18T06:28:38-08:00","id":52328,"title":"Tell me what you want: re: Solar Performance","content":"As the subject says.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T06:42:23-08:00","id":52333,"title":"","content":"I want to inspire. I want to be able to set a flame in their hearts with a song or a speech--maybe it's for my glory, maybe it's for a righteous cause. I want to be able to do that thing mentioned as the pinnacle of performance in the 1e core, where you turn the crowd at your execution into a rallying rebel army to set you free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T06:45:47-08:00","id":52336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52333#post52333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to inspire. I want to be able to set a flame in their hearts with a song or a speech--maybe it's for my glory, maybe it's for a righteous cause. I want to be able to do that thing mentioned as the pinnacle of performance in the 1e core, where you turn the crowd at your execution into a rallying rebel army to set you free.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you see this as being different from what it did in 1e/2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T07:02:58-08:00","id":52347,"title":"","content":"Not necessarily. I always saw Husband-Seducing Demon Dance as being &quot;IInspire with the power of ROCK&quot;, at least in its 2e incarnation. Sadly, I'm visiting in laws at the moment and don't have my books with me, so I can't say for sure what I feel was missing out of 2e--or 1e, for that matter, but that was because I was a dumbass and sold pretty much the entire thing. But regardless, I do think a Solar heavily invested in performance should be considered more of an Icon to her followers than a hero. They champion, they lead, but all too frequently it's done as the vanguard of some movement. The masses will know their name or at least their sobriquet. I'm not sure if I'm coming across as I'd like. Certainly a Solar performance-based character can simply be a celebrity. But should they take it upon themselves to turn their force of personality to a cause, then the world may well take up their banner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T07:10:54-08:00","id":52350,"title":"","content":"I would like a focus on acting. Something that lets Solar Performers take on the personae's of other people they have met, or just act differently then themselves, perhaps with the ability to even throw out fake intimacies that hide or alter their own temporarily. I just think that performance has been very narrowly focused on the &quot;Rousing Speech or Heart-Breaking Song&quot; stuff and needs to open its gates a little to incorporate the ability to turn Solar's into the greatest actors in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/777-bronze-tiger","name":"Bronze Tiger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T07:19:13-08:00","id":52355,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how useful this is, but Solar Performance has always done what I've wanted to do with it. When I wanted to write a series of plays that were metaphors for the Usurpation, setting up the metaphorical Solars in a sympathetic light as to pave the way for improving public opinion about the Anathema, Solar Performance was there for me. When an evil sorcerer was trying to kill me and we decided to bond instead over our love of music, Solar Performance was there for me. When I made a character who only spoke in highly ritualized compound-complex sentences and needed magic to ensure that people would listen to the pompous windbag rather than interrupt him by hitting him in the face with several feet of sharpened, Celestial metal like a sane person, Solar Performance was there for me.<br /> <br /> That all may be the result of me looking at the tools I have and making plans around them rather than making plans and trying to figure out what tools I need, though.<br /> <br /> What's the problem? Is Solar Performance looking a bit malnourished?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T07:19:13-08:00","id":52356,"title":"","content":"1) I want <i>Husband-Seducing Demon Dance</i> to still be a thing.<br /> <br /> 2) I want the ground to shake and things to break when I yell (like the veil ripping during the crucifixion of Jesus but potentially bigger in scope).<br /> <br /> 3) I want wind in my hair and <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dolly_zoom\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Vertigo </i>effects</a> at my beck and call.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T07:19:16-08:00","id":52357,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\">I want Performance to make up its mind on whether it's supposed to be about music and dance or about long-winded speeches, because I have some trouble seeing certain Charms apply to both sides of that coin. <br /> <br /> I like that one of the basic Performance Charms is &quot;stay here until I'm done.&quot; Having spectators unable to turn their eyes away from your Dance of the Seven Veils is very yes. I would like that it not be brain-washing - why the hell is the memory-rewriting Charm in Performance? I want it to play on emotions - to rouse anger or to bring peace of mind, to spur love or hate, and to inspire people to be heroes. Performance should not so much convince people of things as it should draw their attentions, inspire feelings, make you beloved or feared. It should also still summon ephemeral images assisting your art. <br /> <br /> Performance in 1e was pretty big, but that's because it contained most of what later became War; 2e split that into two Abilities without giving Performance new toys, and as a result it is pretty barren. It really needs more stuff to play with, I think.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">In The Phoenix on the Sword, one of the conspirators who plot to assas</span>sinate Conan is a bard, a poet and singer, who almost single-handedly turned the city's opinion on their new king from &quot;rightful savior of the people&quot; to &quot;hated usurper.&quot; And yet still, as he has done that and now is throwing himself at Conan trying to kill him, Conan is reluctant to hurt him until he has no other choice. &quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">A great poet is greater than any king. His songs are mightier than my scepter; for he has near ripped the heart from my breast when he chose to sing for me. I shall die and be forgotten, but Rinaldo's songs will live for ever.&quot;&quot;<br /> <br /> When you are a master of Solar Performance, even your sworn enemies should weep at the thought of killing you. </span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T07:24:31-08:00","id":52360,"title":"","content":"4) I do not recall what the Solar Mirror to the Abyssal Charm <i>Morbid Fascination Style</i>, was or if it even had one, but I want to be able to give monologues in the style of Jules from <b>Pulp Fiction</b> without people interrupting me to shoot me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T07:29:10-08:00","id":52363,"title":"","content":"I would be very disappointed if I couldn't have my Solar warrior boast of his deeds, in song or verse, with such force that the army in front of him decides to defect rather than fight him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T07:33:12-08:00","id":52365,"title":"","content":"I realise I shall have to accept that some abilities, like Presence, Performance and Linguistics, will always have some overlapping areas.<br /> <br /> That said, I think there's a room to differentiate Presence and Performance a bit more. I'd like it if influence through Performance became more about of influence specifically through art: singing, dancing, acting, reciting poetry. Other charms which do not necessarily involve influence could also be based on those qualities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T07:40:09-08:00","id":52373,"title":"","content":"I want Performance to let me run a multiple person Short Con with just my Solar. I know the multiple identities thing is nominally a Sidereal thing, but I don't want to have to play a Sidereal to play Sophie Deveraux.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T07:41:29-08:00","id":52374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52357#post52357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">When you are a master of Solar Performance, even your sworn enemies should weep at the thought of killing you. [/SIZE]</span>[/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny that You and Yours Stance from Sidereal's Socialize kinda do this, but more of a &quot;She gave me a blow-job so good that I can't risk killing her!&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T07:42:48-08:00","id":52375,"title":"","content":"The whole awe inspiring, speech giving, army leading is really the core I think and I liked the previous edition's system very much.<br /> On our table &quot;War&quot; is not actually that good for leading, but is great for the logistics, tactics and strategies (and countering them). So a good leader relied more on Performance and a good second-in-command, or military advisor, relied on War. People leading with War only worked well with highly disciplined units.<br /> <br /> <br /> What I really want to see in Performance is some sort of illusion magic: Setting the correct mood of a scene with light, sound and scents. And on higher levels not only as mind trick, but as physical emanation (allowing for stunts next to bonuses for social rolls).<br /> That could even go so far as illusions of great beast controlled by the Solar's flute which only incapacitates on a kill, but for everyone it looked like the victim was shredded to pieces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://owncloud.scaenicus.net/index.php/s/saLcZXhVcOu0j3W/download?path=%2F&amp;files=ScaenicusBacked_big.png&amp;downloadStartSecret=mflqpfu2cd8\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/ScaenicusBacked.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":1491,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1491-scaenicus","user":"Scaenicus","date":". 01-18-2014, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1491-scaenicus","name":"Scaenicus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1491_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T07:43:51-08:00","id":52377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52355#post52355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how useful this is, but Solar Performance has always done what I've wanted to do with it. When I wanted to write a series of plays that were metaphors for the Usurpation, setting up the metaphorical Solars in a sympathetic light as to pave the way for improving public opinion about the Anathema, Solar Performance was there for me. When an evil sorcerer was trying to kill me and we decided to bond instead over our love of music, Solar Performance was there for me. When I made a character who only spoke in highly ritualized compound-complex sentences and needed magic to ensure that people would listen to the pompous windbag rather than interrupt him by hitting him in the face with several feet of sharpened, Celestial metal like a sane person, Solar Performance was there for me.<br /> <br /> That all may be the result of me looking at the tools I have and making plans around them rather than making plans and trying to figure out what tools I need, though.<br /> <br /> What's the problem? Is Solar Performance looking a bit malnourished?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which Charms are you referring to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T07:44:25-08:00","id":52378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52355#post52355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how useful this is, but Solar Performance has always done what I've wanted to do with it. When I wanted to write a series of plays that were metaphors for the Usurpation, setting up the metaphorical Solars in a sympathetic light as to pave the way for improving public opinion about the Anathema, Solar Performance was there for me. When an evil sorcerer was trying to kill me and we decided to bond instead over our love of music, Solar Performance was there for me. When I made a character who only spoke in highly ritualized compound-complex sentences and needed magic to ensure that people would listen to the pompous windbag rather than interrupt him by hitting him in the face with several feet of sharpened, Celestial metal like a sane person, Solar Performance was there for me.<br /> <br /> That all may be the result of me looking at the tools I have and making plans around them rather than making plans and trying to figure out what tools I need, though.<br /> <br /> What's the problem? Is Solar Performance looking a bit malnourished?</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed on all fronts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T07:56:30-08:00","id":52380,"title":"","content":"For starters, <u><i><b>NOT MASS PRESENCE</b></i></u>.<br /> <br /> This is the #1 thing that I don't like about Performance in Ex2. At some point, it wasn't about performance anymore, it was just using Presence against more than one person. It was entirely redundant and the focus was taken away from the things only Performance could do. I think it was worse for Lunars than Solars, but it's still something that needs to be addressed during development.<br /> <br /> I don't mind if there is some overlap between the end results of Performance, Presence and Socialize, especially for Essence 1 or 2 charms, since there are some things all social characters should be able to do without being forced to favour all social abilities, but they should approach these effects very differently. For example, if you want to give someone a new Intimacy, Presence could do it by convincing someone through argument, Socialize could do it by leveraging local norms and traditions and Performance does it with an inspiring play or song. A general should be able to use Performance to boost the morale of his troops, but he shouldn't <i>need</i> to learn Performance to boost the morale of his troops if he already knows War.<br /> <br /> Performance should be about <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Performing_arts\" target=\"_blank\">performing arts</a> - lots of singing, dancing, acting and poetry. I imagine they should be more emotional, more powerful, but more fleeting and transient than Presence and Socialize. Once the performance ends, its effects linger, but it's not the same as the actual performance.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what the design space for <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Visual_arts\" target=\"_blank\">visual arts</a> should be. There definitely should be space for sculptors and painters, but I'm not sure if it should be Performance charms that are compatible with Craft or Craft charms that replicate some Performance effects. My instincts tell me painting and sculpting should be in Craft, based on Daedalus and Leonardo da Vinci.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":54,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","user":"Tiresias","date":". 01-18-2014, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":18}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T07:59:27-08:00","id":52382,"title":"","content":"Performance is done from afar (before crowds) and is impersonal. A stirring speech, a soul shaking ballad and a damning sermon are all impressive and awesome - but it is not the person that evokes anything. The people don't know how this person feels or who they are - but their words and music are crafted such that it stirs emotions deeply.<br /> <br /> If you become a celebrity, you are just a symbol - they do not revere or honor the individual behind the song and dance. I see the effects being very impressive up front but falling away far faster than presence. When you get to know someone and they impress them-self on you - that lasts a lifetime.<br /> <br /> I really love the song &quot;Meet me Half Way&quot; by the Black Eyed Peas. The meaning behind the song and the visuals just gets the existential wheels moving. That said, the actors and performers get only a minor trickle down of respect that I have for the song itself. Performance is pretty much a craft and what is crafted absorbs people. When you look at a famous painting like Mona Lisa you are in awe of the painting not the painter (in the moment).<br /> <br /> I'd like to see the distinction made between being enamored by the individual and being enamored by the performance.<br /> <br /> Such that if intimacies are made:<br /> Bob uses Presence: (Respect/Love/Friendship towards Bob)<br /> Bob uses Performance: (Love, Amused, Fascination towards the Song/Poem/Speech or the ideal behind it)<br /> Which means performance allows you to target drives and individual instances (hate the king - be devout to your wife - make your donations to the church) while presence would make them want to help their friend (you) without being told and they could act more autonomously.<br /> <br /> Further, I don't think Appearance should even factor into performance. It's just not that relevant - if anything it should provide half of what it does towards presence. See Bob Ross.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1066,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","user":"The Despot","date":". 01-18-2014, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T08:01:52-08:00","id":52384,"title":"","content":"I definitely want more emphasis on the music side of things with Performance. As others have said, having it be mass Presence is not just redundant but counterproductive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/42-aranis","name":"Aranis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar42_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T08:02:03-08:00","id":52385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52377#post52377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which Charms are you referring to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lessee:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52355#post52355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I wanted to write a series of plays that were metaphors for the Usurpation, setting up the metaphorical Solars in a sympathetic light as to pave the way for improving public opinion about the Anathema, Solar Performance was there for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That one is Heart-Compelling Method.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52355#post52355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When an evil sorcerer was trying to kill me and we decided to bond instead over our love of music, Solar Performance was there for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That uh...that was the Second Performance Excellency. *cough*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52355#post52355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I made a character who only spoke in highly ritualized compound-complex sentences and needed magic to ensure that people would listen to the pompous windbag rather than interrupt him by hitting him in the face with several feet of sharpened, Celestial metal like a sane person, Solar Performance was there for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Respect-Commanding Attitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T08:06:55-08:00","id":52390,"title":"","content":"I think that the problem with Solar Performance is that the Corebook charms already do most what a social-beast character want to do, but Solar can't go beyond an Ability theme like Abyssal/DB/Sidereal so they just stuck with creating more specialized charm.<br /> <br /> And for what I want, I want prayer charm so bad, I want a god just begging my Zenith to be his priest because Solar's ambrosia is ten times more delicious than mortal generated ambrosia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T08:10:29-08:00","id":52391,"title":"","content":"Should Acting be Performance, Larceny, or both?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T08:14:09-08:00","id":52395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52390#post52390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the problem with Solar Performance is that the Corebook charms already do most what a social-beast character want to do, but Solar can't go beyond an Ability theme like Abyssal/DB/Sidereal so they just stuck with creating more specialized charm.<br /> <br /> And for what I want, I want prayer charm so bad, I want a god just begging my Zenith to be his priest because Solar's ambrosia is ten times more delicious than mortal generated ambrosia.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what Whitewall is for. Takes so many centuries though - granted that makes ambrosia on par with Games of Divinity potency. So maybe a lesser effect as a charm based effect that in no way compares with the Games of Divinity - but a lesser god would be go out of its way for ya.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T08:15:33-08:00","id":52399,"title":"","content":"I've always thought that Solars have the least interesting social charms. Every single social campaign I've played with solars involved ended up with the players abandoning actual roleplay because the charms made it so that what you actually say had no importance. Most of the time someone just came into town yelling &quot;Love me!&quot; loud enough for people to hear it, and everyone instantly obey. Some may say that solar social charms should do just that, but to me it doesn't encourage the players to roleplay. All of the really interesting social scenes I've played have either been with mortal characters or with non-solar splats. In my opinion it's the sidereals that have the social charms that are most fun to use, like the one in Larceny that makes people disbelieve whatever you say. Using charms like that encourages you to actually be creative and clever.<br /> <br /> I'd love Solar Performance charms that help with establishing intimacies and enhancing your ability to use existing intimacies to encourage behaviour, rather than the brute force mind-control we got in 2ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1935-paradigm","name":"Paradigm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T08:16:13-08:00","id":52402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52382#post52382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Performance is done from afar (before crowds) and is impersonal. A stirring speech, a soul shaking ballad and a damning sermon are all impressive and awesome - but it is not the person that evokes anything. The people don't know how this person feels or who they are - but their words and music are crafted such that it stirs emotions deeply.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So where do street actors fall? I've worked Renaissance Fairs, and you stay in character whether you're on a stage or up close and personal. If you are anywhere a patron can see you, including the privy, you stay in character. And yes, that should be Performance. Not Socialize. Not Presence.<br /> <br /> Performance isn't just before crowds and large groups.<br /> <br /> Actually, as I think about it, Performance and Presence got swapped somewhere. Performance should not just be before the masses, but also for intimate performances for just a few, or just one. Whether that's Scheherazade's tales to entertain the sultan (and keep her head) or maintaining a role while dealing with a drunken guard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T08:22:27-08:00","id":52408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52391#post52391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should Acting be Performance, Larceny, or both?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends. &quot;I belong here, I'm just a servant, ignore me&quot; type acting? Larceny. &quot;Yes, I am the Padisha of Marakesh, and you will give me the respect I deserve&quot; type - Performance. Larceny never struck me as the default Grifter skill (though one any good con-artist would have some ability in).<br /> <br /> Similar to Forgery. If I'm forging documents, then linguistics makes sense. If I'm forging artwork, Craft makes more sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T08:26:30-08:00","id":52411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52391#post52391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should Acting be Performance, Larceny, or both?</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good question.<br /> For me theater acting is more Performance, as it requires you to use a certain kind of speech techniques and expressions which are see-able from greater distances. Also voice acting/storytelling is Performance because the goal is to reach many people (in the sense of audio quality, loudness, etc.)<br /> <br /> Acting to make some one believe you are another person is Larceny.<br /> <br /> TV/movie acting would be somewhere in between, as we pretty much want the roles to be &quot;natural&quot;, but we also have a silent agreement on certain kinds of expressions used to make the viewer understand the inner workings of a role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://owncloud.scaenicus.net/index.php/s/saLcZXhVcOu0j3W/download?path=%2F&amp;files=ScaenicusBacked_big.png&amp;downloadStartSecret=mflqpfu2cd8\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/ScaenicusBacked.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1491-scaenicus","name":"Scaenicus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1491_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T08:27:54-08:00","id":52413,"title":"","content":"I've never been much of a performing arts guy, but I did find interest in the idea of an orator or even more so a priest. Performance has been the ability governing prayers, but little in terms of Solar charms have ever allowed for super prayers. Given that one of the big things for Zeniths is that of the role of priest and the Solar Exalted bear the Mandate of Heaven, I've always felt that support for that specific role was somewhat lacking.<br /> <br /> For something a little more crazy the ability to start a spontaneous song and dance routine in which those around you join in perfect synch Bollywood style would be amazing. More tame would allow nature to play along with bird singing in tune, the wind blowing whistling in the trees just so and the trees gently swaying to the beat, etc.<br /> <br /> Also since Exalted has had something of an association with Metal, I think being able to inflict damage via music would be appropriate too. Guitar riffs that shatter rock, songs so beautiful they break hearts, and the Kung Fu movies aren't exactly lacking in musical notes that can cut. It's been something of DB territory, but it really doesn't seem to fall outside of Solar design space.<br /> <br /> All of that said, the core of the Performance ability is really about the manipulation of emotion and the core of the Charmset should focus in causing emotional responses through your performance, leading into supernaturally strong emotions and even causing seemingly impossible emotions need death to cry, a tree to fall in love with you, or the walls of a city to grovel in fear of you, performance is your ability","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T08:28:03-08:00","id":52414,"title":"","content":"I'd like to be able to play an artist without automatically imposing my will onto others. I think there's plenty of scope for Performance as inspiration before you become The Bard. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T08:30:16-08:00","id":52415,"title":"","content":"I found it odd that Performance had little to no focus on instruments. (for lack of a better analogy, Glorious Solar Lute). I get that Phantom Conjuring Performance was there to replace musical tools and to let you (for example) dance without the need to play your own music too, but it was distinctly lacking in tools.<br /> <br /> There's a certain aesthetic that is gained from an ephemeral harp that is the innermost reflection of the performer's soul, or imbuing mundane musical tools with glorious perfection, that cannot be gained from a performer just willing their music into being around them. Though it might be too small-scale for Solars.<br /> <br /> I'd add, as has been pointed out before, that makeup and made-up characters are part of performance, as are many, many non-song-and-dance forms of art. Dressing yourself up in a way that passes a message simply by looking at you (performance art, quite literally), whether for theater or for live-action political satire (walking through the streets of Paragon dressed as a hung or otherwise defaced Prefect for example).<br /> (because recetly, I've come across <a href=\"http://fata-ku.tumblr.com/post/73216377445/thebestworstidea-softgore-this-piece-was\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> [a little nsfw, trigger warning] and think that it's a method that Performance should take into account, because it can be a very powerful one. )<br /> <br /> (Also, I find it funny, without disagreeing, that Performance was mass Presence, because presence specifically could target mass units of any magnitude, as long as it was a single unit per action (unless you flurry)).<br /> <br /> Mostly though, I think 2e's performance was limited by the workings of the social system (you can only do so much when your options are UMI and Intimacies).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 01-18-2014, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T08:36:05-08:00","id":52421,"title":"","content":"I'm new to Exalted so I could be mad but maybe something that allows me to trap or bond people into my Performance or to gain properties of those who I sing, dance or act as?<br /> <br /> I'm reciting a poem about some hero of old and people listening start reenacting the deeds.<br /> <br /> I'm singing a song about a martyr suffering to save a people and those who hear it <i>feel</i> their flesh burn as the verse talks of hot coals.<br /> <br /> I'm acting a play and I hold role of a cripple and leper and my audience, transfixed fur the duration of the play, wither and suffer as the character does.<br /> <br /> I'm dancing the part of a king and while I dance, as long as I dance, the people who see <i>know</i> I am the king, the guards let me pass, the queen allows me into her chambers, the generals bow to my commands, just so long as I dance...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T08:38:27-08:00","id":52428,"title":"","content":"A twin to Demon-Wracking Glory that lets you enact Defend Other actions with your conjured miracles, rather than attacks. You can either remotely defend allies in a battle through force of voice rather than arms, or you can turtle behind your own musical guard while waiting for allies to save you. Attackers should be able to break through these conjurations, which remain broken until the next round/turn of a continued performance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T08:40:41-08:00","id":52433,"title":"","content":"While I like the generality that 2e Performance had with respect to the type of performance (you could sing, orate, dance, whatever, and the Charms would generally function) it'd be awesome to have some side branches that were more specific to different styles of performance. A Charm that just works on singing, one only for dancing, one only for oration, etc. Ways to specialize, in essence.<br /> <br /> Also, on the higher end, I'd love for Performance to do more blatantly supernatural effects on the world. Like singing so well that your rival's crops die (something that happened in the irish myth of Niall and the Nine Hostages: Laidcenn the poet satirizes his enemy so hard that no corn, grass or leaves grow in Eochaid's lands for a year). The Solar is so good at performing that the world listens and responds.<br /> <br /> I think about this more later when I've got more time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":263,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","user":"Limited Reagent","date":". 01-18-2014, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T08:43:46-08:00","id":52436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52428#post52428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A twin to Demon-Wracking Glory that lets you enact Defend Other actions with your conjured miracles, rather than attacks. You can either remotely defend allies in a battle through force of voice rather than arms, or you can turtle behind your own musical guard while waiting for allies to save you. Attackers should be able to break through these conjurations, which remain broken until the next round/turn of a continued performance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess this is not the appropriated thread to ask this, but will Solar's theme include angelic miracles. Since some people seem to think that Solar can only do human skills turn up to eleven which mean no throwing holy fire (Spirit Weapons can suck my dick), or smashing enemies with your anima 'cause no human can do those stuffs (which I think is a very silly reason).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 01-18-2014, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T08:43:47-08:00","id":52437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52421#post52421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm new to Exalted so I could be mad but maybe something that allows me to trap or bond people into my Performance or to gain properties of those who I sing, dance or act as?<br /> <br /> I'm reciting a poem about some hero of old and people listening start reenacting the deeds.<br /> <br /> I'm singing a song about a martyr suffering to save a people and those who hear it <i>feel</i> their flesh burn as the verse talks of hot coals.<br /> <br /> I'm acting a play and I hold role of a cripple and leper and my audience, transfixed fur the duration of the play, wither and suffer as the character does.<br /> <br /> I'm dancing the part of a king and while I dance, as long as I dance, the people who see <i>know</i> I am the king, the guards let me pass, the queen allows me into her chambers, the generals bow to my commands, just so long as I dance...</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that. Describing/Performing something so well that people actually feel it and believe it, without having to take complete control of their mind to do it.<br /> I'm not sure if it'd have some overlap with Larceny though ... although I think larceny shouldn't be used for impersonation (well, not face-to-face impersonation anyway).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T08:43:50-08:00","id":52438,"title":"","content":"Putting Memory-Weaving Method in Presence makes sense, since Presence is more about messing with people's logic through spoken appeals, bargains and threats, whereas Performance is probably better purified into affecting emotions through performance art. It makes more sense to thoroughly convince someone of a lie by directly speaking to them about &quot;the truth&quot; than to make up and perform on the spot an entire song and dance number for that purpose.<br /> <br /> (That should totally be a Fair Folk thing, in the vein of Genie from Disney's Aladdin. Of COURSE raksha can and would create a whole Broadway show tune at the drop of a hat for one specific situation.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 01-18-2014, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T08:49:18-08:00","id":52441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52436#post52436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess this is not the appropriated thread to ask this, but will Solar's theme include angelic miracles. Since some people seem to think that Solar can only do human skills turn up to eleven which mean no throwing holy fire (Spirit Weapons can suck my dick), or smashing enemies with your anima since no human can do those stuffs (which I think is a very silly reason).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you'll be satisfied with how much scope the developers have found for Solar charms without obviously usurping another Exalt type's conceptual space. Obviously, I can't give details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T08:52:09-08:00","id":52444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52391#post52391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should Acting be Performance, Larceny, or both?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're in costume, it's Performance. If you're in disguise, it's Larceny. This is probably a point where there should be overlap though. For example, at Essence 1, you can use either Performance or Larceny to pose as a guard, but at Essence 3, Performance lets you pose as a really intimidating guard, while Larceny lets you pose as a specific guard that everybody knows and should be able to recognize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T08:52:15-08:00","id":52445,"title":"","content":"When I'm playing a Dawn, I want my songs of battle, and the dread in facing me on the battlefield, to spread like wildfire.<br /> When I'm playing a Zenith, I want my prayers to make gods sit up and take notice.<br /> When I'm playing a Twilight, my storytelling should impart the wisdom of generations of elders.<br /> When I'm playing a Night, my musical talent must seduce the young Dynast so I might steal his secrets.<br /> When I'm playing an Eclipse, my masterpieces shall be sung unto a hundred generations.<br /> <br /> When I'm playing a warlord, the drumming of my troops will make the earth dance along.<br /> When I'm playing a sorcerer, my throat should produce sounds no human could make.<br /> When I'm playing a storyteller, I should never have to pay for my own drinks.<br /> When I'm playing a sailor, my shanties should captivate the waves themselves.<br /> When I'm playing an explorer, my song should keep the Wyld at bay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T08:55:10-08:00","id":52448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52433#post52433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>While I like the generality that 2e Performance had with respect to the type of performance (you could sing, orate, dance, whatever, and the Charms would generally function) it'd be awesome to have some side branches that were more specific to different styles of performance. A Charm that just works on singing, one only for dancing, one only for oration, etc. Ways to specialize, in essence.</b><br /> <br /> Also, on the higher end, I'd love for Performance to do more blatantly supernatural effects on the world. Like singing so well that your rival's crops die (something that happened in the irish myth of Niall and the Nine Hostages: Laidcenn the poet satirizes his enemy so hard that no corn, grass or leaves grow in Eochaid's lands for a year). The Solar is so good at performing that the world listens and responds.<br /> <br /> I think about this more later when I've got more time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually thinking about what kind of new things can be done via Evoactions, and I just realized... what about artifact instruments? Most of Performance could be more general, but if you have an Orichalcum Hapr, the Evocations are more specific on songs of the Unconquered Sun or something.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T09:01:39-08:00","id":52452,"title":"","content":"I feel like Peformance should have some take on memory alteration, at least to play on standards of how rhetoric and political and social narratives can guide people into recontextualizing events.<br /> <br /> But it's a broad kind of thing that can easily overlap with Presence and Socialize.<br /> <br /> I want to say that I think Performance should do the thing in Night's Master, where the blind musician sings a song that brings to stark relief Azhrarn's fear that humanity may one day die out and he'll be left without any entertainment, but I don't know how to distinguish it in game terms.<br /> <br /> I mean, maybe... it's not quite emotion control, but a way of presenting an idea in a form that a person can't ignore or forget...<br /> <br /> Maybe something that allows you to present your perspective or conclusion on things to people in a manner that leaves them sort of unable to come up with their own.<br /> <br /> I still think Performance should include oratory. I think Presence should cover things with a more personal character, even on occasions where you're addressing large numbers of people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T09:07:26-08:00","id":52458,"title":"","content":"For me, the distinction between Performance and Presence can be summed up as follows:<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Performance is what you </u><i><u>do:</u> </i>Performance is acting, singing, playing an instrument speaking before a vast crowd, or leading the masses in prayer (speaking if, we really need prayer charms in the new edition). A Solar poet can bring nations to their knees, weeping at the beauty of their words or songs, make enemies hesitate to destroy such a treasure, make sworn rivals forget for a moment that they hate each other and put aside past harm, so long as they can stay and listen to the Solar. A Solar Priest is one of the most sought after holymen among all the Gods. All of them should be contesting for his or her favor, and eager to do them favors, as opposed to the Solar seeking out the Gods. A Solar Performer should be Orpheus, making Deathlords weep with regret that they cannot restore the Solar's lost love in exchange for his songs and words.<br /> <br /> <u>Presence is what you<i> are:</i></u> When a Solar talks, it is with the utmost guile, charm or charisma. Their sweet words can con you in to selling your kingdom, convince you to betray your best friend or befriend your sworn enemy. When a Solar speaks, it is his raw conviction that convinces you that he is the rightful Prince of the Earth, and that following him is the just thing to do. A Solar's Presence should be able to convince even the psychically crippled ghosts to move beyond their fetters, or convince automatons to let them pass, even though they lack the password.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 01-18-2014, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T09:11:28-08:00","id":52465,"title":"","content":"Oh, while I know that Marama's stat in DotFA is a little over-the-top about the sex part, I do hope that &quot;Performance 5 (Sexual Techniques +3)&quot; will still be a thing in Ex3 ;'D","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T09:15:09-08:00","id":52470,"title":"","content":"I expect this is too vague and abstract to be useful... but...<br /> <br /> When I think about great the archetype of the great creative performers - great musicians, great comedians, great actors - one of the ideas that comes through is that we *don't* think of them as people who understood humanity and the human condition like an average person, but were really good at selling it (were really good salesmen).<br /> <br /> What comes through to me is that they are seen as great artists, in the sense that they had creative insights about what it means to be a human and to live and the right way to live, that we could never have AND expressed that in a way that is beyond the norm.<br /> <br /> Maybe Solar Performance should be true to that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T09:15:40-08:00","id":52472,"title":"","content":"It is ever hard for me to keep them separate.<br /> Presence... Emotional influences, may as well be word- and gesture-less (*).<br /> Performance... Making myself understood without the intensive emotional influence, often word-laden (*).<br /> Larceny... which takes a part of acting where you try to convince someone you are indeed the role you play<br /> Bureaucracy... which takes the part of leading by rules, guidelines and meritism<br /> War... which is good for leading by commands and disciplined troops<br /> <br /> (* The difference for me is: With presence I can instill rage and thirst for action by means of impressing people and being an example. / With performance I can instill rage and thirst by means of telling the story of the unrighteousness of their government.<br /> In the Presence case the people follow me and do what I tell them.<br /> In the Performance I influence the people to make a decision (which means the will propably not do exactly what I want, but will do so without my scrutiny, or even me being around any longer.)<br /> <br /> Would you agree?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://owncloud.scaenicus.net/index.php/s/saLcZXhVcOu0j3W/download?path=%2F&amp;files=ScaenicusBacked_big.png&amp;downloadStartSecret=mflqpfu2cd8\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/ScaenicusBacked.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1491-scaenicus","name":"Scaenicus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1491_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T09:19:29-08:00","id":52475,"title":"","content":"I think a problem Performance had was similar to other really short charm trees. Not only were there not many charms in it to take, so it was hard to really specialize in it (since you'd run out of things to buy so fast), but a couple of those few charms were also broad that it made it difficult to find new territory to expand into.<br /> At least for me, it felt like once I had Heart-Compelling and Memory-Reweaving, I would never need another Performance charm. And that is really disappointing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/103-gsd","name":"GSD","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T10:22:48-08:00","id":52514,"title":"","content":"So, here's what I want Performance to be able to do. I understand not all of this will necessarily be reasonable or doable; I don't know which of these things might already have been allocated to something else. But these are the various things I might want.<br /> <br /> 1. Damage. I want to be able to play the lap harp to cut people up like a scene out of Kung Fu Hustle. I want to be able to shout so hard and loud that I can parry attacks with it. I want to be able to dance a crater into the ground. I want to be able to issue a prayer to the Unconquered Sun to mess up creatures of darkness in my presence, like a priest stopping a vampire in its tracks with a rosary and a word to the Holy Ghost.<br /> <br /> Time and time again in fiction, you see - admittedly over-the-top - things like this. Dance-warriors, musical artillery, and prayers as weapons. There are already examples of this in 2e - Vibrating Strings Defense and Three-String Sword Prana for Dragonblooded, for example, or Withering Phantasmagoria for Abyssals. I would just really like if, more than just a fringe option, it was a solid, viable choice for cinematic action in play.<br /> <br /> 2. Buffs and debuffs. 1e/2e already did this decently, I just want to make sure this is still a thing. If 'supernaturally perfect music that invigorates and improves allies' is something D&amp;D does better with a bard than Exalted does with a Zenith, I'll be wildly disappointed. I'm not expecting to be disappointed on this one, I just want to hedge my bets by saying how important it is to me.<br /> <br /> 3. Large scale social actions. 2e always struck me as odd in that on the mundane side great effort was gone to in order to explain that Presence was mostly for direct, one-on-one interaction and Performance for social area attacks, oratory, and group persuasion, and then many of Presence's charms affected groups, to the point that going with Performance over Presence largely ended up a matter of fluff and an extra long tick per action. I want Presence and Performance to each have their own extremely distinct niches - Presence is for when you're talking to the king, and Performance for when you're orating to the king's court. I feel like if that distinction isn't protected, one or both lose their special mechanical and intellectual space in actual play.<br /> <br /> If you give me 3/3 I'll be ecstatic. If you give me 2/3, I'll be pleased, my expectations and desires well-met. If you give me 1/3, I'll be disappointed. If I don't get any of the above, I'll be, to put it lightly, shocked, and more than a little confused. If you want any clarification, details, or anything else, feel free to ask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T10:23:59-08:00","id":52516,"title":"","content":"I'd like to throw my voice into the chorus of &quot;Please make it feel different from other overlapping abilities&quot;. This is something I feel 2E Performance failed to do meaningfully.<br /> <br /> In 2E the skill felt it should be called &quot;<b>Arts</b> <i>(but not speeches, that's Presence, and not writing, that's Linguistics, and not disguise, that's Larceny, and not making priceless works of art, that's Craft).</i>. I have no idea where the conceptual space begins and ends, and while some overlap is OK (I mean, we have Melee, and Martial Arts with mundane form weapons, so it's not like this isn't unprecedented), right now it's just confusing.<br /> <br /> I really feel like in order to hash out the charm design, you need to know what the ability means, ESPECIALLY for Solars, who's Charm Paradigm is in doing things that are the pinnacle of human endeavor breached through into the supernatural realm... so in order to know what the, say, <b>Athletics</b> equivalent of &quot;Jump so much it's almost like flying (but you aren't flying because that thematic space isn't Solar-ish) is for Performance, you have to define what it is much more strongly. I understand Legacy Issues on ability names is a thing, but this isn't as much a naming issue s &quot;really, what does this do?&quot;.<br /> <br /> I apologize if I've overstated my point, but this one is a big deal and has been for me ever since I've started playing Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":255,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","user":"ParanoiaCombo","date":". 01-18-2014, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T10:27:49-08:00","id":52521,"title":"","content":"I mostly want Performance and Presence to be clearly delineated in Solar Charms. Why is this Charm Performance and not Presence? Does it involve singing, or dancing, or genuine oration (like a monologue or soliloquy)? Is it intended to invoke emotional response from an audience? I want it made clear whether Performance requires a verbal component, including when you're using Performance Charms, or if Solars can make things happen by shaking their hips or playing a mandolin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T10:34:47-08:00","id":52525,"title":"","content":"Persuasion is an important part of Solar Performance, but there is more to art than persuasion. I'd like inspiration and entertainment to be a core feature of Performance in general. As it stands there is very little reason to perform for people who already agree with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/544-deadpoint","name":"Deadpoint","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T10:42:13-08:00","id":52535,"title":"","content":"If prayer is still under Performance, stuff with that would be neat. More things to please gods and other beings, or increasing the potency of prayer or sermons led by the Exalt.<br /> <br /> The Mirror Charm Face the Light was cool too. Kind of sending out loud statements tto draw people or things out to face you.<br /> <br /> Expanding on the Phantom-Conjuring Performance stuff, I think the upgrades we got in Abyssals were neat, but could be done to be simpler mechanically. I also like the idea of doing songs or chants or something to ward off or harm creatures of darkness (if the term stays about in some form). Also the often stated as an effec tthat Solars never got in the form of shouting so loud that stuff explodes. Maybe use it eventually for long-distance or large scale projections.<br /> <br /> General inspiration and group-motivation. Not a surprise there.<br /> <br /> Double-speak performance. Something where you're giving one statement or song or something and very specific people in the audience hear something else, or you put very subtle codes and nuances in your codes. There's stuff like this all over in the original <i>Dune</i> novel I noticed.<br /> <br /> Stuff that whips-up riots or pisses off enemies. If Performance keeps its AOE nature, I can see it being the thing to kind of shoot at groups and things like that with mental influence.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T10:48:03-08:00","id":52546,"title":"","content":"Question for the folks wanting inspiration: What is the difference between inspiration and persuasion? I'd categorize inspiration as persuasion that happened subtly enough you didn't notice yourself being persuaded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T10:56:17-08:00","id":52553,"title":"","content":"Performance has been the most satisfying Solar tree I've played with. Other than the main things\u2014inspiration, emotion-manipulation, leadership, SFX\u2014I'd like to see Performance Charms that deal with:<br /> <br /> - Prayer. I'd love Performance to be a useful tool for a Solar looking to strike deals with local spirit courts, especially if it leads to a one-two prayer-diplomacy combo between the Zenith and the Eclipse.<br /> <br /> - War Charm. There should be room for the Zenith to deliver a speech that boosts the army's morale before the last battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/937-black-paper-moon","name":"Black Paper Moon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar937_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T10:57:02-08:00","id":52554,"title":"","content":"Would things like Kata's and weapon demonstrations be a part of Performance? If so, I'd like to have a charm where I can intimidate people using that, even if I have no actual with a sword at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T10:58:07-08:00","id":52555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52465#post52465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, while I know that Marama's stat in DotFA is a little over-the-top about the sex part, I do hope that &quot;Performance 5 (Sexual Techniques +3)&quot; will still be a thing in Ex3 ;'D</div> </div> </div> </div>The +3 thing won't, as we've heard that Specialities will not add dice any more:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Exalted_3E:_What_We_Know</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Q: Are Specialties still around? If so, do they function in the same way? <b>(BryanChavez)</b></i><br /> A: They are, and they don't. <b>(John M\u00f8rke)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>On the note of Performance as &quot;the sex Ability&quot;, though. First of all, I don't think it's ever been explicitly, canonically stated to be so, has it? It's mostly been talked about like that due to the stat block referred to above and the fact that you say that you &quot;perform&quot; cunnilingus and similar. And Performance is applicable in that it does relate to how well you master the execution of a craft, like singing and dancing surely is as well. However, you also perform a kata and perform surgery, and while I can see the former being possibly jointly covered by Performance and Martial Arts in some way, the latter is clearly Medicine. There's an argument to be made that a Performance speciality in sexual techniques may be more helpful to making you <i>look</i> good while performing them than actually making them <i>feel</i> good for the receiver, but I'm not sure the game would benefit from that kind of granularity either.<br /> <br /> I guess my point here is that sex is <i>very</i> interdisciplinary and boiling it down to one Ability is a gross oversimplification, so I'd say that you could easily put that speciality on a slew of other Abilities as well, while also keeping in mind that not all aspects of it is skill-related either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T10:58:17-08:00","id":52556,"title":"","content":"I need more time to think on this, but one thought that occurs to me is perhaps a sort of extension to the &quot;Pay attention to me&quot; charm... well a charm further down the line. I'm planning on playing a character whose voice is her most attractive trait... a voice who enchants those who hear it. It's going to be in a game set in the West, so... I expect Sirens? Which makes me think of a sort of defense against those by singing or speaking so beautifully, that they can't pay attention to anything but you to a degree. To ignore that which would charm, focusing only on you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T11:02:07-08:00","id":52561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52546#post52546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question for the folks wanting inspiration: What is the difference between inspiration and persuasion? I'd categorize inspiration as persuasion that happened subtly enough you didn't notice yourself being persuaded.</div> </div> </div> </div> You persuade a guy to fight a giant.<br /> <br /> You <i>inspire</i> a guy to knock the giant flat on its ass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 01-18-2014, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T11:03:25-08:00","id":52562,"title":"","content":"Summoning the Loyal Steel...but for instruments. Also being able to form an instrument-of-your-choice out of Essence would be wonderful.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of buffs - war chants to get people ready to fight, songs to demoralize your opponent. Maybe something like a long-range message, where an epic story/song you tell/sing spreads across the land.<br /> <br /> I liked the Haunting Apparition Trick charm from 2e, a handful of Performance charms that have widely varied uses is always welcome in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/41-silverwinglie","name":"silverwinglie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar41_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T11:03:38-08:00","id":52563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52546#post52546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question for the folks wanting inspiration: What is the difference between inspiration and persuasion? I'd categorize inspiration as persuasion that happened subtly enough you didn't notice yourself being persuaded.</div> </div> </div> </div> That works great for being inspired to do something you wouldn't have done otherwise, but it still leaves Performance solely as a way to convince someone to do something. What about performing for people who are already doing what you want them to do? I want room in Performance to write a play as an anniversary present for my Lunar mate, to sing to my troops of our righteous cause on the eve before battle, and to psych my Circle up for the heist we're pulling tonight. The Inspired condition from the new NWoD books is a great example of this. A rousing speech can give someone a single shot buff that they can use on one appropriate roll to increase success and recover willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/544-deadpoint","name":"Deadpoint","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T11:05:56-08:00","id":52566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52556#post52556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need more time to think on this, but one thought that occurs to me is perhaps a sort of extension to the &quot;Pay attention to me&quot; charm... well a charm further down the line. I'm planning on playing a character whose voice is her most attractive trait... a voice who enchants those who hear it. It's going to be in a game set in the West, so... I expect Sirens? Which makes me think of a sort of defense against those by singing or speaking so beautifully, that they can't pay attention to anything but you to a degree. To ignore that which would charm, focusing only on you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hrmmm, kind of a &quot;don't pay any attention to that, just listen to my voice,&quot; kind of thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T11:12:38-08:00","id":52576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52546#post52546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question for the folks wanting inspiration: What is the difference between inspiration and persuasion? I'd categorize inspiration as persuasion that happened subtly enough you didn't notice yourself being persuaded.</div> </div> </div> </div>One is more direct than the other imho. Also more sure. You can <b>persuade</b> someone that the current system sucks and the regime needs overthrowing. You can also<b> inspire </b>someone that the current system sucks and it needs overthrowing... but they might say that the current system sucks and that is why they'll work to improve it from within (where possible). In this way, inspiration has broader targets/effects, not as scalpel-like as persuasion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T11:27:26-08:00","id":52590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deadpoint</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52563#post52563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That works great for being inspired to do something you wouldn't have done otherwise, but it still leaves Performance solely as a way to convince someone to do something. What about performing for people who are already doing what you want them to do?</div> </div> </div> </div>So--and I promise I don't mean this as the insult it might sound like; I'm just framing the discussion in terms of things I recognize--something like bardic performance in D&amp;D?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T11:31:33-08:00","id":52597,"title":"","content":"Performance has traditionally been pretty solid, but I always wanted a sort of &quot;Immortal Ballad Triumphant&quot; effect. The idea is that you perform an act (song, dance, oral story, whatever) so well that it becomes a legend in its own right, inextricably tied to you but also with a life of its own, speeding its propagation through the culture and preserving/enhancing whatever core message your seed performances sent. Sort of the &quot;I Have A Dream&quot; speech effect. Traditionally, the closest you could get to this was stunting it, taking a specialty in that specific performance, and maybe fluffing your more general effects as being related to your signature piece, but it'd be nice to have something that gives you substantive bonuses to your signature <i>because</i> it's That Thing You Do, while also ensuring that it has fire-and-forget repercussions on the broader culture.<br /> <br /> I'm imagining something where an incognito Solar pens a song capturing the zeitgeist in an unstable satrapy and performs it to steadily increasing audiences at a teahouse in town, and because it so perfectly expresses the prevailing unrest and she so perfectly performs it, it becomes the anthem of a revolution and if a year later she shows up during a riot and performs it on a rooftop it's showstopping not just because she's an impossibly skilled musician but because <i>she's the person who sings that song</i> and <i>she's singing that song</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 01-18-2014, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T11:43:34-08:00","id":52607,"title":"","content":"I think Solar Performance already does most of what I'd like it to do. For instance, a Solar should definitely be able to pull off the scenes of Hope Rides Alone depicted in The Will of One and the beginning of Vengeance. <br /> <br /> I would love to see some more support for dueling performances. For instance, I would love to be able to challenge Octavian to a rock off challenge, and if he loses he has to take his sorry ass back to hell. (And also, pay my rent.)<br /> <br /> In a similar vein, I would love to be able to convey combat penalties/bonuses. Imagine, for a moment if you will... A solar is fighting a morale shaking battle against horrors emerging from the underworld. As he looks grimly over the field, he and his generals un-sling their instruments. As they break into their song, their music guides their troop's footwork, as they had done so many times during training exercises. Their masterful footwork takes the undead forces by surprise. That is, until the Abyssal general emerges on the field, surrounded by his close advisers wielding terrible instruments made of bone and sinew. A grim bell tolls just before the howling polka of oblivion bursts from the dark-lord and his backup band, and a legion of skinriding emissaries begin dancing the polka of doom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/219-zid","name":"Zid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T11:54:37-08:00","id":52618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horvagab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52576#post52576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One is more direct than the other imho. Also more sure. You can <b>persuade</b> someone that the current system sucks and the regime needs overthrowing. You can also<b> inspire </b>someone that the current system sucks and it needs overthrowing... but they might say that the current system sucks and that is why they'll work to improve it from within (where possible). In this way, inspiration has broader targets/effects, not as scalpel-like as persuasion?</div> </div> </div> </div>You inspire someone to do something that they already want to do, but otherwise do not have the motivation to do it. It is a lowering of inhibition and a raising of ambition.<br /> <br /> Persuasion is where you convince someone of something that they did not believe prior to your interventions.<br /> <br /> Ie: &quot;The Big Lebowski is awesome. You should make that stage production of it that you've always been talking about!&quot;<br /> &quot;You know, you're right! Hell yes! Let's do this!&quot;<br /> <br /> Vs<br /> <br /> &quot;I know that you think &quot;Dirty Dancing&quot; is the best movie ever, but you have failed to consider the merits of &quot;The Big Lebowski.&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh yea, you're right. The Big Lebowski <i>is</i> the best movie ever.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/219-zid","user":"Zid","date":". 01-18-2014, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/219-zid","name":"Zid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T12:01:16-08:00","id":52626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52590#post52590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So--and I promise I don't mean this as the insult it might sound like; I'm just framing the discussion in terms of things I recognize--something like bardic performance in D&amp;D?</div> </div> </div> </div> Broadly, yes. In the sense that Death of Obsidian Butterflies is like Magic Missle. I would like to see a mechanical benefit to Performance. It doesn't have to be specifically like D&amp;D, but thats something I would consider neat. As an example, look at the buffs in Nightengale Style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/544-deadpoint","name":"Deadpoint","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T12:02:22-08:00","id":52627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52597#post52597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Performance has traditionally been pretty solid, but I always wanted a sort of &quot;Immortal Ballad Triumphant&quot; effect. The idea is that you perform an act (song, dance, oral story, whatever) so well that it becomes a legend in its own right, inextricably tied to you but also with a life of its own, speeding its propagation through the culture and preserving/enhancing whatever core message your seed performances sent. Sort of the &quot;I Have A Dream&quot; speech effect. Traditionally, the closest you could get to this was stunting it, taking a specialty in that specific performance, and maybe fluffing your more general effects as being related to your signature piece, but it'd be nice to have something that gives you substantive bonuses to your signature <i>because</i> it's That Thing You Do, while also ensuring that it has fire-and-forget repercussions on the broader culture.<br /> <br /> I'm imagining something where an incognito Solar pens a song capturing the zeitgeist in an unstable satrapy and performs it to steadily increasing audiences at a teahouse in town, and because it so perfectly expresses the prevailing unrest and she so perfectly performs it, it becomes the anthem of a revolution and if a year later she shows up during a riot and performs it on a rooftop it's showstopping not just because she's an impossibly skilled musician but because <i>she's the person who sings that song</i> and <i>she's singing that song</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me want to create a sort of Reputation system where each such Legend would be handled like a Familiar - it has stats (puissance, reach, etc.), it grows, it can do things for you (sort of) but also get in trouble and get you in trouble too.<br /> Charms (probably Performance, Bureaucracy and Socialize) would be able to influence and mold the way Legends grow and spread, but not necessarily create Legends outright (to avoid fire-and-forget effects)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T12:02:26-08:00","id":52628,"title":"","content":"I want to be a Macross main character. I want to be so compelling with my singing, I can stop a battle in it's tracks<br /> <br /> Something like this<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aAWUue_Cf9g\" data-code=\"aAWUue_Cf9g\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/aAWUue_Cf9g/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2035-matsci","name":"Matsci","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T12:11:53-08:00","id":52634,"title":"","content":"In general, when I've taken Performance, I've been pleased by it. But I do actually like the ability to use Performance to be an orator instead of a singer or a musician; I think that should stay. I want to start as Cicero and work my way up to the Sermon on the Mount; I want to stop a war with a speech (or start one!).<br /> <br /> In 2E terms, I think Performance should be primarily Emotion effects with some Compulsion or Illusion thrown in. Speeches and performances are about the emotional experience far more than they are about making a point -- just look at politics throughout the history of mankind. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T12:16:01-08:00","id":52638,"title":"","content":"I really liked solar performance as it was<br /> <br /> If anything what needed was an lil paragraph saying &quot;There are Presence versions of most, if not all, performance charms (where relevant) and vise versa&quot; - because things like there only being a Salesman Spirit charm for presence and not performance didn't really make sense to me - and there not being a hypno-tongue technique for performance as well.<br /> <br /> Sure, some restrictions might be valid for the alternate versions, like saying that the mass hypno charm only works for a number of hours, not days - or that the performance salesman charm only works if used in the context of a specific kind of action (similar to how some of the integrity charms work) like when the solar is promoting a cause that the solar has a positive intimacy towards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T12:19:22-08:00","id":52642,"title":"","content":"Though I was able to eventually kinda make it work, I was perpetually kinda disappointment by the Presence / Performance / Linguistics / Craft spread and how they related to art in general.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure this design problem can really be fixed. It comes from the binary perception, the idea that something is either lingusitics or it is not... in reality, I find that most art forms are in fact complex blends of many, many skills. Abstracting them into a single talent rating is appealing from a game standpoint (simplicity) but a very poor model. How to fix it? No idea. Sorry I'm not more constructive here but maybe my problems / observations can help somebody else be insightful.<br /> <br /> Here is a thought - in the current model, art is a very adversarial thing. It's a weapon you use to convince people of your opinions / positions. That's a very... I dunno, kinda overly 'nerdish' reaction to art? And I say this as both an artist and a girl nerd. The nerd aspects of my personality want to break art down into the cause and effect, A to B, 'I do this for this reason' object sorta 'aspbergers' way of understanding it. And then the artist aspects of my personality are like, 'No, I absolutely and completely do NOT do this for those reasons, or to achieve those goals'.<br /> <br /> So why -do- people make art?<br /> <br /> What, of value, is created?<br /> <br /> Is there some way to abstract this beyond adversarial 'opinion weapons' that would give meaning to an artist beyond making them a social weapon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":762,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","user":"MissMaddy","date":". 01-18-2014, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T12:26:01-08:00","id":52645,"title":"","content":"I don't want my music to just stop a battle, I want it to be able to turn my enemies to my side.<br /> <br /> Exhibit A:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wckZcVFLU24\" data-code=\"wckZcVFLU24\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/wckZcVFLU24/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T12:34:00-08:00","id":52652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52597#post52597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Performance has traditionally been pretty solid, but I always wanted a sort of &quot;Immortal Ballad Triumphant&quot; effect. The idea is that you perform an act (song, dance, oral story, whatever) so well that it becomes a legend in its own right, inextricably tied to you but also with a life of its own, speeding its propagation through the culture and preserving/enhancing whatever core message your seed performances sent. Sort of the &quot;I Have A Dream&quot; speech effect. Traditionally, the closest you could get to this was stunting it, taking a specialty in that specific performance, and maybe fluffing your more general effects as being related to your signature piece, but it'd be nice to have something that gives you substantive bonuses to your signature <i>because</i> it's That Thing You Do, while also ensuring that it has fire-and-forget repercussions on the broader culture.<br /> <br /> I'm imagining something where an incognito Solar pens a song capturing the zeitgeist in an unstable satrapy and performs it to steadily increasing audiences at a teahouse in town, and because it so perfectly expresses the prevailing unrest and she so perfectly performs it, it becomes the anthem of a revolution and if a year later she shows up during a riot and performs it on a rooftop it's showstopping not just because she's an impossibly skilled musician but because <i>she's the person who sings that song</i> and <i>she's singing that song</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the musical equivalent to the old Thunderbolt Attack Prana &quot;design your own stylish super-attack&quot; Charm?<br /> <br /> Cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T12:34:56-08:00","id":52655,"title":"","content":"I'll add my desire for clearer division between Performance and all the other abilities it overlaps with, especially Presence. Also, I think it would be a good place to put friendly buffs and enemy debuffs that aren't quite as mind-controlly as the current stuff. Anything that lets my players make Support characters who aren't &quot;fighters&quot;, but can still meaningfully contribute to fights, is cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T12:37:42-08:00","id":52657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52546#post52546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question for the folks wanting inspiration: What is the difference between inspiration and persuasion? I'd categorize inspiration as persuasion that happened subtly enough you didn't notice yourself being persuaded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I'm going to elaborate on my earlier answer since other people are giving different answers.<br /> <br /> Inspiring someone to the degree that a Solar Exalted can should do more than persuade them to go out and do something; it should also empower them towards that action. You are emotionally motivating someone to do something regardless of rational logic, and that Solar heart-fire should carry them on to accomplish amazing feats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T12:53:08-08:00","id":52678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52657#post52657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I'm going to elaborate on my earlier answer since other people are giving different answers.<br /> <br /> Inspiring someone to the degree that a Solar Exalted can should do more than persuade them to go out and do something; it should also empower them towards that action. You are emotionally motivating someone to do something regardless of rational logic, and that Solar heart-fire should carry them on to accomplish amazing feats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose the flipside of this is that when a Solar rationally persuades someone of something (as per Presence), that forms an unshakable conviction. Not a motivating force that drives the subject to perform superhuman feats, but a belief to which they can cling even in the depths of unimaginable suffering.<br /> <br /> Solar Performance would thus strongly motivate people for short-term, immediate actions, whereas Solar Presence could enduringly motivate someone for the rest of their life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T12:55:02-08:00","id":52679,"title":"","content":"I, too, would like a clearer distinction between Performance and its points of overlap. I don't think it's necessary that divisions be complete and absolute -- like how Sail can take on things from Integrity, Resistance and elsewhere and then scope them toward being an amazing sailor -- but I definitely think the explanation of what Performance is needs to become clearer and more consistent. It definitely sounds like that's been an issue.<br /> <br /> Really, I just want EX3 Performance not to be AoE EX3 Presence. Which is how I came to think of it in 2e. I admit I come at this from a really weird angle, as I don't think I've gone through the Solar Charmset for any of this, but am quite familiar with the Fair Folk one. Bit of an odd duck, yes. Anyway, the &quot;Performance = AoE Presence&quot; thing is basically how I came to understand it from GWM: I don't remember seeing a Performance roll called for in any other circumstance. I don't know if it was the author not understanding the real distinction or if that was simply what the distinction had crystallized into at that point in the line, but... Never cared for it. It feels kinda worthless to have one ability that's so similar to another it amounts to just being the multi-target version. Please make sure this is distinct and clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T13:00:14-08:00","id":52690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52678#post52678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose the flipside of this is that when a Solar rationally persuades someone of something (as per Presence), that forms an unshakable conviction. Not a motivating force that drives the subject to perform superhuman feats, but a belief to which they can cling even in the depths of unimaginable suffering.<br /> <br /> Solar Performance would thus strongly motivate people for short-term, immediate actions, whereas Solar Presence could enduringly motivate someone for the rest of their life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really know about that. Martin Luther King's &quot;I have a dream&quot; speech certainly seems to have motivated quite a lot of people for their entire lives, and that's pretty obviously Performance.<br /> <br /> In terms of magical effects, it might be nice to see Performance focused on active bonuses/penalties where Presence focuses on resistances. So Performance could give someone fighting civil rights some bonus successes to accomplish tasks, whereas someone Presence might give them something like Righteous Lion Defense.<br /> <br /> Neither one is short or long, but one is about how you project out into the world, and the other is about your person, much like the abilities themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/782-lafing-cat","name":"Lafing Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T13:19:19-08:00","id":52710,"title":"","content":"I really liked ParanoiaCombo's idea that Performance is the arts. I don't have it any more nailed down than he/she does, but I think there are some good thoughts there.<br /> <br /> Painting, composing, singing, all under performance. This would take some of the grift out of craft, too. Sculpture is performance, although actually building something is craft (craft is the engineering side?).<br /> <br /> Presence would be acting and active communication, performance would be more passive communication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/259-overshee","name":"Overshee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar259_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T13:52:08-08:00","id":52742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Overshee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52710#post52710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really liked ParanoiaCombo's idea that Performance is the arts. I don't have it any more nailed down than he/she does, but I think there are some good thoughts there.<br /> <br /> Painting, composing, singing, all under performance. This would take some of the grift out of craft, too. Sculpture is performance, although actually building something is craft (craft is the engineering side?).<br /> <br /> Presence would be acting and active communication, performance would be more passive communication.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't. There is no showmanship in stone-carving, which is basically sculpting. Not unless you're doing some weird show with it. Likewise, there is no showmanship innate in painting, unless you are incorporating it into some street or theater performance.<br /> <br /> Likewise, good performances require that you interact and connect with the audience on some level, and it is a form of active communication, unlike a painting that stays still or a banner on the street.<br /> <br /> Hence, I don't think an active/passive divide is appropriate either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/219-zid","name":"Zid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T15:02:41-08:00","id":52785,"title":"","content":"Prayer charms! Kind of like this thing I wrote for 2E.<br /> <br /> <b>DEMANDING THE SPIRIT'S ATTENTION</b><br /> <br /> Performing a prayer and being heard by a spirit is easy for a Solar of the Zenith Caste, but getting an answer from a prideful spirit is not nearly as easy. This Charm was developed as a means of forcing an instant acknowledgment out of a successful prayer.<br /> <br /> Should the prayer be successful, the Exalt may activate this Charm in order to compel the spirit (as long as it has an Essence rating lower than the Exalt's own) to give an instant reply, either by appearing himself or ackowledging the prayer with an obvious miracle (if the spirit is capable of doing so). The spirit can ignore this influence by spending a number of Temporary Willpower equal to the Resources value of the sacrifices used for the prayer (minimum 1).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T15:45:45-08:00","id":52814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52785#post52785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prayer charms!</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, Charms enhancing prayer would be nice. In fact that's the first thing I thought of when I read the title of the thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T16:17:16-08:00","id":52833,"title":"","content":"Hmm let's see.<br /> <br /> I want to be able to sing so purely it HURTS CREATURES OF DARKNESS (Think of the song from the old movie &quot;Princess and the Goblin&quot; and you'll get it)<br /> <br /> Prayer Charms, yes. Specifically a &quot;you get your ass here RIGHT NOW mister&quot; type deal.<br /> <br /> I want a charm that stops combat and forces folks to talk instead (aka and now we're doing social combat)<br /> <br /> A pied piper effect would be fun--especially if it lead to a &quot;summon animal friends to do stuff&quot; like a disney princess, On the subject a &quot;whistle while you work&quot; type charm to speed crafting.and/or travel time would be fun.<br /> <br /> Can't think of anything else in particular that would be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I'M SORRY, I CAN'T HEAR YOU OVER THE SOUND OF HOW MANY MALFEAS CHARMS I HAVE!!!</b><i>~King Crazy Genius</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/345-kandagger","name":"Kandagger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T16:17:48-08:00","id":52835,"title":"","content":"I was at a conference for English students once. My friends and I, having had our fill of books (and having seen and fawned over Neil Gaimen), went out on the town. It was in Minneapolis, Minnesota, and we didn't have a lot of time, but we wanted to go see something we didn't have in our little podunk New Hampshire college town.<br /> So we walked and walked until we found what the natives termed a &quot;jazz bar,&quot; went in, and sat down. They ordered drinks, the 20-year-old ordered water, I got chocolate milk.<br /> The performer came on, and she looked fairly, you know - she was pretty, she had short hair, she was shy. She sat down and played piano and sang and I felt my bones crumble and the world shake and there was this great sense that there was no ceiling, just the infinite sky, and I was in it. Everyone felt that.<br /> We walked out after in a daze, giggling, wandering around. We wrote poems about it and shared them by a water fountain. We memorized the event and the feeling, sometimes maybe it is replicated, and I tell people &quot;it was that time music got me incredibly unbelievably high,&quot; but that's a joke: it was perhaps one of the only times in this life that I will ever get to feel real and whole.<br /> <br /> I want that out of Solar Performance.<br /> <br /> That or a Charm that lets me stash instruments Elsewhere, and which counts &quot;Podiums&quot; as instruments so I can pull that shit out of nowhere and start speech-makin'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":685,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","user":"Ben Quo","date":". 01-18-2014, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T16:59:19-08:00","id":52860,"title":"","content":"Given the choice between mass lying and disney music I would go for the latter. Not that is should not have other dimensions. I just believe that to be a better direction.<br /> <br /> Prayer charms that are NOT magical instant convince. But rather love poems like Slain use to win the favor of his godess Dana.<br /> <br /> Song charms that boost long term jobs. Working songs or sea shanties. <br /> <br /> illusion/trick charms... like that of magician (the ones with the doves and the bunnies)<br /> <br /> Charms that have lingering effects in pieces of art. Pieces that speak out to certain people in a certain way,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T17:15:51-08:00","id":52868,"title":"","content":"Oh, also? I would totally be okay with a charm that forces combat to turn into a dance-off. Like a Bollywood/Michael Jackson music video. Someone draws a gun or a sword or whatever, then one quick-spin and crotch-grab later and two circles are busting moves, entire armies of mortals joining in as backup performers.<br /> <br /> Obviously I know that's not going to happen. If it was even possible, it would probably undermine much of the weight and impact of real combat by being able to stop it like this. But for some reason, I want to play a game where I spend the first half-dozen sessions as a high-combat figure straight out of Ramayana or Journey to the West, then, out of nowhere, turn the siege of Thorns into a mortals vs. zombies dance off or something.<br /> <br /> But as far as real, actual advice is concerned, I'm much more in support of my previous post than this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T17:23:45-08:00","id":52871,"title":"","content":"What I want from Performance:<br /> <br /> I want to be able to captivate a willing audience and push their emotions in a specific direction.<br /> I want to be able to draw the attention of an unwilling audience and cause them to pause what they were doing for at least a moment, even if that thing was fighting each other on the field of battle.<br /> I want to be able to be heard by everyone in a large city.<br /> I want to be able to reach out to large groups of people as if I were speaking to each one personally.<br /> I want to be able to perform as if I were more than one performer. Think of music looping devices.<br /> I want to be able to inspire people to work harder and fight harder. Think D&amp;D style bardic music. Give a bonus die to actions.<br /> I want to be able to instill fear in people. This could be like the above except reducing their pool by 1.<br /> I want to be able to convey one message to the king while conveying a different message to the rest of the court.<br /> I want to be able to pray to the gods with any act I take, be it song, dance, a rousing sermon, or beneath the bedsheets.<br /> I want to be able to instill a feeling of duty into people. I want them to gain an intimacy towards myself or a subject of my choosing.<br /> I want to be able to disrupt intimacies. I want to give a speech against the ruler of the city so powerful that the city turns on him.<br /> <br /> Edit: I want to be able to train others quickly to act as a troupe. Like Tiger-Performers instead of Tiger-Warriors. I want to be able to impart these fellow performers with some of my ability. In 1e, one of my favourite moments was when I was in a performance contest. I gathered up a troupe of actors and we put on a Commedia dell'arte (<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commedia_dell&#39;arte\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commedia_dell'arte</a>) performance with only a day or so to practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":1224,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","user":"Drakhan Valane","date":".  One more thing. 01-18-2014, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T17:34:52-08:00","id":52875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kandagger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52833#post52833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A pied piper effect would be fun--especially if it lead to a &quot;summon animal friends to do stuff&quot; like a disney princess, ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Such as Snow White as portrayed in Shrek the Third.<br /> <br /> Snow White summons Forest Friends.<br /> Forest Friends use <i>Stampeed!</i><br /> It's super effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T17:39:25-08:00","id":52880,"title":"","content":"I'm sure there are plenty who have already expressed this sentiment, but:<br /> <br /> I don't want Performance to exclusively be toward multiple people. If I'm a spoony bard and I want to make a social attack against a pretty lady with a serenade to her alone, I don't want to have to use Presence for it, because I've already put my dots into Performance to use my lute. Performance should be about the performance and not the audience.<br /> <br /> Also, as an aside, what UMI feels like to targets. If I'm rocking out and everyone wants to join in too, it shouldn't feel like coercion to them. But that's more a complaint about the NMI/UMI distinction/debate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Formerly Exodan","edited":{"userid":715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/715-foorish-shamurai","user":"Foorish Shamurai","date":". 01-18-2014, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/715-foorish-shamurai","name":"Foorish Shamurai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T17:44:58-08:00","id":52882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foorish Shamurai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52880#post52880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure there are plenty who have already expressed this sentiment, but:<br /> <br /> I don't want Performance to exclusively be toward multiple people. If I'm a spoony bard and I want to make a social attack against a pretty lady with a serenade to her alone, I don't want to have to use Presence for it, because I've already put my dots into Performance to use my lute. Performance should be about the performance and not the audience.<br /> <br /> Also, as an aside, what UMI feels like to targets. If I'm rocking out and everyone wants to join in too, it shouldn't feel like coercion to them. But that's more a complaint about the NMI/UMI distinction/debate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want the terms &quot;social attack&quot; or UMI/NMI to be found in the rules at all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T17:57:38-08:00","id":52891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drakhan Valane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52882#post52882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want the terms &quot;social attack&quot; or UMI/NMI to be found in the rules at all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There will still be social combat in 3E, but yeah I agree. I would like a bit more subtlety to the way you can effect someone's mind or actions rather than &quot;either cajole or brute force/DoS attack. No middle ground.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Formerly Exodan","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/715-foorish-shamurai","name":"Foorish Shamurai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T18:14:54-08:00","id":52897,"title":"","content":"I thought they had kicked the concept of &quot;social combat&quot; out in 3e, replacing it with a more nuanced social influence system?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T18:26:33-08:00","id":52909,"title":"","content":"I want to add my voice to those calling out for Prayer Charms, assuming that prayers remain a Performance action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T18:32:40-08:00","id":52913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drakhan Valane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52897#post52897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought they had kicked the concept of &quot;social combat&quot; out in 3e, replacing it with a more nuanced social influence system?</div> </div> </div> </div>They have indeed. <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Exalted_3E:_What_We_Know#Social_Mechanics\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>'s what we know so far, and it certainly looks different enough to justify the name change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T18:49:21-08:00","id":52920,"title":"","content":"Here's what I remembered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Q: And what about social combat? Is it a separate subsystem or the combat engine with words? <b>(pwsnafu)</b></i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">A: EX3 doesn't have social combat. It has social influence mechanics. </span></span><b>(Holden)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T20:42:25-08:00","id":52975,"title":"","content":"What do I want for performance? I'd like to see performance focus on art and communication. I'd like to see music charms that let me influence the emotions of armies, and otherwise be simultaneously be a modern day pop-star, the Phantom of the Opera and a D&amp;D bard at the same time.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see acting charms that could compliment larceny charms. Charms to create a character - a role, a piece of fiction - and increasingly bring it to life in a way the Fair Folk could never do. It the solar version of shaping - The Solar declares to creation that a role, title or character exists, and Creation goes along with it because the Solar is a Lawgiver and his will and want is law. At least until the Sidereal's politely ask the Solar to stop due to the loom snarls he's causing.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see dancing charms. This would augment other skills, dances that can combine with dodge, martial arts (Solar Hero kata), or even occult (somatic components for faster casting! Ritual casting for bigger spells.)<br /> <br /> I'd like to see a public speaking branch to channel our Patrick Henry, or to be a street-rat agitator hawking playbills to change/shape public opinion. <br /> <br /> I'd like to see holy prayer charms that would be the Unconquered Sun's equivalent to the Lord's Prayer, the General Confession, Kyrie elision, Credo, Gloria, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1411-wingnut2292","name":"wingnut2292","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1411_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T21:37:55-08:00","id":52992,"title":"","content":"I'd like to put out a dissenting voice to all the calls for Performance Charms that focus on a specific type of performance, like dancing or painting or whatever. I think Charms ought to be divided according to what you're trying to do rather than how you're trying to do it, so dance-specific Performance Charms would rub me wrong in the same way sword-specific Melee Charms would. I think they'd come off as a very artificial attempt to length the trees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T21:58:44-08:00","id":53008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52992#post52992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to put out a dissenting voice to all the calls for Performance Charms that focus on a specific type of performance, like dancing or painting or whatever. I think Charms ought to be divided according to what you're trying to do rather than how you're trying to do it, so dance-specific Performance Charms would rub me wrong in the same way sword-specific Melee Charms would. I think they'd come off as a very artificial attempt to length the trees.</div> </div> </div> </div>Creating charms by what you do rather than how you do it will get you the extremely short 2ed Corebook charm-tree, but this may not be the case in 3rd Edition since the dev does said that the social system is very robust with lots of effects and result me think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T22:17:19-08:00","id":53014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52992#post52992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to put out a dissenting voice to all the calls for Performance Charms that focus on a specific type of performance, like dancing or painting or whatever. I think Charms ought to be divided according to what you're trying to do rather than how you're trying to do it, so dance-specific Performance Charms would rub me wrong in the same way sword-specific Melee Charms would. I think they'd come off as a very artificial attempt to length the trees.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I mostly agree, I think prayer Charms should be a specific thing in Exalted. I like the idea of praying so hard you can summon a god to your side to aid you. <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tsYpasHUVc8\" target=\"_blank\">Like when an Infernal using a Shintai is attacking your city</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 01-19-2014, 01:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T22:23:18-08:00","id":53021,"title":"","content":"Of course Prayer does feel Eclipsy and Bureaucratic in the Heaven sense. Then again, impassioned pleas for aid are totally Presence/Performance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T23:05:25-08:00","id":53033,"title":"","content":"Performance, unlike Melee, is not actually something people are typically likely to have. Soldiers train in a variety of weapons; Musicians train in ONE instrument, and they certainly don't usually also orate (although some do sing). Music is a place where the hyperspecialist (&quot;I can sword like no one has ever sworded before! What do you mean 'so why did you lose the fistfight with that little old lady'? I never said I could fight unarmed!&quot;) is realistic, because unlike weapons, there's seldom a &quot;wrong&quot; instrument for the situation.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Martial Arts Styles/Form Weapons have meant that there HAVE been Sword-specific Charms. Entire trees, even. For specific subtypes of sword, even.<br /> <br /> <br /> So... yes. I think I agree; there's room for the generalist, I guess, but differentiating between instrument specialists is a good idea. Not least so that you can have the Ultimate Solar Band as your group concept. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe Charms like Salty Dog Style (or whatever it was) for Acting Dance, Oratory, String Instruments... and:<br /> <br /> Acting has disguise and so on built it. (Larceny lite)<br /> Dancing has some grace and agility built in (Athletics lite)<br /> Oratory has inspirational speaking built in (War and Presence lite)<br /> String Instruments,,, not sure. Maybe this is the place for Glorious Solar Lute (and it can be the general 'instruments' section), or maybe it could be subdivided more by archetype (so there's a &quot;Archetypal Minstrel&quot; Charm that includes easy integration into a town and maybe 'bardic knowledge' and there's a &quot;musician to the Emperor&quot; archetype that includes knowledge... actually, this is basically a Socialize-lite Charm, isn't it? Cool)<br /> <br /> <br /> Prayer Charms are also a damn fine ideas.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd also like there to be something that means there's more of a reward in the offering than a die, 2m and maybe 1xp (all very useful, but... kinda bland) for when my players plan out an elaborate and huge and pretty wedding scene, complete with tracking down video clips for individual scenes... that was one of the coolest things a player has ever done in my games and it would've been nice to have been able to maybe highlight it more. Not sure how, but... something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T23:59:12-08:00","id":53049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52356#post52356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2) I want the ground to shake and things to break when I yell (like the veil ripping during the crucifixion of Jesus but potentially bigger in scope).<br /> <br /> 3) I want wind in my hair and <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dolly_zoom\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Vertigo </i>effects</a> at my beck and call.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like these, but I also want to be able to literally &quot;bring down the house&quot; with my performances - causing glass to shatter, wood to split and walls to crumble (the perfect vibrations from my song, dance, instrument, etc. causes imperfections to be amplified breaking them down or something... :-) )<br /> <br /> I'd even love for performance to have direct combat applications - like slowing, surprising, confusing, stunning, etc. your opponent with your sounds.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/68-42","name":"42!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar68_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T00:05:01-08:00","id":53056,"title":"","content":"The most essential Charms I want are ones that allow you to have ambient music/light effects that you can play off of, as well as greater image/shape inducers and something to make Emotions Palpable.<br /> <br /> I would also ways to have magical songs/music/dances that do things like uplift those around you, tame animals, and over all draw upon the Mysterious of Art itself like the Ineffable Dancing of Malfeas touches upon. Not saying Performance needs to be sorcery, but I wouldn't mind Trancendent effect, and well Martial arts became more then just punching...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T00:16:03-08:00","id":53058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>42!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53049#post53049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like these, but I also want to be able to literally &quot;bring down the house&quot; with my performances - causing glass to shatter, wood to split and walls to crumble (the perfect vibrations from my song, dance, instrument, etc. causes imperfections to be amplified breaking them down or something... :-) )<br /> <br /> I'd even love for performance to have direct combat applications - like slowing, surprising, confusing, stunning, etc. your opponent with your sounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>The blaring trumpets bringing down the walls of Jericho?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T00:33:27-08:00","id":53063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53033#post53033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Performance, unlike Melee, is not actually something people are typically likely to have. Soldiers train in a variety of weapons; Musicians train in ONE instrument, and they certainly don't usually also orate (although some do sing). Music is a place where the hyperspecialist (&quot;I can sword like no one has ever sworded before! What do you mean 'so why did you lose the fistfight with that little old lady'? I never said I could fight unarmed!&quot;) is realistic, because unlike weapons, there's seldom a &quot;wrong&quot; instrument for the situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heartily disagree. There are many, many people that sing, act on stage, play piano, and voice act/orate. You've never heard of Musicals? Those involve whole groups of people singing, dancing, and acting all at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":1224,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","user":"Drakhan Valane","date":". 01-19-2014, 03:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T00:40:39-08:00","id":53064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52992#post52992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to put out a dissenting voice to all the calls for Performance Charms that focus on a specific type of performance, like dancing or painting or whatever. I think Charms ought to be divided according to what you're trying to do rather than how you're trying to do it, so dance-specific Performance Charms would rub me wrong in the same way sword-specific Melee Charms would. I think they'd come off as a very artificial attempt to length the trees.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, most of the sail tree is targeted at ships on the water when we have ice-ships and air boats and subs and planes and sky skimmers and so on and so on. Kinda like how the DB charms are focused (in 2E) upon a specific element and there has been talk about the same charm having different effects for different elemental aspects (in 3E) - something like that could be done here. It's hard to apply the same charm to painting and doing a piano recital then a spoken performance (I mean painting and piano are both psychical then you do some oration?). Performance is a hard one just like linguistics - in both you are basically crafting. In the past the craft ability has been split between 5 sub categories and I think it would only add flavor to do the same for performance. It's the social craft to mirror the mental/physical crafts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T01:27:29-08:00","id":53069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drakhan Valane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53063#post53063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heartily disagree. There are many, many people that sing, act on stage, play piano, and voice act/orate. You've never heard of Musicals? Those involve whole groups of people singing, dancing, and acting all at once.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah. You're thinking 'average performer'. I'm thinking more of the 'top end'. Okay, this is also true of athletes... and athletics Charms enhance leaping, running and feats of strength with different Charms, not just one catch-all (barring excellencies, which suck).<br /> <br /> Sure, some people are good at a bit of everything... but if you're a legendary figure - or even world class - you'll (probably) be a specialist in one field of it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T01:52:05-08:00","id":53076,"title":"","content":"I am not thinking average. There are excellent actors that do musicals. There are things for specializing, though. They're called Specialties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T03:17:55-08:00","id":53097,"title":"","content":"<b>Things I Wanna Do With Performance In-Game:</b><br /> 1. Y'know in Victor/Victoria, where the main character, through practice and sheer mastery, can reliably and consistently hit a note that causes wine glasses to explode and champagne corks to pop out? I want to do that. I want to be able to shatter glass or crystal with my voice, or split asunder the glacier covering some First Age Ruin in the reaches of the North.<br /> <br /> 2. &quot;Play it again, Sam.&quot; &quot;Luke, I am your father.&quot; I want the ability to perform something so perfectly that bits of my performance become a meme that just spreads on its own. I want NPCs to be quoting my performances in cities that I've never been to. I want my one-liners to spread like viruses, predisposing people to believe that I'm awesome even though they've never met me.<br /> <br /> 3. I want to inspire passion and change. I want to break a Guild Slaver's heart with a short poem about human cruelty so that he rethinks his way of life. I want to whisper a sonnet from under a balcony and win the prince's heart. I want to sing up popular uprisings by singing a mournful song about how hard life is for whoever I'm singing for. I want the duke who sees me dance to order my companions imprisoned and me put in chains and brought immediately to his bedchamber, because he simply must own me. I want people who hear or see my performance to be driven to ACT, even if it's not always in the way I'd planned for them to act.<br /> <br /> 4. Mythic Music: I want to pull out a flute and play a gentle lullaby that puts an army or a rampaging behemoth to sleep. I want to march into the Underworld and into the Thousand and sing of my love for a dead woman so powerfully that the fell lord of that place sees himself in me and releases his newest ghostly slave. I want the Green Sun of Malfeas to fear my pen, for if he offends me I have sworn to make him the object of a ribald tavern song and a joke throughout Creation. I want to walk up to a tornado and speak a haiku, and watch as the winds stop and the Storm Serpent thrashing within them quiets the thunder so she can hear my voice.<br /> <br /> 5. This is My Whole Deal: I want to be able to invest in Performance as my primary ability, like you say we now can with most Abilities. I'm not so sure about improving the competency of my allies with my inspiration, but I definitely want to be able to give opponents second thoughts by singing about their folly or how terrible I am. I want investing in Performance to give me tools other than just persuading people: I want high-end Performance to start bordering on Sorcery.<br /> <br /> 6. Celebrity: I want to turn my legend into a part of my power. I want Performance charms that play off my Cult or Followers or Reputation for greater potency. I want my performances to be better because I get my legions of screaming fans to sing along. I want my marching army to sing with me as we march and inspire dread in my enemies. I want the Brides of Ahlat as my backup dancer-bodyguards while I turn violence into a ballet. I want to lead my cult in songs of prayer that call down rains of fire from the heavens and split the seas asunder that we might walk across them. I want to sing and inspire others to join in and sing along, because together our voices are so much stronger than mine could ever be alone.<br /> <br /> <b>Some Performance Inspirations:</b><br /> 1. Bilbo Baggins. In the book, you know the silly &quot;Attercop&quot; song he sings, where he terrorizes his deadly opponents to the core by sing-song nonsense as he murders them? That. Also, I like the way the song at the beginning inspires Bilbo to leave his home and go out into danger. When I picture Husband Seducing Demon dance, at least used to recruit men to go to war, I always picture Bilbo listening to the dwarves' song and dreaming of fire and gold and distant lands as he drifts off to sleep, and awakening with a hankering for adventure.<br /> 2. Evita. Like, the entire movie.<br /> 3. Prince of Egypt. Again, the whole movie. Moses has always been great Solar inspiration.<br /> 4. Orpheus. I wanna be able to sing Cerebus to sleep and warm the hearts of the gods of the Underworld.<br /> 5. Constantine: It's a mediocre movie, but at the end when Gabriel sends him flying with a breath, and when Satan blows Gabriel's wings right off with a roar? I want to use my voice as a weapon like that. Might be more Abyssal territory?<br /> 6. Victor/Victoria: Performance as disguise (less about physical disguise and more about acting and creating expectations: everybody's too busy saying &quot;He's totally lying, he can't really be a Count&quot; to question whether you're a &quot;He&quot;), and as a weapon of mass destruction (exploding glasses turned up to Exalted levels of power).<br /> 7. Trigun. There's this scene where pacifist Vash the Stampede wants to clear out a place, so he just sings a creepy song over the intercom about how much he loves killing people and relies on his reputation and performance to scare his opponents away, and to unnerve whoever's left into being less of a problem. He pulls the same trick again later on a whole city by &quot;rampaging&quot; through the streets firing his gun in the air and roaring about the slaughter he's gonna bring to the place, just to make sure there aren't any innocent bystanders when shit goes down.<br /> 8. Mary Poppins...but her songs might be more Raksha performance inspiration...<br /> 9. Six-String Samurai. It's a ridiculous and terrible cult classic, but I want to see music in Exalted in the same sort of &quot;bordering on sorcery&quot; magical sense it appears in this movie. I want an Abyssal and a Solar doing a supernatural rock-off battle over the fate of modern music to be a thing. I want philosophical and artistic differences over genre and style to manifest themselves in Exalted-level violence.<br /> 10. Hendrix smashing his guitar. I want my performances to be so iconic and memorable that people keep copying or satirizing it or ripping them off or misquoting it for decades...along with whatever message and philosophy went with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 01-19-2014, 06:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T05:38:42-08:00","id":53134,"title":"","content":"I would performance that encourages someone to spend more than 0 dots, but less than 5 in it. It's one of the few abilities that I usually see getting either completely ignored or made character-defining, but never in-between. I'd like something to encourage Robin Hood to sink a dot or two in so he can cheer his band of Merry Men around the campfire, or an exorcist to learn to play the flute to quiet the restless dead, without both characters feeling like they must inevitably follow the upward path to &quot;all shall love me and despair&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/894-skeptic-tank","name":"Skeptic Tank","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar894_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T05:51:54-08:00","id":53139,"title":"","content":"Some of you are mentioning prayer Charms. What do you imagine prayer doing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T06:09:39-08:00","id":53143,"title":"","content":"Hm, I can see some prayer charms 'enhancing' your prayers: you provide more Essence, or Willpower, or something, as a baseline charm. One higher up could be that you establish an Intimacy on the spirit that you are praying to (or Exalt, or Yozi or...). You don't necessarily get to decide what kind of Intimacy, but I'm guessing the relevant spirit would feel something in case of a sudden surge of power.<br /> <br /> This also lets Solar play more with gods, both Terrestrial and Celestial. You don't get to necessarily summon the god instantly, but you can establish a line of communication. This can help Solars be involved in the Celestial Bureaucracy in a way, and even wield something against. Hell, this might be something the Gold Faction could try to use to increase their own power? &quot;Do this for me, and I've got a Solar who is interested in honoring you.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T06:09:53-08:00","id":53144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to be a period-appropriate rockstar. Which is to say, I want people who come to the game saying, &quot;I want to be a rock star!&quot; to find a charm that enables that, but in a way which is not anachronistic and fits with the pulp-fantasy tropes of the setting, rather than in a weird thematically inconsistent way.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, one of my players built a Rockstar GSP when I told him, in explaining the premise of Internals, &quot;You guys are kinda Hell's Rockstars.&quot; <br /> &quot;Challenge accepted,&quot; indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T06:16:15-08:00","id":53145,"title":"","content":"Gain the god's attention, at least. Possibly even his favor, though such should generally be subtle and rarely immediate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T06:23:55-08:00","id":53149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52357#post52357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I want Performance to make up its mind on whether it's supposed to be about music and dance or about long-winded speeches, because I have some trouble seeing certain Charms apply to both sides of that coin.<br /> <br /> [/SIZE]</span>[/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1441-ersatz","name":"Ersatz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T06:26:44-08:00","id":53152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52992#post52992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to put out a dissenting voice to all the calls for Performance Charms that focus on a specific type of performance, like dancing or painting or whatever. I think Charms ought to be divided according to what you're trying to do rather than how you're trying to do it, so dance-specific Performance Charms would rub me wrong in the same way sword-specific Melee Charms would. I think they'd come off as a very artificial attempt to length the trees.</div> </div> </div> </div>*taps chin* <br /> <br /> You don't have a problem with manifestly different methods all ending in the same response? It certainly makes it impossible to actually play a dancer or a courtesan without specific Martial Arts styles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T06:48:25-08:00","id":53158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=52992#post52992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to put out a dissenting voice to all the calls for Performance Charms that focus on a specific type of performance, like dancing or painting or whatever. I think Charms ought to be divided according to what you're trying to do rather than how you're trying to do it, so dance-specific Performance Charms would rub me wrong in the same way sword-specific Melee Charms would. I think they'd come off as a very artificial attempt to length the trees.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see John got here before me, but none the less.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, but that's not how Abilities work. The end mechanical result is not the dividing factor, but the means by which you get there. Compare Melee and Martial Arts. They both have the same mechanical outcome: they interact with the combat system, deal damage and such. The only difference between them is if you use a weapon or not, and that is entirely stylistic. That's a means, no an end. I can understand if you'd rather not see too narrow Charms (even if I myself think Charms in 2e were too broad if anything), but that's not the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T06:49:00-08:00","id":53159,"title":"","content":"Would Zhuge Liang's <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UT86xQHGPqE\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;empty fort strategy&quot;</a> against Sima Yi's army in Romance of the Three Kingdoms count? To summarize; Sima outnumbers Zhuge's forces, and unable to retreat or mount a proper defense, Zhuge publicly plays the lute with such calm and poise, that Sima is convinced he has a massive ambush in waiting. It is using the power of his performance to capitalize on his reputation as a master strategist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/691-cadwyn","name":"Cadwyn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar691_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T06:52:09-08:00","id":53160,"title":"","content":"Hm, maybe there could a few scattered charms for specific performances, which could also provide the basis if you want to make your own. What I'm thinking of are specific songs: &quot;Song of Rousing Heroism&quot; is a Performance Charm for the Solars AND an actual Song that's still oft-sung by armies on the march ever since the war against the Primordials. Only the Solars can use it as an actual Charm, the specific intonations and such can only be sung by someone who has the prerquisite mastery of the singing (Excellency and Ability rating) and the necessary Essence to infuse the song with the beneficial potential.<br /> <br /> These could be relatively low-Essence songs, and Performance-based Solars could write their own songs and create their own Charms based on those perhaps. Not sure how this would work for non-song, non-story arts though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T06:52:48-08:00","id":53161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53139#post53139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of you are mentioning prayer Charms. What do you imagine prayer doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Way back in my first Exalted game my players city-state was attacked my a vastly superior army. Prior to the enemy reaching the city the Zenith led the city in prayer to the god of war (We were very new and had no idea who the relevant god was) asking that they bless the warriors of the city and favor their side in battle. I wanted the prayer to be meaningful given the effort put into it, but had no real mechanical basis for it so all I ended up doing was generally take it easier on the players and allowed their tactics to work better than I would have normally allowed.<br /> <br /> Some kind of mechanics for god giving a blessing for a successful prayer would be nice, with charms guaranteeing success or even enhancing the blessing would be welcome.<br /> <br /> Beyond that the ability to actually talk to the god you are praying too, or even compelling a terrestrial god to visit you personally wouldn't be out of place.<br /> <br /> One of the Abyssal charm mentions Abyssals using it to make threatening or intimidating prayers to god, the ability to socially influence those you are praying to would probably work too. Getting a god to favor you or even fall in love with because of your prayers seems appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T06:56:39-08:00","id":53166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53152#post53152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't have a problem with manifestly different methods all ending in the same response?</div> </div> </div> </div>Within the limits of such the abstractions this system embraces, where anyone with a given rank of Performance is equally good at singing and dancing and acting and impromptu rap battles and stand-up comedy despite all those things being distinctly different disciplines that require different skills in the real world...yeah. I'm pretty much okay with it. If we're going to be basing Charms on Abilities, then I'd prefer to base them on Abilities rather than Specialties. I think doing otherwise would be a tacit admission that Performance just doesn't have much to do, mechanically, and we need to extend the Charm tree by coming up with ways to do the same things in different disciplines. I doubt anyone is arguing that we need different Craft Charms for the different kinds of elemental Crafts, or different Lunar Strength Charms for lifting with your legs or with your back.<br /> <br /> Of course, all this is operating from a perhaps mistaken belief Performance will have a similar role in third edition to what it did in second, and that social influence will be comparable to physical combat in that both systems will have goals of causing others to do things they otherwise wouldn't, whether it's signing a treaty or bleeding profusely on the floor. You probably know something I don't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53152#post53152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It certainly makes it impossible to actually play a dancer or a courtesan without specific Martial Arts styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? I mean, Hungry Tiger Technique working for every weapon instead of just spears doesn't mean the Solar Melee Charms make it impossible for me to play a dragoon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T07:05:57-08:00","id":53170,"title":"","content":"God can do all sort of stuff with Solar's prayer:<ul><li>Summoning prayer to increase the god's soaks/HL/dice pools....etc.</li> <li>Easier to upgrade their Sanctum rating.</li> <li>A single Solar priest can count as a dot in Cult or even increase the god's Salary.</li> </ul>In exchange for those benefits, the spirit can either form an positive Intimacy toward the Solar, suffer an Compulsion effect that make it want to take care of its follower or being bound under an Eclipse Oath for each months pass that the spirits enjoying those blessing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T07:16:21-08:00","id":53174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53166#post53166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so? I mean, Hungry Tiger Technique working for every weapon instead of just spears doesn't mean the Solar Melee Charms make it impossible for me to play a dragoon.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is easy to agree that weapons all have the same function, even if they operate a little differently. It is easier to gloss over the difference in operation, because the difference is much smaller, and can be covered by stunts. <br /> <br /> Oration, dancing, singing, playing an instrument and acting all have somewhat different objectives. It is harder to gloss over the differences and yet feel like the character has done anything, or that your choice of method, and ergo the identification of your character as a great speaker or a great dancer, means something significant. Weapons at least have stats to make them different. They suggest the stunts by which they operate differently. Different performances all literally have the same end, making the choice of dancer or speaker completely arbitrary. Stunts don't change this, but rather they highlight the problem even more intensely. No matter how amazing your speech, or great your dance, it has the exact same result. This is appropriate when you stunt swinging an ax or dropping a hammer, but not when you are dancing or speaking. IE, dancing and speaking are sufficiently different as to desire something more in the result, something that affirms your method and makes you feel like one choice is valid and different from another.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T07:21:21-08:00","id":53177,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... wasn't there something about Unarmed Solar Brawl and Improvised Weapons Solar Brawl being different builds (and presumably being part of different charm trees)? I could see Performance doing something like that, with different Charms for dancing and singing, but I'm not sure if you'd be able to do it without getting redundant end effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T07:22:11-08:00","id":53179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53139#post53139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of you are mentioning prayer Charms. What do you imagine prayer doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gain the attemtion and favor of the god in question, as someone else said.<br /> <br /> It could also generate Essence for the god and possibly even heal the god (think of the &quot;resurrection&quot; of Tinkerbell in <b>Peter Pan</b>), giving the Solar in question something to bargain with. <br /> <br /> If Social Combat in third edition is anything like second edition, I would think it made sense to have a Performance Charm that made Social Attacks (whether performed with Presence, Performance, or Investigation) <i>undodgeable </i>because the Solar will not and cannot be ignored. Combined with a prayer that could be pretty sweet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T07:30:02-08:00","id":53180,"title":"","content":"Prayer and religious function is such a large part of society and cultural identity that I have a real problem with boiling it down to freeform magical bonuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T07:33:51-08:00","id":53181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53139#post53139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of you are mentioning prayer Charms. What do you imagine prayer doing?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, now that's not like three in the morning in my country I can actually muster the brainpower to elaborate.<br /> <br /> - I want my prayer to be not only heard, but noticed. Ensuring a method of at least communication with the object of my worship. This should be able to be defended, so a player can't just nag the hell of the UCS even if he ultimately ignores his prayers.<br /> <br /> - I want my prayers to empower the gods that answer them. Not only giving them essence, but making the more able to help. For example, a minor god of war may be able to bless a few of a tribe's warriors, a minor god of war compelled to act by my prayers can bless the whole tribe.<br /> <br /> - I want to lead congregations in prayers of such beauty that gods not only feel compelled to answer but would actually feel heart-broken should they ignore them.<br /> <br /> - I want to be able to withhold prayer from gods that have been dishonest with me in such a way that any other prayer they receive is hollow and &quot;tasteless&quot;.<br /> <br /> Overall I want to encourage gods to answer my prayers without forcing them and to make advantageous for them to work with me, not only because I'm a potent creature of my own right, but because I can help them squeeze so much more form their cult and their own domain that they wouldn't have been able to dream before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","user":"Ravraxas","date":". 01-19-2014, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T07:34:48-08:00","id":53182,"title":"","content":"re: performance differences vs. melee differences<br /> <br /> I'd be fine with effects that depend on specific kinds of Performance -- just like there are Larceny effects that work for different kinds of Larceny (you don't want or expect to use an impersonation charm to forge documents for example).<br /> <br /> Like having Character/Acting charms, Dance, Musc and Singing charms (maybe more generally Voice charms? could cover prayer, singing, oration)<br /> <br /> That said though, a means to differentiate performances might be interesting, like a little sub-system (I like sub-systems) that lets you build up to your end-result, with a small subset of stats to track the performance........... this won't be suitable for the corebook though, i'd wager.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T07:49:18-08:00","id":53189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53180#post53180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prayer and religious function is such a large part of society and cultural identity that I have a real problem with boiling it down to freeform magical bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is understandable. On the other hand, there is an actual Prayer action through Performance, in the last two Editions at least, and I think not having at least a few things key off that feels... strange. Kinda like an unused Chekhov's Gun maybe?<br /> <br /> Also I do think that gods should notice when one of the Greatest Incarna's Chosen Champion prays to them: it can be both a 'material' bonus, or simply a matter of prestige. And I do think it supports involving Solars in Celestial or Terrestrial god politics, if the players or ST are interested in that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T07:49:30-08:00","id":53190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53158#post53158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, but that's not how Abilities work. The end mechanical result is not the dividing factor, but the means by which you get there. Compare Melee and Martial Arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was talking about Charms. You're talking about Abilities. I was pretty happy when Charms got the Merged Keyword so you didn't have to keep buying different versions of Charms that all ultimately do the same thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53174#post53174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oration, dancing, singing, playing an instrument and acting all have somewhat different objectives. It is harder to gloss over the differences and yet feel like the character has done anything, or that your choice of method, and ergo the identification of your character as a great speaker or a great dancer, means something significant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may be the wrong guy to talk to about this. Choosing to express my character's identity through Performance, and his Performance through Specialties and stunts, never bothered me. That someone would feel that way is such a weird idea to me it never even occurred until someone brought it up, and I'm still having a little trouble wrapping my mind around it (I'm sitting here wondering why people would complain about this, but not someone who defines himself as an armorer feeling like his character is weakened by the fact that another Solar with Craft (Fire) can use the same Charms to make pottery).<br /> <br /> If I'm in the minority, then by all means, do what it takes to make the majority happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T07:51:03-08:00","id":53191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53180#post53180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prayer and religious function is such a large part of society and cultural identity that I have a real problem with boiling it down to freeform magical bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well as it stands prayer is largely &quot;I pray and nothing happens,&quot; You need to be quite familiar with the rules for spirits or thaumaturgy before you can actually know what you might accomplish, or as a ST know what you might do for a player. If the core rule book has solid guidelines for gods and what they can do it becomes less of an issue and prayer charms can focus more on communicating with the gods and the ST can work out what if anything the god would do for you.<br /> <br /> Without some kind of guideline to what a god might do for you a simple very small bonus might fit better with a specific note attached to the rules stating there are a wide array of gods and the blessings they might offer are just as varied as the gods themselves. A simple lowering the target number for one specific roll, or simple +1 die to a roll makes prayer a meaningful enough concept to show that prayer does have real power and people do in fact do it for a reason. Though I will leave it to the creative minds as to how to make prayer a meaningful action.<br /> <br /> As it stood in 2e there wasn't anything to distinguish a Zenith Priest from a Zenith Rock Star beyond the stunts employed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T08:10:20-08:00","id":53199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53139#post53139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of you are mentioning prayer Charms. What do you imagine prayer doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Formally led Prayer by a Priest should get the attention of a God. This might result in effects similar to thaumaturgical rituals, as the little gods enact your properly coded desires, or it might request that a more major God do something, which the God is free to ignore, pervert, or grant as they will.<br /> <br /> Solar Prayer charms should allow you to social-fu the God in various ways to get a more desirable outcome. <br /> <br /> ...Ideally this should be done in such a way that no-one goes &quot;Oh, so you're a Cleric now?&quot; as a result, but I'm not entirely sure you can play a priest in an RPG without being compared to D&amp;D Clerics.<br /> <br /> But yeah, some of that mythic music power that lets you calm the win and pause the sun because the spirits are too busy looking at you to do what they're supposed to be doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T08:13:05-08:00","id":53205,"title":"","content":"Pondering, wasn't there something about Linguistic Charms allowing you to channel social charms in unusual ways? In written form, or something about that? If that's still a thing, maybe Prayer charms could allow you to use social Charms without being face to face with the being you are praying to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T08:13:31-08:00","id":53206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horvagab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53160#post53160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, maybe there could a few scattered charms for specific performances, which could also provide the basis if you want to make your own. What I'm thinking of are specific songs: &quot;Song of Rousing Heroism&quot; is a Performance Charm for the Solars AND an actual Song that's still oft-sung by armies on the march ever since the war against the Primordials. Only the Solars can use it as an actual Charm, the specific intonations and such can only be sung by someone who has the prerquisite mastery of the singing (Excellency and Ability rating) and the necessary Essence to infuse the song with the beneficial potential.<br /> <br /> These could be relatively low-Essence songs, and Performance-based Solars could write their own songs and create their own Charms based on those perhaps. Not sure how this would work for non-song, non-story arts though...</div> </div> </div> </div>This almost sounds like opening up the concept of Martial Arts Techniques to other Abilities ...which is honestly something I would like to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T08:16:24-08:00","id":53210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53199#post53199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Formally led Prayer by a Priest should get the attention of a God. This might result in effects similar to thaumaturgical rituals, as the little gods enact your properly coded desires, or it might request that a more major God do something, which the God is free to ignore, pervert, or grant as they will.<br /> <br /> Solar Prayer charms should allow you to social-fu the God in various ways to get a more desirable outcome.<br /> <br /> ...Ideally this should be done in such a way that no-one goes &quot;Oh, so you're a Cleric now?&quot; as a result, but I'm not entirely sure you can play a priest in an RPG without being compared to D&amp;D Clerics.<br /> <br /> But yeah, some of that mythic music power that lets you calm the win and pause the sun because the spirits are too busy looking at you to do what they're supposed to be doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Solar can use his social influence Charms on a spirit in order to persuade it to act. It doesn't require prayer.<br /> <br /> Thanks, everyone. I will think on it and get back to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T08:20:33-08:00","id":53215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53180#post53180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prayer and religious function is such a large part of society and cultural identity that I have a real problem with boiling it down to freeform magical bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then maybe it should focus more on communicating, attracting, and beseeching a specific god, with Solar charms enhancing all of those things further, possibly to the point of borderline summoning of the god?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T08:22:28-08:00","id":53217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53152#post53152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't have a problem with manifestly different methods all ending in the same response? It certainly makes it impossible to actually play a dancer or a courtesan without specific Martial Arts styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at it this way: if you're playing a dancer -- not a general performer, but a dancer -- with Performance as their main thing, wouldn't you want as much room as possible to grow within that Ability without having to go against the established style of the character?<br /> <br /> (This is not a rejection of medium-specific Charms, but a call for a solid base of general Charms to supplement them.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T08:27:25-08:00","id":53220,"title":"","content":"For the record, I agree with all JimB has said about this.<br /> <br /> I <i>actually want</i> all types of performances to have the same end result in most cases. I mean, sure, you generally use acting rather than dance to imitate someone (to go along with that disguise from Larceny, for instance)...Unless you are imitating the mannerisms and style of another dancer. So the Charm that helps in this should work with both, even if in most cases acting is gonna be more appropriate - the rest is stunts.<br /> <br /> I just have a hard time seeing what a method could accomplish that another couldn't in most cases. If I want to make a village distrustful of a neighboring village in preparation to get them into comflict, one might do it through song or a speech. But why not with a dance? Why not with a theatrical performance with no words? Isn't that the sort of thing a mythologically good, say, dancer, should be able to do?<br /> <br /> I'm sure there are some edge cases, though none come to mind right now, in which a specific kind of performance should be the only one to be able to achieve a given effect. I would be pretty happy if these are left to custom Charms, possibly with a couple in the book to serve as examples.<br /> <br /> <br /> I should clarify, though, that this is not something I care all that much about. I prefer it being the way I mention, but as long as the execution is well done, I'll be happy either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T08:31:32-08:00","id":53222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53210#post53210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Solar can use his social influence Charms on a spirit in order to persuade it to act. It doesn't require prayer.<br /> <br /> Thanks, everyone. I will think on it and get back to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIrc, one of the big things about Prayer in previous editions was that it let you communicate with the God directly or gain their attention if they wouldn't normally be awake enough to listen. It's hard to use social influence on a God, if they're hiding in their sanctum going &quot;La La La, I can't hear you.&quot; and prayer potentially offers a way to bypass that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T08:33:33-08:00","id":53223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53180#post53180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prayer and religious function is such a large part of society and cultural identity that I have a real problem with boiling it down to freeform magical bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, as I see it prayer in Exalted is akin to giving yourself to the god (as in an object of worship), you give your time, resources, and sometimes even your life and blood to the god in order to empower it. This vision of prayer has been reinforced by things like Malfeas' prayer mills, and every little town a god extorts for prayer.<br /> <br /> Exalted Prayer (as in prayer made by the Chosen) should be like that, you give something empowered by your essence and your prayer gives a god a rush. Hell, Solar prayer could take thematic elements from the Exigence, just as the Holy Flame of the Unconquered Sun enables a god to reach beyond itself and craft a Miracle the prayers of the Sun's Chosen make god momentarily run on Solar Essence perfecting their acts with their unending Excellence.<br /> <br /> Ultimately a Solar Priest should be able to play Polytheistic Moses, he comes to a land exploited by the Realm it's people and it's gods oppressed by the Dragon-Blooded and empowers the gods of the land to fight back, it all ends with the Solar as the new Priest-King (or simply High Priest depending on his preferences) glorious for all to see. Or as a glorified drug dealer, depending who you're asking to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T08:50:28-08:00","id":53229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53217#post53217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at it this way: if you're playing a dancer -- not a general performer, but a dancer -- with Performance as their main thing, wouldn't you want as much room as possible to grow within that Ability without having to go against the established style of the character?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all. The style is far more important to me than optimization. Any way you shake it, doing a dance that transforms a nation into a tool for your cause feels inherently different than doing that with a speech, and far more sorcerous.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T08:51:42-08:00","id":53230,"title":"","content":"I'm of a mind with Hatewheel that prayer and religious ritual is too deeply rooted in society and culture for Charms that enhance it to just be a set of generic bonuses.<br /> <br /> That said, some prayer Charms would be interesting! I could definitely see room for a prayer Charm that ensured that a Solar's heartfelt entreaty (and it has to be heartfelt!!) will stand out from the background mumble and place itself prominently in the foreground of the spirit's mind.<br /> <br /> As far as what I want from Performance generally:<br /> - Respect-Commanding Attitude, in some form or another.<br /> - Possibly building off of that, I'd like my performances to endear me to people - witness Conan's reluctance to kill Rinaldo, even when Rinaldo directly and openly agitated against him. A Solar's audience, just like the audience of any master, can easily become so besotted with a performer's craft that they will forgive the performer themself a great deal.<br /> - This could also easily branch into Orpheus-style &quot;music soothes the savage beast&quot; effects - I just really want my Solar musician to be so talented that even wild beasts will calmly listen to her play and not harm her.<br /> - Even departing from the strict &quot;your performances endear you to people&quot; thing, you could move more generally into effects that make the Solar a larger-than-life showperson whose flashy moves and inimitable charm mean you can't help but grin. A Dawn with some Performance could be the epitome of the charismatic, show-off, crowd-pleasing superhero with legions of adoring fans. It'd be sort of like Black Claw Style in the way that even your battles, or your ordinary conversations, can be performances that will sway an audience.<br /> - I'd like my music, or speech, or whatever, to penetrate my audience's consciousness even through adversity and distraction. If there are ten thousand rebel soldiers who haven't eaten well for a week or two, haven't bathed in a month, and have been camped out in the wilderness, they might not be in the mood to listen to a rousing rendition of their movement's anthem - but if a Performance-focused Solar is singing, it should still put a fire in their hearts.<br /> - &quot;Command of inanimate objects through the power of your music&quot; may be a little weird for a Solar effect - but I like the idea of the trees and rocks turning to listen as a Solar plays, or of the least gods of furniture and tools and dishes being woken to action by a Solar's house-cleaning song. Go full Disney Princess on this.<br /> - Maybe an effect, related to or an upgrade of Respect-Commanding Attitude, that makes a Solar's performances <i>very noticeable. </i>Even if you're distracted, or your mind is on something else, the distant sounds of a Solar orator's speech will draw you out of your house and wandering through town looking for it. At higher levels, even immaterial spirits may pause in their duties and listen, enchanted by your skill. A really skilled Solar musician might be able to still a sandstorm with a performance, the storm-spirits quieting their own winds so that they might better hear the song - and to Hell with the tongue-lashing they'll catch from their superiors for it!<br /> - An effect to make my voice, or music, or whatever, carry further than it might be expected to, and be less diminished by background noise or distance than it otherwise would be. As a possible upgrade, maybe something that guarantees that people the Solar is close to will hear the Solar's music - the circle takes heart from the faint songs of one of their members, even as they are all confined to separate cells in the Deathlord's vast fortress.<br /> - Solar Performance should set fire to the spirits of its audience! I don't know precisely how that would be represented, but I'd definitely enjoy some kind of effect that allows people to draw strength/determination/comfort from the Solar's performances (or the memories thereof) in times of doubt or hardship. Obviously, that <i>sounds </i>like it would mostly be used for good, but I will note that a Solar dictator could use it to harden the hearts of their secret police just as easily as another Solar could encourage dispossessed refugees not to despair and lose hope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=238\" data-tempid=\"temp_238_1438728365271_197\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1821-golden-demon","name":"Golden Demon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T09:07:47-08:00","id":53240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53222#post53222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IIrc, one of the big things about Prayer in previous editions was that it let you communicate with the God directly or gain their attention if they wouldn't normally be awake enough to listen. It's hard to use social influence on a God, if they're hiding in their sanctum going &quot;La La La, I can't hear you.&quot; and prayer potentially offers a way to bypass that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would that be something Charms cover, though, or would a Priest Merit be more appropriate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T09:08:47-08:00","id":53242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53229#post53229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not at all. The style is far more important to me than optimization. Any way you shake it, doing a dance that transforms a nation into a tool for your cause feels inherently different than doing that with a speech, and far more sorcerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about optimisation. I'm talking about having somewhere to <i>go</i>, even after you've mastered all the glories of dance. This somewhere needn't \u2013 in fact, shouldn't \u2013 be up.<br /> I'm talking about, essentially, being able to mainline Performance without engaging in every <i>kind</i> of performance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T09:15:07-08:00","id":53243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53242#post53242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not talking about optimisation. I'm talking about having somewhere to <i>go</i>, even after you've mastered all the glories of dance. This somewhere needn't \u2013 in fact, shouldn't \u2013 be up.<br /> I'm talking about, essentially, being able to mainline Performance without engaging in every <i>kind</i> of performance.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're talking about it, but I am not sure what you are imagining, or whether you are arguing for or against the idea.<br /> <br /> It's easy to split disciplines. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T09:17:26-08:00","id":53246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53229#post53229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not at all. The style is far more important to me than optimization. Any way you shake it, doing a dance that transforms a nation into a tool for your cause feels inherently different than doing that with a speech, and far more sorcerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the fact that a dance doesn't reach as many people as a song. A dance requires line of sight, whereas a song reaches anyone within earshot. With proper acoustics or a favorable wind, an audible performance can reach much, much farther than a visual one. Phantom Conjuring Performance can offset this somewhat, but projecting a gigantic image of your dancing self over a city still requires line of sight; people inside their homes or on the other side of the mountain cannot see it the way they could hear an amplified song.<br /> <br /> Further, having certain Performance Charms be centered around an effect like Building Confidence (For Superhuman Strength) and having other Performance Charms centered around a specific kind of performance like Dancing allows for more individuation between character Charmsets, and variety of combinations such as seen in Second Edition's Solar Medicine Tree.<br /> <br /> Also, I'd like for a Performance-heavy character to have their investment rewarded when they dance, sing and play an instrument all at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T09:18:25-08:00","id":53248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53242#post53242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not talking about optimisation. I'm talking about having somewhere to <i>go</i>, even after you've mastered all the glories of dance. This somewhere needn't \u2013 in fact, shouldn't \u2013 be up.<br /> I'm talking about, essentially, being able to mainline Performance without engaging in every <i>kind</i> of performance.</div> </div> </div> </div>In other words, you want to see Performance be like Melee in the regard that you can use all Melee Charms with literally any melee weapon imaginable, and likewise all Performance Charms should be usable with any manner of performance a character might specialize in. Is that what you're getting at?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T09:30:32-08:00","id":53263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus Dicere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53248#post53248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In other words, you want to see Performance be like Melee in the regard that you can use all Melee Charms with literally any melee weapon imaginable, and likewise all Performance Charms should be usable with any manner of performance a character might specialize in. Is that what you're getting at?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that was specifically mentioned at one point. And I'm personally inclined to agree with that method. If you want dance specific charms, and song specific charms, and orator specific charms extend the concept of Martial Arts to other abilities such that you have dance styles, and music style, orator techniques.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T09:32:53-08:00","id":53265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53139#post53139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of you are mentioning prayer Charms. What do you imagine prayer doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I rather want prayer to work in one of two ways. And for both of these two ways, I want it accessible to mortal priests too, if only in a lesser form. I want mortal prayer to be the low form of exalted prayer, like thaumaturgy is to sorcery in 2e, or like mundane martial arts systems are to supernatural martial arts.<br /> <br /> 1. The force of true faith. The priest turning back a vampire by brandishing a cross and reciting the lord's prayer with such force of personality and potent faith that the creature of darkness can't help but retreat. Holy effects that protect people praying or repel hostility from approaching people praying. I want my prayers to be able to invoke such fundamental faith and holiness that a deity doesn't even have to answer the prayer for creatures of darkness to flee or be unable to enter my temple for the prayers resonating among its halls.<br /> <br /> I want true faith to be a Holy force that can be harnessed with prayer. Hell, I want stories of mortal priests able to hold off hungry ghosts from their temple with impassioned prayer, with Solar Performance just taking an existing effect to a whole new level.<br /> <br /> 2. Requests to deities that can be answered. I want there to be rules - actual rules, not the half-description of how Prayer works in 2e - for praying to a crafting god in order to gain boons and luck while making a daiklave. I want to be able to pray to a god of health and have disease cast out of someone without invoking a Medicine charm. I want to be able to pray for seas to part. As long as I contact the right deity, pay the right price, and roll high enough, I want to be able to access all kinds of effects with prayer.<br /> <br /> That said, I want there to be a price to the versatility. It should be slower than a charm activation - slower than shaping up some Sorcery, even, unless Sorcery is already slower in 3e. I want it to be expensive to use charms that facilitate you reliably getting an answer. In other words, I want you to be able to pray for effects normally available with other charms and sorcery, but contingent on getting the appropriate god to actually pay attention to you, which costs more essence and more time than doing it yourself would have cost.<br /> <br /> In other words, I want to see Zenith's getting help from gods and spirits using prayer in the same way that, say, an Eclipse might use contract negotiation and bureaucracy, or a Dawn might directly bully them into a task, or a Twilight might summon and bind them to a function, or a Night might blackmail, manipulate, and cajole them.<br /> <br /> For both of the above items, I want them to be accessible in lesser measures to mortals. I want a priest with true faith to cause ghosts and other creatures of darkness to feel pain in his presence as he recites his heartfelt prayers. I want a sufficiently impassioned plea by a mortal supplicant over a moderate period of time to yield an actual miracle from on high. And I want there to be actual rules for making this happen, rather than it being a one-off ST houseruling, which get taken to Exalted levels by someone who's invested in Performance, not something that only becomes accessible at exalted levels in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T09:47:25-08:00","id":53272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53243#post53243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're talking about it, but I am not sure what you are imagining, or whether you are arguing for or against the idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>See the parenthesis in my original post (reposted below): I'm not arguing against discipline-specific Charms, because those are a good idea, but I'm arguing <i>for</i> there being a good number of Charms available to multiple disciplines.<br /> This is doubtlessly a thing you've already considered, but I thought it was worth emphasising anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (This is not a rejection of medium-specific Charms, but a call for a solid base of general Charms to supplement them.) </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 01-19-2014, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T09:55:19-08:00","id":53276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53229#post53229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not at all. The style is far more important to me than optimization. Any way you shake it, doing a dance that transforms a nation into a tool for your cause feels inherently different than doing that with a speech, and far more sorcerous.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree with you there, it worries me a little bit, because such arguments could potentially riddle the performance tree with speedbumps if you're trying to master multiple styles of performance. &quot;Ok, I've gotten the entire dance tree, time to get the singing tree which is full of very similar effects, but because I've decided I want to do both I need to buy them all again. yay.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what the sweet spot there is, honestly. A broad base of generic charms that apply to any performance with a few type specific branches into specialized effects? Calling out certain effects as requiring a specific type of performance? Charms which change slightly, depending on what type of performance you're using? One tree for each type of performance, with judicious use of the Merged Keyword, or some other method of not having to pay for similar charms as long as you've already got one of them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T10:12:25-08:00","id":53283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53276#post53276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what the sweet spot there is, honestly. A broad base of generic charms that apply to any performance with a few type specific branches into specialized effects? Calling out certain effects as requiring a specific type of performance? Charms which change slightly, depending on what type of performance you're using?</div> </div> </div> </div>These are what I'd do. Have a base of all-applicable performance Charms, some perhaps having shifted effects based on exactly what type of performance, then side branches for certain types of performances when it makes sense. And not all Charms would have to be completely specialized; you could have a Charm that works with, say, singing and musical instruments, or another which works with anything with words (most singing, oration), or another that's for non-vocal (dancing, musical instruments), and so on. All depends on the specifics of the effects of the Charm.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T10:20:04-08:00","id":53285,"title":"","content":"I've not read more than the first page of this thread but...<br /> <br /> My favorite Performance Charm has always been Withering Phantasmagoria (And its Solar Equivalent, Demon-Wracking Glory). As long as I can use my music to smite my foes, I'll be happy. A song so sad that hearts stop, a dance so evocative and horrible the people rip their eyes out, a speech so commanding that the sun itself reacts and sears away my opposition.<br /> <br /> Just the basics, you know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T10:21:49-08:00","id":53287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagadaishio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53265#post53265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I rather want prayer to work in one of two ways. And for both of these two ways, I want it accessible to mortal priests too, if only in a lesser form. I want mortal prayer to be the low form of exalted prayer, like thaumaturgy is to sorcery in 2e, or like mundane martial arts systems are to supernatural martial arts.<br /> <br /> 1. The force of true faith. The priest turning back a vampire by brandishing a cross and reciting the lord's prayer with such force of personality and potent faith that the creature of darkness can't help but retreat. Holy effects that protect people praying or repel hostility from approaching people praying. I want my prayers to be able to invoke such fundamental faith and holiness that a deity doesn't even have to answer the prayer for creatures of darkness to flee or be unable to enter my temple for the prayers resonating among its halls.<br /> <br /> I want true faith to be a Holy force that can be harnessed with prayer. Hell, I want stories of mortal priests able to hold off hungry ghosts from their temple with impassioned prayer, with Solar Performance just taking an existing effect to a whole new level.<br /> <br /> 2. Requests to deities that can be answered. I want there to be rules - actual rules, not the half-description of how Prayer works in 2e - for praying to a crafting god in order to gain boons and luck while making a daiklave. I want to be able to pray to a god of health and have disease cast out of someone without invoking a Medicine charm. I want to be able to pray for seas to part. As long as I contact the right deity, pay the right price, and roll high enough, I want to be able to access all kinds of effects with prayer.<br /> <br /> That said, I want there to be a price to the versatility. It should be slower than a charm activation - slower than shaping up some Sorcery, even, unless Sorcery is already slower in 3e. I want it to be expensive to use charms that facilitate you reliably getting an answer. In other words, I want you to be able to pray for effects normally available with other charms and sorcery, but contingent on getting the appropriate god to actually pay attention to you, which costs more essence and more time than doing it yourself would have cost.<br /> <br /> In other words, I want to see Zenith's getting help from gods and spirits using prayer in the same way that, say, an Eclipse might use contract negotiation and bureaucracy, or a Dawn might directly bully them into a task, or a Twilight might summon and bind them to a function, or a Night might blackmail, manipulate, and cajole them.<br /> <br /> For both of the above items, I want them to be accessible in lesser measures to mortals. I want a priest with true faith to cause ghosts and other creatures of darkness to feel pain in his presence as he recites his heartfelt prayers. I want a sufficiently impassioned plea by a mortal supplicant over a moderate period of time to yield an actual miracle from on high. And I want there to be actual rules for making this happen, rather than it being a one-off ST houseruling, which get taken to Exalted levels by someone who's invested in Performance, not something that only becomes accessible at exalted levels in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Gods don't give a fuck. Most prayers go unanswered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T10:26:32-08:00","id":53288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53190#post53190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was talking about Charms. You're talking about Abilities. I was pretty happy when Charms got the Merged Keyword so you didn't have to keep buying different versions of Charms that all ultimately do the same thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> I may be the wrong guy to talk to about this. Choosing to express my character's identity through Performance, and his Performance through Specialties and stunts, never bothered me. That someone would feel that way is such a weird idea to me it never even occurred until someone brought it up, and I'm still having a little trouble wrapping my mind around it (I'm sitting here wondering why people would complain about this, but not someone who defines himself as an armorer feeling like his character is weakened by the fact that another Solar with Craft (Fire) can use the same Charms to make pottery).<br /> <br /> If I'm in the minority, then by all means, do what it takes to make the majority happy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Buying different versions of Charms that do the same thing sucks. I can't imagine anyone wanting &quot;you must buy the entire charmset again, this time with the word 'dance' replaced with 'song'&quot;, rather than 'dance Charms do different things from song Charms'. (Again, my suggestion was a 'dancer' Charm that provides inhuman grace and agility, mostly within the context of dance but useful outside your performances... and would make no sense on a singer who can't dance.)<br /> <br /> <br /> As for armourer vs. pottery: Craft does kinda suck that way. When I built a Solar architect, limiting myself to Craft (Earth) was close enough, but the fact that the same what, ten? Charms were your only options (and most of the low essence ones didn't even involve crafting stuff)? Not great.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, speaking of which, devs? Please keep the Singing Stick, it's kinda awesome. Best. Artifact. Ever. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, point is, YES, the inability to distinguish crafts specialities isn't great either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T10:28:40-08:00","id":53290,"title":"","content":"Honestly? Before I could even start to say what I want out of the Performance ability in Exalted 3e, I'd need to know what it encompasses and how that is different from the Presence and Socialize abilities.<br /> <br /> Even in 2e there was a lot of bleed over with charms in Presence and Performance doing remarkably similar things and in many cases being compatible enough to combo.<br /> <br /> The current view that I hold, is that Presence is when you're trying to convince/impress/influence/jedi-mind-trick a single person, Performance when you're swaying a group, and socialize when you're figuring out social dynamics and politics. Is this accurate for 3e or even 2e? I have no freakin' idea. Over the past week I've had this topic come up repeatedly and gotten divergent answers every single time, and not merely telling me I'm wrong but divergent from each other.<br /> <br /> All I can really say is an excellency and I liked the special effects charms,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T10:40:06-08:00","id":53295,"title":"","content":"As for different forms of Performance... I'd liken it similar to my groups homebrew of craft, since we didn't use it much. You buy your dots in the necessary Performance, but you can only use your performance charms through any avenue in which you have a specialty.<br /> <br /> Then again, preferably, you wouldn't need to do any of that at all. Just like how you can use any melee Charm with swords, and spears, and chains and sais...despite them being quite different to use. If your Performance gives you broad knowledge of all these different ways to incite a crowd, then your Charms should work with all of them. You don't need a &quot;dancing' or a 'singing' tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T10:50:53-08:00","id":53301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53288#post53288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Buying different versions of Charms that do the same thing sucks. I can't imagine anyone wanting &quot;you must buy the entire charmset again, this time with the word 'dance' replaced with 'song'&quot;, rather than 'dance Charms do different things from song Charms'. (Again, my suggestion was a 'dancer' Charm that provides inhuman grace and agility, mostly within the context of dance but useful outside your performances... and would make no sense on a singer who can't dance.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't it also possible that a Solar Dancing Charm would have strengths and weaknesses versus a Solar singing/instrumental Charm?<br /> <br /> Maybe the Solar Dancing Charm is super-effective against an audience within line-of-sight, and also close enough for their respective visual range to pick up all of the details of the Solar's appearance. Whereas a Solar singing Charm has much greater effective range, but less impact. And a Solar instrumental Charm requires the Solar to be using an instrument, but is even more effective than the Sing Charm (though not as much as the Dancing Charm) -- an instrument which prevents the Solar from singing (ie: a wind instrument) would be more powerful to counter-balance the close-off option of singing and playing at the same time; likewise with an instrument too big to dance with.<br /> <br /> I can also see a Dancing or Instrumental Charm being incapable of the same range of effects as a Singing Charm, since a song with lyrics can convey messages through a verbal language that your audience knows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T10:54:20-08:00","id":53303,"title":"","content":"I just think you should be able to dance so beautifully, the gods of the landscape around you would be compelled to appear before you, and be favorably inclined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T10:57:50-08:00","id":53308,"title":"","content":"Ah! One thing that Solar Performance could do that would be cool!<br /> <br /> Extreme quotability! If someone who's witnessed a persuasive speech that the Solar made is reprising the Solar's exact arguments later, maybe they get a tool bonus or something? IDK.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=238\" data-tempid=\"temp_238_1438728365271_197\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1821-golden-demon","name":"Golden Demon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T11:01:48-08:00","id":53314,"title":"","content":"As long as there is a base tree that's style neutral, I personally would love to see things such Husband-Seducing-Demon-Dance (I love that name, btw) and other charms that either are specific to one or maybe two performance styles. That is, as long as it's still possible to simply stunt using a different method. Because then it enriches the game with fluff while at the same time allowing me to play someone who uses the flute to achieve every performance based goal.<br /> <br /> I guess one of the base charms I'd like to see in performance would be one that allows you to speak through your art?<br /> Tell people through dance that their magistrate is bleeding them dry, and that they shouldn't take it. Use the flute to seduce the governor's daughter. Make a spectre doubt the path it has chosen in un-life through the harp. Give a speech about cooking that actually tells people to support a specific candidate in an election.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2UIUH9oaJnHMWIxcVdGMjNUYlE\" target=\"_blank\">3EX Martial Arts basic overview (Weapons, Armor, Attributes &amp; Abilities)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/366-edward-eldritch","name":"Edward Eldritch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T11:03:02-08:00","id":53316,"title":"","content":"I want Solar Performance to be the archetypal storyteller. I want to capture an audience's imaginations and open them to new ideas, new concepts. I want to enrapture a crowd with the stories I weave. When I describe a scene I want it to be laid out in the air above, a giant illusion of what had happened. When I play a song I want to be able to make it so good that the trees lean in to hear me, that the wind stops blowing so as not to disturb my sound. I want to be Orpheus, and have my voice be so grand that the underworld opens to me, and even the rulers of the dead stop and listen to my pleas. When I bow along a viola I want it to rain when I play in a minor key, I want lightning to strike as my bow hops in a staccato rhythm. When I play a Solar with Performance I want the stories I know, and the songs I can play, to be the way I can shape the world for better or for worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2042-madxhatter0","name":"MadxHatter0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T11:04:38-08:00","id":53317,"title":"","content":"Also, something I would miss dearly: Phantom-Conjuring Performance. Being almost entirely free to create whatever image I want to support my description, is just a grand thing.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Although it should be obvious, I'd like to add that it would be nice if it had some kind of effect within the rules this time, beyond &quot;Sure, describe whatever you like&quot;.<br /> Also, I want to be able to use it or a charm following it to make mice dance complicated and choreographed dances to my songs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2UIUH9oaJnHMWIxcVdGMjNUYlE\" target=\"_blank\">3EX Martial Arts basic overview (Weapons, Armor, Attributes &amp; Abilities)</a>","edited":{"userid":366,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/366-edward-eldritch","user":"Edward Eldritch","date":".  Forgot something 01-19-2014, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/366-edward-eldritch","name":"Edward Eldritch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T11:08:50-08:00","id":53320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53288#post53288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Buying different versions of Charms that do the same thing sucks. I can't imagine anyone wanting &quot;You must buy the entire Charmset again, this time with the word 'dance' replaced with 'song,'&quot; rather than 'dance Charms do different things from song Charms.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. I don't mean to suggest I think the writers are going to go all Pathfinder bard on the Performance tree and make identical effects that you can apply to different subsets of Performance only by paying an XP tax. I was only saying I disagree with Weimann's idea that since Abilities are more or less identical, it's okay to produce more or less identical Charms. I guess what I'm saying is, when it comes to a choice between D&amp;D and Mutants &amp; Masterminds, I generally prefer the system that has an effect and lets me create my own fluff around it rather than defining effects by the fluff that was chosen for me. When I violate that general preference, it's because I already agree with the fluff enough that it doesn't bother me to have the flavor of my powers dictated to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T11:10:50-08:00","id":53323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53287#post53287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Gods don't give a fuck. Most prayers go unanswered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not necessarily saying that I want most prayers to be answered. I'm saying I want there to be actual rules for a mortal praying to a god and getting them answered - whether it's a social influence roll playing on a god's intimacies, purview, and sacrifices offered, or a borderline-thaumaturgic ritual invoking the god's glory and power. I want it to be something that the truly magnificent of mortal priests can do without spending any essence, and a reason to justify mass prayer and mortal religious organization.<br /> <br /> And I want it to be something that a Zenith - the priests and performers of the Solars - takes to impossible levels in the same way a Dawn takes Melee and War to impossible levels. I want a Zenith to be able to make a prayer to a god in heaven that it can't - or is unwilling to - refuse. I want a high priest of a religious order to be able to - not with their power, but with the power a god uses through them with a sufficiently advanced but mundane prayer - bring sight to the blind. I want a tribe in a drought who sacrifices their entire herd of cattle and prays without food or sleep for a week straight to be granted a miraculous rain or stream of water.<br /> <br /> And I want rules for it, rather than just ST fiat, in the same way I want any other sort of social influence rules, instead of having stats and strategy be totally freeform.<br /> <br /> I don't necessarily want some random dude to be able to ask Ahlat for sweet kung fu skills for an upcoming fight and get them. I want a priest of Ahlat to be able to sacrifice a bull during a religious ceremonial festival as part of a prayer for success in an upcoming war and have their military actually get some bonuses. And I want a Zenith to be able to do the same thing and manage to cajole Ahlat into personally intervening in a battle, all without meeting face-to-face, with a prayer issued.<br /> <br /> In a setting where prayer is so often talked about, where local gods organize cults, where religions hold massive sway, where an entire faith just dedicated to proper regulation of prayer is the most powerful religion in Creation, I want prayer to actually mean something. For gods to have a real, mechanical reason to want it. For people to have something to gain by giving it, especially in large amounts or the right way. And I want an Exalt to be able to issue prayers with as much perfection and force as the prayers of an entire community of mortals, just as an Exalted martial artist could single-handedly fight an entire town and win.<br /> <br /> So, basically, I'm not saying I want gods to be answering prayers left right and backwards. I want rules for getting gods to give a fuck, I want rules for what happens when prayers are answered, and I want Solar Performance charms to interface with that subsystem in a way that justifies them being called the priests caste.<br /> <br /> Does that make sense, or am I just talking in circles?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T11:17:41-08:00","id":53327,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of separate branches or trees for separate types of performance, at least broadly. It sounds like 3e is expanding the smaller trees, so I'm not too worried about a lack of options for any given character. That said, I do think <i>some</i> Performance charms should be generally applicable, because that helps bulk things up a bit and conveys what Performance is as an Ability, and there isn't really any reason for, say, Phantom-Conjuring Performance to be limited to one type of performance.<br /> <br /> But I don't really think the comparison to a melee tree just for swords is apt, because it's a different level of subdivision -- there are only three or four broad categories of performance that might warrant making a tree for, and they're as different from one another as Melee and Archery, reflecting the higher degree of compression in Abilities that don't have hefty subsystems attached. The best example within Melee would be something like &quot;improvised weapons vs. crafted weapons&quot;, or &quot;weapons designed to inflict nonlethal injuries vs. lethal weapons&quot; or at least the classic piercing/cutting/crushing division.<br /> <br /> JimB has a point, I think, which is that there are real trade-offs associated with the various methods. But while I like some general effects for the reasons I mentioned above, I also think that allowing trees to focus on specific slices of the Ability is very valuable for character. Personally, if I were playing a dancer I'd place much more value on the ability to highlight my character's unique qualities with some dance-focused powers than on the ability to take the entire Performance tree without deviating from concept. You can go too far in that direction, but I don't think &quot;let's have separate branches for singing, dancing and oratory&quot; is going too far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T11:18:05-08:00","id":53328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagadaishio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53323#post53323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ...And I want rules for it, rather than just ST fiat, in the same way I want any other sort of social influence rules, instead of having stats and strategy be totally freeform.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in full agreement there. It wasn't done really well in 2Ex but I was happy there was a system for prayers being answered, even if the result was still completely up to the ST, there was a system that said &quot;this much should be enough to get an answer&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2UIUH9oaJnHMWIxcVdGMjNUYlE\" target=\"_blank\">3EX Martial Arts basic overview (Weapons, Armor, Attributes &amp; Abilities)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/366-edward-eldritch","name":"Edward Eldritch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T11:26:55-08:00","id":53337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53290#post53290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly? Before I could even start to say what I want out of the Performance ability in Exalted 3e, I'd need to know what it encompasses and how that is different from the Presence and Socialize abilities.<br /> <br /> Even in 2e there was a lot of bleed over with charms in Presence and Performance doing remarkably similar things and in many cases being compatible enough to combo.<br /> <br /> The current view that I hold, is that Presence is when you're trying to convince/impress/influence/jedi-mind-trick a single person, Performance when you're swaying a group, and socialize when you're figuring out social dynamics and politics. Is this accurate for 3e or even 2e? I have no freakin' idea. Over the past week I've had this topic come up repeatedly and gotten divergent answers every single time, and not merely telling me I'm wrong but divergent from each other.<br /> <br /> All I can really say is an excellency and I liked the special effects charms,</div> </div> </div> </div>i also have problem with this, giving speech always felt more like Presence for me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T11:28:51-08:00","id":53339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Edward Eldritch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53328#post53328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm in full agreement there. It wasn't done really well in 2Ex but I was happy there was a system for prayers being answered, even if the result was still completely up to the ST, there was a system that said &quot;this much should be enough to get an answer&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think I'd rather just have prayer wired into social influence on some level, rather than a &quot;press button, get effect&quot; framework. Trying to get a god to answer your prayer should be relatively similar to trying to get a Guild factor to respond to your request for a meeting, after accounting for the extra complications associated with prayers (they're not a great medium for social influence, they need extra work to rise above the background noise of Twitter randos that major gods are accustomed to, etc.) Depending on what social influence looks like, this may mean that you need to make the god like you first in order to effect a mechanical compulsion, or that you can only put them in a situation where ignoring you is a strain, rather than impossible, or whatever.<br /> <br /> In general I am against a model where a certain number of successes is presumed sufficient to make the god do something, even if it's something as basic as &quot;respond&quot;. That's a fine way to handwave it when you don't really care, but it should be implemented on top of a system where contextuality is critical, like the social influence mechanics have been hinted to be. There are only two cases where I'd be comfortable with a guaranteed event happening given enough successes: I think it's okay for &quot;bribe size&quot; (how much the God gains from the prayer, etc) to be linked to roll success, and I think it's fine if the number of successes control how <i>noticeable</i> your prayers are. But gods are people in Exalted, and the mechanics shouldn't present them as skinner boxes that dispense magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T11:34:37-08:00","id":53343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53287#post53287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Gods don't give a fuck. Most prayers go unanswered.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Gods damnit, I made an account after lurking all this time just to respond to this)<br /> <br /> See, my problem with the whole &quot;Gods don't give a fuck&quot; argument, in Exalted at least, is that even the most selfish and corrupt little god has reasons to want praise. While it's true not every God is like our favorite field God; acting out of kindness and general compassion for the people who worship them, but there is still one force that can keep the small gods motivated. (As a note, this is all on the assumption you didn't throw this concept onto the burning trash heap as well. If you did, please disregard this post.)<br /> <br /> Ambrosia. And quintessence, but mostly ambrosia.<br /> <br /> If it's vital enough that some gods will strong-arm mortals into praying to them mafia style, what's the difference when a priest with faith prays and leads more prayers because, hell, his prayers are being answered if they pray hard enough! Does a little god need a couple more ambrosia to bribe the censor into looking the other way while he does something? Well, these people really want a good harvest, if I give it to them in a way that makes it more obvious I'm helping, they'll sing my praises. I can envision a largely symbiotic relationship existing in many locations in Creation, where charismatic priests lead their flocks into worshiping one particular small god in return for certain favors. Maybe making sacrifices to them as well, rice, fruit, children, still beating hearts, the normal fare.<br /> <br /> That's where prayer charms can come in. Even if you take out direct references to Ambrosia, it's clear from some fiction that Gods want to be praised, and get something out of it. There's some conceptual leeway on what can be done with this.<br /> - A charm that allows the character to simulate a sacrifice with something lesser, stopping human sacrifice with the burning of certain finely crafted talismans for example.<br /> - Creating an intimacy in the spirit towards his worshipers, giving him a compulsion to provide service in return for prayers.<br /> - Blessing a sacred site to give a bonus towards praying to a particular God.<br /> - Blessing a small God in the name of the UCS, allowing this little God to siphon off some of the prayer juice in his domain dedicated to the UCS (or the Solar who set this charm up, allowing the small God to maintain the Solar's cult and get a benefit from it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2043-ladikn","name":"Ladikn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T11:44:33-08:00","id":53351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53339#post53339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I think I'd rather just have prayer wired into social influence on some level, rather than a &quot;press button, get effect&quot; framework. Trying to get a god to answer your prayer should be relatively similar to trying to get a Guild factor to respond to your request for a meeting, after accounting for the extra complications associated with prayers (they're not a great medium for social influence, they need extra work to rise above the background noise of Twitter randos that major gods are accustomed to, etc.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I see nothing wrong for a certain amount of successes to be needed to get attention through prayer. The important thing is what happens after you get the attention. And maybe variety in how much you need.<br /> In 2EX I was glad we had anything at all. But I'm certainly not against a well thought-out system that makes prayer become an interesting choice to influence a god or start interacting with him on a deeper level. I certainly am not arguing in favor of a magic dispenser. Is there even anyone who would?<br /> <br /> The question remains whether prayer should be more than a telegraph with chocolates to the gods, or whether a whole system could be built around it or it could be integrated into the social system well enough. I have no idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2UIUH9oaJnHMWIxcVdGMjNUYlE\" target=\"_blank\">3EX Martial Arts basic overview (Weapons, Armor, Attributes &amp; Abilities)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/366-edward-eldritch","name":"Edward Eldritch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T11:52:45-08:00","id":53355,"title":"","content":"I personally have no problem envisioning a high-performance individual being roughly as useful to a God as an exceedingly talented accountant might be for a corporation.<br /> <br /> That is to say, I can easily see how mortals / Exalted who are gifted or superlatively talented in the arts of performance might in some way provide a desirable condition for spirits to enjoy.<br /> <br /> I'm not so certain that should mean that Performance can like, summon Gods or anything, but it ought to make one more potent in negotiation with them simply because they do enjoy prayers!<br /> <br /> I'm envisioning a Solar more approaching a despotic spirit privately and negotiating some grand celebration or a term of service in exchange for certain favors. This is distinct from a Solar calling out the name of God so authoritatively that he manifests on the field of battle and scorches enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T11:55:14-08:00","id":53359,"title":"","content":"That's the point of Solar level Prayer: You MAKE the god give a fuck. You might not get what you want (they may be offended and act against you), but that god will turn his attention to your cause at least for a moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T12:18:05-08:00","id":53375,"title":"","content":"In regards to Performance types and charms: I'm of two minds.<br /> <br /> One. It can be argued that the end result is the same with all performance: Emotional manipulation. As far as choice of style goes, that's something for the ST to adjudicate the ultimate effect. No one can see your dance? It doesn't matter how awesome it is or how many motes you threw into it.<br /> <br /> Two. Observe Larceny. It covers disguising, opening locks, and picking pockets. All of these I argue are more disparate than acting and dancing. Unless 3e has changed things up completely, they involve quite different charms but do not break up the Ability into separate sub-abilities.<br /> <br /> If you really believe that Performance types should split up that strongly, I'd recommend doing what I think should be done with Craft: You get one Ability, but gate the disciplines with Merits. You get a free one with your first dot (and maybe extra free ones at 3, 5, however works best for you) and purchase a 1-dot merit to unlock each additional discipline (assuming it works similar to WoD Merits).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T12:57:06-08:00","id":53392,"title":"","content":"Prayer-specific Performance Charms has always felt like a weirdly narrows and branching idea for a collection of Solar Charms to me.<br /> <br /> Like, a basis in which to root some Sidereal Performance Charms maybe, but not Solars.<br /> <br /> I can see the fact that prayer is a Performance action to make it be a viable vector for regular Charms, mind, meaning that it can serve as a way to socially influence the god over range.<br /> <br /> Which, really, seems like the general purpose of prayer anyway; for the most part, I think prayer is a way for people to ask a god to overlook them, often with a tasty sacrifice or offering to go along with it.<br /> <br /> I can see Panther or Perfect Soul using it as a means to tell a god to go fuck themselves, but still through the resolution of Performance Charms that would generally be a forceful means of telling somebody to do that, rather than a specific &quot;tell gods to fuck off&quot; Charm.<br /> <br /> Prayer isn't really a special thing, it's just a way of communicating with spiritual beings in a manner that they're sensitive to, in a way that songs do so with a person who has ears.<br /> <br /> Essence and ambrosia generation are generated through the circumstances described in the Cult Background (now Merit, I suppose), and I don't think it's really worth tracking just how many prayer actions constitute any given level of the Merit (and indeed, most such daily worship is not even such an action).<br /> <br /> There are cases where a prayer provokes a specific and notable kind of response, but even those are still generally a manner of the god already having a predefined relationship with the petitioners, like Ahlat with his Brides. So emulating something like that would still likely require the Solar to have gone to the god and established certain terms of service.<br /> <br /> At its most basic, I'd see prayer actions as like several forms of bureaucracy actions; they send an intent out into the setting that the Storyteller can account for as a consideration for how things play out, but they're not abstracting it all so much as to give the response the kind of definition that, say, an attack would.<br /> <br /> I think there's also something to be said for actions for the sake of actions; where you play out the action as a thing you want the character to be doing in this scene, and where the dice resolve how well you pull it off, but it doesn't actually have a result so much as it's a contribution to the scene. In such instance, I can see a prayer action as something a Solar character does because of its surrounding cultural or circumstantial relevance, including with the invoked god as a spectator, but without direct result. In cases like this, there are Charms that can help, but they're not the point.<br /> <br /> I'm think I'm starting to ramble now, but I feel like I've made some ground in articulating why the idea of Solar prayer Charms has never quite sat well with me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T13:00:05-08:00","id":53394,"title":"","content":"Culturally, the word prayer to me is associated with : humble, supplication, private, sincere, simple and unadorned, personal, quiet. And a cultural tradition where there is the idea that simplest prayers by the weakest and least clever of tongue can be the most powerful. <br /> <br /> So that makes prayer Charms fueled by supernatural command of essence and skill feel a little dissonant (&quot;I offer up with silent, humble wishes and respect to the god... really hard... like, I really mean it&quot;).<br /> <br /> When I mentally rephrase to Solars being totally ill masters of religious ceremonies and masters of honoring the gods, that seems appropriate as Solars, the masters of skill.<br /> <br /> But even then, like having more ways to able to blow stuff up, not even close to in the top I'd think of when I think of Solar Performance, unlike creativity and art.<br /> <br /> Solars generally feel to me more like they'd persuade and manage gods through sheer cussed, shiny force of personality (Presence), slick and cunning mastery of the rules (Bureaucracy) or arcane knowledge (Occult) than through flawless performance of ceremony. Not excluding anything - it just doesn't feel like it fits with the tough, straightforward and worldly vibe that Solars have to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T13:19:47-08:00","id":53408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Golden Demon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53308#post53308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah! One thing that Solar Performance could do that would be cool!<br /> <br /> Extreme quotability! If someone who's witnessed a persuasive speech that the Solar made is reprising the Solar's exact arguments later, maybe they get a tool bonus or something? IDK.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glorious Solar Sound Bite? That's... actually not bad. Huh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T13:27:47-08:00","id":53413,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m wary of prayer charms.<br /> <br /> A PC with a hotline to the gods that they can realistically expect them to answer in a helpful manner is rocking a plot device level power.<br /> Being able to ask a god of a place about its history or recent events is a formidable investigation tool even before you get to more extreme examples like making offerings to Nara-O and gods with a similar purview in order to potentially solve a murder mystery faster than Sherlock Holmes.<br /> <br /> I have no doubt that they can be done right, but the concept has horrifying potential for abuse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T13:27:47-08:00","id":53414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53394#post53394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Culturally, the word prayer to me is associated with : humble, supplication, private, sincere, simple and unadorned, personal, quiet. And a cultural tradition where there is the idea that simplest prayers by the weakest and least clever of tongue can be the most powerful.<br /> <br /> So that makes prayer Charms fueled by supernatural command of essence and skill feel a little dissonant (&quot;I offer up with silent, humble wishes and respect to the god... really hard... like, I really mean it&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>And to me I imagine a Gospel Choir. Sometimes it's more about how much passion you put into your plea. Not cleverness but sincerity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T13:39:44-08:00","id":53421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53413#post53413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m wary of prayer charms.<br /> <br /> A PC with a hotline to the gods that they can realistically expect them to answer in a helpful manner is rocking a plot device level power.<br /> Being able to ask a god of a place about its history or recent events is a formidable investigation tool even before you get to more extreme examples like making offerings to Nara-O and gods with a similar purview in order to potentially solve a murder mystery faster than Sherlock Holmes.<br /> <br /> I have no doubt that they can be done right, but the concept has horrifying potential for abuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Helpful manner? Maybe if you make the right offering. I'd want to see Prayer get you an audience, not get you instant results. It's up to the ST to not just hand over the plot. The gods don't have to be straightforward in their answers and deeds. If you over-do it, you could easily incur their wrath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T13:44:25-08:00","id":53425,"title":"","content":"On my previous request, I have another... ok, making people pay attention to your performance is one thing... but what happens when they pay SO MUCH ATTENTION that you cease to be in their memories? They remember a voice so sublime it could make the night sky rain down tears as stars... a dance so wondrous, the wind asks how it could be as graceful... basically, being able to cloak yourself in a performance that is so unforgettable that it wipes out all other memories of the scene, effectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T13:57:26-08:00","id":53430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53413#post53413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m wary of prayer charms.<br /> <br /> A PC with a hotline to the gods that they can realistically expect them to answer in a helpful manner is rocking a plot device level power.<br /> Being able to ask a god of a place about its history or recent events is a formidable investigation tool even before you get to more extreme examples like making offerings to Nara-O and gods with a similar purview in order to potentially solve a murder mystery faster than Sherlock Holmes.<br /> <br /> I have no doubt that they can be done right, but the concept has horrifying potential for abuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree.<br /> <br /> I do feel that the value of Performance (and other skills) in making oneself a more valuable resource to divinity and therefore significantly affecting your destiny via less direct means is very possible though.<br /> <br /> If you're an Exalted artist at the top of your game, you have some degree of influence and celebrity amongst divinity that acknowledge how talented you are. To some extent, those divinities will bend over backward to accommodate you... or capture/kidnap you, alternately.<br /> <br /> If you rock hard enough, you may even be able to make the most august divinities defer to you, but not precisely in the fashion that you have like... a cellular phone that you dial them up on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T14:04:04-08:00","id":53436,"title":"","content":"I don't see any mechanical space for prayer Charms, bluntly. You either specialize in bringing spirits to heel, or you use your social skills to get what you want. A prayer that forces a spirit to appear before a Solar isn't a prayer, it's a summons, and that's already delineated within the game as an Occult task.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T14:13:24-08:00","id":53447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53430#post53430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do feel that the value of Performance (and other skills) in making oneself a more valuable resource to divinity and therefore significantly affecting your destiny via less direct means is very possible though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I knew I was missing something; the idea of leading a prayer such that a congregation follows with you, providing a base for making or rejuvenating a cult.<br /> <br /> And now I'm thinking of new kinds of prayers that form the basis of shifts in the local cult dynamics and precedence, like putting Amon ahead of Ra (although that's still obviously one component of a bigger process).<br /> <br /> In the context of Exalted's ancient world myth and close to Shinto animism, I see prayer mostly in terms of pageantry and ritual.<br /> <br /> Propitiating gods is kind of like this:<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cdnSc12bx5c\" data-code=\"cdnSc12bx5c\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/cdnSc12bx5c/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T14:19:09-08:00","id":53452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53394#post53394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Culturally, the word prayer to me is associated with : humble, supplication, private, sincere, simple and unadorned, personal, quiet. And a cultural tradition where there is the idea that simplest prayers by the weakest and least clever of tongue can be the most powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the first thing I think of are aztec ritual sacrifices, egyptian monuments and the pay-for-approval-of-the-gods the Romans and later Christians had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2UIUH9oaJnHMWIxcVdGMjNUYlE\" target=\"_blank\">3EX Martial Arts basic overview (Weapons, Armor, Attributes &amp; Abilities)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/366-edward-eldritch","name":"Edward Eldritch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T14:26:56-08:00","id":53456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53436#post53436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see any mechanical space for prayer Charms, bluntly. You either specialize in bringing spirits to heel, or you use your social skills to get what you want. A prayer that forces a spirit to appear before a Solar isn't a prayer, it's a summons, and that's already delineated within the game as an Occult task.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is entirely on how you do it. Binding a spirit is very different from impressing them so much they can't help but pay attention to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T14:42:43-08:00","id":53468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53436#post53436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see any mechanical space for prayer Charms, bluntly. You either specialize in bringing spirits to heel, or you use your social skills to get what you want. A prayer that forces a spirit to appear before a Solar isn't a prayer, it's a summons, and that's already delineated within the game as an Occult task.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would point out that based on the Ride and Sail charms that have been previewed thus far it doesn't seem like the development team considers it vital to restrict an individual ability to tree solely to direct applications of the skill in question. (For which I am thankful, makes Ride and Sail so much more interesting if its about more than just being good riding horses and sailing boats.)<br /> <br /> Personally though, I don't really see prayer charms as prime Solar conceptual space. Not that a Solar priest-king shouldn't be able to sway the hearts of the gods and demons with the awesome majesty of their voice, because they should totally be able to do that. Just that it strikes me that a Solar would just accomplish that sort of thing by being awesomely inspiring rather than having a specific &quot;make spirits do X&quot; performance charm.<br /> <br /> That being said, being able to sing a song so beautiful that it calls designated creatures to you and makes them more likely to want to help you sounds like the sort of thing a Solar could do. (I.e. the Disney Princess and the helpful woodland creatures effect.) I could totally see a Solar singing by a lake to attract local water elementals and gods to his voice. Not uniquely Solar sure, but it sounds like the kind of thing a Solar could do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>-<br /> Formerly Inquisitive Englishman","edited":{"userid":930,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/930-inqy","user":"Inqy","date":". 01-19-2014, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/930-inqy","name":"Inqy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T14:46:38-08:00","id":53476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inqy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53468#post53468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Ride and Sail charms that have been previewed thus far</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall the Ride spoiler. Where was it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T14:57:11-08:00","id":53485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53287#post53287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gods don't give a fuck. Most prayers go unanswered.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gods of Pegana</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Natheless between Pegana and the Earth flutter ten thousand thousand prayers that beat their wings against the face of Death, and never for one of them hath the hand of the Striker been stayed, nor yet have tarried the feet of the Relentless One.<br /> <br /> Utter thy prayer! It may accomplish where failed ten thousand thousand.</div> </div> </div> </div>And thus, all is as it should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T15:01:10-08:00","id":53489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drakhan Valane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53476#post53476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recall the Ride spoiler. Where was it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Must be around here somewhere...<br /> <br /> *digs around*<br /> <br /> Nope. Can't find nothing.<br /> <br /> Guess I was confusing the 3E previews with the Ink Monkeys stuff. Sorry guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>-<br /> Formerly Inquisitive Englishman","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/930-inqy","name":"Inqy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T15:04:18-08:00","id":53490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inqy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53468#post53468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being said, being able to sing a song so beautiful that it calls designated creatures to you and makes them more likely to want to help you sounds like the sort of thing a Solar could do. (I.e. the Disney Princess and the helpful woodland creatures effect.) I could totally see a Solar singing by a lake to attract local water elementals and gods to his voice. Not uniquely Solar sure, but it sounds like the kind of thing a Solar could do.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't a prayer. It's an appropriate use of Performance to persuade a spirit. This is exactly as it should be. But it of course still requires you to actually do the hard work of also tracking down the spirit in question. Which is, you know, something else Zeniths are supposed to be good at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T15:13:01-08:00","id":53493,"title":"","content":"It seems intuitive to me that a spirit is going to be much more accommodating of Lady Gaga (particularly if it is a fan) that Joe Farmer.<br /> <br /> I'd even be comfortable doing some parallels with our modern 'culture of celebrity' here - impressive human beings are SUPER precious and very prestigious.<br /> <br /> Therefore, charms which make you impressive, thought provoking and entertaining on a supernatural level are immensely useful, even if you can't quite text god with 'OMG bein tacked senz zephyr plz kk'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T15:14:10-08:00","id":53496,"title":"","content":"I'm really thrown by the attitude that the point of music as an artform is to make people do things they don't want to. I have no objection to that being part of what it can accomplish, but in 2E that was it's only purpose. That's kinda odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/544-deadpoint","name":"Deadpoint","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T15:22:27-08:00","id":53506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deadpoint</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53496#post53496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really thrown by the attitude that the point of music as an artform is to make people do things they don't want to. I have no objection to that being part of what it can accomplish, but in 2E that was it's only purpose. That's kinda odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the contrary, I'd say it's about drawing attention and instilling emotions, intimacies. It's more about indirect manipulation, not about ordering people around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T15:38:35-08:00","id":53514,"title":"","content":"Prayer in Exalted fuels spirits with essence and other stuff. I would like a prayer that enhanced that effect through ceremony, sacrifice or some other kind of religious ritual. Maybe let this be done of an exalt as. A cult charm if you will. Why well<br /> 1. Gives you leverage to bargain with spirit or exalt<br /> 2. Lets you aid an allied spirit that is low on juice<br /> 3. Gives an source of essence you can use for crafting or CRM-like action or other long term stuff.<br /> 4. Done in a flash it refills your essence mote pool<br /> <br /> EDIT: this need not be the same charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T16:09:04-08:00","id":53528,"title":"","content":"To those talking about Performance doing different things, I'd like to point out that, as of 2e, there were Charms in Athletics that: <br /> -Enhanced movement,<br /> -Improved balance,<br /> -Improved speed,<br /> -Boosted your strength,<br /> -Boosted your jumps,<br /> -And more!<br /> <br /> They certainly didn't <i>all</i> have the same result, and a character who went up one branch would certainly feel different than a character who took another, even if they both had Athletics 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T16:29:17-08:00","id":53534,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53490#post53490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't a prayer. It's an appropriate use of Performance to persuade a spirit. This is exactly as it should be. But it of course still requires you to actually do the hard work of also tracking down the spirit in question. Which is, you know, something else Zeniths are supposed to be good at.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure I expressed it particularly well, but my intention was that the charm would also incorporate the summoning into it. So for example you go into a wood, activate the charm and say. &quot;I sing a song that calls the birds and beasts to my aid.&quot; or go to a lake and say &quot;I sing a song that calls the spirits of the water to my aid.&quot; and all creatures of the desired type within a certain radius will hear your song echoing on the wind like part of a Disney musical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>-<br /> Formerly Inquisitive Englishman","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/930-inqy","name":"Inqy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T16:43:47-08:00","id":53540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drakhan Valane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53506#post53506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> On the contrary, I'd say it's about drawing attention and instilling emotions, intimacies. It's more about indirect manipulation, not about ordering people around.</div> </div> </div> </div> Which is still really odd. Indirect mannipulation is still manipulation. It is still exclusively adversarial. Which really doesn't map very well to what the performing arts actually are. I think it is part of the 2Eism that is social combat, where there is zero mechanical weight to talking to someone without trying in some way to direct their actions. It's not going to make me hate 3E if Performance remains exclusively about control, but it would be a nice bonus if it doesn't. I want an inspiring song of victory in battle played by the greatest bard of all time to have some effect on the army marching to war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/544-deadpoint","name":"Deadpoint","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T16:49:28-08:00","id":53546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inqy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53534#post53534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure I expressed it particularly well, but my intention was that the charm would also incorporate the summoning into it. So for example you go into a wood, activate the charm and say. &quot;I sing a song that calls the birds and beasts to my aid.&quot; or go to a lake and say &quot;I sing a song that calls the spirits of the water to my aid.&quot; and all creatures of the desired type within a certain radius will hear your song echoing on the wind like part of a Disney musical.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would the singing summon things that are out of hearing range?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T16:50:40-08:00","id":53547,"title":"","content":"So you're saying that music is not about stirring emotions, that acting is not about telling stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T17:19:01-08:00","id":53571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drakhan Valane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53547#post53547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you're saying that music is not about stirring emotions, that acting is not about telling stories.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not at all. I'm saying that &quot;get someone to do something they don't want to&quot; is not the only purpose of art. It is a valid use, but not the only possible one. You seem to be maintaining that manipulating people into doing actions is the only possible use of art. Am I understanding your position correctly? As a counterexample, I often listen to music to pump me up for an action that I already intend to do. There is totally thematic space to play music in situations where the audience is already doing what you want it to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/544-deadpoint","name":"Deadpoint","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T17:35:30-08:00","id":53585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deadpoint</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53571#post53571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not at all. I'm saying that &quot;get someone to do something they don't want to&quot; is not the only purpose of art. It is a valid use, but not the only possible one. You seem to be maintaining that manipulating people into doing actions is the only possible use of art. Am I understanding your position correctly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. I made a long list a few pages back with a bunch of things I want Performance to do. What I'm railing against here is the idea that Performance can't make people think about things that make them uncomfortable. The Crucible is a play about the Salem witch trials, but it's a social commentary on the Red Scare and McCarthyism. A Solar should be able to amp that up to the level where even the hard-hearted stop and consider the message. But I also ask that Solars be able to inspire troops and be able to lead and train troupes of musicians/actors/etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T17:57:19-08:00","id":53600,"title":"","content":"Something I've done in my games is suggest that performance it rather more termed expression. I really wanted to differentiate it from presence. I allowed purely expressive art in all forms to be enhanced by it. Primarily to make it interesting to my players. If painting and sculpture, and also literature can be bordered by this skill i think it's a good thing. A charismatic presence skill isn't impinged upon but does enhance performing arts. Craft is still essential for artifice but it would also aid in a painter or sculptor. Linguistics is still the skill for didactic literature, comprehension of cultures and ciphers but it would enhance poetry and saga writing. Finally larceny would still be the rascals home land but could be enhanced with character acting, selling a con; convincing lies etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/669-hermes12","name":"Hermes12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T17:59:47-08:00","id":53601,"title":"","content":"There's a Sail Charm that makes you Solar Sea-Captain. I want a Performance Charm to make you Solar Carnival Barker/Opera Singer.<br /> <br /> STEP RIGHT UP STEP RIGHT UP SEEK FAME AND FORTUNE ON THE HIGH SEAS!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/936-erichzahn","name":"ErichZahn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T18:31:33-08:00","id":53614,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ncj-wpBhr5E\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Performance saves the day again.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":90,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","user":"Gonzo","date":". 01-19-2014, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T20:05:57-08:00","id":53650,"title":"","content":"I love Performance, conceptually, but frankly most of the use my players have got from it has been from Excellencies. Many of the effects that they thought they could/should pull off with Performance seemed to turn up in Presence or Socialize, or in another Exalt's ability set altogether. So they either reskinned those Charms, stunted, or ran with the Excellency and called it good.<br /> <br /> Some charms that have been great: Respect-commanding Attitude, Phantom-Conjuring Performance, Demon-Wracking Glory, the Demon-wracking Shout. I say great because my players have loved and used these to good effect on occasion, though not as their core capability. Heart-Compelling Method, Memory Reweaving Discipline, and Husband Seducing Demon Dance have tended to not work out quite so well for them, though I am not sure if that was due to bad rolls, bad situations, or bad ideas.<br /> <br /> My group also loves to use prayers - they see rectifying the local divine situation as a way to help almost any plan, where rectify means get the gods working for them. So, prayer-oriented charms would be cool, but I would prefer them to be about the Solar rather than the god - because otherwise, the charms take the focus away from the character. I suggest some specific ways I think would be cool to handle it in a follow up post. However, here is the general idea framework.<br /> <br /> Generally, Exalted's prayer system has historically been a modification of the social system, for dealing with a fairly indifferent entity that is obliged to at least sort of pay attention if you yell at a particular volume...and nothing more. Prayer has never been about summoning or getting special bonuses beyond attention, and I sort of think it should stay that way - I prefer the focus to stay on PC power, rather than NPC power.<br /> <br /> Therefore, if you had a Charm that was a 'prayer' charm, it does things pretty much regardless of what the god in question thinks, either drawing on the nature of the Exalt, the congregation involved, or the Creation Ruling Mandate, for example. If the prayer roll also happens to hit the 6+ successes needed to get the god's attention, well, bonus, and maybe it comes to see what the Exalt is doing in its name, but otherwise, <u><b>gods don't really care</b></u>.<br /> <br /> The other type of prayer Charm might be god-focused, and be a prayer with hooks - the Exalt rolls a good prayer roll, and maybe there is a system where the god gets bonus bennies if it decides to care (develops an intimacy).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/798-joshua","name":"Joshua","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar798_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T20:17:47-08:00","id":53655,"title":"","content":"Considering that Performance is used with Prayer in 2e, and this will remain the same in 3e, some Performance charms involving Prayers would be neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T20:22:00-08:00","id":53658,"title":"","content":"In a previous post, I gave sort of a thought-ramble on Performance, and how it has been used in my games.<br /> <br /> Here is my Performance wish list: <br /> <br /> Low-end charms<ul><li>Flavor Examples<ul><li>Tell a story to inspire a fearful village to rise against tyranny, or to break to will of an invader</li> <li>Use music to calm an angry crowd, inspire a king to mercy, or gather followers</li> <li>Use dance to inspire lust to convince a magistrate to execute a dissident, express grief to allow a community to heal after mourning their dead</li> <li>Give a speech that moves a nation to war, or that forms an idea that lasts a thousand years</li> <li>Lead a prayer that unites the congregants in the principles espoused in the prayer, or otherwise helps those doing the praying, regardless of the result's impact on the god in question</li> </ul></li> <li>Mechanically*, they might be something like:<ul><li>Allow Performances to shape emotions</li> <li>Use Performances to convey meanings in unusual ways</li> <li>Make people remember or share a message for a long time</li> <li>Improving the range of the Performance</li> <li>Allow Performances to make arguments or debate points, without the use of words</li> </ul></li> </ul>Higher end powers<ul><li>Flavor Examples<ul><li>Songs that calm storms, shatter stones, and call forth light and hope in the darkest places</li> <li>Stories that empower their hearers with the virtues or vices of the characters therein (like the Ancestor sashes from An-Teng), or change their understanding of events - rewriting history</li> <li>Dances that enslave their viewers minds or set them free of their addictions</li> <li>Music that heals the sick or inspires such passion that it kills</li> <li>Prayers that call upon the Creation Ruling Mandate to channel some portion of the god's domain or nature into the congregation - or the world, again, regardless of the god's will.</li> <li>Prayers that are so supremely skilled that they provide an extra hook for the god to respond, perhaps by creating/reinforcing an intimacy of the supplicant's choice.</li> <li><i>&quot;Glories stream from heaven afar, Heavenly hosts sing Alleluia&quot;</i></li> </ul></li> <li>Mechanically*, they might be something like:<ul><li>Allow Performances to become weapons or tools of healing</li> <li>Turn Performances into acts of creation</li> <li>Performances as vehicles for temporary training or similar effects</li> <li>Use Performances to control the world around the performer</li> <li>Use Performances to create or break long-term intimacies</li> </ul></li> </ul>In between these I see things like &quot;the-song-you-can't-get-out-of-your-head and it drives you crazy&quot;, the talking-point everyone remembers - and shares, viral memes, phantasmal performance aids. I would love a charm that allows for tool-dependent performers to spin one from their soul, but in a way that felt more flavorful that the weapon Charms have in previous editions.<br /> <br /> *Obviously, the mechanical breakdowns are speculative, based on previous editions and spoilers, and don't cover the full range of effects in the flavor examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/798-joshua","name":"Joshua","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar798_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T20:27:24-08:00","id":53660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ladikn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53343#post53343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Gods damnit, I made an account after lurking all this time just to respond to this)<br /> <br /> See, my problem with the whole &quot;Gods don't give a fuck&quot; argument, in Exalted at least, is that even the most selfish and corrupt little god has reasons to want praise. While it's true not every God is like our favorite field God; acting out of kindness and general compassion for the people who worship them, but there is still one force that can keep the small gods motivated. (As a note, this is all on the assumption you didn't throw this concept onto the burning trash heap as well. If you did, please disregard this post.)<br /> <br /> Ambrosia. And quintessence, but mostly ambrosia.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not an argument. The more powerful the god, the more someone would want to pray to it, and the more likely that it's going to ignore that prayer, because there are hundreds or thousands more that it is going to receive. A god whose cult is very strong will never spend a day answering prayers. He will mete out boons randomly, curse his enemies, seduce and inveigh and amass heaps and heaps of prayer and sacrifice with no attention at all paid to his supplicants. The temple bureaucracy is founded on and profits from this fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T20:29:39-08:00","id":53664,"title":"","content":"Apologies for the Wall of Posts (TM) - I started to write my response to this earlier today, and kept tinkering in a text editor while dealing with an angry toddler, and when I copied it over, I realized it was too long for a single post, and so split it - and I still feel they are too long, but at least you can feel better for ignoring multiple posts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I notice from some comments up thread some interesting interpretations of what 'prayer' is, or is not. Protestant Europeans have a fairly narrow view of what is real prayer - part of the whole protest issue that led to the movement. It would be worthwhile to point out that prayers in the real world have encompassed everything from quickly murmured invocations and silent pleas to the carefully articulated exortations written in advance for public addresses that many of us have heard, but also can include the above mentioned week-long Mesoamerican rites involving many captives, lots of priests, pyramids, knives, etc, or spinning Tibetan prayer wheels carved with mantras, or hundreds of carefully choreographed dancers, or a choir of chanting monks, or any number of other methods - all of which would fall under Performance. An exception might be the games dedicated to gods in various Mediterranean and Mesoamerican cultures - I would probably rule those were opened with a normal prayer, but the subsequent Athletics rolls would add to the extended test, just to let the Dawns and Nights feel useful <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Suffice it to say, humans are very creative in their devotional activities, and by the standards of Western Europeans, many of them are quite naughty. I kept those particular prayer activities out of this post - as I said, writing with a toddler, and some things, I am just not ready to explain for a few more years.<br /> <br /> Exalted should have a prayer system that can handle all of what we humans came up with in reality, and more. After all - we probably do not have chthonic entities cruising around using us as prayer batteries <i>solely</i> for their own amusement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/798-joshua","name":"Joshua","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar798_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T20:30:57-08:00","id":53665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53660#post53660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not an argument. The more powerful the god, the more someone would want to pray to it, and the more likely that it's going to ignore that prayer, because there are hundreds or thousands more that it is going to receive. A god whose cult is very strong will never spend a day answering prayers. He will mete out boons randomly, curse his enemies, seduce and inveigh and amass heaps and heaps of prayer and sacrifice with no attention at all paid to his supplicants. The temple bureaucracy is founded on and profits from this fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Solars. . . . well, you know the story of Perfect Soul's exaltation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T20:33:31-08:00","id":53666,"title":"","content":"The salt rate in the Realm is the lowest in Creation, and it isn't because the Dragon-Blooded use sweet-ass Performance Charms to pray down the price of sacrifices. It's because they track down a recalcitrant salt spirit and beat that ass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T20:33:36-08:00","id":53667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53660#post53660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not an argument. The more powerful the god, the more someone would want to pray to it, and the more likely that it's going to ignore that prayer, because there are hundreds or thousands more that it is going to receive. A god whose cult is very strong will never spend a day answering prayers. He will mete out boons randomly, curse his enemies, seduce and inveigh and amass heaps and heaps of prayer and sacrifice with no attention at all paid to his supplicants. The temple bureaucracy is founded on and profits from this fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>One would think that this would be the reason why the entry charm on the Solar Prayer tree would be something that makes a god sit up and say &quot;Oh shit! There's a <i>Solar</i> praying to me!&quot; It provides incentive for him to show up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T20:41:27-08:00","id":53673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53660#post53660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not an argument. The more powerful the god, the more someone would want to pray to it, and the more likely that it's going to ignore that prayer, because there are hundreds or thousands more that it is going to receive. A god whose cult is very strong will never spend a day answering prayers. He will mete out boons randomly, curse his enemies, seduce and inveigh and amass heaps and heaps of prayer and sacrifice with no attention at all paid to his supplicants. The temple bureaucracy is founded on and profits from this fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>And human nature is such that this sort of variable response will actually increase prayer. It is why gambling is so addictive - because <i><b>THIS TIME</b></i> you will win (or get your prayer answered). <br /> <br /> In order for 'Prayer Charms' to work in the Exalted paradigm, they actually need to focus either on the congregation, and what prayer does for them - bringing them together, inspiring them, etc. or they need to draw on the divine power the gods have already given to the Exalted, either directly via Exaltation or later via things like the Creation Ruling Mandate. I think there is some space there that could be explored to generate interesting effects for prayers that would not require the gods to care.<br /> <br /> And they could also support the narrative that certain capabilities the Solars developed eventually surprised the gods, and made some of them nervous, and those capabilities don't all need to be things like Ghost Eating Technique, Big Scary Sorcery, or going insane - being able to hack the prayer system would be fairly destabilizing. If that narrative is still around, and needs feeding, that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/798-joshua","name":"Joshua","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar798_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T20:49:16-08:00","id":53676,"title":"","content":"Perhaps something to enhance group prayer? As a priest of the Unconquered Sun leading his congregation to multiply its effect? Perhaps to a point where it might sway even the mightiest gods' attentions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T20:50:49-08:00","id":53678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53666#post53666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The salt rate in the Realm is the lowest in Creation, and it isn't because the Dragon-Blooded use sweet-ass Performance Charms to pray down the price of sacrifices. It's because they track down a recalcitrant salt spirit and beat that ass.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that is true in setting, I honestly have always struggled with the whole setting of the salt rate thing, ever since it was introduced in 1e. Based on what I understand about salt production, it seems like this would work for the Blessed Isle, and maybe the Satrapies in the North, but beyond that, it would break down pretty quickly - all the independent nations would want to find alternate deals, and even the various Satrapies where salt production is possible would be uncontrollable sources. Unless the premise is that Realm Dragon-Blooded are the ONLY beings capable of negotiating deals with the salt gods.<br /> <br /> And I am curious what was used prior to the Scarlet Empire for setting interest rates, if this was a new relationship...?<br /> Not to derail this thread, really - more the sort of thing that, if it gets space to be addressed, would be nice to know somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/798-joshua","name":"Joshua","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar798_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T20:50:51-08:00","id":53679,"title":"","content":"It's not in the nature of Solar Essence to supplicate. Who, in all the universe, does the Unconquered Sun pray to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T20:54:51-08:00","id":53685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53679#post53679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not in the nature of Solar Essence to supplicate. Who, in all the universe, does the Unconquered Sun pray to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice.<br /> <br /> I wonder... could UMI be used through prayer as a social attack? Not so much as supplication, but as a long-range verbal ass-kicking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T20:55:56-08:00","id":53687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53679#post53679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who, in all the universe, does the Unconquered Sun pray to?</div> </div> </div> </div>That implies something very, very dangerous best left for the ST to decide.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://owncloud.scaenicus.net/index.php/s/saLcZXhVcOu0j3W/download?path=%2F&amp;files=ScaenicusBacked_big.png&amp;downloadStartSecret=mflqpfu2cd8\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/ScaenicusBacked.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1491-scaenicus","name":"Scaenicus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1491_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T20:56:22-08:00","id":53689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53679#post53679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not in the nature of Solar Essence to supplicate. Who, in all the universe, does the Unconquered Sun pray to?</div> </div> </div> </div>I find that this is something I've been feeling a bit during these discussions. Prayer . . . is a mortal thing. In the case of Sidereals, it's their dealings with the Bureaucracy that get them dealing with Prayer Strips, but for Solars . . . they get cults. They get prayed TO. But I can still see a Solar LEADING a prayer of multitudes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T20:57:55-08:00","id":53692,"title":"","content":"What about the &quot;get over here now or I'll beat the divinity out of you&quot; kind of prayers? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T20:59:30-08:00","id":53693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scaenicus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53687#post53687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That implies something very, very dangerous best left for the ST to decide.</div> </div> </div> </div>The canon response should be &quot;No one. He's the top dog.&quot; That's the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T21:00:14-08:00","id":53694,"title":"","content":"In modern terms, little Timmy has to write a letter asking Santa why he didn't get what he wanted for Christmas.<br /> <br /> A Solar could certainly write an amazing letter on Timmy's behalf, using Linguistics Charms.<br /> <br /> Or he could fly up to the North Pole and drag Santa's fat ass out of bed to make him answer his fucking e-mail like a 21st century adult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T21:00:41-08:00","id":53695,"title":"","content":"What I'm getting from the prayer conversation is that Creation's gods are essentially the creators of Farmville. (shudder). As for what I want from solar Performance: <br /> <br /> I want to be able to go down to the palace of Hades and sing a song so heartbreaking that his queen forces him to let me take back my lady love.<br /> I want to stand upon the walls of a city, preaching to the assembled ranks of the invader's army. I want the members of that army to cast off their shields, beat their swords into ploughshares, and follow me in peace.<br /> I want to play a tune so lively that the winds and stones and streams dance to it, according to my direction.<br /> I want to preach from my pulpit a legacy which will be written down and discussed and live in the culture and the hearts of the people for more than two thousand years. <br /> I want to be able to slay my enemies through the power of ROCK.<br /> I want to be able to enter a restaurant seeking an old ally, strike up a song, and instantly be surrounded not only by invisible instruments which perform in perfect tune and time, but by bystanders who have stepped up and become backup singers and dancers, with impeccable choreography. If they then sit down at the end of the song as though nothing had even happened, that would be a bonus. <br /> I want to be able to perform an allegorical play which pierces directly to the heart of a guilty king, causing him to incriminate himself *without* leading to my death and the deaths of everyone close to me.<br /> If performance is for composing as well as performing, I want to be able to write a body of work so influential that it shapes cultures for generations.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T21:04:11-08:00","id":53698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drakhan Valane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53693#post53693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The canon response should be &quot;No one. He's the top dog.&quot; That's the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, I know.<br /> But the notion frightened me nevertheless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://owncloud.scaenicus.net/index.php/s/saLcZXhVcOu0j3W/download?path=%2F&amp;files=ScaenicusBacked_big.png&amp;downloadStartSecret=mflqpfu2cd8\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/ScaenicusBacked.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1491-scaenicus","name":"Scaenicus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1491_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T21:08:41-08:00","id":53699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53694#post53694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In modern terms, little Timmy has to write a letter asking Santa why he didn't get what he wanted for Christmas.<br /> <br /> A Solar could certainly write an amazing letter on Timmy's behalf, using Linguistics Charms.<br /> <br /> Or he could fly up to the North Pole and drag Santa's fat ass out of bed to make him answer his fucking e-mail like a 21st century adult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the Solar required to hold one hand out in front of his face in order to do so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T21:10:31-08:00","id":53701,"title":"","content":"Going down this rabbit hole I'm digging: At the top of the food, er, prayer chain, you have the gods. They're the end goal of prayer. Under the gods are the Exalted, and below them are the Mortals. It's a rough sketch, bear with me. For the Prayers from the Mortals to reach the gods, is there nothing the Exalts ever do to hasten or amplify it? After all, are the Zeniths not considered priests? If the Exalts themselves are outside the prayer chain, then there's no reason for prayer charms. If they are part of it, then shouldn't they get something to assist them? If not Solars, what type of Exalt handles it? Only Sidereals? Another type? I'm referring to praise being sent to the gods as prayers as well. If that's a mistake, please correct me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T21:18:24-08:00","id":53705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53679#post53679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not in the nature of Solar Essence to supplicate. Who, in all the universe, does the Unconquered Sun pray to?</div> </div> </div> </div>I see this point, and do not contest it.<br /> Yet I would also suggest that the view that prayer is solely about supplication to a deity is needlessly narrow for a few reasons, especially in a world like Creation.<br /> 1. Sincere prayer can be about supplication, but it can also be about communication, friendship, and insight.<br /> 2. Prayer can serve as an aid for focus, meditation, or expression, regardless of actual religious sentiment<br /> 3. Insincere prayer can be used as a tool to focus attention on the pray-<i>er</i>, giving that person a platform to present their ideas as the group's, and so forth<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think 90% of what I want Solar's to do with prayer <i><b>should</b></i> be doable with their regular Performance Charms. And that is my point - in the past, the system for prayer really was such that the only Charms that could be used were Excellencies. The remaining 10%, if that, are things that really emphasize that at some level, the Chosen of the Sun carry a bit of the Essence of the King of the Gods within them, and so when they &quot;pray&quot; it means something a little different. Maybe they are asking nicely, because they are being polite, but...<br /> Or the effect they want <i><b>HAPPENS</b></i>, because they asked, and the god is left to fill out the paperwork...<br /> Either of those would go beyond the scope of social Performance, but would expand down an interesting Prayer Performance path. <br /> Anyway, it is late here - I hope this was useful. I will check back later <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/798-joshua","name":"Joshua","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar798_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T22:01:27-08:00","id":53720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53679#post53679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not in the nature of Solar Essence to supplicate. Who, in all the universe, does the Unconquered Sun pray to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that kind of like saying that Solars never serve as samurai or otherwise under a ruler?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T22:04:09-08:00","id":53721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53139#post53139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of you are mentioning prayer Charms. What do you imagine prayer doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine a Solar Exalt praying to the thing that makes the Sun so fucking great.<br /> <br /> e:I also imagine them being incredibly bombastic and pious in their devotions, over-inflating the importance of even the smallest deity until they're a servant of some higher truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/936-erichzahn","user":"ErichZahn","date":". 01-20-2014, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/936-erichzahn","name":"ErichZahn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T22:09:40-08:00","id":53724,"title":"","content":"In general, I think it's possible for a Solar to take the majesty and position of the gods seriously even while being aware that the actual gods kind of fall short of their notional glory, and that doing so gives them the stature that something called a &quot;god&quot; really ought to have, even a corrupt one.<br /> <br /> For Solars dealing with gods, here's an artifact I made up several years ago. It reads a bit clunky now but it still feels like a good example of how a Solar might interact with gods:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Five Directions Treasure Wheel: Artifact 5</b><br /> <br /> (historical pablum snipped)<br /> <br /> The wheel, a symbol of the righteous Lawgiver's authority, grants a virtuous ruler the power to call the gods to account. When attuned for a cost of eight motes, the wheel sparks to life in a corona of Solar Essence and hovers before its owner, reflecting his face. If necessary, the wheel darts from side to side to shield its owner from attack, providing the protection of a tower shield without requiring the use of either hand. However, this is only a fringe benefit.<br /> <br /> When the master of the treasure wheel channels a Virtue on a prayer roll, the wheel's true power activates, granting him automatic success with a threshold of 10 successes. The owner need not know a god's name or attributes, but may invoke a god by his purview and be assured of evoking the correct divinity. (\u201cGod of this river, your charge grows unruly and blocks the passage of the Sun's Chosen! Hear my charge and answer!\u201d)<br /> <br /> The god called by this prayer will be pleased to receive an unexpected portion of Ambrosia, and then less pleased when the image of the treasure wheel appears before him, reflecting its owner's image in the central mirror. The owner likewise sees the god and the two may communicate and engage in social combat through the link as though they were present together. No other effects can pass through the link, but gods who may target petitioners with their Charms or other magic may do so normally. The link created by the treasure wheel lasts for the remainder of the scene or until the wheel's owner dismisses it. Should any effect attempt to sever it before that time, the wheel's owner adds an extra ten successes to the roll-off.<br /> <br /> The power of the wheel is even more binding upon those gods who have grown fat and corrupt. If the god in question has suppressed the Virtue channeled by the owner in his prayer roll during the current scene, she is overcome by a sense of the owner's righteous virtue, suffering a penalty to her MDV for the scene equal to her rating in the given Virtue. This is an unnatural Emotion effect costing three Willpower to resist. If the owner has himself suppressed any Virtues during the scene, this power fails to function, but the operation of the wheel is otherwise unchanged.<br /> <br /> The five-directions treasure wheel is explicitly able to establish communication with the Incarnae and the Primordials. The owner who chooses to force open a connection to the greatest of gods would be wise to have either a very good spiel or a perfect defense. The ruler who opens a window to the Yozis will be unwise even if he has both. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T22:16:25-08:00","id":53728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53413#post53413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m wary of prayer charms.<br /> <br /> A PC with a hotline to the gods that they can realistically expect them to answer in a helpful manner is rocking a plot device level power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I would suggest that people take a look at 1e and 2e Sidereals and think long and hard if a direct pipeline to a god is something they <i>actually want</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53679#post53679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who, in all the universe, does the Unconquered Sun pray to?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pcxthg885ZY\" target=\"_blank\">Who indeed...</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T01:08:21-08:00","id":53797,"title":"","content":"Actually. Considering that there's a Sail charm that just makes you a kickass sailor, able to face the fears of the deep, fight on ship, navigate and survive at sea in general I'd like something similar for the 'core' performance styles.<br /> <br /> A Dancer charm that makes you in control of your limbs and center of balance at all times and good at communicating through body language.<br /> <br /> A Singing charm that allows you to regulate emotion and volume of your voice etc.<br /> <br /> Essentially One Stop Shop charms that give you a basic package of things that allow you to be a specific type of performer. the Sail charm makes you essentially an experienced, girzzled sailor in one go. So a charm that makes you an experienced, professional dancer (be it at some village cultural dance tradition or as a dancer-concubine at a sprawling temple complex in some great city where your dance is used more to seduce the wealthy who then donate to the corrupt temple to ejoy your 'company' at a private 'dance' parlour, temple prostitute style but with more dancing) in one go, with whatever is deemed necessary to be that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","user":"Scutarii","date":". 01-20-2014, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T01:12:21-08:00","id":53798,"title":"","content":"If it's not in the book, I'll use one of my bought charm design slots for it, but as Orpheus is one of the most iconic &quot;Solar Heroes&quot; in real world anthropological study of myth - I'd like to see some of his musical abilities reflected in Solar Performance. Namely he could raise nature to his defense, or calm a raging storm, etc through the sheer beauty of his music. Like I said, it's pretty iconic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T01:30:58-08:00","id":53810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53798#post53798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's not in the book, I'll use one of my bought charm design slots for it, but as Orpheus is one of the most iconic &quot;Solar Heroes&quot; in real world anthropological study of myth - I'd like to see some of his musical abilities reflected in Solar Performance. Namely he could raise nature to his defense, or calm a raging storm, etc through the sheer beauty of his music. Like I said, it's pretty iconic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From Wikipedia<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amergin_Gl%C3%BAingel\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/da/Amergin_Gl%C3%BAingel_%28Se%C3%B3irse_Ua_F%C3%A1g%C3%A1in%2C_1904%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amergin_Gl%C3%BAingel\" target=\"_blank\"> Amergin Gl&uacute;ingel - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amergin_Gl%C3%BAingel\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amergin_Gl%C3%BAingel </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Amergin<sup><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/#cite_note-1\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[1]</span></a></sup> <i>Gl\u00faingel</i></b> (&quot;white knees&quot;) or <i><b>Gl\u00fanmar</b></i> (&quot;big knee&quot;) is a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/wiki/Bard\">bard</a> and judge for the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/wiki/Milesians_(Irish)\">Milesians</a> in the Irish <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/wiki/Mythological_Cycle\">Mythological Cycle</a>. He was appointed <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/wiki/Chief_Ollam_of_Ireland\">Chief Ollam of Ireland</a> by his two brothers the kings of Ireland. A number of poems attributed to Amergin are part of the Milesian mythology.<br /> One of the seven sons of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/wiki/M%C3%ADl_Esp%C3%A1ine\">M\u00edl Esp\u00e1ine</a>, he took part in the Milesian conquest of Ireland from the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/wiki/Tuatha_D%C3%A9_Danann\">Tuatha D\u00e9 Danann</a>, in revenge for their great-uncle \u00cdth, who had been treacherously killed by the three kings of the Tuatha D\u00e9 Danann, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/wiki/Mac_Cuill\">Mac Cuill</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/wiki/Mac_Cecht\">Mac Cecht</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/wiki/Mac_Gr%C3%A9ine\">Mac Gr\u00e9ine</a>. They landed at the estuary of Inber Sc\u00e9ne, named after Amergin's wife Sc\u00e9ne, who had died at sea. The three queens of the Tuatha D\u00e9 Danann, (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/wiki/Banba\">Banba</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/wiki/%C3%89riu\">\u00c9riu</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/wiki/F%C3%B3dla\">F\u00f3dla</a>), gave, in turn, permission for Amergin and his people to settle in Ireland. Each of the sisters required Amergin to name the island after each of them, which he did: \u00c9riu is the origin of the modern name <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/wiki/%C3%89ire\">\u00c9ire</a>, while Banba and F\u00f3dla are used as poetic names for Ireland, much as <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/wiki/Albion\">Albion</a> is for Great Britain.<br /> The Milesians had to win the island by engaging in battle with the three kings, their druids and warriors. Amergin acted as an impartial judge for the parties, setting the rules of engagement. The Milesians agreed to leave the island and retreat a short distance back into the ocean beyond the ninth wave, a magical boundary. Upon a signal, they moved toward the beach, but the druids of the <b>Tuatha D\u00e9 Danann raised a magical storm to keep them from reaching land</b>. However, <b>Amergin sang an invocation calling upon the spirit of Ireland that has come to be known as <i>The Song of Amergin</i>, and he was able to part the storm and bring the ship safely to land</b>. There were heavy losses on all sides, with more than one major battle, but the Milesians carried the day. The three kings of the Tuatha D\u00e9 Danann were each killed in single combat by three of the surviving sons of M\u00edl, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/wiki/Eber_Finn\">Eber Finn</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/wiki/%C3%89rim%C3%B3n\">\u00c9rim\u00f3n</a> and Amergin. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T01:37:52-08:00","id":53813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53694#post53694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In modern terms, little Timmy has to write a letter asking Santa why he didn't get what he wanted for Christmas.<br /> <br /> A Solar could certainly write an amazing letter on Timmy's behalf, using Linguistics Charms.<br /> <br /> Or he could fly up to the North Pole and drag Santa's fat ass out of bed to make him answer his fucking e-mail like a 21st century adult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then... why in the name of all that is logical are Zeniths the Priest-King caste?<br /> <br /> <br /> Since, apparently, they don't actually pray to anyone and in fact are apparently supposed to treat gods like minions?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, Zeniths have that caste feature - always counts as a Priest of the Unconquered Sun - and it just feels like this should MEAN something.<br /> <br /> Okay, maybe the Solar should be the one doing the miracles themselves. Kinda makes sense, I guess.<br /> <br /> Actually, no, that sounds pretty cool. So, suggestion: Solars can turn the faith of a congregation into [tangible effect] through sheer faith (of the masses) and divine mojo (of the Solar). Maybe Faith Healing, maybe casting out spirits - I know, purview of other Abilities, but... there should be a way to draw power from the faith of your followers. Maybe as a way to fuel Sorcery? Although ideally the Priest would have different powers from the Sorceror (Sorceror-Priests, of course, get to do both).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T01:45:57-08:00","id":53819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53679#post53679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not in the nature of Solar Essence to supplicate. Who, in all the universe, does the Unconquered Sun pray to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Last time I checked Human Excellence was the principal stick of Solar Exalted even before imitating the Sun. I can see plenty of Humans praying. Also, Zenith Caste, <b>Priest</b>-Kings. It's in the job description, one would think they should be good at praying.<br /> <br /> And, as I pointed out before, if you want a thematic tie with the Sun you can draw from the Exigence as prayer is meant to be a way to empower divinities in the first place. Yes, the Sun doesn't pray to empower his subjects but he is a god and the Solars are Human, they would empower gods as Humans do not as the Sun does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53694#post53694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In modern terms, little Timmy has to write a letter asking Santa why he didn't get what he wanted for Christmas.<br /> <br /> A Solar could certainly write an amazing letter on Timmy's behalf, using Linguistics Charms.<br /> <br /> Or he could fly up to the North Pole and drag Santa's fat ass out of bed to make him answer his fucking e-mail like a 21st century adult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or he could still write the letter first because maybe he isn't an asshole that automatically assumes that there is no reason for Timmy's letters being ignored.<br /> <br /> Or maybe Santa was his ally already and he puts some bucks on the envelope to help Santa make the gift extra special.<br /> <br /> Or he is sending a letter to Santa himself to apply to be one of his helpers because he agrees with this whole giving gifts to deserving children thing.<br /> <br /> And yes, I totally agree that the more letters Santa recieves the more difficult it should be for that particular letter to be noticed. That is called difficulty and is a good thing for making stories last time I checked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","user":"Ravraxas","date":". 01-20-2014, 04:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T01:48:20-08:00","id":53821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rand Brittain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53720#post53720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that kind of like saying that Solars never serve as samurai or otherwise under a ruler?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can do or be a thing without needing Charms to do it.<br /> <br /> It does mean that Solars won't have Charms that specifically benefit their liege, or enhance them for serving under others, the way Sidereals and Terrestrials and any number of Exigents might, mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T01:49:14-08:00","id":53823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53679#post53679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not in the nature of Solar Essence to supplicate. Who, in all the universe, does the Unconquered Sun pray to?</div> </div> </div> </div>In previous editions:<br /> <br /> 1) Priests gonna pray.<br /> 2) Prayer is something you do by way of the Performance Ability.<br /> 3) Performance is a Caste Ability of Zeniths.<br /> 4) Zeniths are said to count not just as priests of the Unconquered Sun, but as priests of every god.<br /> <br /> This, to me, points to Zeniths being pretty bad-ass in their praying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T01:54:16-08:00","id":53827,"title":"","content":"Maybe it points to it, but it kind of flounders on the way to finding something for that to actually mean.<br /> <br /> Prayer can be a thing that a Solar does, even a meaningful one, that still doesn't really have any Charms to do with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T02:08:19-08:00","id":53832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53827#post53827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it points to it, but it kind of flounders on the way to finding something for that to actually mean.<br /> <br /> Prayer can be a thing that a Solar does, even a meaningful one, that still doesn't really have any Charms to do with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> <br /> Prayer is an action, it has requirements, procedures and effects. There is space for it to be enhanced by charms, equipment and preparation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T02:42:46-08:00","id":53852,"title":"","content":"Damn it, I had to make an account just to bump in as well.<br /> <br /> I think that the point is that the whole Solars don't pray and prayers don't work business is supposed to be a long, hard, decontructive and realistic look on what religion truly is- a scam designed to bully and manipulate people into giving mindless praise. From this persepctive, it's cool that John is taking this particular stance.<br /> <br /> At the same time, praying is supposed to be such a huge part of human condition (in Exalted) that stating outright that Solars are so obviously beyond it, sends the wrong kind of message. It's pretty strange to me that Solars, being all about things that humans do, but brought to inhuman level, can't bring something so basic like prayer, to that level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T03:12:05-08:00","id":53864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53813#post53813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then... why in the name of all that is logical are Zeniths the Priest-King caste?<br /> <br /> <br /> Since, apparently, they don't actually pray to anyone and in fact are apparently supposed to treat gods like minions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Prayer is a valid thing for Zeniths to do.<br /> A performance charm that goes &quot;I command you to answer my prayers!&quot; is somewhat missing the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T03:25:05-08:00","id":53869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rand Brittain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53720#post53720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that kind of like saying that Solars never serve as samurai or otherwise under a ruler?</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you seen what people say about Scarlet Whisper for being The Perfect's minion. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T04:02:08-08:00","id":53880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53864#post53864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prayer is a valid thing for Zeniths to do.<br /> A performance charm that goes &quot;I command you to answer my prayers!&quot; is somewhat missing the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Commands are not prayers, obviously such a thing wouldn't be compatible with Prayer Charms. &quot;I make you better at answering my prayers&quot;, &quot;I give you or reinforce intimacies when you answer my prayers&quot; and &quot;my prayers are very convincing&quot; are still valid if somewhat superficial effects. Things like &quot;If you can receive benefit from my prayers you can hear it even when you shouldn't be able to&quot; is another possibility as is &quot;I grant a bonus to the benefits form your cult when I direct the oration&quot; or &quot;I grant you part of my cult rating without having to go to the hassle of telling my cult to pray to you&quot;.<br /> <br /> So yea, I don't see any problems inherent to Prayer Chams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T04:14:30-08:00","id":53884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravraxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53832#post53832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>In specific to prayer, I've already said why the idea falls flat to me.<br /> <br /> In the general idea of why it should be valid to approach the system and setting in terms of things that don't have Charms to do with them, that's a whole big that I can ultimately boil down to &quot;it provides space for characters to do things when Charms aren't or shouldn't be available&quot;, which generally matters in cases where you're an Exalt type who shouldn't really have certain kinds of Charms, as well as for general things where Charms don't really seem suitable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravraxes</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prayer is an action, it has requirements, procedures and effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's another thing about recognising that prayer being a discrete action is just a system abstraction which doesn't really need to strictly intersect with other system abstractions, especially when the game's general approach to powers is a holistic exception-based method.<br /> <br /> So that's where you get into the matter of there being Performance Charms that might logically intersect with the context of prayer, either in terms of its social perception or being a method of communicating with a god, but not Charms that are specifically for prayer.<br /> <br /> A similar matter goes for Cult, which is an abstraction of what the effects of worship for the subject do, rather than a codification of the breakdown of individual prayers.<br /> <br /> Which plays into another thing that makes the idea of a special super prayer that gives even more Essence is the fact that, generally speaking, prayer is directed offscreen. Arbitrating exactly how many resources a character offscreen gets for a Charm that you paid experience for seems pretty silly when you think about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravraxes</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is space for it to be enhanced by charms, equipment and preparation.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, there was space for the development and evolution of your character in the actual mechanics and for the cultivation in the personality of a Yozi in the eyes of the fans for Infernals, and those still weren't good ideas.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T04:23:35-08:00","id":53888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravraxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53832#post53832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why?<br /> <br /> Prayer is an action, it has requirements, procedures and effects. There is space for it to be enhanced by charms, equipment and preparation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, anything could be enhanced by a Charm. Not everything is within the thematic space for a <i>Solar</i> Charm, even if it is an action which can be done by mortals. I would not say, for example, that a Charm that enhances begging for one's life to keep someone from killing you would be thematically appropriate for a Solar Charm, even though that is an action that people can do.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I think prayer is one of the more boring ways of interacting with the gods. I'd much rather encourage a Solar to go out and find spirits directly and talk to them than encourage sitting somewhere and praying to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T04:48:15-08:00","id":53891,"title":"","content":"What does being a Priest-King to the Gods mean and how does a Zenith embody this in a way that other castes do not? What makes the Zenith better at Priesting than a Dawn?<br /> <br /> Bearing in mind our example of Solar interaction with Gods is flying to the north pole and dragging them out of bed to and making them do something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T04:58:37-08:00","id":53895,"title":"","content":"What if a Solar Prayer Charm gave a god an ability they don't normally have? Like, you could pray to a god of volcanoes for snow, and he could give you that because you asked. Mortal beliefs and prayers (Cult rating) already have the power to add Charms to a god they don't normally have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T05:02:42-08:00","id":53899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53884#post53884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In specific to prayer, I've already said why the idea falls flat to me.<br /> <br /> In the general idea of why it should be valid to approach the system and setting in terms of things that don't have Charms to do with them, that's a whole big that I can ultimately boil down to &quot;it provides space for characters to do things when Charms aren't or shouldn't be available&quot;, which generally matters in cases where you're an Exalt type who shouldn't really have certain kinds of Charms, as well as for general things where Charms don't really seem suitable.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there is a roll to it there are going to be Charms enhancing it. Even if it's just the Excellency. Saying that it's an action that shouldn't have Charms enhancing it kind of falls flat when you can already explicitly do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53884#post53884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's another thing about recognizing that prayer being a discrete action is just a system abstraction which doesn't really need to strictly intersect with other system abstractions, especially when the game's general approach to powers is a holistic exception-based method.<br /> <br /> So that's where you get into the matter of there being Performance Charms that might logically intersect with the context of prayer, either in terms of its social perception or being a method of communicating with a god, but not Charms that are specifically for prayer.<br /> <br /> A similar matter goes for Cult, which is an abstraction of what the effects of worship for the subject do, rather than a codification of the breakdown of individual prayers.<br /> <br /> Which plays into another thing that makes the idea of a special super prayer that gives even more Essence is the fact that, generally speaking, prayer is directed offscreen. Arbitrating exactly how many resources a character offscreen gets for a Charm that you paid experience for seems pretty silly when you think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you read mis posts carefully you'll notice I never mention Prayer Charms giving Essence, I speak of enhancing actions that answer prayers and granting other benefits to gods that collaborate with the Solar. The charms I propose are mostly meant as an additional carrot for a god to become your ally and as a way for you to help those gods that are already your allies to help you.<br /> <br /> A god that is completely off screen wouldn't care for your prayers, a god that is off screen is probably powerful and worshiped enough that he either wouldn't notice or care about it. A powerful god who is on screen or has been on screen recently is another mater entirely. A weak god who is off screen has to be relevant to the situation or you wouldn't be praying to it, and such a prayer is the kind of invitation to the GM that will make him not be off screen for much longer. Gods are people you can meet, thinking that objects of worship are going to remain nebulous is a dangerous trap to fall on when you play this game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53884#post53884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, there was space for the development and evolution of your character in the actual mechanics and for the cultivation in the personality of a Yozi in the eyes of the fans for Infernals, and those still weren't good ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree on principle. But this is not the place to discuss this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53888#post53888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, anything could be enhanced by a Charm. Not everything is within the thematic space for a <i>Solar</i> Charm, even if it is an action which can be done by mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans pray. Human Excellence is THE thematic space of Solar charms. A whole Caste is meant to have prayer as a main activity. This doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53888#post53888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would not say, for example, that a Charm that enhances begging for one's life to keep someone from killing you would be thematically appropriate for a Solar Charm, even though that is an action that people can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presence and Socialize Charms. In fact the first spoiled Socialize Charm can be used to do this very effectively. Granted, it's not an specific effect. Begging for ones life isn't also as specific or iconic an action as prayer nor has such a thematic importance in the setting nor has a Caste that should be doing it regularly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53888#post53888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I think prayer is one of the more boring ways of interacting with the gods. I'd much rather encourage a Solar to go out and find spirits directly and talk to them than encourage sitting somewhere and praying to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I say in this very post this is an easy trap to fall on when it comes to Exalted. Gods are not nebulous things that are far, far away. Gods are people you can meet, people that can seek you to cash in you debts, that may be grateful if your prayer was convenient to them, that may be you allies previously due to other interactions. And prayer and religion are important, central, aspects of being a god, they help underline the idiosyncrasies of having an ally that is a god.<br /> <br /> I think of Prayer Charms as incentives for Priests to go out and ingratiate themselves with as many gods as they can, because the more friends they have among the divine more options will they have latter. And an incentive for gods to want Exalted Priest as allies, because for as long as their prayers coincide with their objectives, not only they have a powerful ally, but they are more potent themselves.<br /> <br /> Obviously an unrelated god shouldn't and wouldn't give a fuck about your prayers, although maybe they do and that's the beginning of future interactions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T05:06:35-08:00","id":53901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rand Brittain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53720#post53720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that kind of like saying that Solars never serve as samurai or otherwise under a ruler?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. What a Solar does is a matter of free will. What his Essence is intended to do was decided for him a very long time ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T05:10:12-08:00","id":53904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53891#post53891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does being a Priest-King to the Gods mean and how does a Zenith embody this in a way that other castes do not? What makes the Zenith better at Priesting than a Dawn?<br /> <br /> Bearing in mind our example of Solar interaction with Gods is flying to the north pole and dragging them out of bed to and making them do something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're reading too much into the example.<br /> The letter approach is basically distilling the whole resolution down to a dice roll while confronting Santa personally is something that moves the plot along.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T05:15:14-08:00","id":53910,"title":"","content":"I'd also say that there's a point for how Exalted in general and Solars in particular don't really want to go with a depiction of priests or gods in which you've got a Dungeons and Dragons situation of &quot;being a priest means that gods are the source of your superpowers&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not even just for the sake of disassociating with Dungeons and Dragons (although that does play a bit of a part), mostly just because it doesn't fit the tone.<br /> <br /> Zeniths might be priests, but they're primarily priests in a manner that resonates with what priests tend to be in real life, I think, the existence of actual gods notwithstanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T05:24:25-08:00","id":53913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53910#post53910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also say that there's a point for how Exalted in general and Solars in particular don't really want to go with a depiction of priests or gods in which you've got a Dungeons and Dragons situation of &quot;being a priest means that gods are the source of your superpowers&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not even just for the sake of disassociating with Dungeons and Dragons (although that does play a bit of a part), mostly just because it doesn't fit the tone.<br /> <br /> Zeniths might be priests, but they're primarily priests in a manner that resonates with what priests tend to be in real life, I think, the existence of actual gods notwithstanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you know what priest do in real life? They pray, a lot, the existence (or not) of actual gods notwithstanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T05:24:45-08:00","id":53914,"title":"","content":"You know, this is now making me think of Zeniths as divine mobsters... they send you a note with a packet full of a bribe and one bullet. There's a note and all it says is &quot;Pick one and be happy with it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T05:39:00-08:00","id":53922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravraxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53913#post53913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And you know what priest do in real life? They pray, a lot, the existence (or not) of actual gods notwithstanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to me that the preisty aspect the Zeniths are supposed to embody is not as much prayer aspect and &quot;being the physical link of the community to the divine&quot;, but more the &quot;sheparding the flock of mindless followers to be servile and weak&quot; aspect. It seems like the UCS (or any other god for that matter) isn't interested in answering prayers at all, but is very much interested in making people pray to him. That's the point of Zeniths- they aren't supposed to be good at making gods respond, on the contrary, they're supposed to be good at making people pray. Which they undoubtly are good at.<br /> <br /> Is that terribly pessimistic? Well, yeah, but that's Exalted for you innit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T06:06:33-08:00","id":53933,"title":"","content":"... I think this is where someone with a dissenting viewpoint steps in, and points out how <i>incredibly</i> arrogant your last post is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T06:33:12-08:00","id":53944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53823#post53823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In previous editions:<br /> <br /> 1) Priests gonna pray.<br /> 2) Prayer is something you do by way of the Performance Ability.<br /> 3) Performance is a Caste Ability of Zeniths.<br /> 4) Zeniths are said to count not just as priests of the Unconquered Sun, but as priests of every god.<br /> <br /> This, to me, points to Zeniths being pretty bad-ass in their praying.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Zenith who wants to be a gardener is also going to be really good at it, but there aren't any Charms specifically for that either. There's a big difference between having a Charm designed directly into the set for a certain, stated, specific task, and having one that supplements it indirectly. A specific Charm colors the character of the entire splat, where an indirect Charm allows for players to individualize their characters and set them apart from everyone else. Traditionally, you can use your Performance Charms to pray, but there aren't any specifically for prayer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T06:43:51-08:00","id":53949,"title":"","content":"If your interpretation of prayer is summoning a spirit (Sorcery), or unleashing random environmental miracles (Sorcery) or gaining powerful random bonuses (Sidereal Astrology), none of those things are going to happen\u2014not only because they make an absurdity of prayer and Zeniths by being too on-the-nose, but also because it goes against the entire setting to suppose that you can beg a god into action by being a really good beggar.<br /> <br /> Being a priest means a lot of very important things to culture, and society. Prayer is a ritual that unites and conforms communities under certain beliefs, and upholds the temple bureaucracy, benefiting the priesthood by giving it social and political power. It also earns the god a vast sum of worship and reduces its need or desire to actually answer prayer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":86,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","user":"John M\u00f8rke","date":". 01-20-2014, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T06:59:33-08:00","id":53958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53944#post53944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Zenith who wants to be a gardener is also going to be really good at it, but there aren't any Charms specifically for that either. There's a big difference between having a Charm designed directly into the set for a certain, stated, specific task, and having one that supplements it indirectly. A specific Charm colors the character of the entire splat, where an indirect Charm allows for players to individualize their characters and set them apart from everyone else. Traditionally, you can use your Performance Charms to pray, but there aren't any specifically for prayer.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a little bit disappointing to me, and sort of make me wonders what the theme of the Zenith caste is supposed to be in this new edition. In 2e, one of the central schicks of the Zenith was that, as an official priest of everything, all prayer rolls they made were at -1 difficulty. That's not a huge bonus or anything, but it's something apparently central enough to the concept to be included as an anima effect for their entire caste. It means that Zeniths are supposed to be doing specifically that - praying or, when they have a congregation, leading prayer - aside from their other assorted responsibilities, like corpse disposal and messing up Creatures of Darkness.<br /> <br /> 2e failed to add charms that tied in to that apparently-central-to-the-theme role. They made their Zeniths priests with an actual mechanical benefit when it came to prayer - whose whole roll is to get a god to pay attention and mete out some kind of boon - and then didn't really give anything to help that along other than an excellency. They could have given charms that give a god a bonus when they fulfill that prayer, or a penalty when they fail to, or otherwise help convince a god to help, reward it when it does, punish it when it doesn't, and facilitate its effects coming into existence. As the priests of the Solar Exalts, it seems like authoritative management of deities would totally be their thing, and I feel like 2e not including charms for that is a failing, not a success.<br /> <br /> So, I suppose my question is, what are the Zeniths' role in 3e if they weren't the priest-kings of previous editions? If they can't use prayer to get gods to pay attention and hand out goodies, can't pray to turn aside creatures of darkness, are you going to be completely restructuring the themes and anima effects of Zeniths to make them musicians and statesmen instead of priests? Because otherwise, it seems like there's going to be that empty design space again, despite Zeniths being primed for it already.<br /> <br /> Even if it's just a single short branch of prayer charms on the Performance tree, it seems like there's everything to gain for including it, and like there would definitely be a sense of something missing for a lack of it.<br /> <br /> Unless, of course, prayer is just included in the social influence system that's been hinted at. If prayer is playing on intimacies, if prayer is affected by all the other performance charms that convince someone of something, if performance already includes systems for attracting immediate attention, rewarding those who follow your requests and orders, and penalizing those who refuse. If, in 3e, prayer is just an avenue of otherwise-normal social influencing - like sending a letter or calling someone on the phone, social influence but at a range - then I could see prayer just using the charms that Performance already has to get gods to do what you want.<br /> <br /> But if that's not the case, then I really do wonder how Zeniths are supposed to fill their primary role as priests. They were better musicians than priests in 2e, and I find that, to put it lightly, odd. So, I'm hoping either prayer will be better facilitated in 3e or for the central theme of the Zenith to be changed to something else.<br /> <br /> That's all, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T07:06:37-08:00","id":53961,"title":"","content":"Priest-Kings aren't <i>priests</i>, they're priest-<i>kings</i>. The presence of an active god in their temple bureaucracy makes them obsolete, as the god would handle all the actual work.<br /> <br /> Besides, negotiating with gods as what the Eclipse Caste does. The Zenith Caste commands, and priests don't command their gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T07:14:27-08:00","id":53964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53949#post53949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your interpretation of prayer is summoning a spirit (Sorcery), or unleashing random environmental miracles (Sorcery) or gaining powerful random bonuses (Sidereal Astrology), none of those things are going to happen\u2014not only because they make an absurdity of prayer and Zeniths by being too on-the-nose, but also because it goes against the entire setting to suppose that you can beg a god into action by being a really good beggar.<br /> <br /> Being a priest means a lot of very important things to culture, and society. Prayer is a ritual that unites and conforms communities under certain beliefs, and upholds the temple bureaucracy, benefiting the priesthood by giving it social and political power. It also earns the god a vast sum of worship and reduces its need or desire to actually answer prayer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Question then - for the uninitiated in the ways of Exalted - what does 'being a priest' mean in terms of actions performed day to day, in times of war, in times of celebration? What are these important things that priests do? How are these distinct from the actions of, for example, a revolutionary leader riding on charisma and rhetoric skill?<br /> <br /> What makes the Zenith approach different to the approach of a charismatic Dawn?<br /> <br /> Or, reversed, why would a charismatic community leader exat as a Zenith rather than a charismatic member of any other caste?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T07:14:29-08:00","id":53965,"title":"","content":"Zeniths are prophets. They are Biblical-level holy men, evangelists and judges, like Samson, John the Baptist, Moses, and the Nazarene himself. Priest is a bureaucratic function and a social position. Prophets invoke the spirit and power of the divine, giving them an understood universality that is not diminished by the whims of a dominant cult or a state religion. They have the authority of heaven because they represent it. They can perform the functions of a priest\u2014see also: water-into-wine\u2014but such men are as far beyond priests as the eagle is above the salmon. See also: water-into-wine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":86,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","user":"John M\u00f8rke","date":". 01-20-2014, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T07:26:27-08:00","id":53971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53949#post53949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your interpretation of prayer is summoning a spirit (Sorcery), or unleashing random environmental miracles (Sorcery) or gaining powerful random bonuses (Sidereal Astrology), none of those things are going to happen\u2014not only because they make an absurdity of prayer and Zeniths by being too on-the-nose, but also because it goes against the entire setting to suppose that you can beg a god into action by being a really good beggar.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me think that I'm either failing fantastically at making myself understood or nobody is actually reading my posts. The worst part is that the former is actually the most likely as English is not my first language.<br /> <br /> What I want is twofold:<br /> <br /> First, prayer is a Social interaction with a character which is done with a Social ability, I want to be able to <b>meaningfully</b> engage in it. This should be covered by regular Performance Charms.<br /> <br /> Second, prayer is a thematic element of Exalted that serves a function in the setting. That of empowering the gods. I want to be able to engage this part of the setting, to have reason to be a priest with many friends among the divine and go on quests to befriend more. As it stands the diplomatic has more reason to do this than the priest.<br /> <br /> Pardon my French but, \u200bfuck summoning, fuck sorcerous imitation and fuck random bonuses. I want to Buff my god allies. Any bonus that I would personally get would be there without my intervention <b>because the god should be my ally already or because what I'm doing is to his best interest even if we haven't met <i>yet</i></b>. Yes, I'm talking about making this effects more powerful in part, but it's still not something that comes from nowhere, not something I can do whenever I want or without reason. Engaging in that kind of politics and having it have an impact for both parties is part of the appeal for me. Having Charms that help me feel like I personally add to the actual purpose of prayer so my god allies and I can &quot;rub each others back&quot; so to speak would be appreciated.<br /> <br /> And the begging issue. I will refrain of calling too much attention to the fact that anyone can be begged into action by a good enough beggar. But I would like to point out that not every prayer is framed as begging, not even in the real world. For example, Taoist Fu are more like bureaucratic formulae that invoke imperial authority to compel the god to act and most prayers that include sacrifices are framed more as bribes than begging.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53949#post53949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being a priest means a lot of very important things to culture, and society. Prayer is a ritual that unites and conforms communities under certain beliefs, and upholds the temple bureaucracy, benefiting the priesthood by giving it social and political power. It also earns the god a vast sum of worship and reduces its need or desire to actually answer prayer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, on all accounts. It still amounts to little when you personally know the god and are reasonably sure he is going to respond. Also, practically everything a Solar does can be said to mean a lot of important things to culture and society and it doesn't stop them from doing it and having Charms that enhance it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","user":"Ravraxas","date":". 01-20-2014, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T07:35:43-08:00","id":53975,"title":"","content":"Now that I think about, every Sidereal have the Priest merit as Zenith too, and they treat god the same way they treat everyone, no using mysterious prayer beads or burning a<span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">quilaria</span></span> incense to call down wrath of the god (well, there is Spirit-Binding Battle Pattern, but you do need to sacrifice a shit load of your own soldiers though).<br /> <br /> So I guess that I'm on anti-prayer charm team now.........","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T07:39:12-08:00","id":53977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53813#post53813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then... why in the name of all that is logical are Zeniths the Priest-King caste?<br /> <br /> Since, apparently, they don't actually pray to anyone and in fact are apparently supposed to treat gods like minions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which god are they priests of? When does the UCS answer prayers? Why would Zeniths pray to other gods? If you're still not convinced, just ask yourself &quot;What would Socrates ask next?&quot; and keep going.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53813#post53813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, Zeniths have that caste feature - always counts as a Priest of the Unconquered Sun - and it just feels like this should MEAN something.<br /> <br /> Okay, maybe the Solar should be the one doing the miracles themselves. Kinda makes sense, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does. It means they have the divine right to track down the god of whatever and kick the shit out of him OR dress him down for a) doing his job or b) not doing his job. Whichever the Zenith prefers. But the key here is that they're supposed to track the gods down. The other side of the swing set, sorcery, can be used to summon a god directly to you and bind them. This is only rarely done because it's a great way to fuck things up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53813#post53813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, no, that sounds pretty cool. So, suggestion: Solars can turn the faith of a congregation into [tangible effect] through sheer faith (of the masses) and divine mojo (of the Solar). Maybe Faith Healing, maybe casting out spirits - I know, purview of other Abilities, but... there should be a way to draw power from the faith of your followers. Maybe as a way to fuel Sorcery? Although ideally the Priest would have different powers from the Sorceror (Sorceror-Priests, of course, get to do both).</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything you've suggested was possible in 2e, provided you were willing to flavor it that way. Solar Medicine is perhaps the best at healing others (Dragon-Blooded Medicine is nearly as good, in one of those strokes of getting things right), which would certainly look like fucking magic to mortals because it is. Casting out spirits is within the primary skillset of all Celestial Exalts, although Sidereals are arguably the best at it because Terminal Sanction; that shouldn't stop you from making an Solar exorcist, though. You draw power from worshipers through Cult. Cults don't necessarily have to worship you, after all. The heavenly bureaucracy is set up to provide the benefits of worship in appropriate proportion to the effort expended in the bureaucracies. Your Zenith runs a major cult of the UCS and thus gets some benefit out of it. Not that there's anything wrong with a Solar setting themselves up as a being to worship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T07:43:37-08:00","id":53978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53975#post53975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that I think about, every Sidereal have the Priest merit as Zenith too, and they treat god the same way they treat everyone, no using mysterious prayer beads or burning a<span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">quilaria</span></span> incense to call down wrath of the god (well, there is Spirit-Binding Battle Pattern, but you do need to sacrifice a shit load of your own soldiers though).<br /> <br /> So I guess that I'm on anti-prayer charm team now.........</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually if we got Prayer Charms for Solars I would want Sidereal Prayer Charms too. But that's another matter entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T07:45:00-08:00","id":53979,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I can picture a situation where a Zenith who's particularly loyal to a god for whatever reason uses her charms to perform miracles and give credit to the god. This would still require that Zenith pray, but it would not require that the god actually answer the prayers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T07:47:16-08:00","id":53981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53964#post53964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Question then - for the uninitiated in the ways of Exalted - what does 'being a priest' mean in terms of actions performed day to day, in times of war, in times of celebration? What are these important things that priests do? How are these distinct from the actions of, for example, a revolutionary leader riding on charisma and rhetoric skill?<br /> <br /> What makes the Zenith approach different to the approach of a charismatic Dawn?<br /> <br /> Or, reversed, why would a charismatic community leader exat as a Zenith rather than a charismatic member of any other caste?</div> </div> </div> </div>The gods want priests who will organize continuous mass-worship and exorbitant and repeated sacrifice. Performance helps with this, because being able to dance, sing, play instruments or orate helps you to identify yourself with a higher power. Such behavior inspires awe, and creates a sense of worship. Effective priests not only lead prayer through worship and ritual, but are also part of the temple bureaucracy and are relatively wealthy, based on the size of the temple, size of the cult, dominance of the religion, etc. A god won't tolerate an ineffective priest. He wants someone that will inspire the people to worship and will manage funds and use resources to perform acts in his name, to keep the people worshiping and sacrificing to him. Having high Performance is a great bonus, but if the god is particularly powerful, entrenched or prominent, such as Ahlat, or if people are particularly afraid (such as in outlands regions where shaman-exorcists make a living), Performance is less necessary, and Bureaucracy and Occult are more effective talents for a priest. Siakal's priests may or may not have Performance, but every last one of them has War and Sail.<br /> <br /> At best, an effective priest organizes sacrifice and worship and uses this to bargain with the god more successfully. At worst, the priest is a lackey whose temporal power allows him to sign off on public works, military action, etc. in the name of the god, and who is supported by the god so long as he keeps the sacrifices coming.<br /> <br /> When Buddha Elvis rolls into town with his glorious Solar sanxian, every respectable god is either going to be terrified and looking to kill him, or wanting to make nice, because he's got every quality of an S-rank priest but can also steal all their worshipers, reform or destroy their cult, or even put the gods themselves to the question.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":86,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","user":"John M\u00f8rke","date":". 01-20-2014, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T07:49:25-08:00","id":53983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53965#post53965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zeniths are prophets. They are Biblical-level holy men, evangelists and judges, like Samson, John the Baptist, Moses, and the Nazarene himself. Priest is a bureaucratic function and a social position. Prophets invoke the spirit and power of the divine, giving them an understood universality that is not diminished by the whims of a dominant cult or a state religion. They have the authority of heaven because they represent it. They can perform the functions of a priest\u2014see also: water-into-wine\u2014but such men are as far beyond priests as the eagle is above the salmon. See also: water-into-wine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so 3e is making Zenith's less priests and more self-central prophets and actual targets or worship? Maybe along with losing that automatic decrease in prayer difficulty, and therefore no longer having prayer and priestly activities be a relevant core them to Zeniths? I can live with that change, as long as it's addressed head-on instead of sidestepped or ignored. I would still be pretty interested in prayer just being another avenue of social influence, through which all the normal Performance charms can work, shooting a message up to a god they way you would deliver a letter to a king. It's all good, though, as long as you're removing priestliness and prayer from the core themes of the caste. Maybe removing Performance's function as the prayer ability entirely?<br /> <br /> I'm mostly coming to this point with how 2e presented the Zenith caste, with 2e's rules for prayer, and 2e's lack of support for actually enhancing prayers with charms. When a core component of the Zenith was that all prayers were at -1 difficulty and they were called the priests of the Solars, when the (pre-errata) Malefactor anima was all about consecrating an area for easier prayer to the Yozi via personal prayer, it seemed bizarre to have there be no charms that helped it along shy of a basic excellency and, in the case of Malefactors, additional consecration. So, when asked what I would want Performance to be able to do in a new edition, right near the top of my list is definitely 'that thing the castes of Performance were supposed to be specifically specialized in would be good, thanks.'<br /> <br /> But if the core themes, concepts, and presuppositions of what the Zeniths actually are, what they do, has changed between 2e and 3e, that's useful information, and terribly relevant to this conversation. It would have been really useful to include that in the initial post, so we didn't make assumptions about design space for Zenith's and Performance that have been already established without our knowledge, but I can understand how, from your perspective, it must have not seemed like a significant change - or even like there wasn't any change at all, if this was how you've seen Zeniths all along, despite how they were presented in the books.<br /> <br /> So, I suppose my questions are, will rolling Performance for prayer still be a thing, or will it be moved to a different Ability or removed as a roll entirely? Will Zeniths still count as automatic priests, along with the benefits regarding prayer, as they've been in past editions, or are you shifting much more to them being the core figures of religions in their own right? If it's the latter rather than the former, will you include charms that allow Zeniths to lead prayers to themselves to, say, increase their Cult rewards for the scene, or gain other benefits? Are there any other details about what you've already decided Performance and Zeniths will involve or feature that we might need to be clued in to in order to make more educated suggestions, or does that just about cover it?<br /> <br /> Oh, and thanks for the time spent collecting feedback and clarifying points for the community. I always appreciate developers doing this kind of thing while the product is still in development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T07:55:41-08:00","id":53988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53965#post53965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zeniths are prophets. They are Biblical-level holy men, evangelists and judges, like Samson, John the Baptist, Moses, and the Nazarene himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of the UCS? What does the UCS want pepole to do? Pray to him? Or would it be for some personal cause, whatever the Zenith PC wants to champion be it concepts of logical thought or firebrand pogroms?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Prophets invoke the spirit and power of the divine, giving them an understood universality that is not diminished by the whims of a dominant cult or a state religion. </div> </div> </div>In game how does that differ from the use of charms in general? Or magic? Is a river god maintaining the flow of the river divine and the Zenith does stuff like that? Or are the prophets of the UCS and thus divinity is really shiny gold/yellow/etc.?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They have the authority of heaven because they represent it. They can perform the functions of a priest\u2014see also: water-into-wine\u2014but such men are as far beyond priests as the eagle is above the salmon. See also: water-into-wine. </div> </div> </div>What does the 'authority of heaven' mean? As in, you walk into a hostile court and castigate the king for their unjust actions and no one will willingly interfere to stop you because you have a certain gravitas? Or do people literally know you are the representative of the UCS directly?<br /> <br /> Is water into wine a caste thing or just a charm thing that they have easier access to? Or sorcery?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T07:59:19-08:00","id":53990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagadaishio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53983#post53983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if the core themes, concepts, and presuppositions of what the Zeniths actually are, what they do, has changed between 2e and 3e, that's useful information, and terribly relevant to this conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps not. The discussion on Performance, prayer and the gods in general is extremely interesting, and might not have happened if the role of the Zenith Caste had been clarified beforehand. Plus, Performance isn't just about the Zenith Caste, so its role isn't <i>the</i> most important consideration here.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T08:03:27-08:00","id":53993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagadaishio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53983#post53983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so 3e is making Zenith's less priests and more self-central prophets and actual targets or worship? Maybe along with losing that automatic decrease in prayer difficulty, and therefore no longer having prayer and priestly activities be a relevant core them to Zeniths? I can live with that change, as long as it's addressed head-on instead of sidestepped or ignored. I would still be pretty interested in prayer just being another avenue of social influence, through which all the normal Performance charms can work, shooting a message up to a god they way you would deliver a letter to a king. It's all good, though, as long as you're removing priestliness and prayer from the core themes of the caste. Maybe removing Performance's function as the prayer ability entirely?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing within the context of defining the role of Zenith as prophet makes what they do and how they do it at all different from what they did when their role was defined as priest-king, except it's clearer that they have both a means and a need to spread the worship of the UCS. It's not clear right now what their need will be, but I expect it will be something of minor import but significant convenience.<br /> <br /> But Performance is how you lead others to prayer. Have you ever sung hymns? What about danced the Awa? Delivered a sermon?<br /> <br /> But prayer isn't a direct result of performance. Some people will be inspired to bend knee and others will not. Some people will be moved and others will not. Done correctly, of course, there is an overwhelming sense of participation in something greater than yourself when a congregation sings together, or dances together. An adept sermon, particularly one that does not rest its foundation upon a holy text with which most listeners would be intimately familiar, can induce a sense of revelation.<br /> <br /> But none of this is more or less likely to make any given god answer any given person's prayer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagadaishio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53983#post53983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if the core themes, concepts, and presuppositions of what the Zeniths actually are, what they do, has changed between 2e and 3e, that's useful information, and terribly relevant to this conversation. It would have been really useful to include that in the initial post, so we didn't make assumptions about design space for Zenith's and Performance that have been already established without our knowledge, but I can understand how, from your perspective, it must have not seemed like a significant change - or even like there wasn't any change at all, if this was how you've seen Zeniths all along, despite how they were presented in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>They haven't. This has <i>always </i>been the Zenith's role. Expand the worship of the UCS. Through words, deeds, or ass-kicking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T08:03:33-08:00","id":53994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagadaishio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53983#post53983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, so 3e is making Zenith's less priests and more self-central prophets and actual targets or worship? Maybe along with losing that automatic decrease in prayer difficulty, and therefore no longer having prayer and priestly activities be a relevant core them to Zeniths? I can live with that change, as long as it's addressed head-on instead of sidestepped or ignored. I would still be pretty interested in prayer just being another avenue of social influence, through which all the normal Performance charms can work, shooting a message up to a god they way you would deliver a letter to a king. It's all good, though, as long as you're removing priestliness and prayer from the core themes of the caste. Maybe removing Performance's function as the prayer ability entirely?<br /> <br /> I'm mostly coming to this point with how 2e presented the Zenith caste, with 2e's rules for prayer, and 2e's lack of support for actually enhancing prayers with charms. When a core component of the Zenith was that all prayers were at -1 difficulty and they were called the priests of the Solars, when the (pre-errata) Malefactor anima was all about consecrating an area for easier prayer to the Yozi via personal prayer, it seemed bizarre to have there be no charms that helped it along shy of a basic excellency and, in the case of Malefactors, additional consecration. So, when asked what I would want Performance to be able to do in a new edition, right near the top of my list is definitely 'that thing the castes of Performance were supposed to be specifically specialized in would be good, thanks.'<br /> <br /> But if the core themes, concepts, and presuppositions of what the Zeniths actually are, what they do, has changed between 2e and 3e, that's useful information, and terribly relevant to this conversation. It would have been really useful to include that in the initial post, so we didn't make assumptions about design space for Zenith's and Performance that have been already established without our knowledge, but I can understand how, from your perspective, it must have not seemed like a significant change - or even like there wasn't any change at all, if this was how you've seen Zeniths all along, despite how they were presented in the books.<br /> <br /> So, I suppose my questions are, will rolling Performance for prayer still be a thing, or will it be moved to a different Ability or removed as a roll entirely? Will Zeniths still count as automatic priests, along with the benefits regarding prayer, as they've been in past editions, or are you shifting much more to them being the core figures of religions in their own right? If it's the latter rather than the former, will you include charms that allow Zeniths to lead prayers to themselves to, say, increase their Cult rewards for the scene, or gain other benefits? Are there any other details about what you've already decided Performance and Zeniths will involve or feature that we might need to be clued in to in order to make more educated suggestions, or does that just about cover it?<br /> <br /> Oh, and thanks for the time spent collecting feedback and clarifying points for the community. I always appreciate developers doing this kind of thing while the product is still in development.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not a change, tbh. Zeniths are still priest-kings because every god would want one leading his religion. But calling a Zenith a priest is like calling the Terminator a bodyguard or an assassin and leaving it there. It is a bit of a simplification. You note yourself that in 2e, prayer was not supported and doesn't really do anything concrete. That's not an oversight. It was that way in 1e as well. Meanwhile the Zenith Charms point to the Zenith being the beneficiary of divine ardor, might, primacy, and worship.<br /> <br /> Think of it this way. If a person claims he is a police officer, you ask to see his badge. In Creation, claiming &quot;I am a priest&quot; requires similar verification. You say &quot;I'm a priest,&quot; I ask &quot;Where's your khakkhara?&quot; Or maybe &quot;Where's your robes? Where's your beads?&quot; etc. But John the Baptist, naked and smeared with dirt and honey, with the legs of a locust caught in his beard, claims no such title, and is backed by no organization, and yet he invokes the divine. You may question his authority, but you don't question his position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T08:06:52-08:00","id":53995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53990#post53990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps not. The discussion on Performance, prayer and the gods in general is extremely interesting, and might not have happened if the role of the Zenith Caste had been clarified beforehand. Plus, Performance isn't just about the Zenith Caste, so its role isn't <i>the</i> most important consideration here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course not. But the conversation seems to have moved on from what we want Performance to have in general, and what we all expected prayer to be and feature in the new edition. For that particular discussion, Zeniths in particular would be eminently relevant. Or, rather, they would be eminently relevant to that discussion if they were still priest castes who universally received a decrease in difficulty to all rolls to pray. Since they aren't, it seems, that anymore, having Performance charms that directly interact with the mechanics of prayer are also less relevant, since it seems that's no longer necessarily a Solar thing to do and there won't be any real design space wasted.<br /> <br /> I'm much more interested now in whether or not the act of prayer can be used as an avenue of social influence through which normal Performance charms can be used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T08:16:54-08:00","id":54005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagadaishio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53995#post53995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course not. But the conversation seems to have moved on from what we want Performance to have in general, and what we all expected prayer to be and feature in the new edition. For that particular discussion, Zeniths in particular would be eminently relevant. Or, rather, they would be eminently relevant to that discussion if they were still priest castes who universally received a decrease in difficulty to all rolls to pray. Since they aren't, it seems, that anymore, having Performance charms that directly interact with the mechanics of prayer are also less relevant, since it seems that's no longer necessarily a Solar thing to do and there won't be any real design space wasted.<br /> <br /> I'm much more interested now in whether or not the act of prayer can be used as an avenue of social influence through which normal Performance charms can be used.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hopefully this conversation clarifies that for me as well. <br /> <br /> Please note that if you dropped Michael Jackson into the outskirts of Creation and had him dance, the effect would not be &quot;wow cool, he can dance really well.&quot; It would shake the foundations of belief. They would think he was a divine madman, surely touched by the gods. His dancing would provoke mania, fear, rage, awe. The people of Creation have never seen such movements before. They would be provoked by them. They would conclude that he was possessed by demons or by the spirits of the air and sky. If he claimed &quot;I am the representative of X god,&quot; they would be far more inclined to believe him, because he dances as if possessed.<br /> <br /> Dance, oration, singing\u2014the heart of Performance\u2014invokes the divine madman. It leads people to believe the person speaks / acts / embodies Heaven. Gods want priests who have high Performance because people think these things about people who can dance, speak passionately before large crowds, etc. This idea makes them want to listen to that person, it makes them want to believe what that person says. And if the god truly backs such a one, that person can stand in for him, run a bureaucracy and do all his temporal work while he soaks up the prayer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T08:22:35-08:00","id":54011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53994#post53994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is not a change, tbh. Zeniths are still priest-kings because every god would want one leading his religion. But calling a Zenith a priest is like calling the Terminator a bodyguard or an assassin and leaving it there. It is a bit of a simplification. You note yourself that in 2e, prayer was not supported and doesn't really do anything concrete. That's not an oversight. It was that way in 1e as well. Meanwhile the Zenith Charms point to the Zenith being the beneficiary of divine ardor, might, primacy, and worship.<br /> <br /> Think of it this way. If a person claims he is a police officer, you ask to see his badge. In Creation, claiming &quot;I am a priest&quot; requires similar verification. You say &quot;I'm a priest,&quot; I ask &quot;Where's your khakkhara?&quot; Or maybe &quot;Where's your robes? Where's your beads?&quot; etc. But John the Baptist, naked and smeared with dirt and honey, with the legs of a locust caught in his beard, claims no such title, and is backed by no organization, and yet he invokes the divine. You may question his authority, but you don't question his position.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand entirely where you're coming from, but the simple fact that Zeniths got a decrease in all prayer roll difficulties - the equivalent of one free automatic success - suggests to me that they were supposed to be able to pray, get heard, and get a response accordingly, and that the interaction was then largely forgotten about for more cinematic uses of charms because people find receiving power from an external source underwhelming. There was clear space in their direction of design and inherent bonuses to interact with that system, it was just never explored; it was design space squandered.<br /> <br /> I find it encouraging that it seems that won't be a thing at all for them in 3e, because it means there won't be any issue of, 'Well, here's a prayer system, and Zeniths' anima gives them a bonus for it the same way a Dawn's anima gives them a bonus for combat and an Eclipse's for spiritual diplomacy, but the prayer interaction isn't even remotely as explored as normal physical or social combat.' It's encouraging because instead of it being a tantalizing teaser of a system that the caste could or even should be using, but lacks any real means or incentive, it's just going to be largely avoided for a different role entirely. The Zeniths will be central figures of a faith, and the recipients of those prayers, rather than guiding prayers as they were enabled to do in 2e.<br /> <br /> At any rate, I'm hoping that means there will be charms that do what I said above. Charms that boost their benefits from their cult, or charms that let them turn the force of prayer from a cult led by them against a creature of darkness, warding their holy temples consecrated in their name and image from intrusion by unholy spirits. Charms that make them Nazarene and Buddha, rather than just the Pied Piper. So, I still want prayer charms, just of a very different bent. Even if they're changing from being the givers of prayer to the recipients, that still means prayer should play a role for them.<br /> <br /> And if that's just a suite of charms that gives them benefits for having an audience? That's fine too. Whether they're getting an influx of essence motes from giving the sermon on the mount or performing a ballet for a filled house, they can both be built on the same charms. Whether you're chanting a prayer with your warrior-priests to steel them before a battle or raising your sword for a battle cry and for the war drums to start, giving your viking troops bonuses before a battle, they can both be built on the same charms.<br /> <br /> But whether they're prophets or priests, prayer should play some role, have some meaningful mechanics and interactions and display. If being a prophet is as central to their concept as being a priest supposedly was - and by all appearances, by the universal bonuses they got to praying, it really was supposed to be much more central, at least at some point - then there should still be some reason to court faith, worship, and prayer - for yourself and others - aside from just regular maintenance on the Cult background, or 3e's equivalent.<br /> <br /> It just seems, I don't know, strange that a caste characterized as holy men have more reason to be bards and statesmen than high priests or living gods. Strange to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","user":"jagadaishio","date":".  clarification on the first sentence 01-20-2014, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T08:25:24-08:00","id":54012,"title":"","content":"If you are a god, the Unconquered Sun is your boss.<br /> <br /> Here comes his select and beloved daughter, Perfect Soul, with words of revolution burning on her lips. A wise spirit would do well to accept her as his priest. But she's really so much more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T08:27:13-08:00","id":54013,"title":"","content":"If I follow the direction of this thread:<br /> The better Performance-charm to support the Solar as a priest would be a charm which motivates people to actively participate in a performance. This could be street dancing as well as participation in a elaborate prayer ritual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://owncloud.scaenicus.net/index.php/s/saLcZXhVcOu0j3W/download?path=%2F&amp;files=ScaenicusBacked_big.png&amp;downloadStartSecret=mflqpfu2cd8\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/ScaenicusBacked.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1491-scaenicus","name":"Scaenicus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1491_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T08:30:02-08:00","id":54015,"title":"","content":"I think a solar prayer shouldn't work as a petition but instead it should work as an order. The spirits of weather are wrecking a region? The solar comes an brings them to submission and restores the heavenly order. Sure this might overlap a bit with summoning sorcery. But incantation of effective restoration already overlaps with crafting charms...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T08:33:58-08:00","id":54017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54015#post54015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The solar comes an brings them to submission and restores the heavenly order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed... however not as a Charm effect or simple roll-off... this is the story I wanted to tell as ST and I would be pretty angry at the book for allowing my players to just roll my whole arc away.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://owncloud.scaenicus.net/index.php/s/saLcZXhVcOu0j3W/download?path=%2F&amp;files=ScaenicusBacked_big.png&amp;downloadStartSecret=mflqpfu2cd8\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/ScaenicusBacked.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1491-scaenicus","name":"Scaenicus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1491_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T08:42:01-08:00","id":54025,"title":"","content":"I would think that if anything, Solar prayer stuff would not so much summon or get favors from the god directly but the Solar is so able to whip up a sermon and get the prayers of his followers so well orchestrated that the reward the god gets for those prayers is particularly effective. Or loud.<br /> <br /> This would result in the Solar not so much being one to ask the god for much but able to give the god what he wants as a bargaining chip. You as a Solar can walk to a god, tell them, &quot;I'm a priest of the sun. You want in on some of this I'll make it worth your while.&quot; In effect, you don't go and become a supplicant, but tap into your worthiness to be a priest for the King of Heaven in order to be a bargaining chip for others.<br /> <br /> It's in a way like being a rocket scientist or nuclear engineer and offering your skills to a kid's science fair project. That kid's project is probably going to be a badass atom smasher or soemthing and the kid gets perks for it but is very dependent on you to get the reuslts again.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T08:50:38-08:00","id":54029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53975#post53975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that I think about, every Sidereal have the Priest merit as Zenith too, and they treat god the same way they treat everyone, no using mysterious prayer beads or burning a<span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">quilaria</span></span> incense to call down wrath of the god (well, there is Spirit-Binding Battle Pattern, but you do need to sacrifice a shit load of your own soldiers though).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always seen Sidereals treating prayer like a business transaction...a form of payment at best. Gods are like the UPS guy...they perform a vital function (in theory, at least) without which current society probably wouldn't be able to function (again, theory), but to actually <i>worship</i> them or pay them homage? Odd quirk at best, complete pants-on-head madness at worst.<br /> <br /> It took my last character quite a while to wrap her head around the fact that the Solars of her acquaintance (ie the other PCs) worshiped the Unconquered Sun out of real devotion and not as a tool to control mortals. She actually very intensely interrogated the Eclipse about it.<br /> <br /> (And, again...look at how well being priests works out for Sidereals. I'm trying desperately not to make a joke about how their most commonly used ritual gear is lube.<br /> <br /> ...bollocks, I just made that joke, didn't I?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T10:22:09-08:00","id":54071,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's just me, but I would like a performance charm that allows an Solar to pull together a scene. To better explain, Prince Dum-dee-do of the sho-wop's bursts out into song about how great the market plaza is to be in. people without a high enough dv slowly/quickly start finding themselves joining in. Butchers cleaving cuts of meat, bakers kneading and shuffling bread dough, nearby bar patrons pounding on the tables all start to form a beat, a melody. Pretty soon the entire marketplace is filled with people singing along in a grand musical number, buying and selling, trading and exchanging. So caught up in it none of them notice Prince Dum-dee-do casually exit stage left and receive a coin purse from the region's Guild representative who needed to boost numbers for his visiting superior.<br /> <br /> Performance leading up and towards something like this would be nice, imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/841-okamigrif","name":"Okamigrif","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T10:43:27-08:00","id":54079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okamigrif</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54071#post54071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's just me, but I would like a performance charm that allows an Solar to pull together a scene. To better explain, Prince Dum-dee-do of the sho-wop's bursts out into song about how great the market plaza is to be in. people without a high enough dv slowly/quickly start finding themselves joining in. Butchers cleaving cuts of meat, bakers kneading and shuffling bread dough, nearby bar patrons pounding on the tables all start to form a beat, a melody. Pretty soon the entire marketplace is filled with people singing along in a grand musical number, buying and selling, trading and exchanging. So caught up in it none of them notice Prince Dum-dee-do casually exit stage left and receive a coin purse from the region's Guild representative who needed to boost numbers for his visiting superior.<br /> <br /> Performance leading up and towards something like this would be nice, imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Instant bollywood/disney musical scene? I like the idea!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T10:51:40-08:00","id":54083,"title":"","content":"I think the discussion on prayer and performance has been really helpful for me so for. I think a few examples in the book would be helpful, if there is room. <br /> <br /> That said, Performance being associated with the ecstatic or divine madman is interesting. It is not a path I had really seen Charm support for, except Husband Seducing Demon Dance, and even that had a different fluff presentation if I recall. It is also somewhat different in presentation from mythic icons like Orpheus or Amergin. Although Orpheus' power over beasts is probably easily modeled with Performance plus some version of Friendship with Animals. Amergin's storm calming song, and that of other musicians, might be handled in a similar fashion - a charm that let's the Exalt channel Charms from another ability they possess through Performance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/798-joshua","name":"Joshua","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar798_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T10:52:36-08:00","id":54084,"title":"","content":"Per my crew: <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">Being able to effect people emotions.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">Some kind of dancing stance for dodging (bit like snake style but looks prettier).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">Being able to make music from thin air could be cool too.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">and maybe something to turn you into the ultimate Mick Jagger equse frontman </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">* The ability to sway an audience to my cause through my performance (words not required).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">* The ability to turn my anima into a special-effects light show bonanza</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">* Some sort of ability to actually attack through Performance\ufeff<br /> <br /> being able to blow someone away with a power chord, or be able to play a song that knocks them back, is awesome!</span></span><br /> <br /> Example given: <a href=\"http://youtu.be/wVjf5CccAwY\" target=\"_blank\">http://youtu.be/wVjf5CccAwY</a> (Kung Fu Hustle Fight Scene<br /> <br /> Hammer<br /> GM of PSA<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/238-hammerofheaven","name":"HammerofHeaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar238_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T11:02:41-08:00","id":54093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54079#post54079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instant bollywood/disney musical scene? I like the idea!</div> </div> </div> </div> Pretty much. An example of performance for evil would be like the Buffy musical episode, causing people to dance past the brink of their stamina. An example for good would be the barn raising scene in 7 brides for 7 brothers, or the ice cutter scene from Frozen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/841-okamigrif","name":"Okamigrif","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T11:05:42-08:00","id":54096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okamigrif</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54093#post54093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much. An example of performance for evil would be like the Buffy musical episode, causing people to dance past the brink of their stamina. An example for good would be the barn raising scene in 7 brides for 7 brothers, or the ice cutter scene from Frozen.</div> </div> </div> </div>That Charm already exists. It's called Easily Accepted Proposition Stance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T11:24:28-08:00","id":54111,"title":"","content":"From reading John's responses about Prayer, I've come to the following understanding about Prayer and I want to make sure I'm right.<br /> <br /> A Prayer is, functionally, a request that the god do something (or a thank you or some other brief note) coupled with a bit of power. The God on the other end has no responsibility to do anything about it, although they could.<br /> <br /> Anyone can pray to a given God. A Priest leads formal prayers and sacrifices, serves as a church bureaucrat, and so on. These formal prayers and sacrifices send a lot of power to the god, but again, the God doesn't have to do jack about it.<br /> <br /> On the human side, a Priest who is an excellent speaker, dancer, etc. can impress the people by being &quot;divinely inspired&quot; and/or enhance the reputation of their God by attracting more cult members or leading them in more impressive prayer. This potentially gives the Priest leverage over the God to pry out divine blessings by threatening what is, essentially, a strike.<br /> <br /> <br /> From looking at all of this, it seems like you don't really need anything extra charmise for a Zenith to be able to be an awesome Priest, since the existing social influence charms should probably work fine in all of the above situations. I could see potential charms for messing with the power you get from prayer, but I don't know that they're necessary or necessarily in theme.<br /> <br /> A god should want a Zenith on their side, because they can motivate the people to do things like build a humongous temple or mass sacrifice thousands of cattle. A God should not want a Zenith going against them because said Zenith could turn all of their followers against the god. This is completely aside the likelihood that said Zenith can beat up said god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T11:29:48-08:00","id":54113,"title":"","content":"Priests being necessarily lower in scale or more quotidian than prophets feels like a shaky idea. The Church Fathers, the Saints, Martin Luther, Popes, etc. particularly once they're finished being are mythologized by worshipers in their religion. Maybe they could totally take John the Baptist?<br /> <br /> However, it is completely right to skew Zeniths as prophets and non priests.<br /> <br /> Priests unavoidably are initiated into and work through a human tradition passed across and down to them - they have peers, they are part of a church, they have a hierarchy, they have a congregation. They may bring new revelations, but they who they are is part of the structures and inheritance.<br /> <br /> Prophets pretty much by definition aren't - they're just men (and women) who were chosen and have a mission and purpose.<br /> <br /> One of these things works greats with the backstory and feel of the Solars, the other isn't such a great fit (except in the &quot;I was a priest of this religion, now I'm not really&quot; sense).<br /> <br /> (Plus priests is totes D&amp;D?).<br /> <br /> Also, passionate, people changing lord of the dance sounds cool (no knowing winks obligatory plz).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T11:39:21-08:00","id":54117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54096#post54096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That Charm already exists. It's called Easily Accepted Proposition Stance.</div> </div> </div> </div>First time I've even opened my sidereal pdf, woo! Hadn't even known about this charm.<br /> Anyways, from what I've read of it, Easily Accepted Proposition Stance is directly a one off charm. It causes a single possible event to happen in the background that prove advantageous in the fight. What I want from performance is the ability and charm back-up to start and develop the event myself. Guide, feed and wield the boisterous crowd with every spin of my dance, every strum or toot on my instrument, every line of my oration. Easily Accepted Proposition Stance is more of a, an uproar in a southern city hinders and stalls the reinforcements the opposing general is waiting on benefits me on the field/in negotiations. I want charms that allow me to cause the uproar in the southern city that hinders reinforcements so my Solar General buddy has a better advantage on the field. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/841-okamigrif","name":"Okamigrif","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T11:48:04-08:00","id":54119,"title":"","content":"I'm just gonna note here that I have run a TON of Zenith games, and I know how Zenith players have fun, and this thread is not really 'getting' it.<br /> <br /> Every Zenith I have ever run a game for LOVES running around and making things right with Gods ; praying to them, setting things in order, essentially fixing the world. Yes, this does mean they occasionally do 'worship other beings' even if the Sun is a bit arrogant.<br /> <br /> Actually, I'm gonna double down on this and call out the statement 'The Sun Worships Nothing' as kinda... bad, and caustic to Zenith themes and play experiences. Not that I think that's a bad statement of Sol's character, but just that extending it to this degree is not good.<br /> <br /> I really hope that this opinion changes, because it doesn't seem like it's very tuned in to how most of the Zenith players I've run for have fun.<br /> <br /> And the Zenith castebook was one of the more popular Castebooks at my table, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T11:49:55-08:00","id":54121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okamigrif</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54117#post54117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First time I've even opened my sidereal pdf, woo! Hadn't even known about this charm.<br /> Anyways, from what I've read of it, Easily Accepted Proposition Stance is directly a one off charm. It causes a single possible event to happen in the background that prove advantageous in the fight. What I want from performance is the ability and charm back-up to start and develop the event myself. Guide, feed and wield the boisterous crowd with every spin of my dance, every strum or toot on my instrument, every line of my oration. Easily Accepted Proposition Stance is more of a, an uproar in a southern city hinders and stalls the reinforcements the opposing general is waiting on benefits me on the field/in negotiations. I want charms that allow me to cause the uproar in the southern city that hinders reinforcements so my Solar General buddy has a better advantage on the field.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you haven't already, read the version in the Scroll of Errata. The Charm is completely rewritten to be more useful and generally applicable.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T11:59:32-08:00","id":54125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53977#post53977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which god are they priests of? When does the UCS answer prayers? Why would Zeniths pray to other gods? If you're still not convinced, just ask yourself &quot;What would Socrates ask next?&quot; and keep going.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's try this again, shall we? A Zenith is a Prophet of the Unconquered Sun (yay!). Okay. So no need to pray to lesser gods and (point of fact) no need to pray to the Unconquered Sun, either. Sure thing! Makes sense.<br /> <br /> ...so everyone who makes a devout Zenith is playing an idiot?<br /> <br /> <br /> The Zenith IS a miracle of the Unconquered Sun. Prayer should be a way to bring out that power. No need to tap the big man for extra mojo, but it should totally be an effective way of channeling the mojo he already gave you. Ordinary folks can believe in a god. Solars can Believe.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It does. It means they have the divine right to track down the god of whatever and kick the shit out of him OR dress him down for a) doing his job or b) not doing his job. Whichever the Zenith prefers. But the key here is that they're supposed to track the gods down. The other side of the swing set, sorcery, can be used to summon a god directly to you and bind them. This is only rarely done because it's a great way to fuck things up. </div> </div> </div>That's not &quot;a priest&quot;, that's &quot;their boss&quot;. If Solars can forcibly impose the narrative of &quot;and then the hero rides off into the sunset, and the people cheer&quot; with a specific Charm, having religion that has real power, rather than just the ordinary mortal level &quot;get people working together&quot; is something it practically cries out for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Everything you've suggested was possible in 2e, provided you were willing to flavor it that way. Solar Medicine is perhaps the best at healing others (Dragon-Blooded Medicine is nearly as good, in one of those strokes of getting things right), which would certainly look like fucking magic to mortals because it is. Casting out spirits is within the primary skillset of all Celestial Exalts, although Sidereals are arguably the best at it because Terminal Sanction; that shouldn't stop you from making an Solar exorcist, though. You draw power from worshipers through Cult. Cults don't necessarily have to worship you, after all. The heavenly bureaucracy is set up to provide the benefits of worship in appropriate proportion to the effort expended in the bureaucracies. Your Zenith runs a major cult of the UCS and thus gets some benefit out of it. Not that there's anything wrong with a Solar setting themselves up as a being to worship. </div> </div> </div>Screw reskinning. <br /> <br /> If I can heal someone because I have Medicine N and a Charm, that is *not* faith healing. That's regular old healing, spiced up with magic. Faith healing would be healing that, you know, *requires faith*. Analogy: if Glorious Solar Sabre didn't exist, saying &quot;well you can take an orichalcum daiklaive&quot; is not, in fact, an adequate of representing turning raw Solar essence into a sword. Even if you CAN banish it to Elsewhere and resummon it.<br /> <br /> Solar Exorcist? Should have some reason to chant prayers as he does his casting out, rather than it being window dressing (it shouldn't be the ONLY way to do it, but it should be A way and it should be different from the way a scholar/sorceror would do it).<br /> <br /> Cult? Sure, you can take it. So can any other essence-channeler in the setting. Solars shouldn't just be good at getting it, they should be good at USING it once they have it (analogy: Charms only let you raise an army, they don't actually help you use it more effectively once you've got it)<br /> <br /> Basically, playing up the Priest-King angle should have some Charmspace all it's own. There should be a reason for a player to want to build a Zenith who uses religion, specifically, rather than just &quot;yeah, religion is good stunt fodder for your basic 'I am in charge!' spiel&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T12:04:53-08:00","id":54129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54119#post54119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just gonna note here that I have run a TON of Zenith games, and I know how Zenith players have fun, and this thread is not really 'getting' it.<br /> <br /> Every Zenith I have ever run a game for LOVES running around and making things right with Gods ; praying to them, setting things in order, essentially fixing the world. Yes, this does mean they occasionally do 'worship other beings' even if the Sun is a bit arrogant.<br /> <br /> Actually, I'm gonna double down on this and call out the statement 'The Sun Worships Nothing' as kinda... bad, and caustic to Zenith themes and play experiences. Not that I think that's a bad statement of Sol's character, but just that extending it to this degree is not good. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I agree. What, pray tell, would the Sun worship? He is ruler of Heaven. His creators are locked away in Hell or dead. The raksha are his enemies, the Ishvarra usurper-gods and the shinma have no will or volition. The Solar Exalted are <i>his Chosen</i> and the Exigence comes from him. He is first amongst equals wiht his peers of the Incarna.<br /> <br /> Nothing in Creation is something he reasonably is expected to worship. Worship, at leas to me, has something to do with submission to greater power. No greater power exists above him in Creation. His worshipping would be like Zeus or Amaterasu worshipping anything. They don't need to: they tell other gods what to fucking do on their own terms, not those who rank below them under Heaven.<br /> <br /> His priests, the Zeniths, as a result have no greater power they can worship either. I would say the way to get Zentihs going about bossing things about as Priest of the Sun is the same as i note earlier: Being a personally ordained Pillar of Heaven means you get to boss gods around by authority, and maybe pull on some of that authority to give them what htey might want or need or fear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54119#post54119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I really hope that this opinion changes, because it doesn't seem like it's very tuned in to how most of the Zenith players I've run for have fun.<br /> <br /> And the Zenith castebook was one of the more popular Castebooks at my table, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Zenith was actually my second-least Castebook personally (all goody two-shoe characters, generally ambiguous ideas of what hte Caste does and some fairly oddly specific Charms). It was mostly boring and not as useful or defining as Eclipse, Dawn or Night were for me.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":353,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","user":"Blaque","date":".  Copy-paste error. -_- 01-20-2014, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T12:06:18-08:00","id":54130,"title":"","content":"Also, let's examine this a bit further -<br /> <br /> Is the August Lord of Heaven -that stingy- with his respect?<br /> <br /> Does he horde his esteem in a similar fashion to a monotheistic JHVA?<br /> <br /> Does he BOW TO NONE??!?<br /> <br /> No, I say. That's very... well, again, Christian in the viewpoint ascribed to him. He probably DOES offer prayer, out of respect, to many of his subordinates in a magnanimous fashion. Obviously he is always the most August, the most Respected, but it is good and proper if he will occasionally remove his shoes and have tea with other divinities. Whether one calls this 'prayer' is largely a matter of semantics.<br /> <br /> He will occasionally sing praises of other divinities. This does not diminish him or his glory. It is akin to being invited to the house of a friend and offering thanks for a meal well prepared, or compliments on the home, or any number of other things.<br /> <br /> The setting -is- polytheistic, after all, and the Sun has never really been portrayed as having a 'Mine All Mine' mentality save in regards to the games.<br /> <br /> He is the Just and Proper Overlord of Heaven, not the despot. He is the august emperor, the grandfather, the idealistic pillar of Yu-Shan. He is not an angry child that cannot acknowledge the greatness or impact of others. He gives them respect in proportion to what they have earned, but he does not deny just due either. As is proper.<br /> <br /> He would probably disapprove of -inappropriate- worship that was poorly considered or inauspicious, but arranging a proper heaven via right and polite action is completely within my understanding of what he could be capable of. He doesn't just punch people good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":762,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","user":"MissMaddy","date":". 01-20-2014, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T12:11:32-08:00","id":54135,"title":"","content":"Definitely more useful and generally applicable, but it's still declaring X happens and sitting back as opposed to causing X to happen. I suppose that could be due to how expensive high requirement it is ( it may not be high requirement, I have zero experience with sidereal pcs).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/841-okamigrif","name":"Okamigrif","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T12:12:06-08:00","id":54136,"title":"","content":"Perhaps if Performance has a Salty Dog Method style charm, a small prayer bene could be in there. E.g. &quot;All Prayer rolls are reduced by one, and the prayers of those you lead in prayer are marked as coming from a chosen of the Sun.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T12:12:48-08:00","id":54137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54125#post54125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I can heal someone because I have Medicine N and a Charm, that is *not* faith healing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Medicine Charms are very obviously based on faith healing. This might change in Ex3, but it's unlikely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T12:21:01-08:00","id":54140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54130#post54130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, let's examine this a bit further -<br /> <br /> Is the August Lord of Heaven -that stingy- with his respect?<br /> <br /> Does he horde his esteem in a similar fashion to a monotheistic JHVA?<br /> <br /> Does he BOW TO NONE??!?<br /> <br /> No, I say. That's very... well, again, Christian in the viewpoint ascribed to him. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Does Brahman worship anything? Does Ameterasu? Izanagi? I'm pretty sure Zeus doesn't worship shit either. It's only Christian if you force it to be so. The Unconquered Sun by his title is that: Unconquered. The title kind of implies he kneels to no one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54130#post54130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... He probably DOES offer prayer, out of respect, to many of his subordinates in a magnanimous fashion. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Do we have evidence to this? Because he's again, King of Heaven. And Creation is a setting where you can get by being the CEO who just skims off the top. Nothing has ever implied his humiltiy is to a level where he has to send token &quot;prayer&quot;. It depends greatly on how defines prayer. In most cases, they're probably &quot;Do this. I say so&quot; and that's that. When you have the Mandate of Divine Subordination, why do you ever need to pray to anyone?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54130#post54130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Obviously he is always the most August, the most Respected, but it is good and proper if he will occasionally remove his shoes and have tea with other divinities. Whether one calls this 'prayer' is largely a matter of semantics....</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't seem to me to be &quot;prayer&quot; or &quot;worship&quot; but being a boss people likes. That a boss sends me a Christmas card every now and again doesn't mean he is at all treating me in the same regard as I would when I give him a gift. For him it's a token bit of motivation, not a way for me to get something I want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54130#post54130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...He will occasionally sing praises of other divinities. This does not diminish him or his glory. It is akin to being invited to the house of a friend and offering thanks for a meal well prepared, or compliments on the home, or any number of other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>So are we now entirely in &quot;How i think it should be but no evidence to suppor this mode?&quot; Because as far as I can tell, he is like this about once a year at the effective Halloween/New Year/Christmas party and off being an aloof King of Heaven when it's not that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54130#post54130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The setting -is- polytheistic, after all, and the Sun has never really been portrayed as having a 'Mine All Mine' mentality save in regards to the games.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's in charge of Heaven. If he wanted to, the buck stops at him for all purposes in Yu-Shan. He gets a cut of all ambrosia ever sent there in addition to his stuff. He had to be asked (not told, asked) to not go and kill all the Yozi along with the rest of the Neverborn. It might not be &quot;mine all mine&quot; but nothing says he has ever given a fuck to be the Best Boss Ever. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54130#post54130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He is the Just and Proper Overlord of Heaven, not the despot. He is the august emperor, the grandfather, the idealistic pillar of Yu-Shan. He is not an angry child that cannot acknowledge the greatness or impact of others. He gives them respect in proportion to what they have earned, but he does not deny just due either. As is proper.</div> </div> </div> </div>And none of this mandates he have anything that at all looks like prayer or worship save a very stretched definition of the term &quot;Saying stuff in a ritual fashion to a god.' WHich still for him probably is &quot;Do this, because I'm right.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54130#post54130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He would probably disapprove of -inappropriate- worship that was poorly considered or inauspicious, but arranging a proper heaven via right and polite action is completely within my understanding of what he could be capable of. He doesn't just punch people good.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you approach him how you would any other deity or deity-incarnate. You use proper rituals and stuff or he'll ignore you. I think most of the time he does that: not pay attention since folks presetn things not worth his time or effort hwen he has an entire Celestial Bureaucracy that is supposed to handle the petty shit for him.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T12:33:35-08:00","id":54144,"title":"","content":"This coming from somebody who is popular of more gritty, darker Sun takes...<br /> <br /> ... I'm not sure what that interpretation lends to the game, really.<br /> <br /> The value of this character seems very Malfeas-esque.<br /> <br /> I like to see the sun as well-intentioned and generally a fairly good guy even in my darkest interpretations ; in such cases, he's usually a warrior/soldier struggling with the analogy of substance abuse and PTSD, rather than a despotic overlord.<br /> <br /> I never really give him the JHVA/Malfeas 'ONLY ME' ego trip thing.<br /> <br /> He's awesome enough so that stuff is self-evident without him insisting on it.<br /> <br /> In his best moments... he is the General that leads by example ; not the General that screams at you until you bow to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T12:34:08-08:00","id":54145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54125#post54125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's try this again, shall we? A Zenith is a Prophet of the Unconquered Sun (yay!). Okay. So no need to pray to lesser gods and (point of fact) no need to pray to the Unconquered Sun, either. Sure thing! Makes sense.<br /> <br /> ...so everyone who makes a devout Zenith is playing an idiot?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if you ascribe a definition of &quot;faith&quot; which is some ambiguous force that can do shit like people here on Earth seem to think it is in regards to religion and magic. It doens't make you a fool unless you buy into some idea that you are given a mandate that your actions are ordained by god, in effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54125#post54125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Zenith IS a miracle of the Unconquered Sun. Prayer should be a way to bring out that power. No need to tap the big man for extra mojo, but it should totally be an effective way of channeling the mojo he already gave you. Ordinary folks can believe in a god. Solars can Believe.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;If I believe hard enough it'll be true&quot; is not how Creation works. There's no willworking. There's no Tinkerbells about. Gods don't have some key to their domains that if you poke at htem hard enough unlock things. Gods can influence their domain. If you convince them, they might do so in a way they like. If not, too bad. Being a priest in Creation is being the frontman of the god's cult. Or in other words, his official middleman. There's no mojo that faith has access to that lets you somehow get gods to do what youw ant i fthey don't want to do it. Because Exalted doesn't appear to run on an idea that faith is anything special like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54125#post54125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not &quot;a priest&quot;, that's &quot;their boss&quot;. If Solars can forcibly impose the narrative of &quot;and then the hero rides off into the sunset, and the people cheer&quot; with a specific Charm, having religion that has real power, rather than just the ordinary mortal level &quot;get people working together&quot; is something it practically cries out for.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? And what would that be that doens't just turn Performance and prayer into freeform mojo stuff? I woudl argue that the similar effect is getting a cult that super-charges the god to maybe get a lot out of that prayer. True believers hwo feed your worship a lot in their fervent ritual. It's a carrot that might encourage a god to do things in a way you might like. But the god might just be an exploitive ass still too. <br /> <br /> Hero Rides Away plays on genre conceits that are felt appropriate by an author. Gods answering prayers based on their personal biases and whims is also a genre conceit that the idea of &quot;faith is magic world-influency stuff&quot; some religions hold doens't fit with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54125#post54125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Screw reskinning.<br /> <br /> If I can heal someone because I have Medicine N and a Charm, that is *not* faith healing. That's regular old healing, spiced up with magic. Faith healing would be healing that, you know, *requires faith*. Analogy: if Glorious Solar Sabre didn't exist, saying &quot;well you can take an orichalcum daiklaive&quot; is not, in fact, an adequate of representing turning raw Solar essence into a sword. Even if you CAN banish it to Elsewhere and resummon it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how much you are turning raw Solar Essence into healing bits. But seeing as the world runs on Essence, not faith or belief, I am not sure what you get out of faith healing besides maybe a friendly god. I mean, technically summoning a stomach bottle bug is also a form fo faith healing if you really want to give a few chants to it now and again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54125#post54125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar Exorcist? Should have some reason to chant prayers as he does his casting out, rather than it being window dressing (it shouldn't be the ONLY way to do it, but it should be A way and it should be different from the way a scholar/sorceror would do it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on your religion, an exorcist is just a scholar/healer. Omyoujis and other forms fo Taoists come to mind. THose changs, prayers, summons and scriptures? All are being used to channel ki and get the world to work in a way. That's Lore and Occult. They're mantras that channel stuff, not explications of faith. I would imagine most exorcists in Creation follow this then some &quot;true believer&quot; thing. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54125#post54125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cult? Sure, you can take it. So can any other essence-channeler in the setting. Solars shouldn't just be good at getting it, they should be good at USING it once they have it (analogy: Charms only let you raise an army, they don't actually help you use it more effectively once you've got it)</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems able to be done by having powerful intimacies built on faith of you or your proxy. You don't need fancy fate shit to do this, just hyper-powered charisma and ability to get folks to follow you. Faith is actually just window dressing to this I feel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54125#post54125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, playing up the Priest-King angle should have some Charmspace all it's own. There should be a reason for a player to want to build a Zenith who uses religion, specifically, rather than just &quot;yeah, religion is good stunt fodder for your basic 'I am in charge!' spiel&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why should it? I feel that if you try too hard to force it it starts pushing into genres or thematics Exalted never really bothered to give a shit before and I dont' see a benefit of giving a shit about now. It goes with a very cynical view of religion and worhsip of gods. Since ever. Having more &quot;genuine&quot; faith feels kind of antithetical to a bit of the wants Exalted does iwth religoin and cults. Citing source material, Flat Earth does just fine and interesting stuff with temples worhsipping gods who don't care and priests using charisma and training to keep being pwoerful and getting what they want.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T12:36:23-08:00","id":54146,"title":"","content":"Coming late to this party...<br /> <br /> I'd like to see Solar Performance being honest. It should be about being able to powerfully portray the truth, not about spinning illusions to beguile the masses. When Micheal Jackson does his possessed dance in Creation, he's showing off the power and majesty of his performance (and his patron if we're running with MJ as a Solar). I've got nothing against Solar MJ having a light show to accentuate his dance, but the charm should be <b>about </b><i>enhancing the dance</i>, <b>not </b>providing the light show.<br /> <br /> Solars are the shining heroes of the Sun. I feel they should be honest about their legacy. I don't like the idea of putting charms to do with lying and fake memories in their Performance tree. Or, to put it another way, David Tenant and Hugh Laurie use Lunar Performance Charms: when they act they completely change their accent. Sean Connery is using Solar Performance charms: whether he's playing a Russian, an American, a Roman, an Egyptian, an Alien, an Englishman or what-have-you he always speaks with his own Scottish accent. Brian Blessed also uses Solar Performance charms. A child dressed up <a href=\"http://www.running-w-scissors.com/2010/10/halloween-costume-ewok.html\" target=\"_blank\">as an Ewok</a> is clearly not an Ewok, but is still as adorable. A Solar acting like something else should still have his greatness shine through.<br /> <br /> And, because Performance is huge, going back to comments made at the start of the thread, the Charm tree should have a clear idea of what it's doing. It's OK that Performance covers a broad range of tasks, but the charm trees shouldn't bounce around. The Charms that effect every type of Performance should be accessible to everyone and I shouldn't have to buy a Charm that's only effect is to let me play mad riffs on a Saxian to get to the charm that makes me a better public speaker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T12:37:53-08:00","id":54147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54144#post54144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This coming from somebody who is popular of more gritty, darker Sun takes...<br /> <br /> ... I'm not sure what that interpretation lends to the game, really.<br /> <br /> The value of this character seems very Malfeas-esque.<br /> <br /> I like to see the sun as well-intentioned and generally a fairly good guy even in my darkest interpretations ; in such cases, he's usually a warrior/soldier struggling with the analogy of substance abuse and PTSD, rather than a despotic overlord.<br /> <br /> I never really give him the JHVA/Malfeas 'ONLY ME' ego trip thing.<br /> <br /> He's awesome enough so that stuff is self-evident without him insisting on it.<br /> <br /> In his best moments... he is the General that leads by example ; not the General that screams at you until you bow to him.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said he'll scream at you. But he's still the boss. And I doubt he'll do anything that makes anyone doubt that. He might be a very nice and persuasive boss who occassionally sees you're not doing so well, gives you a pep talk or even sends you a card. But I don't think he'll be the sort of guy who'll actually do anything that ever makes him seem truly your equal or below you. Worship and prayer are this. He'll give orders. They might be nice orders and not pretty demanding ones within the area of your expertise. But he isn't going to ask you of anything. <br /> <br /> To me that's the big crux. Prayer is usually a request. It's asking something out of the god and hoping they respond. The Sun doens't request. WHen he says something, he wants it done. And he's the boss, so it better get done. He won't smite you like Malfeas does but I severely doubt he'll present things in any fashion other than statements of what he wants rather htan a hope of soemthing you'll do.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T12:44:34-08:00","id":54149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54147#post54147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I don't think he'll be the sort of guy who'll actually do anything that ever makes him seem truly your equal or below you. Worship and prayer are this.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very western monotheistic outlook.<br /> <br /> I propose, because it'd mesh better with our 'DMV Yu-Shan' setting, that alternately prayer might be similar to small talk amongst divinities. Obviously they wouldn't insist or expect demeaning or insulting prayers, but essentially saying 'You have a nice and respectable house, may you reign for 10,000 years' isn't much more impacting than saying 'Hello' to an old friend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T12:48:54-08:00","id":54151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54149#post54149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a very western monotheistic outlook.</div> </div> </div> </div>I restate then, who does Ameterasu or Zeus worship, who are deities in similar positions? Because the idea of Zeus doing anything but telling people what to do or Ameterasu giving very polite orders is all I can come up with.<br /> <br /> The idea that other things are prayer or worship is also a Western outlook in itself, as a note, since it is in a sense co-opting other systems of religious practice into Western terms and ideas. This can get circular. So I state a definition: prayer and worship is plactating to greater powers (or supernaturlaly more capable ones) in hopes that such acts influence the action of deities or their subordinates. Under such a definition a Shinto kami might not be more powerful than me, but more competent and able to impact things I do. They also can still say no. In such a context, the Sun still has no one to prayer to, as no one can actually say no to him who matters, isn't an enemy or an Exalt.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T12:49:07-08:00","id":54152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54005#post54005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hopefully this conversation clarifies that for me as well.<br /> <br /> Please note that if you dropped Michael Jackson into the outskirts of Creation and had him dance, the effect would not be &quot;wow cool, he can dance really well.&quot; It would shake the foundations of belief. They would think he was a divine madman, surely touched by the gods. His dancing would provoke mania, fear, rage, awe. The people of Creation have never seen such movements before. They would be provoked by them. They would conclude that he was possessed by demons or by the spirits of the air and sky. If he claimed &quot;I am the representative of X god,&quot; they would be far more inclined to believe him, because he dances as if possessed.<br /> <br /> Dance, oration, singing\u2014the heart of Performance\u2014invokes the divine madman. It leads people to believe the person speaks / acts / embodies Heaven. Gods want priests who have high Performance because people think these things about people who can dance, speak passionately before large crowds, etc. This idea makes them want to listen to that person, it makes them want to believe what that person says. And if the god truly backs such a one, that person can stand in for him, run a bureaucracy and do all his temporal work while he soaks up the prayer.</div> </div> </div> </div>And were he an Abyssal, the dead would rise from their graves to dance with him, telling a tale of fear and madness... even if it was only a nightmare in the mind of one woman. (I recently rewartched the video for Thriller). His very nature would seemlessly flow from being seemingly mortal to dead (or divine)...<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually this makes me want to see an Abyssal and Solar dancing together... telling a tale of a person, living, burning bright, then their flame guttering out as they descend into death... and eventually rising again like the sun from the ashes of the East.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","user":"haren","date":".  Realized something 01-20-2014, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T12:56:52-08:00","id":54166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54151#post54151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I restate then, who does Ameterasu or Zeus worship, who are deities in similar positions? Because the idea of Zeus doing anything but telling people what to do or Ameterasu giving very polite orders is all I can come up with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering Exalted essentially lifts Chinese cosmology more than Greek or Japanese, I'd look to there for inspiration.<br /> <br /> The <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jade_Emperor\" target=\"_blank\">Jade Emperor</a> is a much closer fit for how I have always envisioned the Sun acting, with the caveat that it's a retired soldier who has earned wisdom through war and suffering to give a subtle tweak to the character.<br /> <br /> The key is to evoke an analogy for good and proper rule with the character ; to make it symbolic of what the ideal of a good monarch should be. In this respect, I feel that isolating some of these more western notions of 'God' from that idea might be productive.<br /> <br /> I don't imagine the Jade Emperor would have a big problem with saying a prayer to a noble house as a polite gesture, if only to set a proper example!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":762,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","user":"MissMaddy","date":". 01-20-2014, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T12:57:49-08:00","id":54168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54140#post54140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Brahman worship anything? Does Ameterasu? Izanagi? I'm pretty sure Zeus doesn't worship shit either. It's only Christian if you force it to be so. The Unconquered Sun by his title is that: Unconquered. The title kind of implies he kneels to no one.<br /> <br /> <br /> Do we have evidence to this? Because he's again, King of Heaven. And Creation is a setting where you can get by being the CEO who just skims off the top. Nothing has ever implied his humiltiy is to a level where he has to send token &quot;prayer&quot;. It depends greatly on how defines prayer. In most cases, they're probably &quot;Do this. I say so&quot; and that's that. When you have the Mandate of Divine Subordination, why do you ever need to pray to anyone?<br /> <br /> <br /> This doesn't seem to me to be &quot;prayer&quot; or &quot;worship&quot; but being a boss people likes. That a boss sends me a Christmas card every now and again doesn't mean he is at all treating me in the same regard as I would when I give him a gift. For him it's a token bit of motivation, not a way for me to get something I want.<br /> <br /> <br /> So are we now entirely in &quot;How i think it should be but no evidence to suppor this mode?&quot; Because as far as I can tell, he is like this about once a year at the effective Halloween/New Year/Christmas party and off being an aloof King of Heaven when it's not that.<br /> <br /> <br /> He's in charge of Heaven. If he wanted to, the buck stops at him for all purposes in Yu-Shan. He gets a cut of all ambrosia ever sent there in addition to his stuff. He had to be asked (not told, asked) to not go and kill all the Yozi along with the rest of the Neverborn. It might not be &quot;mine all mine&quot; but nothing says he has ever given a fuck to be the Best Boss Ever.<br /> <br /> <br /> And none of this mandates he have anything that at all looks like prayer or worship save a very stretched definition of the term &quot;Saying stuff in a ritual fashion to a god.' WHich still for him probably is &quot;Do this, because I'm right.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So you approach him how you would any other deity or deity-incarnate. You use proper rituals and stuff or he'll ignore you. I think most of the time he does that: not pay attention since folks presetn things not worth his time or effort hwen he has an entire Celestial Bureaucracy that is supposed to handle the petty shit for him.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just for point of clarification, it's canon that the Unconquered Sun collects a bit of prayer from everybody, then redistributes it as prayer welfare to the poorest gods. Even if he is not, personally, praying, he's guiding and redirecting prayer to those who need it in a goodly and efficient manner. I see no reason why a Zenith shouldn't be able to similarly able to guide, enhance, or even redistribute prayer, if you're just trying to fit the theme of them being the chosen of the Unconquered Sun, rather than concentrating on the more salient theme of them being paragons of human perfection taken to inhuman levels.<br /> <br /> Prayer is literally money in heaven. I don't see why it would be inappropriate for Zeniths to be able to tamper with, manipulate, or augment these revenue streams since that's what their patron already does. And, that aside, I don't see why they shouldn't be able to manipulate their own Cult-based revenue streams to game bigger short-term benefits by putting in some effort, or other things built on the idea of yourself getting worshiped.<br /> <br /> A prayer charm doesn't necessarily mean a Zenith is personally submitting and supplicating themselves before a deity. It means they are, in some way, manipulating the flow of belief, prayer, and ritual that is literally both nourishment and money to spiritual beings, and a steady trickle of essence and willpower to exalted beings. Since Performance has always been the Ability that governed prayer, and every edition up to this point had actual rules - crappy ones, often, but ones that existed - for prayer, it seems obvious that these social controls of prayer streams would be in the Performance charm tree.<br /> <br /> I think that one of the big problems with this discussion is that we collectively have a very different idea of what prayer means. I, and a few others, are looking at it more in terms of guiding and manipulating acts of worship which can be used as bribery, threats to cut off revenue sources, and personal empowerment by an exalt with the right skills at public speaking for sermons, singing for hymns, and other acts of guiding worship. You, I believe - and please do correct me if I'm wrong - see it more in terms of supplication, giving yourself over to the will of a deity, and other acts of begging performed in displays of personal purity of faith.<br /> <br /> We're talking about entirely different things, but both calling it 'prayer.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T13:03:28-08:00","id":54171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54152#post54152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And were he an Abyssal, the dead would rise from their graves to dance with him, telling a tale of fear and madness... even if it was only a nightmare in the mind of one woman. (I recently rewartched the video for Thriller). His very nature would seemlessly flow from being seemingly mortal to dead (or divine)...<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually this makes me want to see an Abyssal and Solar dancing together... telling a tale of a person, living, burning bright, then their flame guttering out as they descend into death... and eventually rising again like the sun from the ashes of the East.</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me of the best canonical Zenith.<br /> Bittersea Blackfalcon!<br /> John can we get her back in 3e? Oh please! Please! Please! Please!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T13:19:19-08:00","id":54184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagadaishio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54168#post54168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just for point of clarification, it's canon that the Unconquered Sun collects a bit of prayer from everybody, then redistributes it as prayer welfare to the poorest gods. Even if he is not, personally, praying, he's guiding and redirecting prayer to those who need it in a goodly and efficient manner. I see no reason why a Zenith shouldn't be able to similarly able to guide, enhance, or even redistribute prayer, if you're just trying to fit the theme of them being the chosen of the Unconquered Sun, rather than concentrating on the more salient theme of them being paragons of human perfection taken to inhuman levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>That prayer wellfare is produced as quintessence and ambrosia spewing out of fountains. I doub thter's any ritual that is concerned at that point other than mechanisms which move the stuff around. Prayer after it is generated is stuff that you move around physically, and as I can gather, no act is needed to perpetuate this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagadaishio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54168#post54168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prayer is literally money in heaven. I don't see why it would be inappropriate for Zeniths to be able to tamper with, manipulate, or augment these revenue streams since that's what their patron already does. And, that aside, I don't see why they shouldn't be able to manipulate their own Cult-based revenue streams to game bigger short-term benefits by putting in some effort, or other things built on the idea of yourself getting worshiped.<br /> <br /> A prayer charm doesn't necessarily mean a Zenith is personally submitting and supplicating themselves before a deity. It means they are, in some way, manipulating the flow of belief, prayer, and ritual that is literally both nourishment and money to spiritual beings, and a steady trickle of essence and willpower to exalted beings. Since Performance has always been the Ability that governed prayer, and every edition up to this point had actual rules - crappy ones, often, but ones that existed - for prayer, it seems obvious that these social controls of prayer streams would be in the Performance charm tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see issues with this either. It's what I've been mostly advocating for Solar Performance stuff that impacts prayers: make it so that Solar-led worship is so good that you want it more than some other potential priest can give you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagadaishio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54168#post54168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that one of the big problems with this discussion is that we collectively have a very different idea of what prayer means. I, and a few others, are looking at it more in terms of guiding and manipulating acts of worship which can be used as bribery, threats to cut off revenue sources, and personal empowerment by an exalt with the right skills at public speaking for sermons, singing for hymns, and other acts of guiding worship. You, I believe - and please do correct me if I'm wrong - see it more in terms of supplication, giving yourself over to the will of a deity, and other acts of begging performed in displays of personal purity of faith.<br /> <br /> We're talking about entirely different things, but both calling it 'prayer.'</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, the acts of prayer and worship are supplication and requests. This is how it appears to be in the setting too. When humans pray to something, it is submisssion in some form. When ghosts pray, they pray to ancestors. When gods pray, they pray to superiors. Stuff like that. Prayer requires certain acts and actions which put the deity in an elevated station.<br /> <br /> The results of that prayer, ambrosia and quintessence, are things that move around and are traded for and bargained. I thin, the big disconnect I'm having here is that I see it that prayer is the generative act of the substance gods wnat. And that method of generation is something I don't see a deity like the Unconqured Sun going out of his way to do.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T13:28:11-08:00","id":54198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54130#post54130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does he BOW TO NONE??!?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The Unconquered Sun is highest in Heaven. He prays to no one.<br /> <br /> Nor does the Sun peel onions, but your Solar is free to be onion king.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T13:30:14-08:00","id":54199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54166#post54166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering Exalted essentially lifts Chinese cosmology more than Greek or Japanese, I'd look to there for inspiration.<br /> <br /> The <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jade_Emperor\" target=\"_blank\">Jade Emperor</a> is a much closer fit for how I have always envisioned the Sun acting, with the caveat that it's a retired soldier who has earned wisdom through war and suffering to give a subtle tweak to the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted <i>also</i> draws on <i>Paradise Lost</i> and the Greek Titanomachy. The latter of which also includes the ruler of the gods usurping his superiors and being left with no other being capable of challenging him anymore. Zeus is king of Olympus. His creators are dead or imprisoned. No other god can overpower him. Any other being is an enemy or not worth his time. Zeus worships no one.<br /> <br /> The Sun indeed to some extent draws on the Jade Emporer. He's not an ass, and he's probably one of the most benevolent and competent rulers of the universe in most fantasy pantheons. But he is also an amalgation with Zeus, Indra, Huizilopochtli and Izanagi, among probably a bunch of other stuff. And saying he is X and so extending everything based solely on X to me misses out on ptoential nuance and is putting a positon of what he &quot;should be&quot; that is not going to ever line up with what in the end authors will probably make him actually be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54166#post54166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The key is to evoke an analogy for good and proper rule with the character ; to make it symbolic of what the ideal of a good monarch should be. In this respect, I feel that isolating some of these more western notions of 'God' from that idea might be productive.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be noted by some accounts, the Unconquered Sun is a failure in this regard. As a ruler he has been too hands off, to passive and probably too thinking people knowing what they are doing. Even if he tells people to do stuff and expects such edicts to happen doesn' tmean they will. And it should be noted that in the end he led a coup, whcih itself brings into question in some regards his righteousness in comparison to the Jade Emperor and historic Chinese political philosophy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54166#post54166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't imagine the Jade Emperor would have a big problem with saying a prayer to a noble house as a polite gesture, if only to set a proper example!</div> </div> </div> </div>Then again, I can see some of his other inspirations (Zeus and Indra and Amaterasu being the big ones here) not really ever going out of their way to acknowledge folks for doing wha thtey were told to do in the first place.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T13:46:15-08:00","id":54211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54145#post54145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if you ascribe a definition of &quot;faith&quot; which is some ambiguous force that can do shit like people here on Earth seem to think it is in regards to religion and magic. It doens't make you a fool unless you buy into some idea that you are given a mandate that your actions are ordained by god, in effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? It doesn't make you a fool unless you think it's actually meaningful (i.e. that's there's something behind it)? Are we even speaking the same language here?<br /> <br /> Loyalty to and Adoration of the Unconquered Sun should mean more than Loyalty to and Adoration of Bobinius, the king I served when I was a mortal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;If I believe hard enough it'll be true&quot; is not how Creation works. There's no willworking. There's no Tinkerbells about. Gods don't have some key to their domains that if you poke at htem hard enough unlock things. Gods can influence their domain. If you convince them, they might do so in a way they like. If not, too bad. Being a priest in Creation is being the frontman of the god's cult. Or in other words, his official middleman. There's no mojo that faith has access to that lets you somehow get gods to do what youw ant i fthey don't want to do it. Because Exalted doesn't appear to run on an idea that faith is anything special like that. </div> </div> </div>It's called an Exaltation. A Solar already has the power of the Unconquered Sun and actually? Yes, through sheer heroic willpower they can work miracles. That's how Solars *work*. That's what they *are*. That's why some Charms have (had? probably will remain have) willpower costs.<br /> <br /> In a setting where prayer generates real, measurable quantities of mystical mojo (*points to the Cult background*) and faith is thus literally powerful?<br /> <br /> This set of ideas has nothing to do with the gods anymore, it's about the Zenith and his flock being more powerful because their faith empowers him (like Cult, but turned up to 11, because turning things up to eleven is what Solars do)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How so? And what would that be that doens't just turn Performance and prayer into freeform mojo stuff? I woudl argue that the similar effect is getting a cult that super-charges the god to maybe get a lot out of that prayer. True believers hwo feed your worship a lot in their fervent ritual. It's a carrot that might encourage a god to do things in a way you might like. But the god might just be an exploitive ass still too. </div> </div> </div>Sod the gods. &quot;I am the hand of the Sun upon Creation, and in his name, I cast these unclean spirits out&quot; as it's own distinct banishing Charm, rather than just a stunt for the standard Occult based stuff. I'd suggest that it get bonuses to the relevant rolls based on how many people you have there, how strongly they believe in you, and whether or not you do so in a ritual form (i.e. Performance, because the belief of the crowd is a fuel source). Probably also a similar healing Charm, that is different (not strictly better or worse) when compared to Medicine Charms (I'd suggest that it be less &quot;spammable&quot; - that is, higher costs and more set-up required - but a little more flexible)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hero Rides Away plays on genre conceits that are felt appropriate by an author. Gods answering prayers based on their personal biases and whims is also a genre conceit that the idea of &quot;faith is magic world-influency stuff&quot; some religions hold doens't fit with.<br /> <br /> <br /> Depends on how much you are turning raw Solar Essence into healing bits. But seeing as the world runs on Essence, not faith or belief, I am not sure what you get out of faith healing besides maybe a friendly god. I mean, technically summoning a stomach bottle bug is also a form fo faith healing if you really want to give a few chants to it now and again. </div> </div> </div>Prayers generate Essence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Depending on your religion, an exorcist is just a scholar/healer. Omyoujis and other forms fo Taoists come to mind. THose changs, prayers, summons and scriptures? All are being used to channel ki and get the world to work in a way. That's Lore and Occult. They're mantras that channel stuff, not explications of faith. I would imagine most exorcists in Creation follow this then some &quot;true believer&quot; thing. </div> </div> </div>Uh huh. I'm sure most of those exorcists totally hold the belief that all the prayers, summons and scripture are complete bunk that they just do because it's a handy way to focus your mind in the right pattern. That sounds totally sensible and not at all ridiculous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This seems able to be done by having powerful intimacies built on faith of you or your proxy. You don't need fancy fate shit to do this, just hyper-powered charisma and ability to get folks to follow you. Faith is actually just window dressing to this I feel. </div> </div> </div>Hyper-powered charisma will get people to follow you, yes. Having this be a thing that is *useful* requires more than just hyper-powered charisma. A bunch of untrained unskilled mortals is pretty much a net drain on your resources, however loyal. If they believe in you, pray when you tell them to pray... those glorified essence converters are suddenly doing something *useful*.<br /> <br /> A Dawn uses War to turn their useless mortal followers into killing machines. A Twilight uses Lore to turn their useless mortal followers into savants. A Zenith should be able to use Performance to turn their faith into a tide of Quintessence-fueled miracles. (always assuming they have the right Charms, of course)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why should it? I feel that if you try too hard to force it it starts pushing into genres or thematics Exalted never really bothered to give a shit before and I dont' see a benefit of giving a shit about now. It goes with a very cynical view of religion and worhsip of gods. Since ever. Having more &quot;genuine&quot; faith feels kind of antithetical to a bit of the wants Exalted does iwth religoin and cults. Citing source material, Flat Earth does just fine and interesting stuff with temples worhsipping gods who don't care and priests using charisma and training to keep being pwoerful and getting what they want.<br /> <br /> And stuff. </div> </div> </div>I think &quot;prayer batteries&quot; is pretty cynical, but it feels less pointless if you have some &quot;electronic&quot; toys to plug into the batteries.<br /> Also, frankly, the overwhelming cynicism of 2e sucked the fun and joy out of being a Solar. Cynicism is not, in fact, fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T13:48:41-08:00","id":54214,"title":"","content":"Already wrote this in the Performance vs. Presence thread, but since it's relevant to the topic and since it looks like you're still reading this one, Morke...<br /> <br /> I want Presence to be about leadership and command, and Performance to be about emotion.<br /> <br /> Presence is about telling someone what to do. You can bark an order and the new recruits will obey and hold the line. You can whisper a threat your prisoner will tell you the location of the rebel base. You can demand that the other guy surrender or retreat, or that the king hear out the list of grievances you against his vizier instead of just throwing you out of the court. They'll do what you say, but you don't get to decide how they feel about it. Presence without another social skill to back it up can inspire respect and loyalty if things are going well...but if following your orders isn't working out well it can lead to mere obedience and simmering resentment.<br /> <br /> Performance is about telling someone how to feel. You can play music that breaks someone's heart or inspires love, or you can tell a joke that has the whole tavern laughing, or you can dance a dance so seductive that anyone who sees it starts to fall in love with you. Now, you don't get to decide what they do about those feelings: if your sonnet made the prince fall in love with you, he gets to decide whether to court you or have you kidnapped for his seraglio or whether to not act on his love because what he wants is less important than the political marriage he needs to make for the good of his city. His course of action is up to him, but he can't be a witness to your performance and NOT feel the love (or hate or grief or whatever emotional context you gave to the performance) you were trying to inspire.<br /> <br /> Now, as you can see, the two go together like peanut butter and chocolate. If you invest in both, you'll be way better at dealing with other humans.<br /> <br /> Note also: I want Performances to be rife with unintended consequences that make for good stories. If a PC singer is bandying about kickass supernatural melodies, she needs to worry about the Phantom of the Opera falling for her. If a PC is a poet, politicians will try to get her into their courts and writing complimentary things they can distribute. Princes will try to get you to write love songs to help them seduce their lovers, and then try to murder you when their lovers fall for you instead of the Prince. Your song inspiring the peasants to fury about their oppression might spark a riot, but unless you've got some Presence to back it up that riot is gonna be directionless fury and you might even get caught up in it. Your poem about the cruelties of slavery will make the Guildsman feel remorse...but he might commit suicide instead of freeing the slaves like you wanted. I want Performance to move people, but not always predictably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T14:18:19-08:00","id":54228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54211#post54211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? It doesn't make you a fool unless you think it's actually meaningful (i.e. that's there's something behind it)? Are we even speaking the same language here?<br /> <br /> Loyalty to and Adoration of the Unconquered Sun should mean more than Loyalty to and Adoration of Bobinius, the king I served when I was a mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? You have your power. You have carte blanch to use it how you will. The Sun is no different than your old king besdies being more personally powerful. Gods in Creation might be a different sort of being but in the end they're more powerful people. If I served my king unto what you expect out of a god, then I would be consdiered loyal and naive. Nothing on the nature of him being a god a priori means I should a priori have a different sort of loyalty to him than any other ruler or commander or granter of power. That assumption to me is simply nothing more than a statement of preference than a nominal should.<br /> <br /> So I guess let me then rephrase. You probably are a fool if you go whole hog with such an attitude, since I think part of the point of your Exaltation is you do the work yourself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54211#post54211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's called an Exaltation. A Solar already has the power of the Unconquered Sun and actually? Yes, through sheer heroic willpower they can work miracles. That's how Solars *work*. That's what they *are*. That's why some Charms have (had? probably will remain have) willpower costs.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't go around willworking the world. Creation isn't some Twilight Zone show where if you will hard enough wheels show up on your plane and it can land. Solars use <i>skill</i> and sometimes tap into strenght of will to express this skill through the themes of their deity, the Unconquered Sun. Using stats on the character sheet simply shows some things take more effort, but willpower the thing of drive and Willpower the trait are ambiguous at best. And again, even if I worshipped all I wanted wheels don't show up on my plane.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54211#post54211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a setting where prayer generates real, measurable quantities of mystical mojo (*points to the Cult background*) and faith is thus literally powerful?</div> </div> </div> </div>Prayer and faith are resource generators for stuff that's useful. Note that quintessence and ambrosia are quiessence, they don't do anything, until someone with skill does something with them. Or they're eaten due to being delicious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54211#post54211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This set of ideas has nothing to do with the gods anymore, it's about the Zenith and his flock being more powerful because their faith empowers him (like Cult, but turned up to 11, because turning things up to eleven is what Solars do)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is usually equated to more of the results of prayer: ambrosia and quintessence. It gives you resources to work with and Essence and willpower to fuel yourself more with. Solars probably have some of the most effecient cults in Creation for this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54211#post54211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sod the gods. &quot;I am the hand of the Sun upon Creation, and in his name, I cast these unclean spirits out&quot; as it's own distinct banishing Charm, rather than just a stunt for the standard Occult based stuff. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars probably have more powerful generic Occult stuff. Or sorcery. That will have their own mantras and declarations calling upon the Five Directions, Four Seas or whatever just fine. But in the end, it probably is mostly stunt fodder. See again the priest who can do the neat religious stuff and mantras and also is a corrupt fucker, which is laso in-genre and not doable if genuine faith meant something. You can have your true believers and you can have your atheists like Nobunaga or Caesar who still do stuff because that's the way shit gets done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54211#post54211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I'd suggest that it get bonuses to the relevant rolls based on how many people you have there, how strongly they believe in you, and whether or not you do so in a ritual form (i.e. Performance, because the belief of the crowd is a fuel source). Probably also a similar healing Charm, that is different (not strictly better or worse) when compared to Medicine Charms (I'd suggest that it be less &quot;spammable&quot; - that is, higher costs and more set-up required - but a little more flexible)</div> </div> </div> </div>Or it could be simpler and just be a stunt. Seems a bit less clunky a way to deal with soemthing that I question as to whether it is even genre appropriate or running on some view of faith as an elevated state that for some reason needs to be made more specialer in context of the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54211#post54211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prayers generate Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>So do manses. Prayers do it pretty effectively though apparently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54211#post54211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh huh. I'm sure most of those exorcists totally hold the belief that all the prayers, summons and scripture are complete bunk that they just do because it's a handy way to focus your mind in the right pattern. That sounds totally sensible and not at all ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the presentation. I've seen a few interesting anime, for instnace, try to &quot;science&quot; some of the effects. One series right now I enjoy is <i>Tokyo Ravens</i>, which does go a bit too magitechy for Exalted but also runs with an idea that Omyouji stuff seems to run on both mastery of key and knoweldge of spells. As I noted earlier, even in antiquity you had people who probably didn't believe in the actual menaing of rituals (Julius Caesar gets called out on this a bit osmetimes) but still did them. So yes, they probably are in the end handy ways that get patterns going. It's why Solars are great at it: they're the best god-damend Performers between Heaven and Earth, so will be able to get the best out of the rituals and actions as needed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54211#post54211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hyper-powered charisma will get people to follow you, yes. Having this be a thing that is *useful* requires more than just hyper-powered charisma. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Masses of followers seem useful to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54211#post54211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... A bunch of untrained unskilled mortals is pretty much a net drain on your resources, however loyal. If they believe in you, pray when you tell them to pray... those glorified essence converters are suddenly doing something *useful*.</div> </div> </div> </div>Them beholden to your cult lets them bein place for other things. Like indoctrination. Elation (making your sermons feel good could be up there I guess). It is also a group that is an easy to target population for Tiger Warrior Training Technique and similar effects. Their faith is a good foundation to make your Fremen horde if you want. You have to actually be able to raise a Fremen horde though. A lot of believing really hard isn't going to get you that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54211#post54211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Dawn uses War to turn their useless mortal followers into killing machines. A Twilight uses Lore to turn their useless mortal followers into savants. A Zenith should be able to use Performance to turn their faith into a tide of Quintessence-fueled miracles. (always assuming they have the right Charms, of course)</div> </div> </div> </div>If &quot;quintessence-fueled miracle&quot; was a thing that existed in Creation that'd be one thing. It isn't. Quintessence is stuff that you make things out of. It requires people who know how to make things out of stuff or turn it into fuel for doing other stuff. Quintessence is liked because you can make more or less anything from it. I would argue a Solar probably is liked by a god since his cultists are going to be able to get the most out of it. And such a god would probably then be incentivized to give a little bit back to these obviously &quot;favored' worshippers. Because religion in Exalted is an economic thing, not some special statement of faith.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54211#post54211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think &quot;prayer batteries&quot; is pretty cynical, but it feels less pointless if you have some &quot;electronic&quot; toys to plug into the batteries.<br /> Also, frankly, the overwhelming cynicism of 2e sucked the fun and joy out of being a Solar. Cynicism is not, in fact, fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not being cynical, I should note. I just think that making faith some special super juice to get what you want out of it is stupid in the real world and not something I really see working in Exalted as it has historiclaly been presented either.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T15:04:05-08:00","id":54245,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I hate to continue with the prayer digression, but here is a thing that the discussion made me realize. I was envisioning a Zenith who leads the people in prayer of his favoured gods, either out of piousness or for leverage, and I'm thinking, this is a hugely important thing in the game world, but it feels like I'm just showboating for flavour if I do that, and why is that? Part of the problem with prayer, and why I think people (myself included) are clinging to what mechanics and effects we've seen for it in previous editions, is that it's really hard to envision what it <i>does.</i><br /> <br /> Gods want prayer, and the game largely uses an &quot;income model&quot; to represent this, but unlike real income, players can't relate to prayer income at all, so there's no real sense of what it <i>means</i> if a god gets more or less prayer. Like, if a god loses 25% of their prayer, clearly they're going to be angry and worried, but is that an existential threat? Is it like with money where suddenly you're end up living way beyond your means because you can't unspool your expenses quickly enough? Gods don't need food or shelter, and aside from &quot;powering charms&quot; it's hard to know what they actually <i>do</i> with their prayer outlay, so it's very hard to connect this sort of thing to a real outcome. You could cross-reference Ambrosia and mote-regeneration rules against divine statblocks and plot out budgets and expenses and try to extrapolate from there, but I'm sure no writer has ever done that, so it's not going to necessarily produce good results.<br /> <br /> To someone with a congregation, the main value of prayer is leverage, but the fuzziness of it really complicates that from a player's perspective, because you know a god wants as much prayer as possible but you don't really have a handle on what it <i>means</i> if you can offer or threaten a source of worship. From a business perspective, you can't get within an order of magnitude of their <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Best_alternative_to_a_negotiated_agreement\" target=\"_blank\">BATNA</a> unless you roll some dice and ask the ST to tell you, and that puts a lot of pressure on the ST, because they don't have any idea either.<br /> <br /> I don't know what the solution to this is, really. The best I can think of is to give some idea of what kind of Cult rating a god needs to sustain a particular lifestyle, and that's pretty handwavey and unsatisfying, not to mention that it'd be a bit esoteric for any book that's not focused on gods. But I do think this helps to explain why people are grasping for prayer mechanics and charms to an extent that they wouldn't for, say, food or money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 01-20-2014, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T15:20:01-08:00","id":54255,"title":"","content":"Yeah, didn't realize the prayer stuff was gonna explode like this for tens of pages. Sorry John.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T15:29:59-08:00","id":54259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54005#post54005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hopefully this conversation clarifies that for me as well.<br /> <br /> Please note that if you dropped Michael Jackson into the outskirts of Creation and had him dance, the effect would not be &quot;wow cool, he can dance really well.&quot; It would shake the foundations of belief. They would think he was a divine madman, surely touched by the gods. His dancing would provoke mania, fear, rage, awe. The people of Creation have never seen such movements before. They would be provoked by them. They would conclude that he was possessed by demons or by the spirits of the air and sky. If he claimed &quot;I am the representative of X god,&quot; they would be far more inclined to believe him, because he dances as if possessed.<br /> <br /> Dance, oration, singing\u2014the heart of Performance\u2014invokes the divine madman. It leads people to believe the person speaks / acts / embodies Heaven. Gods want priests who have high Performance because people think these things about people who can dance, speak passionately before large crowds, etc. This idea makes them want to listen to that person, it makes them want to believe what that person says. And if the god truly backs such a one, that person can stand in for him, run a bureaucracy and do all his temporal work while he soaks up the prayer.</div> </div> </div> </div>After mulling this over most of the day, I was checking the thread to see if I could contribute my thoughts here...<br /> <br /> ...but, John gets it, so I'm content. Continue on as you are, good sir, and I shall subscribe to your proverbial newsletter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T15:56:00-08:00","id":54281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54255#post54255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, didn't realize the prayer stuff was gonna explode like this for tens of pages. Sorry John.</div> </div> </div> </div>In all fairness, he not only asked, he spent about as many words on the conversation as anyone. I'm not sure how much apology is called for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T15:57:16-08:00","id":54284,"title":"","content":"By no means am I an expert on Chinese culture and mythology. My knowledge comes from being Chinese. But given that the debate surrounding prayer, the Celestial Bureaucracy, and Jade Emperor as a comparison to Sol, I figured I'd chime in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54198#post54198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. The Unconquered Sun is highest in Heaven. He prays to no one.<br /> <br /> Nor does the Sun peel onions, but your Solar is free to be onion king.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This. Very much this.<br /> <br /> In Chinese culture, something like praying or bowing is only done by a subordinate to their superior. Full stop. Even in modern day China, you'd still see the same thing. I don't think you'd ever see a superior bow to their subordinate if they worked in the same company. The lower ranking employee is always the one who does it, it's a demonstration of respect to someone more powerful than you. And even when you have a situation where two people are bowing to each other, the person bowing more deeply is acknowledging that the other person is their superior. This happens quite a bit in the business world.<br /> <br /> So no, the UCS would never ever pray or bow to anyone. It's virtually unheard of for the Chinese Emperors to do so, and since Heaven structure bares an uncanny resemblance to the Earthly one, the Jade Emperor would never be expected to bow his head, unless it was to the three Pure Ones but that's because they are superior to him. The only situations I could possibly expect a Chinese Emperor, Divine or not, to ever bow their head is either to someone who conquered them OR the person they are bowing to did a service so grand, so epic, that it thoroughly moved the Emperor to show that level of respect. In which case it would be expected that every one else present in the room would have to bow their heads even lower than the Emperor, because of positions of power and so on.<br /> <br /> Now, if we're talking about Prayer as in Ambrosia, then yea maybe the UCS would hand it out, but it'd be the equivalent of handing out lucky money and you bet that the recipient would be groveling for all they're worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/723-talam","name":"Talam","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T16:18:23-08:00","id":54300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54284#post54284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, if we're talking about prayer as in Ambrosia, then yeah, maybe the Unconquered Sun would hand it out, but it'd be the equivalent of handing out lucky money and you bet that the recipient would be groveling for all they're worth.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's lucky money?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T16:37:06-08:00","id":54312,"title":"","content":"I agree with a previous poster in that we seem to be running up against a lack of a consensus of what prayer is.<br /> <br /> Is prayer a respectful 'thank you'? Or is it a symbolic kowtow?<br /> <br /> I'd definitely agree that I don't see the sun deeply bowing to anybody, but again, I can definitely see him signing an honorary prayer strip that says 'This Octopus Goddess Make The Fuckin' Best Ambrosia Stew I Ever Ate And She Fuckin' Rocks' and giving it a big golden lipstick kiss before moving on.<br /> <br /> I agree that the Sun wouldn't ever really suggest via his actions that he was inferior or subservient.<br /> <br /> He might sing a psalm or two if he was a bit drunk or in a good mood, though, and I bet those marks of esteem are highly regarded amongst the elite.<br /> <br /> Heck, I might imagine even a few rare humble individuals who most feel 'don't deserve it' have earned a few of these rare prayers...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T16:43:53-08:00","id":54319,"title":"","content":"See and to me there's no assumption he goes around spouting random poetry or prayers. The aformentioned thanks letter? It's not a prayer. It's probably a letter actually sent with a bit of his own ambrosia tied to it.<br /> <br /> That's the hang-up, again. To me, prayer is the thing that generates the magic makey stuff. The Sun has plenty of that to go around that he can send swank memos and recommendations and gifts without it having to be tied up in the magic stuff generaiton mechanism. I consider prayer the action that generates the important stuff, not the actual stuff bieng passed around.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T16:47:32-08:00","id":54321,"title":"","content":"The infamous red envelope, it's a tradition of giving out a talisman to provide good luck and ward off evils spirits. Usually given out to children, unmarried people and at weddings, and I know the amount is supposed to end in a even digit. Happens at weddings and New Years that I know of/have experienced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/841-okamigrif","name":"Okamigrif","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T16:56:02-08:00","id":54326,"title":"","content":"A Prayer is &quot;You have the power to Help me/Give me/leave me and mine alone&quot;<br /> <br /> A Praise is &quot;You are Awesome (that is, inspiring Awe), and worthy of my Respect/Adoration/worship&quot;<br /> <br /> Most prayers probably include Praises, but I can't see the UCS bothering with them. Occasionally handing out a little Praise? That I can see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T17:35:21-08:00","id":54346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54005#post54005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please note that if you dropped Michael Jackson into the outskirts of Creation and had him dance, the effect would not be &quot;wow cool, he can dance really well.&quot; It would shake the foundations of belief. They would think he was a divine madman, surely touched by the gods. His dancing would provoke mania, fear, rage, awe. The people of Creation have never seen such movements before. They would be provoked by them. They would conclude that he was possessed by demons or by the spirits of the air and sky. If he claimed &quot;I am the representative of X god,&quot; they would be far more inclined to believe him, because he dances as if possessed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then, should Solar Performance have a Charm that allows a nearby spirit to possess him as he sings and/or dances?<br /> <br /> The spirit is already present, so &quot;prayers aren't heard&quot; is preserved. In the previous two Editions and presumably the next, most spirits won't have any of the Possession Charms that would let them enter into a willing or unwilling host.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T17:39:13-08:00","id":54349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okamigrif</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54321#post54321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The infamous red envelope, it's a tradition of giving out a talisman to provide good luck and ward off evils spirits. Usually given out to children, unmarried people and at weddings, and I know the amount is supposed to end in a even digit. Happens at weddings and New Years that I know of/have experienced.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually usually supposed to end in an 8, not just any even digit. Because 4, 14 and 44 are even, but 4 and 10 are kind of bad numbers. Usually, 8, 28, 88 and 128 are the numbers you're looking at because 8 symbolizes wealth and infinity, and 28 kind of translates to &quot;Great Wealth&quot;.<br /> <br /> Anyways, it wouldn't surprise me if the UCS was like &quot;That was pretty good what you did, here's a little bonus&quot; and handed a little packet of Ambrosia, which I thought was generated from prayers. The act of praying and offering prayer is I believe different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/723-talam","name":"Talam","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T18:16:44-08:00","id":54366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54137#post54137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Solar Medicine Charms are very obviously based on faith healing. This might change in Ex3, but it's unlikely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure every Medicine charm in Ex2 turn you into super doctor/herbalist and not DnD Priest, the only exception is Contagion-Curing Touch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Medicine Charms generally supplement or replace the normal dramatic action for medical treatment (see p. 137). Solar physicians use ordinary techniques rather than \u201chealing magic\u201d\u2014herbal remedies, dressing wounds, splinting broken legs, personal inspiration and the like. Medical supplies are necessary unless otherwise stated. Experienced Solar physicians can master Combos that approximate healing with a touch, but the core of their talents is actual medical skill. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T18:19:18-08:00","id":54368,"title":"","content":"No, they could also YELL at you until you healed, stare at you until you healed, do a grand invocation that healed you, etc. etc. Their options got VAST about two Charms into the tree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T18:28:11-08:00","id":54374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54368#post54368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they could also YELL at you until you healed, stare at you until you healed, do a grand invocation that healed you, etc. etc. Their options got VAST about two Charms into the tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even when they're yelling at you, they're using their masterful knowledge of medicine to understand how a precisely modulated shout can work on your body to produce the desired result.<br /> <br /> They're <i>not </i>just wishing you well really really hard or asking some outside power to heal you, which is what &quot;faith healing&quot; would be all about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T18:31:36-08:00","id":54377,"title":"","content":"When one of the given methods they can use is <i>staring at you to heal you</i>, or inspiring you with words, without a touch, it goes beyond mortal power. It is <i>magic</i> that they know, 100% will work. To them, it's an expression of Essence through Charms and magic that they know works. To <i>you</i>, or anyone else watching, it's faith healing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T18:33:59-08:00","id":54378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54366#post54366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure every Medicine charm in Ex2 turn you into super doctor/herbalist and not DnD Priest, the only exception is Contagion-Curing Touch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Curing leprosy, giving sight to the blind and healing the limbs of the crippled are the basics of the tree, while Contagion-Curing Touch is the capstone. Once you've got that, you've completed your transformation into Jesus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T18:39:44-08:00","id":54381,"title":"","content":"Not quite. You still can't raise the dead, but it's close.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T18:43:00-08:00","id":54384,"title":"","content":"There is a big problem with this discussion. Everyone is using their own definition of prayer to justify their position, most aren't even close to what prayer is in Exalted.<br /> <br /> In Abyssals it makes references to prayers used to threaten and intimidate both gods and ghosts including at least one charm that actually makes use of the Prayer Action. This clearly indicated that prayer is not an act of supplication or even begging by definition. Prayer is exactly one thing a method of communicating with a being capable of hearing prayers that provides a Cult rating. Any other definition is not at all useful to this discussion. <br /> <br /> Under this definition the most obvious charm is in fact, the being I'm praying to cannot ignore me if capable of hearing my prayer. I fact Abyssals currently get exactly that as part of a charm.<br /> <br /> So long as we get clear guidelines of what spirits can and can't do right out of the core book, I'm cool with prayer providing no direct benefit because ST's would have enough to make it up on their own. In which case keep prayer charms about manipulating the communication with spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T18:45:39-08:00","id":54386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54377#post54377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When one of the given methods they can use is <i>staring at you to heal you</i>, or inspiring you with words, without a touch, it goes beyond mortal power. It is <i>magic</i> that they know, 100% will work. To them, it's an expression of Essence through Charms and magic that they know works. To <i>you</i>, or anyone else watching, it's faith healing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't matter what the people watching think, because their perception does not change the reality.<br /> <br /> And the reality is that the Solar is operating by knowledge, not faith. If absolutely surety of your ability was faith, then all of the attack abilities belong to Zeniths because they have absolute faith that they will defeat their enemies through force of arms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T18:54:30-08:00","id":54392,"title":"","content":"... Okay, explain to me exactly what knowledge the Solar is operating on that allows them to <i>regenerate limbs</i>, <i>cure cancer</i>, and <i>regrow hearts</i> by talking to someone. It's fucking magic. It's Biblical magic, man. They are doing something <i>impossible by mortal means</i> sheerly through the use of magic and divine power, and you don't call that <i>faith healing?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T18:58:08-08:00","id":54395,"title":"","content":"Hell, to put it another way, any time a Cleric casts Cure Light Wounds in D&amp;D, it's visible faith healing, and you're saying a Solar in full-on super-healer mode is somehow <i>less</i> <i>involved </i>than that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T19:08:55-08:00","id":54401,"title":"","content":"It seems to be the old &quot;faith versus knowledge&quot; thing I see in other areas. Where faith is belief in something, regardless of evidence. Healing with Medicine is healing because of how the Solar doctor knows how a person can be put together right (their Ability in Medicine) and how to arrange their Solar-flavored Essence to achieve that via their skills (Solar Exalted expression through knowledge and implementation of skill).<br /> <br /> Faith healing is healing despite knowing what goes on. It's as I gather defined by using hope mojo to get stuff going an being ignorant of the process, just that divine will made it happen. <br /> <br /> The issue with this for Solars is a fewfold:<br /> <br /> - It means the Solar is getting things done by having someone else do it for them. Solar Exalted the Exalts who are peerless at acts of skill. Healing people is an act of Medical skill and the Solar who wants to do that already has a blazing miracle burning in their soul to go and do that without having to go ask a god to do it for them.<br /> <br /> - It turns Performance and prayer into a catch-all power, since apparently you can just beg the right god hard enough and they'll do shit for you, rather than use your god-given supreme agency to do it your damned self better.<br /> <br /> - A bit with above, the god you got power from and represent is the boss. You don't go about asking gods to heal things because of faith in them. You tell them to do them because you represent their boss.<br /> <br /> - It assumes &quot;faith&quot; on itself is menaingful at all. That it has some nice mojo to it that there's something valuable in it inherently. Which has never been the case in Exalted. Cults are described oftentimes as more or less protection rackets or acts of corruption. The Immaculate calendar exists as a bargaining chip. Prayer isn't soemthing that's valuable other then the sense it grants gods power and genereates stuff they want. Just in the same way a steady flow of money does for mortals. Prayer is a resource which gods use to get what they want. It's currency, not some magic compulsion. And gods, like any other potential bully or politican, are free often to just pocket the money and do nothing anyhow in response. It's no power over gods anymore than bribe money is to politicans.<br /> <br /> So for me, that &quot;faith healing&quot; isn't anything more than a fluff is an &quot;of course that's what it is.&quot; It's either you as a Solar using your inherent knowledge to make people pray to you more, or it is you using your bribes with gods who do that sort of thing to maybe do it for you. But ambiguous &quot;faith heals&quot; things are just not how Exalted's metaphysics appear to work. Faith is nothing but a tool, not some special mojo fairy that exists as long as you believe in it real hard.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T19:08:58-08:00","id":54402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54378#post54378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Curing leprosy, giving sight to the blind and healing the limbs of the crippled are the basics of the tree, while Contagion-Curing Touch is the capstone. Once you've got that, you've completed your transformation into Jesus.</div> </div> </div> </div>All those &quot;Curing leprosy, giving sight to the blind and healing the limbs of the crippled&quot; charms supplement an Intelligence + Medicine roll, not a praying really really hard roll unless you enchant your action with Contagion-Curing Touch, but the charm also list normal medical technique (pressure points) along with <i>DnD Priest Technique</i> (inspire new strength in their patients through words and actions.) so it's obvious that Solar Medicine is not all about &quot;faith healing&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T19:10:08-08:00","id":54403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54392#post54392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Okay, explain to me exactly what knowledge the Solar is operating on that allows them to <i>regenerate limbs</i>, <i>cure cancer</i>, and <i>regrow hearts</i> by talking to someone. It's fucking magic. It's Biblical magic, man. They are doing something <i>impossible by mortal means</i> sheerly through the use of magic and divine power, and you don't call that <i>faith healing?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, what he seems to be saying is that, since Medicine charms require dots in Medicine - which is the skill of both practical and academic knowledge of healing techniques, anatomy, and physiology - that someone using Solar Medicine is, in fact, about being a glowy super-doctor who uses raw magical essence instead of surgical tools or medicines. He's not in any way saying that magical medicine is somehow less magical than faith healing. He's saying that there's no component of faith in it, and that it's just medical science being performed with magical charm-tools.<br /> <br /> Which would make it, by definition, not faith-healing.<br /> <br /> It's comparable to someone making the distinction between someone hitting someone really hard with melee charms, and smiting someone with the divine force of their faith. One is built on personal martial skill and knowledge taken to a brand new degree using essence as a tool. The other is channeling the raw force of your faith into an effect that can harm creatures of darkness and heathens because of how hard you believe.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying the distinction is relevant, or that I agree with either of you, but you're pretty clearly the one misunderstanding him here, not the other way around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T19:12:12-08:00","id":54404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54392#post54392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Okay, explain to me exactly what knowledge the Solar is operating on that allows them to <i>regenerate limbs</i>, <i>cure cancer</i>, and <i>regrow hearts</i> by talking to someone. It's fucking magic. It's Biblical magic, man. They are doing something <i>impossible by mortal means</i> sheerly through the use of magic and divine power, and you don't call that <i>faith healing?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>What skill is a Solar swordsman using to generate swordwaves and swords of light that burn demons? Obviously, faith-smiting, and thus more appropriate to Zeniths than Dawns.<br /> <br /> Stealth Charms to turn invisible are obviously magical as well, and should be Twilight spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T19:19:23-08:00","id":54406,"title":"","content":"... And I'm done here. Trust me, I fully understood where TW was coming from, the problem is that I disagree heavily with his premise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T19:24:18-08:00","id":54409,"title":"","content":"I am not using my own definition of prayer. My own definition of prayer is not the Christian definition and therefore would be foreign to many of the participants. They would not understand things like meaningful sacrifice and <i>geasa </i>in return for favor. I am therefore using the Christian definition, which is to beseech action from a being greater than yourself to intercede on your behalf offering nothing but your devotion.<br /> <br /> There is functionally no difference in Exalted if the Charm includes an elaborate performance or if it is delivered clinically. But that's where players get to make choices about their characters. Taking away those choices by trying to pin down Charms as this OR that is stupid when they can easily function as this AND that.<br /> <br /> The Abilities themselves need to be tightly defined. The Charms should follow. Granted, I realize this means Lunars and Alchemicals will provide their own set of headaches. Which is what it is, but it's not a reason to try to straightjacket Charm thematics. Realistically, Lunars and Alchemicals <i>should </i>have Charms that traipse across Ability boundaries when and where appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T19:32:34-08:00","id":54417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54404#post54404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What skill is a Solar swordsman using to generate swordwaves and swords of light that burn demons? Obviously, faith-smiting, and thus more appropriate to Zeniths than Dawns.<br /> <br /> Stealth Charms to turn invisible are obviously magical as well, and should be Twilight spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, why don't you go further than that TW. Every single ability any Exalt does is faith based, so they're all Zeniths!<br /> <br /> <br /> Except for the simple fact that quite a few of them don't fit. Oh, and the fact that the Charms and tree we're discussing is <i>explicitly based </i>on abilities and powers that men and women of supreme faith in different religions have been purported to have, including even the ability to raise the dead, heal the crippled, and restore sight to the blind. It is based off of faith healing, and many of the ways described that it is used make it clear that the power doing it is nothing mortal, but divine, which is kind of the definition of faith healing.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm more than a bit irritable about asinine discussions lately, so I'm going to end this here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T19:34:31-08:00","id":54419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54392#post54392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Okay, explain to me exactly what knowledge the Solar is operating on that allows them to <i>regenerate limbs</i>, <i>cure cancer</i>, and <i>regrow hearts</i> by talking to someone. It's fucking magic. It's Biblical magic, man. They are doing something <i>impossible by mortal means</i> sheerly through the use of magic and divine power, and you don't call that <i>faith healing?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>It's my understanding that faith healing is dependent on the faith of the person to be healed, whereas Solar magic doesn't give a rusty toss what the patient believes or doesn't believe. The distinction may be a bit fine, though. You are still causing people to grow back entire limbs and shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T19:48:49-08:00","id":54427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54419#post54419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's my understanding that faith healing is dependent on the faith of the person to be healed, whereas Solar magic doesn't give a rusty toss what the patient believes or doesn't believe. The distinction may be a bit fine, though. You are still causing people to grow back entire limbs and shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>People are getting so unnecessarily hung up on the &quot;faith&quot; part of faith healing. :T<br /> <br /> Let's just call it &quot;miraculous healing&quot; since apparently the meaning is not getting across. It's not about actual <i>faith</i>, it's about working the kind of healing miracles that Jesus did, or Catholic saints do. It's divine power bringing the world into order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=238\" data-tempid=\"temp_238_1438728365271_197\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1821-golden-demon","name":"Golden Demon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T19:49:17-08:00","id":54428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54419#post54419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's my understanding that faith healing is dependent on the faith of the person to be healed, whereas Solar magic doesn't give a rusty toss what the patient believes or doesn't believe. The distinction may be a bit fine, though. You are still causing people to grow back entire limbs and shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>This can also be accomplished with Infernal Charms, but THAT isn't just Solar Medicine reflavoured.<br /> <br /> <br /> The main appeal of Exalted, on a rules level, is that it's NOT a generic system. You don't take the &quot;Heal&quot; power and then apply power modifications until it works the way it does in your head - there are specific magical healing effects in the setting, and your character can learn those specific effects.<br /> <br /> The idea that you can refluff something as something else doesn't work. If you're willing to do that, why would you even think for more than five seconds about using the Ex2e rules?<br /> <br /> And Ex3e? Supposedly, they're not planning on making THAT a generic game either.<br /> <br /> <br /> Solar Medicine Charms are doctoring. They are not faith healing.<br /> <br /> And hey, if someone thinks faith healing is too D&amp;D Cleric, that's cool. Exalted doesn't specifically need that - but what it DOES need is Charms that let you build a priest who feels like a priest. IMNSHO, naturally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T20:13:25-08:00","id":54438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54125#post54125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Solars can forcibly impose the narrative of &quot;and then the hero rides off into the sunset, and the people cheer&quot; with a specific Charm, having religion that has real power, rather than just the ordinary mortal level &quot;get people working together&quot; is something it practically cries out for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can Solars forcibly impose the narrative of &quot;and then the hero rides off into the sunset, and the people cheer&quot; with a specific Charm?<br /> <br /> Because everything in my head tells me that that was dumb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/936-erichzahn","name":"ErichZahn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T20:18:59-08:00","id":54440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErichZahn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54438#post54438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can Solars forcibly impose the narrative of &quot;and then the hero rides off into the sunset, and the people cheer&quot; with a specific Charm?<br /> <br /> Because everything in my head tells me that that was dumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hero Rides Away I think in Ink Monkeys.<br /> <br /> Which it should be noted, was a Ride Charm. Playing on being a badass cowboy Rider dude. Not another Charm forcing the universe to do stuff based on feels.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T20:45:47-08:00","id":54454,"title":"","content":"If I may ask a question regarding Zeniths, which character from Terry Pratchett's <i>Small Gods</i> would be a Zenith? Because, from my previous understanding, it would be Brutha, who spends most of the book interacting with the god Om, searching for a way to restore the god to his previous stature. However, the impression I have gotten from this thread is that, while Brutha might be a valid Zenith, the intended role for a Zenith would be that of Vorbis, the head of the church-state of Omnia, under whose rule prayers have stopped going to Om, and instead have been directed at the idea of the church, and who is incapable of hearing the voice of Om.<br /> <br /> While I could see both of them as viable Zenith concepts, I am rather surprised that it seems that Vorbis is what Zeniths are supposed to be, and not Brutha, as every Zenith character concept I can remember having heard from people in person, that involves the Priest-King aspect of Zeniths, has fallen far closer to 'Holy Man' than 'front man'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T21:15:59-08:00","id":54468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jorlem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54454#post54454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may ask a question regarding Zeniths, which character from Terry Pratchett's <i>Small Gods</i> would be a Zenith? Because, from my previous understanding, it would be Brutha, who spends most of the book interacting with the god Om, searching for a way to restore the god to his previous stature. However, the impression I have gotten from this thread is that, while Brutha might be a valid Zenith, the intended role for a Zenith would be that of Vorbis, the head of the church-state of Omnia, under whose rule prayers have stopped going to Om, and instead have been directed at the idea of the church, and who is incapable of hearing the voice of Om.<br /> <br /> While I could see both of them as viable Zenith concepts, I am rather surprised that it seems that Vorbis is what Zeniths are supposed to be, and not Brutha, as every Zenith character concept I can remember having heard from people in person, that involves the Priest-King aspect of Zeniths, has fallen far closer to 'Holy Man' than 'front man'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vorbis is definitely not the iconic, archetypical hero-Zenith. He could potentially be a Zenith Caste villain, but he would not be an iconic character given as an example of what that caste is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T21:52:00-08:00","id":54478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54468#post54468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vorbis is definitely not the iconic, archetypical hero-Zenith. He could potentially be a Zenith Caste villain, but he would not be an iconic character given as an example of what that caste is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But neither is Brutha?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T22:07:25-08:00","id":54485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54478#post54478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But neither is Brutha?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been too long since I've read the book to recall with perfect clarity, but I think he hits a lot of Zenith notes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T23:02:33-08:00","id":54497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54417#post54417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, why don't you go further than that TW. Every single ability any Exalt does is faith based, so they're all Zeniths!</div> </div> </div> </div>Er, you realize he wasn't being serious, right? He was jokingly saying &quot;well, if Medicine Charms are faith-healing, then I guess Melee Charms are really faith-smiting!&quot; Except they're not. All Solar magic is based on the skill of the user. I have no idea how you can use your medical knowledge to heal people with words, but I also don't have any idea how to be so good at swinging swords that an arc of light comes out to cut my enemies down from afar. Doesn't really matter.<br /> <br /> You can make a Solar wise holy man who tells a cripple &quot;rise, and be healed&quot;, and the cripple will walk. And sure, ultimately, the reason you're able to do it is that God decided to make you Awesome. But you healed him using your skill, not by asking God to heal him for you. So it's not a faith healing because faith wasn't actually involved in the healing process. I mean, I don't understand why some people seem to think that's a problem. I think making your wise holy man <i>actually knowledgeable</i> works just fine. But Medicine Charms don't seem to be what they want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Solar Medicine Charms are doctoring. They are not faith healing.<br /> <br /> And hey, if someone thinks faith healing is too D&amp;D Cleric, that's cool. Exalted doesn't specifically need that - but what it DOES need is Charms that let you build a priest who feels like a priest. IMNSHO, naturally. </div> </div> </div>I repeat: you can make a Solar wise holy man who tells a cripple &quot;rise, and be healed&quot;, and the cripple will walk. You can make someone whose knowledge of Creation is so refined that he can heal with words. I agree: it's not faith healing. The healing depends on neither the faith of the healer nor the faith of the healed. My question is: <i>how is this a problem?</i> How is your character not made infinitely more awesome by the fact that his mastery of the secrets of the universe allow him to accomplish such miracles?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T23:12:12-08:00","id":54504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54497#post54497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I repeat: you can make a Solar wise holy man who tells a cripple &quot;rise, and be healed&quot;, and the cripple will walk. You can make someone whose knowledge of Creation is so refined that he can heal with words. I agree: it's not faith healing. The healing depends on neither the faith of the healer nor the faith of the healed. My question is: <i>how is this a problem?</i> How is your character not made infinitely more awesome by the fact that his mastery of the secrets of the universe allow him to accomplish such miracles?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because some people seem to think that the apex of Solar Medicine is you becoming Jesus whose holy pimp hands can slap the shit out of disease and broken-arm without any medical knowledge while dismissing real <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">physician, doctor and herbalist like H</span></span>ua Tuo or Hippocrates<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> as low-level Solar who using low-Essence charms ? </span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T23:26:14-08:00","id":54507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54409#post54409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not using my own definition of prayer. My own definition of prayer is not the Christian definition and therefore would be foreign to many of the participants. They would not understand things like meaningful sacrifice and <i>geasa</i> in return for favor. I am therefore using the Christian definition, which is to beseech action from a being greater than yourself to intercede on your behalf offering nothing but your devotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last I checked, the prayer mechanics included stuff like how slaughtering a cow during the ceremony will help you with your prayer. I don't remember seeing THAT the few times I've entered a church. So while it might not fit your personal definition, I don't think calling it the &quot;Christian definition&quot; is exact. There have certainly been other religions on Earth with the whole &quot;beseech action from a being greater than yourself using praise and/or bribes and/or devotion&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> If I'm being cheeky, showing devotion to the Christian God involves living how he prescribes you should live, which could be considered a form of sacrifice. You might not be all that happy with the whole pardon and compassion stuff, but hey, if it lets you make wine anytime you want and punish impertinent youths by sending bears to maul them, it's kind of a good deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T23:51:32-08:00","id":54510,"title":"","content":"Setting and gameplay question.<br /> <br /> Let's say there's a God, climbing the ranks of heaven and that God is my enemy. I want to cripple them by converting/redirecting/destroying/etc. their prayer base.<br /> <br /> How big a task is this? How many people do I need to convert/corrupt/etc. to bring the God to poverty? Or seize their attention and make them come and pay attention to me?<br /> <br /> Or are gods essentially safe regardless of worship and cults and the like are pocket change for splurging on a super-size meal rather than regular size?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T00:10:42-08:00","id":54513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54478#post54478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But neither is Brutha?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, fits pretty well - starts out as a man of supreme faith, ends up telling his god to shape his shit up and get out of the way, takes over to make the church into something not shit. Pretty Zenith, all in all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/855-magistrate","name":"Magistrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T00:31:48-08:00","id":54516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54497#post54497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Er, you realize he wasn't being serious, right? He was jokingly saying &quot;well, if Medicine Charms are faith-healing, then I guess Melee Charms are really faith-smiting!&quot; Except they're not. All Solar magic is based on the skill of the user. I have no idea how you can use your medical knowledge to heal people with words, but I also don't have any idea how to be so good at swinging swords that an arc of light comes out to cut my enemies down from afar. Doesn't really matter.<br /> <br /> You can make a Solar wise holy man who tells a cripple &quot;rise, and be healed&quot;, and the cripple will walk. And sure, ultimately, the reason you're able to do it is that God decided to make you Awesome. But you healed him using your skill, not by asking God to heal him for you. So it's not a faith healing because faith wasn't actually involved in the healing process. I mean, I don't understand why some people seem to think that's a problem. I think making your wise holy man <i>actually knowledgeable</i> works just fine. But Medicine Charms don't seem to be what they want.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I repeat: you can make a Solar wise holy man who tells a cripple &quot;rise, and be healed&quot;, and the cripple will walk. You can make someone whose knowledge of Creation is so refined that he can heal with words. I agree: it's not faith healing. The healing depends on neither the faith of the healer nor the faith of the healed. My question is: <i>how is this a problem?</i> How is your character not made infinitely more awesome by the fact that his mastery of the secrets of the universe allow him to accomplish such miracles?</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome is in the eye of the beholder. However, the objective part? Objectively, this means there's a character archetype (Man of God) that has no rules-based differentiation from another archetype (cynical manipulative charlatan). Which makes the former feel like they might as well be the latter.<br /> <br /> Also: Don't care what the specific effect is, but there should be at least one sodding Charm that makes your Solar Priest more priesty than your Solar militant antitheist (&quot;there are gods, this is a soluble problem, lock and load) who is pragmatic enough to smile and schmooze and charm the common folk.<br /> <br /> Characters should be differentiable. A Solar archetype as fundamental as &quot;Holy Man&quot; should have more meat to it than &quot;take Social Charms and roleplay it&quot;. (AKA this is not supported, and according to a good chunk of the thread, isn't really something that should be part of Exalted. Which if they're right, means the Zenith Caste needs a dramatic and sweeping overhaul)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T00:35:20-08:00","id":54518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54504#post54504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because some people seem to think that the apex of Solar Medicine is you becoming Jesus whose holy pimp hands can slap the shit out of disease and broken-arm without any medical knowledge while dismissing real <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">physician, doctor and herbalist like H</span></span>ua Tuo or Hippocrates<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> as low-level Solar who using low-Essence charms ? </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> without any medical knowledge </div> </div> </div>...Some people do? That seems silly. It doesn't really matter if you're using words or whatever as your preferred method of treatment, that's just personal style. It's still knowledge underneath.<br /> <br /> Or is your point that you dislike the Jesus analogies? Because &quot;personal inspiration&quot; is right there in the This Isn't Healing Magic sidebar, and Contagion-Curing Touch mentions inspiring new strength in patients through words and actions. If &quot;your sins are forgiven, rise and walk&quot; isn't personal inspiration, I don't know what is. Once you accept that as a valid treatment method, saying Solar Medicine is &quot;based on faith-healing&quot; like Tiresias did isn't that much of a stretch, even if Solar Medicine itself works on skill, not faith. And whatever he says, you don't HAVE to learn Contagion-Curing Touch if you prefer your character as a herbalist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T00:44:32-08:00","id":54522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magistrate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54513#post54513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know, fits pretty well - starts out as a man of supreme faith, ends up telling his god to shape his shit up and get out of the way, takes over to make the church into something not shit. Pretty Zenith, all in all.</div> </div> </div> </div>A prophet who redeems his God as well as his followers?<br /> <br /> Sounds perfect for a Zenith. There's even a God he can worship who needs some redeeming (although he's not as bad as Om).<br /> <br /> <br /> FTR, my question was because the question being replied to was &quot;Is Brutha or Vorbis more of a Zenith?&quot;.<br /> <br /> Because, again, the official party line appears to be strict Vorbisian - religion is the opiate of the masses, no sensible Solar would actually feel reverence for a mere god, it's all really just social control through rituals and rules. Faith is for chumps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T01:09:43-08:00","id":54525,"title":"","content":"I want Performance to have a bit more mystical/magical vibe . For the Primordials it is a big thing - we have the Brass Dancer, music keeps Adorjan at bay, etc.<br /> <br /> It seems there is a metaphysical link between the Performance ability and the nature of the world, I just need charms/plot-hooks about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1372-locke","name":"Locke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T01:14:28-08:00","id":54527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54516#post54516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome is in the eye of the beholder. However, the objective part? Objectively, this means there's a character archetype (Man of God) that has no rules-based differentiation from another archetype (cynical manipulative charlatan). Which makes the former feel like they might as well be the latter.<br /> <br /> Also: Don't care what the specific effect is, but there should be at least one sodding Charm that makes your Solar Priest more priesty than your Solar militant antitheist (&quot;there are gods, this is a soluble problem, lock and load) who is pragmatic enough to smile and schmooze and charm the common folk.<br /> <br /> Characters should be differentiable. A Solar archetype as fundamental as &quot;Holy Man&quot; should have more meat to it than &quot;take Social Charms and roleplay it&quot;. (AKA this is not supported, and according to a good chunk of the thread, isn't really something that should be part of Exalted. Which if they're right, means the Zenith Caste needs a dramatic and sweeping overhaul)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's silly, my personal opinion of what is awesome is objective truth.<br /> <br /> More seriously, I would argue that Man of God is kind of inherent in all castes, in that you were Exalted above simple mortals by the mightiest of gods. I also fail to see how the Solar who actually knows how a human body works is a cynical manipulative charlatan, instead of a holy man who has achieved a greater understanding of the world thanks to the grace of the Unconquered Sun. I also fail to see how a hypothetical Solar using a Performance-based ritual to heal people is inherently a holy man, and cannot be a cynical manipulative charlatan.<br /> <br /> The thing is, two characters with the same Charms can be different, and this is a right and proper thing. Which means that yes, the difference between the holy man and the charlatan is the role-playing. But then, there's no rules-based differentiation between a valiant hero and a monster: they both use the same combat Charms. This doesn't make me feel as though I might as well be the latter. (The instances in which I feel as though I might as well be the latter come purely from my own personality, and they occur even when I'm playing a D&amp;D paladin whose abilities are completely based on being holy.)<br /> <br /> And saying that the holy man archetype is not supported and shouldn't be part of Exalted... No. Point me to those heretics: you have all the tools you need to make Jesus Zenith out to spread the worship of the Sun. You are a prophet of God (a Solar), and you show everyone the miracles that are possible for someone recognized worthy by God, and if someone else shows appropriate greatness, they can become saints (other Solars) who perform miracles themselves.<br /> <br /> Just remember: &quot;You shall have no other gods before me. [...] You shall not bow down to them or worship them; for I, the LORD your God, am a jealous God&quot;.<br /> <br /> You don't have to fall on your knees and pray to every random field god to be a priest and a holy man. And you don't have to ask for help when help was already given.<br /> <br /> (Man, I don't think I've ever googled bible verses and related quotes as much as I'm doing today.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T01:20:45-08:00","id":54529,"title":"","content":"This is what I see when I think about prayer charms:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xxyOTFQFWQ0\" data-code=\"xxyOTFQFWQ0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/xxyOTFQFWQ0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> And I *SO* want to do this!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54516#post54516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Awesome is in the eye of the beholder. However, the objective part? Objectively, this means there's a character archetype (Man of God) that has no rules-based differentiation from another archetype (cynical manipulative charlatan). Which makes the former feel like they might as well be the latter.<br /> <br /> Also: Don't care what the specific effect is, but there should be at least one sodding Charm that makes your Solar Priest more priesty than your Solar militant antitheist (&quot;there are gods, this is a soluble problem, lock and load) who is pragmatic enough to smile and schmooze and charm the common folk.<br /> <br /> Characters should be differentiable. A Solar archetype as fundamental as &quot;Holy Man&quot; should have more meat to it than &quot;take Social Charms and roleplay it&quot;. (AKA this is not supported, and according to a good chunk of the thread, isn't really something that should be part of Exalted. Which if they're right, means the Zenith Caste needs a dramatic and sweeping overhaul)</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a priest merit. So there clearly *is* a way of differenting your Holy Man character from Actually-Smart-and-Skilled Man. There might also be some evocations that let you do that. You just can't do it with charms. Charms aren't everything.<br /> <br /> I think you're simply missunderstanding a very crucial thing about Exalted. See the scene from Prince of Egypt I posted above. In the real life, Moses is a holy man with unflinching devotion who can begg his god into performing miracles for him (allegedly) and the priests are charlatans who merely fool others into thinking that their gods are doing stuff for them and also gave them magical powers.<br /> <br /> But in Exalted? They are sorcerers. All of them. The egyptian priests might just be mortal thaumaturges, but they might as well be endowed mortals, or Exigents of their respective gods. Sure, Moses is a solar here- his peerless knowledge of performance means he can actually turn his staff into a serpant, instead of it all being make-believe. But he's doing that, not his god. In essence, there is no real difference between the priests and Moses, except in relative power.<br /> <br /> And the pillars of flame, plagues and all that? Sorcery. He can summon, bind and command forces of nature. Because he's badass. Not because his god is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 01-21-2014, 04:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T01:23:31-08:00","id":54530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54518#post54518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...Some people do? That seems silly. It doesn't really matter if you're using words or whatever as your preferred method of treatment, that's just personal style. It's still knowledge underneath.<br /> <br /> Or is your point that you dislike the Jesus analogies? Because &quot;personal inspiration&quot; is right there in the This Isn't Healing Magic sidebar, and Contagion-Curing Touch mentions inspiring new strength in patients through words and actions. If &quot;your sins are forgiven, rise and walk&quot; isn't personal inspiration, I don't know what is. Once you accept that as a valid treatment method, saying Solar Medicine is &quot;based on faith-healing&quot; like Tiresias did isn't that much of a stretch, even if Solar Medicine itself works on skill, not faith. And whatever he says, you don't HAVE to learn Contagion-Curing Touch if you prefer your character as a herbalist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just think that if you want to be Jesus so much then you really should just roll with being a Malefactor and their wish-granting charms :'P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T01:36:31-08:00","id":54533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54522#post54522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">religion is the opiate of the masses, no sensible Solar would actually feel reverence for a mere god, it's all really just social control through rituals and rules. Faith is for chumps.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... more cynical than - but similar to - my opinion of real life religion. That doesn't mean faith doesn't have power. It doesn't have power in the &quot;make miracles happen&quot; way, but it has power in the &quot;make people act&quot; way. And people have done some pretty cool stuff with religion as a motivation. That is a faith I feel has a place in Creation, even if plenty of people don't have it. And if faithful people can do awesome stuff in our world where (I believe) there are no miracles, then surely they can do the same in a Creation with the miracle of Exaltation, even if there aren't any others?<br /> <br /> Mostly, though, gods in Exalted aren't God. They're functionaries and caretakers. You can have faith in them in the same sense that you can have faith in a person. They just happen to have some magical powers. People DO have faith in other people however, which means it's possible to genuinely have faith in a god, even when you're Exalted and you can crush his little godly head with your bare hands. But it's tough to be religious the mortal way once you're Exalted, unless you're worshiping the Incarnae. Just... don't expect your prayers to be answered with miracles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T01:46:20-08:00","id":54535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54530#post54530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just think that if you want to be Jesus so much then you really should just roll with being a Malefactor and their wish-granting charms :'P</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, nobody ever said the Solars were the only ones who could be Jesus. After all, Infernals have a very good Charm to heal people with a touch. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T02:08:47-08:00","id":54540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54527#post54527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's silly, my personal opinion of what is awesome is objective truth.<br /> <br /> More seriously, I would argue that Man of God is kind of inherent in all castes, in that you were Exalted above simple mortals by the mightiest of gods. I also fail to see how the Solar who actually knows how a human body works is a cynical manipulative charlatan, instead of a holy man who has achieved a greater understanding of the world thanks to the grace of the Unconquered Sun. I also fail to see how a hypothetical Solar using a Performance-based ritual to heal people is inherently a holy man, and cannot be a cynical manipulative charlatan.<br /> <br /> The thing is, two characters with the same Charms can be different, and this is a right and proper thing. Which means that yes, the difference between the holy man and the charlatan is the role-playing. But then, there's no rules-based differentiation between a valiant hero and a monster: they both use the same combat Charms. This doesn't make me feel as though I might as well be the latter. (The instances in which I feel as though I might as well be the latter come purely from my own personality, and they occur even when I'm playing a D&amp;D paladin whose abilities are completely based on being holy.)<br /> <br /> And saying that the holy man archetype is not supported and shouldn't be part of Exalted... No. Point me to those heretics: you have all the tools you need to make Jesus Zenith out to spread the worship of the Sun. You are a prophet of God (a Solar), and you show everyone the miracles that are possible for someone recognized worthy by God, and if someone else shows appropriate greatness, they can become saints (other Solars) who perform miracles themselves.<br /> <br /> Just remember: &quot;You shall have no other gods before me. [...] You shall not bow down to them or worship them; for I, the LORD your God, am a jealous God&quot;.<br /> <br /> You don't have to fall on your knees and pray to every random field god to be a priest and a holy man. And you don't have to ask for help when help was already given.<br /> <br /> (Man, I don't think I've ever googled bible verses and related quotes as much as I'm doing today.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Miracles should be in the Zenith Caste abilities. Even better, there should be some miracles you can do that require big Performance rituals to pull off. There's a motonic physics explanation (prayer -&gt; essence -&gt; miracle, via the Solar), there's a 'Solars turn it up to 11 explanation' (humans pray for miracles and hope they get them. Solars pray for miracles and in doing so, make sure they happen). Christian traditions AREN'T standard Euro-Fantasy, but they ARE in Exalted's pedigree.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, to be clear, I abandoned the idea of anyone other than the Solar and their devoted crowd being involved in the proposed miracles PAGES ago. I haven't been talking about Gods - I've been talking about what the Solar might be able to do with nothing more than a community of frightened villagers and their own understanding of essence. About a Prayer Charm that doesn't involve the unworthy gods of the Terrestrial and Celestial Bureaucracies at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think that when you build Jesus Zenith, you should be taking some (not all) of his miracles from the Performance tree, because in Creation, prayers are an aspect of Performance, and so Solars should be able to turn those up to 11.<br /> <br /> And I have been getting told that has no place in Exalted. That it doesn't matter one whit what your character believes, it's all just about power. Same old cynical shit that took the shine off Solars last edition.<br /> <br /> I say no. Solars have tools that were designed to make them heroes, exemplars, shining bastions of hope. Of course this can be twisted to other ends - but the basic magical structure should show an *intent* of heroism, in the modern AND classical sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T02:28:55-08:00","id":54543,"title":"","content":"But the thing is- faith has no power in Creation. Not overwhelmingly magical at least. You can channel Conviction, that's somewhat like faith. If you do that on Medicine test, isn't it sort of faith-healing?<br /> <br /> And that's also irrelevant because &quot;the power of faith&quot; is not within the purview of Solar Exalted. Maybe Sidereal Exalted, since &quot;faith&quot; is a very esoteric concept indeed. But Solars generally do not &quot;gather around faith particles&quot; and use that to create miracles. And even then... That's sorcery. I am pretty sure you can fluff sorcery this way. Maybe make a custom initiation charm that lets you cast spells by prayer, that can be cool. But to put such charms in performance? That doesn't make much sense to me personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T02:30:32-08:00","id":54544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54507#post54507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last I checked, the prayer mechanics included stuff like how slaughtering a cow during the ceremony will help you with your prayer. I don't remember seeing THAT the few times I've entered a church. So while it might not fit your personal definition, I don't think calling it the &quot;Christian definition&quot; is exact. There have certainly been other religions on Earth with the whole &quot;beseech action from a being greater than yourself using praise and/or bribes and/or devotion&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> If I'm being cheeky, showing devotion to the Christian God involves living how he prescribes you should live, which could be considered a form of sacrifice. You might not be all that happy with the whole pardon and compassion stuff, but hey, if it lets you make wine anytime you want and punish impertinent youths by sending bears to maul them, it's kind of a good deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't being cheeky. The Christian definition of prayer is requesting intercession in exchange for devotion. It's in the dictionary. They used to have a more traditional understanding of sacrifice and offering in exchange for intercession (hey, Passover), but 'sacrifice' gave way to tithing as the Roman Catholic Church became more powerful and priests figured they may as well enjoy the sacrificed animals.<br /> <br /> The prayer section in the core rules mentions sacrificing a cow, but it clearly has no idea why you might sacrifice a cow and what that sacrifice would and should mean. It skips over quite a lot of the more traditional offerings in prayers that <i>do </i>get answered, after a manner. But it does correctly note that the more elaborate and more entertaining an offering is the more likely the prayer attached to it will be answered. This isn't a place that a Charm should be doing anything except helping the Zenith (or whomever) make a better-presented offering. Keep in mind that knowing what the perfect offering at the perfect time is would be either Lore or Occult test(s), depending on how you go about trying to deduce that knowledge.<br /> <br /> For example, sacrificing a bull to Ahlat is not going to do more than let him know you're near his herds. Sacrificing the most powerful and virile bull in an entire herd in conjunction with an elaborate war dance? Ahlat's probably coming for dinner. If he doesn't, well, that's when your circle kicks in his fucking door and curbstomps him for failing to answer his telephone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T02:47:24-08:00","id":54553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54543#post54543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the thing is- faith has no power in Creation. Not overwhelmingly magical at least. You can channel Conviction, that's somewhat like faith. If you do that on Medicine test, isn't it sort of faith-healing?<br /> <br /> And that's also irrelevant because &quot;the power of faith&quot; is not within the purview of Solar Exalted. Maybe Sidereal Exalted, since &quot;faith&quot; is a very esoteric concept indeed. But Solars generally do not &quot;gather around faith particles&quot; and use that to create miracles. And even then... That's sorcery. I am pretty sure you can fluff sorcery this way. Maybe make a custom initiation charm that lets you cast spells by prayer, that can be cool. But to put such charms in performance? That doesn't make much sense to me personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to flat out say that you're wrong: I have been hammering on &quot;why&quot; the power of faith is appropriate for Solar Exalted for pages now, so if the best you have is &quot;no it isn't&quot; you are not contributing to the conversation.<br /> <br /> But hey, why not explain all over again? They absolutely do. The mote-drip from Cult? Spending said motes on Solar Charms?<br /> <br /> That's using the power of faith to work miracles. It's also a fairly crappy and boring way of using the power of faith to work miracles, but that's the execution of the rules, not the principle of setting. In setting, faith (channeled through a Solar) can indeed move mountains.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, if you need 3 different Twilight Caste Abilities to build a Zenith, something is WRONG with the system. So this whole 'just use Medicine/Lore/Occult Charms&quot;? Medicine, Lore and Occult Charms aren't priestly. They're not in the Caste Abilities of the Priest Caste. Even expanded to be 7, and stealing two out of three of those? One of them is STILL going to be out of Caste.<br /> <br /> Or maybe, just maybe, it's appropriate to put Charms involving prayer under the auspices of the Ability governing prayer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T02:54:29-08:00","id":54557,"title":"","content":"Something I thought about last night regarding the relevance of Zeniths as priest-kings was how in several ancient cultures, most notable to my mind being Rome, religious rites were public ceremonies of such importance that they were actually state functions; elected magistrates doubled up as high priests, and most affairs of state needed to be prefaced by proper spiritual obeisance.<br /> <br /> I sadly don't know as much about Japan, but I think there may be something similar in the role of the emperor throughout history.<br /> <br /> Part of me was thinking about how this is a cultural conduct that would be nigh incomprehensible to us today, but then I thought about how many modern state functions stand on perfunctory ceremony, perhaps most notably coronations and inaugurations.<br /> <br /> Harborhead might be a state where Ahlat is so ingrained that the need to impress him or his worshipers might not really be necessary anymore, but I could still see the rituals to him being a matter of public ceremony and state function, and that would be resolved as a prayer.<br /> <br /> Note that if the presiding official flubs it, it won't really functionally be a big deal, not in the sense that Ahlat immediately and disastrously draws whatever he's contributing and everything collapses. In most cases where gods are supposed to be regularly focused on a place (such as when a Zenith Caste is there to preside over their public ceremonies or incorporate them into state functions), that's a thing that should be generally abstracted into a kind of background radiation that informs the assumptions and occurrences of everyday life.<br /> <br /> Messing up a prayer at the heart of these things isn't disastrous, it just affects the confidence of the people, and may even be seen as somewhat ominous. It's like kicking a fit if somebody flubs the recitation of their inauguration oath a bit; it contributes to the cultural backdrop, but nothing really happens over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T02:58:46-08:00","id":54559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54540#post54540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I say no. Solars have tools that were designed to make them heroes, exemplars, shining bastions of hope.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the distribution of those tools is delineated by Ability, so if you want to heal somebody you buy Medicine.<br /> <br /> Exalted doesn't need to validate any given individual's morality or ideology in order to not be excessively cynical. Belief can be an important thing for a character without them having Heart of the Cards Charms.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T03:13:50-08:00","id":54563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54559#post54559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the distribution of those tools is delineated by Ability, so if you want to heal somebody you buy Medicine.<br /> <br /> Exalted doesn't need to validate any given individual's morality or ideology in order to not be excessively cynical. Belief can be an important thing for a character without them having Heart of the Cards Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if you want to hurt someone, you buy Hurtiness.<br /> <br /> Wait, no, there's more than one way to hurt someone.<br /> <br /> Well, if you want to evade harm, buy Dod-<br /> <br /> Convince people, buy Pre-<br /> <br /> Know stuff about cultures, buy Lore. And Occult. And Socialize.<br /> <br /> <br /> And if you want to see spirits, that's definitely a job for Occult. Or Awareness.<br /> <br /> <br /> Putting two distinct types of abilities that achieve the same ends into two different Abilities has a massive stackload of precedent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T03:17:07-08:00","id":54565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54553#post54553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to flat out say that you're wrong: I have been hammering on &quot;why&quot; the power of faith is appropriate for Solar Exalted for pages now, so if the best you have is &quot;no it isn't&quot; you are not contributing to the conversation.<br /> <br /> But hey, why not explain all over again? They absolutely do. The mote-drip from Cult? Spending said motes on Solar Charms?<br /> <br /> That's using the power of faith to work miracles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except not: that's the power of prayer, not faith. Having people make cool rituals in your name gives you power. They might love you or fear you or just not care about you because it's just tradition. People having faith in you? Doesn't do anything. Your having faith in someone else? Zero effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T03:20:39-08:00","id":54567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54553#post54553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to flat out say that you're wrong: I have been hammering on &quot;why&quot; the power of faith is appropriate for Solar Exalted for pages now, so if the best you have is &quot;no it isn't&quot; you are not contributing to the conversation.<br /> <br /> But hey, why not explain all over again? They absolutely do. The mote-drip from Cult? Spending said motes on Solar Charms?<br /> <br /> That's using the power of faith to work miracles. It's also a fairly crappy and boring way of using the power of faith to work miracles, but that's the execution of the rules, not the principle of setting. In setting, faith (channeled through a Solar) can indeed move mountains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. I see your faith moves mountains and raise you exceptional individuals move mountains and sometimes faith helps. If, you know, it involves negotiating with the mountain god before you kick the shit out of him for being in your way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54553#post54553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if you need 3 different Twilight Caste Abilities to build a Zenith, something is WRONG with the system. So this whole 'just use Medicine/Lore/Occult Charms&quot;? Medicine, Lore and Occult Charms aren't priestly. They're not in the Caste Abilities of the Priest Caste. Even expanded to be 7, and stealing two out of three of those? One of them is STILL going to be out of Caste.<br /> <br /> Or maybe, just maybe, it's appropriate to put Charms involving prayer under the auspices of the Ability governing prayer.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to play a faith healer, you're going to need Occult and Medicine. If you want to play an Ascetic, you probably can get by with just Lore because your need to interact with gods is fairly low.<br /> <br /> &quot;Needing&quot; out-of-Caste abilities to fulfill desired archetypes is nothing new and the faith healer is hardly the most onerous (see also: functional Night Caste).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T03:26:03-08:00","id":54571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54563#post54563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Putting two distinct types of abilities that achieve the same ends into two different Abilities has a massive stackload of precedent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and it's always a sensible form, rather than &quot;I'm personally invested in prayers being a thing that can heal people, and prayer is represented in this system by Performance, so Performance has to heal people&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T03:35:04-08:00","id":54574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54563#post54563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And if you want to hurt someone, you buy Hurtiness.<br /> <br /> Wait, no, there's more than one way to hurt someone.<br /> <br /> Well, if you want to evade harm, buy Dod-<br /> <br /> Convince people, buy Pre-<br /> <br /> Know stuff about cultures, buy Lore. And Occult. And Socialize.<br /> <br /> <br /> And if you want to see spirits, that's definitely a job for Occult. Or Awareness.<br /> <br /> <br /> Putting two distinct types of abilities that achieve the same ends into two different Abilities has a massive stackload of precedent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am willing to give in and say that if you can create a cool custom charm that actually turns your *performance* into a medium of healing, like a song so soothing that it actually restores Willpower, or a dance so furious that it makes people immune to morale effects, great, I'd buy those charms.<br /> <br /> But &quot;pray to a random god with a bunch of people so well that their faith turns into a healing power&quot; is just not something Solars do. I'd posit that, sure, you can &quot;pray so nicely that it heals&quot;. But it has nothing to do with faith. It has everything to do with your performance. But hay, that's just me. Most people I think will tell you that &quot;healing&quot; is not an apropriate effect for performance because it undermines the purpose of medicine and makes characters too homogenic if they all can get all the effects they want with any ability they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T03:35:11-08:00","id":54575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I have been getting told that has no place in Exalted. That it doesn't matter one whit what your character believes, it's all just about power. Same old cynical shit that took the shine off Solars last edition. </div> </div> </div>That's how real life works, along with a whole lot of RPGs. Except with D&amp;D, with its divine magic... unless you play in Eberron, where there are no alignment requirements for clerics.<br /> <br /> Doesn't mean faith and ideals are worthless just because they don't give you magic power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, if you need 3 different Twilight Caste Abilities to build a Zenith, something is WRONG with the system. </div> </div> </div>Hey, you're the one who wants a holy man performing miraculous healings. Nobody here said that was a requirement for a Zenith. There are prophets and leaders who kick ass instead of healing the sick: they're gonna &quot;need&quot; some melee or martial arts.<br /> <br /> Though when it comes to calling down the fire of heaven, I've always been amused by how it's mentioned as being in theme for Solars in the Rules of Charms sidebar in the corebook, and yet there are no Charms to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T03:40:53-08:00","id":54576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54575#post54575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though when it comes to calling down the fire of heaven, I've always been amused by how it's mentioned as being in theme for Solars in the Rules of Charms sidebar in the corebook, and yet there are no Charms to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always took that as a suggestion for a probable three die stunt usage of Fire and Stones Strike, myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T03:52:25-08:00","id":54581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54575#post54575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though when it comes to calling down the fire of heaven, I've always been amused by how it's mentioned as being in theme for Solars in the Rules of Charms sidebar in the corebook, and yet there are no Charms to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Just replace Spirit Weapons with a mirrored Crypt-Bolt Attack and all shall be well, do be careful with the &quot;Lol Solars can't throw holy bolt 'cause that too inhuman&quot; crowd though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T04:14:32-08:00","id":54593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54567#post54567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. I see your faith moves mountains and raise you exceptional individuals move mountains and sometimes faith helps. If, you know, it involves negotiating with the mountain god before you kick the shit out of him for being in your way.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you want to play a faith healer, you're going to need Occult and Medicine. If you want to play an Ascetic, you probably can get by with just Lore because your need to interact with gods is fairly low.<br /> <br /> &quot;Needing&quot; out-of-Caste abilities to fulfill desired archetypes is nothing new and the faith healer is hardly the most onerous (see also: functional Night Caste).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm only going to say this once, so sorry if it seems like you're getting ignored.<br /> <br /> Faith healing was ONE example of the kind of miracles that seemed appropriate for Performance. Why? Because the typical example of it is this massive production - audience participation, preaching... as a myth, it's a case of magical Performance.<br /> <br /> My other go-to example? Exorcism (*again* it uses Twilight Caste Abilities). Oh! Divinations! Oh, right, Occult again.<br /> <br /> In short, Occult is the &quot;real magic&quot; skill of the setting, and the priests are left with a &quot;charlatan&quot; badge, because... why? Why do sorcerors get real magic and priests get to be phonies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T04:46:03-08:00","id":54601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54593#post54593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short, Occult is the &quot;real magic&quot; skill of the setting, and the priests are left with a &quot;charlatan&quot; badge, because... why? Why do sorcerors get real magic and priests get to be phonies?</div> </div> </div> </div>...? Because this isn't D&amp;D with arcane and divine magic? Being a priest isn't about magic, it's about your relationship with a god. This CAN mean you get some magic: maybe he gifts you with some kind of power, maybe he teaches you secret techniques. One might say... occult techniques...<br /> <br /> Plenty of mortal priests probably aren't even thaumaturges, nevermind being sorcerers or Exigents or having some kind of artifact or endowment or whatever. Being a priest is a social role. It's about being the link between the god and the population: keeping the god placated with prayers, transmitting the edicts of the god, etc. An Exalted version of the same will STILL be focused on the social role.<br /> <br /> Casting spells and exorcising is Occult. This is something a priest CAN do, but it is not a core competency for Zeniths. If you want to do it, you pick Occult as one of your favored Abilities. If you want to heal people, you pick Medicine. Beating people up is something a warrior-priest CAN do, but it is not a core competency for Zeniths. If you want it... You get the picture.<br /> <br /> As an aside, gods are usually considered very good sources of knowledge and wisdom and occult secrets, so of course you're going to take a bunch of Twilight Abilities if you priest concept is focused around being a learned man. In fact, there's nothing wrong with making a Twilight priest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T04:54:27-08:00","id":54605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54575#post54575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though when it comes to calling down the fire of heaven, I've always been amused by how it's mentioned as being in theme for Solars in the Rules of Charms sidebar in the corebook, and yet there are no Charms to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were Charms in 1e that did it. And there is an Archery Charm in 2e that creates fire (and Firearms, for that matter). It was never explored much, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T04:54:54-08:00","id":54607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54593#post54593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm only going to say this once, so sorry if it seems like you're getting ignored.<br /> <br /> Faith healing was ONE example of the kind of miracles that seemed appropriate for Performance. Why? Because the typical example of it is this massive production - audience participation, preaching... as a myth, it's a case of magical Performance.<br /> <br /> My other go-to example? Exorcism (*again* it uses Twilight Caste Abilities). Oh! Divinations! Oh, right, Occult again.<br /> <br /> In short, Occult is the &quot;real magic&quot; skill of the setting, and the priests are left with a &quot;charlatan&quot; badge, because... why? Why do sorcerors get real magic and priests get to be phonies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Loaded question, but whatever, I'll answer it: because they are.<br /> <br /> At least from the perspective of whether or not they can work &quot;real&quot; magic, where &quot;real&quot; is defined as sorcery. If you define real magic as using Charms, then they are no more or less phonies than any other Exalt.<br /> <br /> In summary: the problem is your definition of magic, not the game's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T05:17:26-08:00","id":54610,"title":"","content":"Correct me if I'm wrong but the issue is, I think, that a priest has no meaningful ability to do anything. They can pretend God(s) care what they do but they don't. God(s) do whatever they want regardless of what you do. Essentially making one of the descriptors of the Zenith cast non-protagonist.<br /> <br /> Being the best priest ever and doing the things unique to priests that differentiate them from sorcerors and wordsmiths and so on achieves absolutely nothing as it's entirely dependant on God(s) doing what you ask...which they are under absolutely no obligation to do. So, the key unique selling point of being a priest type character (note, I did not say Zenith here, just the priest archetype) is bugger all. Because really, anyone who could speak to a God or interact with it (Exalts for example) could make it do something anyway and the priest part is utterly irrelevant.<br /> <br /> So, we're left with the social role, how pepole react to a priest. But the net result of being treated as a divine link is easily replicated by any archetype with good group social/leadership skills anyway. And, arguably, the Eclipse as diplomat has the same protections and perks of access offered to a priest.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER.<br /> <br /> This is somewhat predicated on the idea that the populace in general <i>know</i> that Gods are under no obligation at all to answer prayers or act and that a priest is essentially a public figurehead with no actual power to enact the things the devotees want. Then you're left with God(s) saying 'Do X in my worship' and the priest basically just relaying that to the general populace and organising the things required for that to occur. Which is not particularly proactive and excellence in this area still does bugger all because the God(s) can still just go &quot;meh, ain't doin' what you ask, but I'll punish you if you stop&quot;.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> If we're playing a game and a PC is playing up the <b>Priest</b>-King Zenith archetype, what actions to they take in a game session that is meaningfully different to the Priest-<b>King</b> archetype or the Philosopher-Moraliser or the Judge archetypes? What is unique about being a priest that doesn't boil down to claiming some divine link that is ultimately pointless as your divine link can't be used proactively.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Alternatively: Why play a <b>Priest</b>-King rather than a <b>King</b>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T06:00:54-08:00","id":54622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54610#post54610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I'm wrong but the issue is, I think, that a priest has no meaningful ability to do anything. They can pretend God(s) care what they do but they don't. God(s) do whatever they want regardless of what you do. Essentially making one of the descriptors of the Zenith cast non-protagonist.<br /> <br /> Being the best priest ever and doing the things unique to priests that differentiate them from sorcerors and wordsmiths and so on achieves absolutely nothing as it's entirely dependant on God(s) doing what you ask...which they are under absolutely no obligation to do. So, the key unique selling point of being a priest type character (note, I did not say Zenith here, just the priest archetype) is bugger all. Because really, anyone who could speak to a God or interact with it (Exalts for example) could make it do something anyway and the priest part is utterly irrelevant.<br /> <br /> So, we're left with the social role, how pepole react to a priest. But the net result of being treated as a divine link is easily replicated by any archetype with good group social/leadership skills anyway. And, arguably, the Eclipse as diplomat has the same protections and perks of access offered to a priest.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER.<br /> <br /> This is somewhat predicated on the idea that the populace in general <i>know</i> that Gods are under no obligation at all to answer prayers or act and that a priest is essentially a public figurehead with no actual power to enact the things the devotees want. Then you're left with God(s) saying 'Do X in my worship' and the priest basically just relaying that to the general populace and organising the things required for that to occur. Which is not particularly proactive and excellence in this area still does bugger all because the God(s) can still just go &quot;meh, ain't doin' what you ask, but I'll punish you if you stop&quot;.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> If we're playing a game and a PC is playing up the <b>Priest</b>-King Zenith archetype, what actions to they take in a game session that is meaningfully different to the Priest-<b>King</b> archetype or the Philosopher-Moraliser or the Judge archetypes? What is unique about being a priest that doesn't boil down to claiming some divine link that is ultimately pointless as your divine link can't be used proactively.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Alternatively: Why play a <b>Priest</b>-King rather than a <b>King</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because if you're good at being a priest, the gods get a lot out of it and so might give you the miraculous effects as part of a bargain. Being the priest-king of a city near a river and pumping lots of effective prayer towards the river god might make him actually listen to you guys instead of those nobodies downstream. Same with your field, city or weather gods about.<br /> <br /> Prayer is a token, a resource, in Creation. Cults are and always have been, a form of protection racket. A Solar priest-king is going ot be the best union negotiator that the local human populace can get, since he'll probably be able to get the best deals on things for prayer. If he wants to do things that aren't predicated on the god doing stuff though, the power of hope and feelings isn't going to cut it, he'll need actual skill to ge that done.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T08:18:30-08:00","id":54677,"title":"","content":"All I really want for prayer charms is the following:<br /> <br /> 1. Personal cult manipulation. Being able to set my own cult to intense prayer for a scene to give me some kind of bonus - enhanced mote regen, a discount on charm activation costs, whatever - for a climactic battle or something. I want to be able to sing a hymn to my glory, have my cult in the streets below sing along, and be empowered by the faith of my people as I battle in the sky against an abyssal threat - or whatever.<br /> <br /> 2. Deity resource manipulation. Being able to offer a deity a one-time intense spike in prayer in exchange for something. Being able to threaten turning his cult away from him in order to pray to a rival. Generally being able to manipulate - including enhance - the amount of prayer going somewhere by leading the actual rituals personally.<br /> <br /> 3. Being able to directly send a message to a deity using the prayer system. I don't mean begging or submissive please, necessarily. I mean opening a channel for one-way social influence in the exact same way as someone using Linguistics to send a social influence letter. I want to be able to communicate something to a deity - whether it's a whisper in his ear or a thundering rumble in his entire sanctum - through a properly-executed prayer. And I want to be able to use my normal Performance charms as social influence through that link.<br /> <br /> So, in short, I want to be able to alter prayer revenue streams and be able to socially influence through prayer. Honestly, that could be handled by just two charms if you make the one that manipulates your own cult's prayer and the one that manipulate's another cult's prayer the same charm - being able to lead the cult of another exalt or deity in prayer to augment them just as well as augmenting yourself. But those are the two things related to 'prayer' that I definitely want included in the Performance charm trees.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any suggestions, criticisms, or points of clarification on this? Anything I've missed or failed to consider?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T08:34:43-08:00","id":54681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=53660#post53660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not an argument. The more powerful the god, the more someone would want to pray to it, and the more likely that it's going to ignore that prayer, because there are hundreds or thousands more that it is going to receive.</div> </div> </div> </div>In actual play, I've found this to be pretty inaccurate, at least so far as it describes the way PCs interact with the gods. Players aren't interested in trying to petition the big gods very often, but they're immensely interested in trying to get the attention of local gods for things like, say:<br /> <br /> -&quot;God of this mountain, are there any troops lurking in ambush on you?&quot;<br /> -&quot;God of the local roads, confound the people trying to flee from me!&quot;<br /> -&quot;God of these fields, bless my people's harvest and help them flourish.&quot;<br /> -&quot;God of the local smallpox outbreak, quit being a jerk, dude.&quot;<br /> -&quot;God of the nearby waterways, so, I'm looking for this boat that went down...&quot;<br /> <br /> And so on - and for almost all of these, it's the local gods (the ones connected to the phenomenon in question), who have relatively sparse resources, who are being reached out to. Honestly, it's difficult to explain in many cases why the gods <i>wouldn't</i> jump to answer these calls, when the Solars could offer what is (for them) a pretty trivial expenditure that is (for the gods) a pretty huge boost in how much prayer they get - selfishness and greed seem like they'd be pretty powerful motivators to respond immediately.<br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> There's a lot of &quot;Who does the Unconquered Sun pray to?&quot; conversation in the past few pages, which is weird to me, because, like... do any of the gods pray to other gods? Is that a thing? That seems kind of counter to the whole &quot;We need humans as prayer batteries&quot; deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T08:39:16-08:00","id":54683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54681#post54681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems kind of counter to the whole &quot;We need humans as prayer batteries&quot; deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regardless of the merits of supporting or disputing gods praying to anything, this is a bad idea that should be countered at every turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T08:50:39-08:00","id":54691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54553#post54553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to flat out say that you're wrong: I have been hammering on &quot;why&quot; the power of faith is appropriate for Solar Exalted for pages now, so if the best you have is &quot;no it isn't&quot; you are not contributing to the conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prayer has power in Creation. Faith is not the same as prayer. Faith is some belief of something very deeply against any other evidence (as it has often been presented to me). Prayer is an act, not something you have but something you do. Prayer generates resources in Creation that powerful beings want (Essence, willpower, quintessence, ambrosia). Faith helps convince people to do these acts that generate these. It's not clear if actual fiath is a ncessary component, though. Again, Caesar and Oda Nobunaga were probably atheists in the modern sense of not believing in gods (or buddhas). Caesar still did the rituals because that's what you did. Nobunaga went to funerals because those were important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54553#post54553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But hey, why not explain all over again? They absolutely do. The mote-drip from Cult? Spending said motes on Solar Charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>The act of prayer generates those specific resource. It allows no special leap from there to let you go and willweave the universe based on Tinkerbelling things about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54553#post54553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's using the power of faith to work miracles. It's also a fairly crappy and boring way of using the power of faith to work miracles, but that's the execution of the rules, not the principle of setting. In setting, faith (channeled through a Solar) can indeed move mountains.</div> </div> </div> </div>By giving the Solar extra resources to move the damned mountains himself. Faith itself is inert and useless until a will goes and puts the resources to something. My belief that I will be health if I work out and eat right means shit all if I don't actually then go and od the things to initiate that. Prayer without an actor willing to use its effects is nothing but free motes floating about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54553#post54553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if you need 3 different Twilight Caste Abilities to build a Zenith, something is WRONG with the system. So this whole 'just use Medicine/Lore/Occult Charms&quot;? Medicine, Lore and Occult Charms aren't priestly. They're not in the Caste Abilities of the Priest Caste. Even expanded to be 7, and stealing two out of three of those? One of them is STILL going to be out of Caste.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of this is a bit of confusion on what priests do. In some cultures, scholars do a lot of what some folks think priests should do. Or priests tended to be scholars. An omyouji or a Taoist or a guru isn't necessarily going to be a &quot;priest&quot; in the whole communing with gods things. Some priests probably aren't known for the priest thing and are more notable for their experiments on pea plants. That priest=healy dude is straight-up a D&amp;Dism anyhow. Zeniths are preachers, ascetics and leaders. They have those Abilites now. If they are expected also to commune with gods and fonts of wisdom, that helps too. But having lay on hands or faith healing is not universal to the priest archetype, just some priests. And so to do that, you'll favor non-Zeniths to be that guy. Just like the warrior-smith Twilight will favor Melee, or the Night assassin favors any combat Abilityt hey don't favor inherently anyhow. Castes are not entire concepts in themselves, simply archetypes you start with and use your favoreds to flesh out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54553#post54553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe, just maybe, it's appropriate to put Charms involving prayer under the auspices of the Ability governing prayer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is Performance. But prayers are again a resource generater and communciations tool. Mudras, mantras and sutras of various aspects of the universe you invoke are probably more just pushing the wiring of the universe. And when it gets extra flashy about it, probably sorcery.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T08:53:20-08:00","id":54694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagadaishio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54677#post54677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I really want for prayer charms is the following:<br /> <br /> 1. Personal cult manipulation. Being able to set my own cult to intense prayer for a scene to give me some kind of bonus - enhanced mote regen, a discount on charm activation costs, whatever - for a climactic battle or something. I want to be able to sing a hymn to my glory, have my cult in the streets below sing along, and be empowered by the faith of my people as I battle in the sky against an abyssal threat - or whatever.<br /> <br /> 2. Deity resource manipulation. Being able to offer a deity a one-time intense spike in prayer in exchange for something. Being able to threaten turning his cult away from him in order to pray to a rival. Generally being able to manipulate - including enhance - the amount of prayer going somewhere by leading the actual rituals personally.<br /> <br /> 3. Being able to directly send a message to a deity using the prayer system. I don't mean begging or submissive please, necessarily. I mean opening a channel for one-way social influence in the exact same way as someone using Linguistics to send a social influence letter. I want to be able to communicate something to a deity - whether it's a whisper in his ear or a thundering rumble in his entire sanctum - through a properly-executed prayer. And I want to be able to use my normal Performance charms as social influence through that link.<br /> <br /> So, in short, I want to be able to alter prayer revenue streams and be able to socially influence through prayer. Honestly, that could be handled by just two charms if you make the one that manipulates your own cult's prayer and the one that manipulate's another cult's prayer the same charm - being able to lead the cult of another exalt or deity in prayer to augment them just as well as augmenting yourself. But those are the two things related to 'prayer' that I definitely want included in the Performance charm trees.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any suggestions, criticisms, or points of clarification on this? Anything I've missed or failed to consider?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is about what I would say it should be. Prayer is a resource generator and communications apparatus. Zeniths are able to push it into overdrive for various political negoitaty things. Not to get pseudo-sorcery feels magic.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T09:15:03-08:00","id":54711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54522#post54522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A prophet who redeems his God as well as his followers?<br /> <br /> Sounds perfect for a Zenith. There's even a God he can worship who needs some redeeming (although he's not as bad as Om).<br /> <br /> <br /> FTR, my question was because the question being replied to was &quot;Is Brutha or Vorbis more of a Zenith?&quot;.<br /> <br /> Because, again, the official party line appears to be strict Vorbisian - religion is the opiate of the masses, no sensible Solar would actually feel reverence for a mere god, it's all really just social control through rituals and rules. Faith is for chumps.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. This is exactly what I was trying to get at. And while it is reassuring to hear that Vorbis isn't intended to be the role model for Zeniths, that is how it is coming off to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T09:31:52-08:00","id":54722,"title":"","content":"The thing is that religion has not really ever presented as anything but the opiate of the masses, in a sense.<br /> <br /> The Immaculate Philosophy is a social control program created to elevate the Terrestrial Exalted, retard the will of the populace towards potential Celestial Exaltation, keep gods in the pockets of the Sidereals and to enforce order upon the world.<br /> <br /> The Cult of the Illuminated is the result of a drug-addled hippy's doomsday cult being co-opted into a Solar traiing conspiracy and indoctrination programme.<br /> <br /> The Hundred Gods Heresy is in the end a series of ponzi schemes, protection rackets or bribery chains. Gods normally only do the jobs they do because they have to or get paid to do it and corruption with no consequence results in cults.<br /> <br /> The cult of Autochthon is pretty utilitarian. Gods and humans do get along there, there is actual reverence of the Great Maker and his subroutines, but note that in the end, it's still an expectation somewha to reciprocity. Humans worship the pantheon, the pantheon does its job. It is part of the great system, a fuel. Faith itself doesn't bouie things up, prayer's generative properties do.<br /> <br /> The ancestor cult is more or less the above thing with the Hundred Gods Heresy, but even more cynical.<br /> <br /> Faith in Exalted isn't some special source of power in itself. It is not a praiseworthy source of anything in itself. Believing really hard in stuff doens't go and make it real. Prayer is a source of resources and power. It is the currency of the divine. Zeniths as priests help to mediate this. They create situations that use this resoruce to their advantage. As priests of the Sun, they already have the highest authority to call on to get what they want and are given Exaltations to make that manifest. Other gods are in theory deferrent to the authority vested into the Zenith as the voice fo their boss. No matter how much folks decide they really believe in it, the world works how it works and any outcome of prayer is convincing the gods that it's worth their time to act on those prayers.<br /> <br /> I guess it might just be me thinking religion in the real world is not so much better, but Exalted investigates most politcal organizations through a lense of real politk. Religions don't get some special pass because &quot;faith is important.&quot; It never has been stated as such in Exalted as a special place that needs protection or power, anymore than love, morality, humilty or niceness would (as in it doens't).<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T10:17:51-08:00","id":54739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54681#post54681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-&quot;God of this mountain, are there any troops lurking in ambush on you?&quot;<br /> -&quot;God of the local roads, confound the people trying to flee from me!&quot;<br /> -&quot;God of these fields, bless my people's harvest and help them flourish.&quot;<br /> -&quot;God of the local smallpox outbreak, quit being a jerk, dude.&quot;<br /> -&quot;God of the nearby waterways, so, I'm looking for this boat that went down...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of my caution towards prayer charms is that I can see all of these coming from the same PC with a ST who doesn't like saying no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T10:35:51-08:00","id":54753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54681#post54681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-&quot;God of this mountain, are there any troops lurking in ambush on you?&quot;<br /> -&quot;God of the local roads, confound the people trying to flee from me!&quot;<br /> -&quot;God of these fields, bless my people's harvest and help them flourish.&quot;<br /> -&quot;God of the local smallpox outbreak, quit being a jerk, dude.&quot;<br /> -&quot;God of the nearby waterways, so, I'm looking for this boat that went down...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>But um... how is this different from what an Eclipse can do, when said Eclipse can literally just walk up to said god and ask them, and beat their face in when they refuse to tell you?<br /> <br /> Also, prayers are, in exalted, essentially communication. There's no reason that communication charms can't augment it. You could, for example, use Respect-Commanding Attitude or Heart-Compelling Method on your Performance roll for praying. You don't <i>need</i> prayer-specific versions of those charms for a god to listen to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 01-21-2014, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T11:21:44-08:00","id":54772,"title":"","content":"This gives me an idea for an NPC.<br /> <br /> Wandering the threshold there a man known to the Wyld Hunt as The Hundred God Heretic. He resembles a vagabond wearing trappings of at least 9 or 10 different faiths and is often considered to be madman when he starts talking to inanimate objects or stopping everything he\u2019s currently doing to pray to a far off god.<br /> <br /> Despite being seeming harmless the Hundred God Heretic is deadly in a fight, his constant pattern of ritual behaviour seems to give him a charmed life and his charms seem to require prayer to distant or local divinities to activate. It's unknown how much the gods actually help the Heretic but he has been observed being at less than full strength when he had reason to believe he'd recently offended a god. If the gods have some capacity to withhold power or if his abilities are shaped by his beliefs is the subject of speculation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T11:31:50-08:00","id":54783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54722#post54722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Faith in Exalted isn't some special source of power in itself. It is not a praiseworthy source of anything in itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>In itself is the important bit. The solidity of human belief was real useful in maintaining the existence of world against the onslaught of the Wyld and Fair Folk. Apparently.<br /> <br /> Faith is real powerful in this game's world. Because that's real. The setting tends to call belief by more morally multihued terms like Conviction and Willpower rather than faith because they lead to more morally interesting places and a world more in more colors than black, white and grey.<br /> <br /> Faith, and conviction, though, powerful as they are, aren't some force that overpowers history, curiosity and knowing something about reality and people. (Except maybe somewhere out in the Wyld.)<br /> <br /> Like, I think although it's not stated that the solidity of human belief that kept out the Fair Folk and the Wyld wasn't just their belief as such, but human belief in a real world, with real history and real laws, that they bothered to know and understand.<br /> <br /> Not so much cynicism about faith (it's a force), but cynical towards ignorance and cynical towards giving unquestioning trust to any kind of authority or any appealing anti-authority group that talks the talk and promises you you'll finally get what you deserve.<br /> <br /> Faith as a supplement to real knowledge and real know how is a force. Faith as a substitute, not so much. That's where any power that edges into the territory &quot;Oh, well, I don't know anything, I just believe real hard&quot; has problems (for any Exalted, but especially the heroes of being skillful and knowing stuff).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T12:24:49-08:00","id":54820,"title":"","content":"Also, I wanna note that PRIMARILY?...<br /> <br /> ...what I most want from Performance is for it to be written in a book that I can buy for money.<br /> <br /> Because, seriously. This is like watching my dog circle around her sleeping spot... for a billion years. YOU FOUND A SPOT. SLEEP. &gt;&lt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T12:39:20-08:00","id":54828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54622#post54622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because if you're good at being a priest, the gods get a lot out of it and so might give you the miraculous effects as part of a bargain. Being the priest-king of a city near a river and pumping lots of effective prayer towards the river god might make him actually listen to you guys instead of those nobodies downstream. Same with your field, city or weather gods about.</div> </div> </div> </div>But isn't this the purpose of the Eclipse Caste? To forge and maintain relationships between peoples and spirits and such to their mutual benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T12:39:48-08:00","id":54829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54540#post54540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Miracles should be in the Zenith Caste abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Miracles . . . should be in every single Solar ability. Miracles are what Solars are about.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T12:42:09-08:00","id":54831,"title":"","content":"I think the takeaway from all this prayer discussion is that the books need to spend more time talking about what priests actually <i>do</i>. Before, they sort of threw the basic mechanics for a prayer roll at you and left you to figure out a lot of it on your own.<br /> <br /> A few religion-related charms of some sort for Zeniths would be excellent; I think it's fine to say that prayer (and, maybe more importantly, preaching and interacting with your flock) is fundamentally communication, but most of the other castes have charms that are immediately and obviously relevant to their main definition, while the Zenith charms have generally been more &quot;well, these <i>could</i> be useful to a priest, in addition to a ton of other people.&quot; The only really specifically priestly charm they have in 2e is the Smite Evil stuff in Presence. I'm not saying they need a bunch of priest charms (Zeniths are not <i>just</i> priests, and besides, the abilities are used by other castes to an extent and need to stand on their own rather than just as a caste's powers), but at least a few would be good.<br /> <br /> But I think there also needs to be more discussion of how being a priest works in Exalted even without charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T12:49:42-08:00","id":54834,"title":"","content":"Here's the thing about prayer-healing in Exalted. You pray your heart out to the UCS to heal this follower of yours. The UCS speaks to you and says, &quot;Try looking in the Medicine Charms. I gave you 5 Favoured Abilities for a reason.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T14:00:18-08:00","id":54883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Best case scenario: the UCS nails you with a training effect that grants you medical skill. (Although that's putting it dryly. I imagine that having medical insight and knowledge lanced in to your mind with a thunderbolt from heaven is a religious experience only slightly less profound and gut-rattling than zen enlightenment or partaking in human sacrifice.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Or how about you are temporarily possessed by a lesser aspect of the UCS, his divine radiance pouring into you, working small miracles before the celestial light, divine wind, holy scents and whatnot dissipate?<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Zenith Caste are the only ones with this potential. It's not something the Eclipse or Twilight Caste could pull off and it's also outside of their themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T14:20:28-08:00","id":54898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54883#post54883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or how about you are temporarily possessed by a lesser aspect of the UCS, his divine radiance pouring into you, working small miracles before the celestial light, divine wind, holy scents and whatnot dissipate?<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Zenith Caste are the only ones with this potential. It's not something the Eclipse or Twilight Caste could pull off and it's also outside of their themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>No thank you. I wholeheartedly agree with Drakhan abuve. The powers you wield as an Exalt are yours and yours alone. If you want to be a healer, then invest in Medicine. <br /> <br /> There's room for &quot;possessed by a deity to do things&quot;, and the Ochilike are a good place to start. And divine intercession (that isn't directly embodied by the presence of the PC's) is also something that can have a place*. But &quot;I work miracles&quot;--even little ones--as an even remotely reliably invokable power (especially if freeform) is dangerous ground to tread. You run risks of making the actual medic look like a chump, or the role look pretty unnecessary if your base Zenith set comes with amazing healing powers without having to actually invest in healing.<br /> <br /> It's not a place I want to go, and I don't think it's a net positive here.<br /> <br /> *Disclaimer: Yes, I think it can work, the prayer to the Sun, etc. But unless you're calling in some serious divine favors this is the sort of thing that should be so vanishingly rare that it falls under the heading of ST Fiat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T14:27:08-08:00","id":54903,"title":"","content":"So then we're left again with the question of: What do priests do that isn't covered by other roles already? Communication between gods and people is something that doesn't require an Exalt and, when it does, it's better left to the Eclipse caste as that's exactly their role. The Eclipse caste also handles <i>travel</i> (potentially) to spiritual realms such as Heaven itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T14:40:39-08:00","id":54916,"title":"","content":"I could see it being somehow tied with Zenith Anima power. Something that makes perayers concieved by the Priests being more easilly heard by the gods perhaps? It does makes sense that when the Zenith speaks in prayer his voice is like an echo of thunder, nearly stunning the god with it's force and clarity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T14:54:31-08:00","id":54928,"title":"","content":"After much consideration, I have determined this is the best way to answer John's question:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lYFGTf3M3Sc\" data-code=\"lYFGTf3M3Sc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/lYFGTf3M3Sc/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T15:20:59-08:00","id":54951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54916#post54916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see it being somehow tied with Zenith Anima power. Something that makes perayers concieved by the Priests being more easilly heard by the gods perhaps? It does makes sense that when the Zenith speaks in prayer his voice is like an echo of thunder, nearly stunning the god with it's force and clarity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly speaking, they already do, at least in 2e - we don't know what their anima effects in 3e will be. A passive anima effect for all Zeniths is that they're considered priests to every god. They get a -1 to the difficulty of all prayer rolls, which is the equivalent to one free automatic success on all prayer rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T15:47:06-08:00","id":54970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagadaishio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54951#post54951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Strictly speaking, they already do, at least in 2e - we don't know what their anima effects in 3e will be. A passive anima effect for all Zeniths is that they're considered priests to every god. They get a -1 to the difficulty of all prayer rolls, which is the equivalent to one free automatic success on all prayer rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, exactly? Why isn't that enough?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T15:51:08-08:00","id":54975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54739#post54739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of my caution towards prayer charms is that I can see all of these coming from the same PC with a ST who doesn't like saying no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, that's a struggle I've had to deal with re: prayer. But it comes up even without prayer Charms - or more to the point: the issue isn't prayer Charms, it's the whole concept of how prayer and gods work in Creation. A Solar can make a pretty good pitch to a local god with absolutely no magical backup; the first step is to make sure <i>that</i> isn't some insane unstoppable grab-bag of powers.<br /> <br /> My gut sense is that, if you fix Charm-free prayer, you'll open lots of design space for Charm-enhanced prayer. If you don't, well, the system's already busted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T15:51:42-08:00","id":54977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54970#post54970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, exactly? Why isn't that enough?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand your question. You suggested there should be something in the Zenith anima power that makes them better at making their prayers heard. I explained that there already is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T15:56:26-08:00","id":54983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54753#post54753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But um... how is this different from what an Eclipse can do, when said Eclipse can literally just walk up to said god and ask them, and beat their face in when they refuse to tell you?<br /> <br /> Also, prayers are, in exalted, essentially communication. There's no reason that communication charms can't augment it. You could, for example, use Respect-Commanding Attitude or Heart-Compelling Method on your Performance roll for praying. You don't <i>need</i> prayer-specific versions of those charms for a god to listen to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize - I'm not sure how either of these are counter to the point I was making, i.e., &quot;Exalts are actually more likely to contact small gods than large ones, in my actual play experience, and so the effects of beseeching the gods can't be dismissed as being unnoticeable and irrelevant in the vast flood of prayer.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T15:57:36-08:00","id":54985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54683#post54683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Regardless of the merits of supporting or disputing gods praying to anything, this is a bad idea that should be countered at every turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's... fine for you to feel that way, and YCMV, and all, but when discussing what's true in the canon setting, no, this is a relevant fact that shapes our fundamental understanding of what prayer <i>is</i> in Creation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T15:58:56-08:00","id":54988,"title":"","content":"Solar Charms are not the Charms of the Unconquered Sun. They come from the Solar. <br /> <br /> That said, if a Solar shouts &quot;I CALL UPON THE POWER OF THE UNCONQUERED SUN&quot; when using Nine Aeons Thew and Titan-Straightening Method to shake down the walls of Ostagul with his bare hands, he's not incorrect. Solars are the spiritual successors of the Unconquered Sun, and at the origin level their Essence is exactly the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T16:00:44-08:00","id":54993,"title":"","content":"I appreciate the great length at which prayer has been discussed. I feel the topic has been unveiled in ways that have been constructive.<br /> <br /> But I also derailed my thread by discussing it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T16:08:59-08:00","id":55005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54993#post54993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate the great length at which prayer has been discussed. I feel the topic has been unveiled in ways that have been constructive.<br /> <br /> But I also derailed my thread by discussing it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>At least it proved to be a constructive derail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T16:11:39-08:00","id":55009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54988#post54988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nine Aeons Thew and Titan-Straightening Method</div> </div> </div> </div>This response is longer than necessary due to character restrictions on posted replies. I had originally intended just a sly &quot;mm-hm.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T16:14:12-08:00","id":55011,"title":"","content":"I think the big thing is that you need to make sure the Religion chapter is <i>really</i> tight and clear on the role of priests and - fundamentally - why a PC would want to play someone who is lord and master of temple bureaucracy, because that seems to be the key part of being a priest that is actually unique to them. (Though I do note bureaucracy isn't a Zenith favoured so I'm still unsure why they're better at it than a well educated Eclipse as they have the god-talking, bureaucracy and general populace social skills too)<br /> <br /> How does Zenith Moses differ from Eclipse Moses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T16:17:23-08:00","id":55013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54993#post54993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate the great length at which prayer has been discussed. I feel the topic has been unveiled in ways that have been constructive. But I also derailed my thread by discussing it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe the thread's Road Spirit was dissapointed in the amount of prayers that was directed at him. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1920-kim","name":"Kim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T16:21:53-08:00","id":55018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54970#post54970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, exactly? Why isn't that enough?</div> </div> </div> </div>3rd edition I meant. I really don't see the need for more canon suport/reflection of this &quot;Zeniths are Priests&quot; dichotomy then that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T16:28:11-08:00","id":55023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55011#post55011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the big thing is that you need to make sure the Religion chapter is <i>really</i> tight and clear on the role of priests and - fundamentally - why a PC would want to play someone who is lord and master of temple bureaucracy,</div> </div> </div> </div>The character sheet has Bureaucracy but not Pray. It also has Sail, but not Pray.<br /> <br /> So, there were things that were rendered important on purpose, and other things which just don't matter a whole lot.<br /> <br /> Exalted <i>doesn't</i> have freeform magic channeled by belief in gods. This <i>isn't</i> just a mechanical decision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":86,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","user":"John M\u00f8rke","date":". 01-21-2014, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T16:32:58-08:00","id":55027,"title":"","content":"Moses would make a better Eclipse than a Zenith, to be honest. Most of what he pulls parallels Taboo-Inflicting Diatribe fairly well, assuming the spoilers we got way back when are still generally representative of Socialize. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T16:33:31-08:00","id":55028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54831#post54831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few religion-related charms of some sort for Zeniths would be excellent; I think it's fine to say that prayer (and, maybe more importantly, preaching and interacting with your flock) is fundamentally communication, but most of the other castes have charms that are immediately and obviously relevant to their main definition, while the Zenith charms have generally been more &quot;well, these <i>could</i> be useful to a priest, in addition to a ton of other people.&quot; The only really specifically priestly charm they have in 2e is the Smite Evil stuff in Presence. I'm not saying they need a bunch of priest charms (Zeniths are not <i>just</i> priests, and besides, the abilities are used by other castes to an extent and need to stand on their own rather than just as a caste's powers), but at least a few would be good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going off of what Hatewheel and others have said about priests and prayer being fundamentally inextricable from their sociocultural contexts, a &quot;prayer&quot; Charm idea that would have obvious religious utility but could also serve other character concepts:<br /> <br /> If the Solar leads a group performance (like a festival dance or a mass prayer or a protest march), the participants will all feel some emotional connection to each other, or to the object of their shared devotion, or to both. This is sort of conceptually related to Alchemical Charms like Patriotism-Provoking Display and Perfected Union Patterning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=238\" data-tempid=\"temp_238_1438728365271_197\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1821-golden-demon","name":"Golden Demon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T17:09:01-08:00","id":55047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55023#post55023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The character sheet has Bureaucracy but not Pray. It also has Sail, but not Pray.<br /> <br /> So, there were things that were rendered important on purpose, and other things which just don't matter a whole lot.<br /> <br /> Exalted <i>doesn't</i> have freeform magic channeled by belief in gods. This <i>isn't</i> just a mechanical decision.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a false comparison. That's like saying the sheet has Performance, but not Investment. That it has Performance, but not Kayaking. Leading and making prayers is a component of Performance, just like how investment and kayaking are components of Bureaucracy and Sail. So, if coinage, salt rates, and so forth are going to play as big of a role as they did in 2e, taking up page after page of the equipment section, there should probably be at least some sort of section describing how gods interact with worshippers and what prayer is and is not.<br /> <br /> Unless you just can't manage that with 3e's page/word count constraints. I don't know what kind of limitations you're working with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T17:42:41-08:00","id":55063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54691#post54691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prayer has power in Creation. Faith is not the same as prayer. Faith is some belief of something very deeply against any other evidence (as it has often been presented to me). Prayer is an act, not something you have but something you do. Prayer generates resources in Creation that powerful beings want (Essence, willpower, quintessence, ambrosia). Faith helps convince people to do these acts that generate these. It's not clear if actual fiath is a ncessary component, though. Again, Caesar and Oda Nobunaga were probably atheists in the modern sense of not believing in gods (or buddhas). Caesar still did the rituals because that's what you did. Nobunaga went to funerals because those were important.<br /> <br /> <br /> The act of prayer generates those specific resource. It allows no special leap from there to let you go and willweave the universe based on Tinkerbelling things about.<br /> <br /> <br /> By giving the Solar extra resources to move the damned mountains himself. Faith itself is inert and useless until a will goes and puts the resources to something. My belief that I will be health if I work out and eat right means shit all if I don't actually then go and od the things to initiate that. Prayer without an actor willing to use its effects is nothing but free motes floating about.<br /> <br /> <br /> Part of this is a bit of confusion on what priests do. In some cultures, scholars do a lot of what some folks think priests should do. Or priests tended to be scholars. An omyouji or a Taoist or a guru isn't necessarily going to be a &quot;priest&quot; in the whole communing with gods things. Some priests probably aren't known for the priest thing and are more notable for their experiments on pea plants. That priest=healy dude is straight-up a D&amp;Dism anyhow. Zeniths are preachers, ascetics and leaders. They have those Abilites now. If they are expected also to commune with gods and fonts of wisdom, that helps too. But having lay on hands or faith healing is not universal to the priest archetype, just some priests. And so to do that, you'll favor non-Zeniths to be that guy. Just like the warrior-smith Twilight will favor Melee, or the Night assassin favors any combat Abilityt hey don't favor inherently anyhow. Castes are not entire concepts in themselves, simply archetypes you start with and use your favoreds to flesh out.<br /> <br /> Which is Performance. But prayers are again a resource generater and communciations tool. Mudras, mantras and sutras of various aspects of the universe you invoke are probably more just pushing the wiring of the universe. And when it gets extra flashy about it, probably sorcery.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faith_healing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Elias_healing_the_son_of_the_widow%2C_engraving._Wellcome_M0017808.jpg/960px-Elias_healing_the_son_of_the_widow%2C_engraving._Wellcome_M0017808.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faith_healing\" target=\"_blank\"> Faith healing - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faith_healing\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faith_healing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If you think the conversation has been about importing D&amp;D's Cure Light Wounds, you have been fundamentally misunderstanding the entire conversation. Cure Light Wounds is not remotely Performance-y and would make no sense under Performance. Yes, Zeniths are Preachers - faith healing is one of the kinds of miracle commonly attributed TO Preachers.<br /> <br /> BTW, Willweaving the universe? A strawman. &quot;Individual Charms that work like so&quot; is not asking for Willweaving.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also &quot;not universal to the Archetype&quot;? Ridiculous. No Archetype has enough &quot;universals&quot; to fill up five in-Caste Abilities. In fact, I'd wager there is NO single ability that every single instance of ANY particular archetype can be said to have. Out of Caste abilities should be for things that aren't linked to the archetype at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T17:45:29-08:00","id":55066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55027#post55027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moses would make a better Eclipse than a Zenith, to be honest. Most of what he pulls parallels Taboo-Inflicting Diatribe fairly well, assuming the spoilers we got way back when are still generally representative of Socialize.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is especially true when you go back and read the account of the Exodus, and realize that Moses was not doing the talking directly - his brother Aaron was his mouthpiece (as the KJV puts it) - Moses was less good at talking all around. Frankly, he is probably better modeled by Eclipse or Twilight <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Old Testament Zeniths are really more Elijah, Elisha, some of the Judges, maybe Joshua - though he could be a Dawn. And my favorite candidates - Ruth and Jeremiah. I tend to use a definition of prophet that is less focused of foretelling and miracles, though those can be important, but rather on forth telling or setting a right example. That seems to unite all the folks I use as Zenith inspiration. And that should be a fundamental undeinning of the performance Charms - to let them show their example most effectively - and have it stick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/798-joshua","name":"Joshua","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar798_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T18:13:37-08:00","id":55080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Golden Demon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55028#post55028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going off of what Hatewheel and others have said about priests and prayer being fundamentally inextricable from their sociocultural contexts, a &quot;prayer&quot; Charm idea that would have obvious religious utility but could also serve other character concepts:<br /> <br /> If the Solar leads a group performance (like a festival dance or a mass prayer or a protest march), the participants will all feel some emotional connection to each other, or to the object of their shared devotion, or to both. This is sort of conceptually related to Alchemical Charms like Patriotism-Provoking Display and Perfected Union Patterning.</div> </div> </div> </div>One idea I had for a Solar charm I had was some sort of 'consecration' charm, where you bestow a sort of aura of reverence or other emotional impact on an area or object, which causes people to treat it as holy or whatever (with attendant mental-influence effects as necessary.) I think that &quot;make this temple seem like a place where people will go for respectful, quiet contemplation&quot; fits into Solar social charms, anyway.<br /> <br /> It could also, eventually, perhaps upgrade to protect against undead or creatures of darkness or things antagonistic to whatever ideology, god, concept or mood you consecrated the area to, protecting people there from those things to a certain degree -- which happens to work out all right because the Solar 'smite evil' charms are also in presence and performance.<br /> <br /> It also has the advantage that you can describe it in religious Zenith-y ways, while still leaving the charm flexible enough to have non-religious uses.<br /> <br /> (However, creating lasting social effects unbound to any specific people with performance or presence might be stepping on Linguistics' toes...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T18:28:42-08:00","id":55095,"title":"","content":"To answer the original question, I feel like Performance should focus around emotion. An inspiring speech grants confidence or a desire for change. A dance can evoke strange thoughts and remind us of past events, or even be used for seduction. Music resonates with our very soul. All of the things are emotional, and generally suited for more immediate influences, rather than long-term. From the point of view of charms ... I don't really know. A song or dance might remind someone of a memory they had long forgotten, or a rousing speech might inspire troops to greater heroics on the battlefield.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/242-mindworm-jim","name":"Mindworm Jim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T18:38:18-08:00","id":55099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55063#post55063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of Caste abilities should be for things that aren't linked to the archetype at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is absolutely ridiculous. There is no way the devs could possibly choose five Abilities that would encompass all the facets of a given archetype, nevermind <i>all related archetypes</i> players could possibly want to draw on.<br /> <br /> The Zenith Abilities are all related to the archetype of the holy man in one way or another. The holy man's words sway the people. The holy man has an unbreakable will. The holy man can walk through the desert, he can fast for days, the beasts of the wild do not touch him.. The fact that YOUR personal preference includes healing and magic only means that it is your personal preference. In Exalted, an executive decision was made to give those Abilities to Twilights.<br /> <br /> You can deny it if you want, but making sure your character has what he needs to fit what you want IS the point of Favored Abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T18:58:18-08:00","id":55111,"title":"","content":"The Holy Man knows Kung-Fu and Kicks Ass for the Lord.<br /> The Holy Man leads his knights in a great Crusade.<br /> The Holy Man heals the wounded.<br /> The Holy Man is a scholar.<br /> The Holy Man performs exorcisms.<br /> The Holy Man can see and hear all that happens in his god's domain.<br /> The Holy Man will travel to all ends of Creation to spread the word of his god, be it by boat, horse, or foot.<br /> The Holy Man can speak in Tongues.<br /> The Holy Man will handle the finances of his church.<br /> The Holy Man will understand the needs of his congregation and be deft in his dealing with all people.<br /> <br /> How many of these fall under Zenith Abilities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T19:01:29-08:00","id":55114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagadaishio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55047#post55047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a false comparison. That's like saying the sheet has Performance, but not Investment. That it has Performance, but not Kayaking. Leading and making prayers is a component of Performance, just like how investment and kayaking are components of Bureaucracy and Sail. So, if coinage, salt rates, and so forth are going to play as big of a role as they did in 2e, taking up page after page of the equipment section, there should probably be at least some sort of section describing how gods interact with worshippers and what prayer is and is not.<br /> <br /> Unless you just can't manage that with 3e's page/word count constraints. I don't know what kind of limitations you're working with.</div> </div> </div> </div>You probably didn't understand what I said.<br /> <br /> The sheet doesn't have Drive, Firearms, Gardening, or Scrimshaw. These things are not central to how the game is played, or important enough to the play experience that they be there. Some of them are actively inappropriate. So, what is Prayer? Is it inappropriate, or simply not central, or somewhere in between? That is not conjecture, it is a developmental fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T19:11:52-08:00","id":55121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55099#post55099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is absolutely ridiculous. There is no way the devs could possibly choose five Abilities that would encompass all the facets of a given archetype, nevermind <i>all related archetypes</i> players could possibly want to draw on.<br /> <br /> The Zenith Abilities are all related to the archetype of the holy man in one way or another. The holy man's words sway the people. The holy man has an unbreakable will. The holy man can walk through the desert, he can fast for days, the beasts of the wild do not touch him.. The fact that YOUR personal preference includes healing and magic only means that it is your personal preference. In Exalted, an executive decision was made to give those Abilities to Twilights.<br /> <br /> You can deny it if you want, but making sure your character has what he needs to fit what you want IS the point of Favored Abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>*points to the new Sail Charm that means you don't need to favour Athletics to do appropriate Sailor-y athletic stuff*<br /> <br /> They don't need to make the kind of compromises you're calling for.<br /> <br /> <br /> My personal preferences, for the record, have nothing to do with &quot;healing magic&quot;. I think that if you're going to have &quot;praying&quot; be Performance-based, then there should be Charms that enhance ability to pray. THAT is my preference. Faith healing was a suggestion, not the one true thing without which Zenith's would be fucked forever.<br /> <br /> Of course, the fact that the (apparently) Prophet archetype lacks anything in the way of foresight and prayers (even ones charged with Solar essence) are completely useless against demons and the undead... no, nobody wants to try and defend those, they just rant about the faith healing suggestion and pretend that that's a comprehensive dismissal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, the thing people keep ignoring in favour of &quot;just take Medicine, dumbass&quot; is that Medicine Charms *do not work like faith healing*. My suggestion for the latter is something that involves huge, showy, rituals of restoration *and don't work without it*. They'd be about the Solar and their congregation being empowered to heal the petitioner. Which is, incidentally and once again, nothing like Cure Light Wounds. Or, more generally, Messianic (as in the Infernals keyword) effects. Much like a Dawn would have War Charms to make their Followers more effective, the Zenith would have (probably Performance) Charms to make their Cult more effective. (If restoring motes wasn't such a boring and meta-y effect, I'd've suggested that the Performance Charm be one that simply augments Cult - but it IS boring, so I think specific Charms that allow you to channel your Cult rating into specific Miracles would make for more interesting gameplay)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T19:20:19-08:00","id":55129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55063#post55063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faith_healing\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faith_healing</a><br /> <br /> If you think the conversation has been about importing D&amp;D's Cure Light Wounds, you have been fundamentally misunderstanding the entire conversation. Cure Light Wounds is not remotely Performance-y and would make no sense under Performance. Yes, Zeniths are Preachers - faith healing is one of the kinds of miracle commonly attributed TO Preachers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The performance is getting people into the belief that their faith matters. It might get a god to pay attention and do something. Faith healing has been claims that you have a channel to a deity and your belief in that deity gets them to intercede. YOu give them the job to do. In Creation, that job is on you. Faith isn't doing shit, it's your knoweldge of actually healing folks doing it. If you want to be a holyman and not a scam artist, you know actual Medicine. If you want to be a healer going around as a holyman, you also learn Medicine. Faith healing is oftentimes (actually on Earth, pretty much all times) a scam if the person doesn't actually have some medical knoweldge. Creation supports the crook as much as the honest man. The honest man knows how people are actually put together, since his magic works on skill and expertise rather than feels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55063#post55063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW, Willweaving the universe? A strawman. &quot;Individual Charms that work like so&quot; is not asking for Willweaving.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prayer to do generic miracles is willweaving. It's getting enough &quot;faith stuff&quot; together to impact the universe. Which is not how the unvierse works. Faith and prayer make stuff. Concsious beings do something with that stuff in their conscious acts. Faith has no power in itself beyond what potential someone with actual power can do with it. It's fuel and rewrard, not action. Performance makes you really good at praying. Praying is a way to get a message and a present to a god. It's not any way to tap into that god for some magic faith boonies beyond it deciding your'e worth its time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55063#post55063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also &quot;not universal to the Archetype&quot;? Ridiculous. No Archetype has enough &quot;universals&quot; to fill up five in-Caste Abilities. In fact, I'd wager there is NO single ability that every single instance of ANY particular archetype can be said to have. Out of Caste abilities should be for things that aren't linked to the archetype at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is in part why, as has been spoiled so far, we're getting the &quot;Eight pick five&quot; thing, so you can have some more inherent Abilities and flesh out closer with Caste some things that fit archetypes. If your faith healer doesn't reallylike being a loud boistrous performer or taming animals, good for her. She might have Occult or Medicine instead to go about doing real stuff involving spirits instead of showmanship.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T19:25:36-08:00","id":55134,"title":"","content":"I think that Exalted rightly distinguishes between &quot;prophet&quot; and &quot;seer&quot; (which is quite firmly Sidereal turf). A prophet is one who carries the word of god, an intermediary between mortal and divine. &quot;Prophecy&quot; originally simply meant the divine message, whether that be a vision of the End of Days or a commandment to care for the less fortunate; it's simply that, in our world, so many prophets proclaimed visions of the future that the concepts became colloquially linked. In and of itself, being a prophet implies no special ability to foretell the future -- especially in Exalted, where the gods are often as ignorant as mortals about what is to come.<br /> <br /> (As for prayer against the undead, to what should the Solar pray that is more potent against creatures of darkness than herself? The cleansing fire is within her and at her command; she needs no god to draw it forth, though as a stunt she might call upon the judgement of the Sun as she smites her enemies.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T19:33:05-08:00","id":55140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55121#post55121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal preferences, for the record, have nothing to do with &quot;healing magic&quot;. I think that if you're going to have &quot;praying&quot; be Performance-based, then there should be Charms that enhance ability to pray. THAT is my preference. Faith healing was a suggestion, not the one true thing without which Zenith's would be fucked forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's how prayer works in Exalted:<br /> 1- A priest prays to Uvanavu for healing.<br /> 2- Uvanavu might choose to come down and use his charms to bestow the healing.<br /> <br /> At no point in time does the priest ever possess the ability to heal people aside from whatever medical skills he possesses. Performance charms might be able to enhance a Solar's ability to pray, but they are utterly incapable of answering prayers because that has absolutely nothing to do with the Solar. It all depends on the god receiving the prayer. <br /> <br /> Doesn't matter if it's healing or exorcism or anything else. The only miracles Performance is capable to performing are those that are related to Performance. That's how Solar charms work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T19:33:21-08:00","id":55141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55121#post55121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *points to the new Sail Charm that means you don't need to favour Athletics to do appropriate Sailor-y athletic stuff*</div> </div> </div> </div>So you get really good prayer rolls. Stuff maybe that helps you be more priestly or not worry about the cash as much. If Zeniths get access to Occult, maybe something that makes you more intuned wiht spirits. Or as previous editions had, maybe just always having the priest discount, regardless of actual priestness. I fail to see what more needs done there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55121#post55121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... My personal preferences, for the record, have nothing to do with &quot;healing magic&quot;. I think that if you're going to have &quot;praying&quot; be Performance-based, then there should be Charms that enhance ability to pray. THAT is my preference. Faith healing was a suggestion, not the one true thing without which Zenith's would be fucked forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>And folks have said what they think that means. Make the Exalt's prayer participants louder or the results of prayer more beneficial to a target. Or find ways to send magic social influence through prayer to boss things around. But no one agrees that prayer in itself should have some pwoers besides what it does and what I hold is all it does: generate resources and send a message to the target.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55121#post55121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, the fact that the (apparently) Prophet archetype lacks anything in the way of foresight and prayers (even ones charged with Solar essence) are completely useless against demons and the undead... no, nobody wants to try and defend those, they just rant about the faith healing suggestion and pretend that that's a comprehensive dismissal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prophets don't necessarily fight demons and Solars aren't really the prophecy sort of Exalt anyhow (Sidereals do prophecy). Zeniths go around being prophets in that they have a line to their god, their god is the boss of Heaven and so they get some weight in their proclamations. They also wander through deserts, take suffering and stick to the course pretty good. They are very much Casted to being preachers. Things adding ot the holy man and preacher thing though is for other Abilities. Just like Dawns can't really do Achilles just with Dawn Abilities (Ride, Resistance, Athletics) or you can't really do Sindbad with just Eclipse ones (Dodge, Athletics, Melee). Caste is a starting point, not the entire concept.<br /> <br /> And even then, they look to be making them broader, so maybe the missing Abilites are on the new lists anyhow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55121#post55121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the thing people keep ignoring in favour of &quot;just take Medicine, dumbass&quot; is that Medicine Charms *do not work like faith healing*. My suggestion for the latter is something that involves huge, showy, rituals of restoration *and don't work without it*. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>The other option is making it so the huge show and flash helps keep people coming back to your healing and also get your deity friend in on things. Or making them worhsip you for your actual skills in healing. Kind of like the real world: You either are a good scam artist or good showman at your art. Exalted may be overly cynical but in cases of religion has never been really forgiving.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55121#post55121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... They'd be about the Solar and their congregation being empowered to heal the petitioner. Which is, incidentally and once again, nothing like Cure Light Wounds. Or, more generally, Messianic (as in the Infernals keyword) effects. Much like a Dawn would have War Charms to make their Followers more effective, the Zenith would have (probably Performance) Charms to make their Cult more effective. (If restoring motes wasn't such a boring and meta-y effect, I'd've suggested that the Performance Charm be one that simply augments Cult - but it IS boring, so I think specific Charms that allow you to channel your Cult rating into specific Miracles would make for more interesting gameplay)</div> </div> </div> </div>Or just keep it what it is, which is economics and leave the miracle working to sorcerers, or gods you are pushing to actually do the work. I still don't see any argument for there being special faith buttons you poke gods with and you get effects out of them besides some view that faith and prayer should be anything more than it is. It also creates a setup where folks can get something out of asshole gods regardless of the god wanting it to be that way or not, undermining a bit of what Exalted always has had in its presentation of the shiftiness of the divine.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T19:47:33-08:00","id":55146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55129#post55129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The performance is getting people into the belief that their faith matters. It might get a god to pay attention and do something. Faith healing has been claims that you have a channel to a deity and your belief in that deity gets them to intercede. YOu give them the job to do. In Creation, that job is on you. Faith isn't doing shit, it's your knoweldge of actually healing folks doing it. If you want to be a holyman and not a scam artist, you know actual Medicine. If you want to be a healer going around as a holyman, you also learn Medicine. Faith healing is oftentimes (actually on Earth, pretty much all times) a scam if the person doesn't actually have some medical knoweldge. Creation supports the crook as much as the honest man. The honest man knows how people are actually put together, since his magic works on skill and expertise rather than feels.<br /> <br /> <br /> Prayer to do generic miracles is willweaving. It's getting enough &quot;faith stuff&quot; together to impact the universe. Which is not how the unvierse works. Faith and prayer make stuff. Concsious beings do something with that stuff in their conscious acts. Faith has no power in itself beyond what potential someone with actual power can do with it. It's fuel and rewrard, not action. Performance makes you really good at praying. Praying is a way to get a message and a present to a god. It's not any way to tap into that god for some magic faith boonies beyond it deciding your'e worth its time.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is in part why, as has been spoiled so far, we're getting the &quot;Eight pick five&quot; thing, so you can have some more inherent Abilities and flesh out closer with Caste some things that fit archetypes. If your faith healer doesn't reallylike being a loud boistrous performer or taming animals, good for her. She might have Occult or Medicine instead to go about doing real stuff involving spirits instead of showmanship.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it really hard to imagine a louder and more boisterous performance than a faith healing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, if you're really, really insistent on Prayer being solely a fuel source, FINE. I henceforth concede any and all arguments that you should include a use for the mojo you get from having a congregation in the Charm for getting said mojo. Clearly Performance-based Prayer Charms should be boring-ass &quot;get extra mote&quot; effects, because that's better for some asinine reason.<br /> <br /> Now tell me, why shouldn't a Charm exist for turning prayers directly into motes? That is, turning faith into power? It's not that you CAN'T turn prayers into motes, they actually do that automatically... so why should there not be a Solar Charm for doing so *better*?<br /> <br /> <br /> (Also, by the way, in real life? There are actually real benefits to the placebo effect. A Solar ramping the placebo effect up to the point of curing diseases it has no business curing sounds epic, but also very much a &quot;super skill&quot; effect... wait, sorry, I said I conceded that point)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T20:29:10-08:00","id":55169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drakhan Valane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55111#post55111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Holy Man knows Kung-Fu and Kicks Ass for the Lord.<br /> The Holy Man leads his knights in a great Crusade.<br /> The Holy Man heals the wounded.<br /> The Holy Man is a scholar.<br /> The Holy Man performs exorcisms.<br /> The Holy Man can see and hear all that happens in his god's domain.<br /> The Holy Man will travel to all ends of Creation to spread the word of his god, be it by boat, horse, or foot.<br /> The Holy Man can speak in Tongues.<br /> The Holy Man will handle the finances of his church.<br /> The Holy Man will understand the needs of his congregation and be deft in his dealing with all people.<br /> <br /> How many of these fall under Zenith Abilities?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you're trying to say. The fact that those things don't fall under Zenith Abilities is exactly what I'm saying: there are too many things in an archetype to encompass with five Abilities. So they picked 5 which were appropriate and also left appropriate Abilities for the other Castes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55121#post55121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*points to the new Sail Charm that means you don't need to favour Athletics to do appropriate Sailor-y athletic stuff*<br /> <br /> They don't need to make the kind of compromises you're calling for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Salty Dog is nice, but hardly a replacement for the whole Athletics Charm tree. If Athletics is an important part of your Eclipse sailor, you'll Favor it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My personal preferences, for the record, have nothing to do with &quot;healing magic&quot;. I think that if you're going to have &quot;praying&quot; be Performance-based, then there should be Charms that enhance ability to pray. THAT is my preference. Faith healing was a suggestion, not the one true thing without which Zenith's would be fucked forever. </div> </div> </div>You'll notice I said &quot;healing and magic&quot;, two different things you have argued a priest should be able to do, not &quot;healing magic&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course, the fact that the (apparently) Prophet archetype lacks anything in the way of foresight and prayers (even ones charged with Solar essence) are completely useless against demons and the undead... no, nobody wants to try and defend those, they just rant about the faith healing suggestion and pretend that that's a comprehensive dismissal. </div> </div> </div>Ysadrel explains the foresight thing very well. As for prayers being useful against demons and undead... ignoring the Zenith ability to use Holy effects... I'll borrow your words: &quot;just take Occult, dumbass&quot;. In Creation, exorcism does not work because of the strength of your faith, it works because of your mystical knowledge.<br /> <br /> Less catholic, more... I want to say japanese/asian, but I'm basically working off anime here, not actual cultural knowledge, so I'll restrain myself to &quot;less catholic&quot;. Then again, a catholic exorcist should be well educated, and able to recite relevant prayers by heart, so there's some &quot;mystical&quot; knowledge right there, out of the grasp of the common man. Some random dude can occasionally keep evil at bay with faith alone, not helped by education, but that's getting outside of a discussion about priests. So, yeah, actually, you can argue that even catholic priests aren't just working off their Performance score.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, the thing people keep ignoring in favour of &quot;just take Medicine, dumbass&quot; is that Medicine Charms *do not work like faith healing*. My suggestion for the latter is something that involves huge, showy, rituals of restoration *and don't work without it*. They'd be about the Solar and their congregation being empowered to heal the petitioner. Which is, incidentally and once again, nothing like Cure Light Wounds. Or, more generally, Messianic (as in the Infernals keyword) effects. Much like a Dawn would have War Charms to make their Followers more effective, the Zenith would have (probably Performance) Charms to make their Cult more effective. (If restoring motes wasn't such a boring and meta-y effect, I'd've suggested that the Performance Charm be one that simply augments Cult - but it IS boring, so I think specific Charms that allow you to channel your Cult rating into specific Miracles would make for more interesting gameplay) </div> </div> </div>And what I'm saying is... wait a minute, I got it... right, your character is &quot;infinitely more awesome&quot; when his &quot;mastery of the secrets of the universe&quot; allows him to &quot;accomplish such miracles&quot;. My opinion is objective truth, haven't we been over this already?<br /> <br /> More seriously, while I'm not interested by such Charms as you're suggesting, I've been arguing less against your basic thesis and more against your specific arguments (like your saying that a character who heals like Jesus but is using Medicine to do so is automatically a charlatan instead of a holy man, or your saying that the Cult background proves faith has power, or your saying faith would be worthless if it doesn't let you do miracles and that would be &quot;cynical shit&quot;).<br /> <br /> For the record, I still don't grasp why saying belief doesn't have magic power is cynical. I'm not religious, and that doesn't stop me from being optimistic in real life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T20:36:08-08:00","id":55177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55146#post55146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also, by the way, in real life? There are actually real benefits to the placebo effect. A Solar ramping the placebo effect up to the point of curing diseases it has no business curing sounds epic, but also very much a &quot;super skill&quot; effect... wait, sorry, I said I conceded that point)</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, a master psychologist who fools people into thinking they're healed <i>until it actually happens</i> is kind of a cool concept. I hope you won't mind if I steal it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T20:50:29-08:00","id":55187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55146#post55146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find it really hard to imagine a louder and more boisterous performance than a faith healing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which again is usually a scam or a cover.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55146#post55146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if you're really, really insistent on Prayer being solely a fuel source, FINE. I henceforth concede any and all arguments that you should include a use for the mojo you get from having a congregation in the Charm for getting said mojo. Clearly Performance-based Prayer Charms should be boring-ass &quot;get extra mote&quot; effects, because that's better for some asinine reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because faith and prayer has never been anything more in Exalted. It's not even a result of 2e being assholey. Exalted has always had a fairly blunt &quot;Religion is the opiate of the masses&quot; presentation of faith since early 1e. Hence my arguments. Anything adding more to it is bringing in a thematic (the power of faith) that is not in Creation's presentation up to now. It's to me like saying the power of love means anything also (see some bitching when folks freaked out how apparently Sidereals can just nuke that and there's not much anyone can do to stop them).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55146#post55146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now tell me, why shouldn't a Charm exist for turning prayers directly into motes? That is, turning faith into power? It's not that you CAN'T turn prayers into motes, they actually do that automatically... so why should there not be a Solar Charm for doing so *better*?</div> </div> </div> </div>I already said getting more out of your prayer's quantifiable results is probably a good thing. It's up to you to put that quantifiable stuff it generates to use, since the result of player is inert unless acte dupon (or in otherwords, the motes don't do shit unless you go out of yoru way to use them).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55146#post55146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also, by the way, in real life? There are actually real benefits to the placebo effect. A Solar ramping the placebo effect up to the point of curing diseases it has no business curing sounds epic, but also very much a &quot;super skill&quot; effect... wait, sorry, I said I conceded that point)</div> </div> </div> </div>Understanding the concept of placebo effect and then praying on it seems more like a mental influence effect (not prayer) or an appllication of Medicine to me. Not using the rituals and statements and admonishments of prayer to tap into god faith codes to get results. Placebo effects also don't regrow limbs, give sight to the blind or cure cancer.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T21:03:38-08:00","id":55196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55187#post55187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Understanding the concept of placebo effect and then praying on it seems more like a mental influence effect (not prayer) or an appllication of Medicine to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Original application of Contagion-Curing Touch, the way I see it. I'm having a blast thinking up this social Twilight with such a keen insight on people he can do this sort of thing. This just displaced my Eclipse shaman concept as the first character I want to play in Ex3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T21:07:48-08:00","id":55201,"title":"","content":"&quot;Oh, yes. This is a tincture of Placebo Root. It's wonderful stuff - grows out in the wyld. It's basically a panacea. It'll cure anything that ails you. Trust me on this, I'm a doctor.&quot; <br /> <br /> &quot;It tastes just like sugar water!&quot; <br /> <br /> &quot;Incredible, isn't it?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T21:10:38-08:00","id":55205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55169#post55169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure what you're trying to say. The fact that those things don't fall under Zenith Abilities is exactly what I'm saying: there are too many things in an archetype to encompass with five Abilities. So they picked 5 which were appropriate and also left appropriate Abilities for the other Castes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was agreeing with you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T21:21:36-08:00","id":55216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drakhan Valane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55205#post55205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was agreeing with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! ...Well, that makes sense. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T21:48:29-08:00","id":55233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55201#post55201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Oh, yes. This is a tincture of Placebo Root. It's wonderful stuff - grows out in the wyld. It's basically a panacea. It'll cure anything that ails you. Trust me on this, I'm a doctor.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It tastes just like sugar water!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Incredible, isn't it?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I'm a herbalist, take off your cloth ~ &lt;3 &quot;. And then Twilight become the best Caste ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T21:53:17-08:00","id":55238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55169#post55169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Salty Dog is nice, but hardly a replacement for the whole Athletics Charm tree. If Athletics is an important part of your Eclipse sailor, you'll Favor it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Thing is, I've never said that a hypothetical faith healing Charm should be as good as &quot;all of Medicine put together&quot;. If you want to build a doctor, take Medicine, I agree. If I were outlining it's relative restrictions, I'd probably go with &quot;extremely Obvious&quot;, &quot;requires a congregation of faithful [Messianic keyword?]&quot;, probably &quot;extremely high mote cost&quot;, maybe tack on (higher) willpower costs... in many ways, a Sorcery-style counterpart to a Solar Medicine Charm, but not available to other splats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You'll notice I said &quot;healing and magic&quot;, two different things you have argued a priest should be able to do, not &quot;healing magic&quot;. </div> </div> </div>o.0<br /> <br /> All Charms are magic. I assumed a typo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ysadrel explains the foresight thing very well. As for prayers being useful against demons and undead... ignoring the Zenith ability to use Holy effects... I'll borrow your words: &quot;just take Occult, dumbass&quot;. In Creation, exorcism does not work because of the strength of your faith, it works because of your mystical knowledge. </div> </div> </div>Doesn't? Sure, duh, that's kind of a gimme - this is a &quot;what should be added&quot; thread. Kinda stupid to argue from &quot;how it is&quot;.<br /> <br /> Plus &quot;the way Creation works&quot; gets manhandled by Solar Charms on a regular basis. Love is absolutely breakable... unless the Intimacy is backed by Righteous Lion Defense, in which case no, no power in Creation can stop you loving them.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the strength of your faith (your Conviction in 2e) is absolutely relevant - channel Conviction, and you can do things you otherwise couldn't (bonus to rolls are handy things).<br /> <br /> And Solars turn things up to 11. Except this, and that's something that can be *fixed*. We don't need to attack all proposed changes &quot;because that's not how it currently works&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Less catholic, more... I want to say japanese/asian, but I'm basically working off anime here, not actual cultural knowledge, so I'll restrain myself to &quot;less catholic&quot;. Then again, a catholic exorcist should be well educated, and able to recite relevant prayers by heart, so there's some &quot;mystical&quot; knowledge right there, out of the grasp of the common man. Some random dude can occasionally keep evil at bay with faith alone, not helped by education, but that's getting outside of a discussion about priests. So, yeah, actually, you can argue that even catholic priests aren't just working off their Performance score. </div> </div> </div>Occult does not help you make Prayer Rolls in Exalted, remember? Not everything that involves knowing something is Lore or Occult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what I'm saying is... wait a minute, I got it... right, your character is &quot;infinitely more awesome&quot; when his &quot;mastery of the secrets of the universe&quot; allows him to &quot;accomplish such miracles&quot;. My opinion is objective truth, haven't we been over this already?<br /> <br /> More seriously, while I'm not interested by such Charms as you're suggesting, I've been arguing less against your basic thesis and more against your specific arguments (like your saying that a character who heals like Jesus but is using Medicine to do so is automatically a charlatan instead of a holy man, or your saying that the Cult background proves faith has power, or your saying faith would be worthless if it doesn't let you do miracles and that would be &quot;cynical shit&quot;). </div> </div> </div>- A character who heals with a touch using Medicine Charms isn't a charlatan. My objection there was that sticking within Zenith caste abilities only made it possible to make a charlatan - because people wanted Performance and religion to only be good for convincing people of things, rather than actually doing something in and of itself.<br /> <br /> (yes, the Immaculate Faith is mostly just an instrument of social control. This is an *excellent* reason for Zeniths to try and tear it down and replace it with a better religion... and it's extremely cynical to say that the only way a new religion would be better is 'because I'm in charge of it, so it's better for me')<br /> <br /> - Cult does show that in Creation in every edition, faith has had power, it's just been a very boring kind of power. So okay, that one I'll defend.<br /> <br /> - The cynical shit that drowned 2e was the endless deconstruction and realpolitik. Guess what? Prayer batteries is part of that. It's one of the aspects of Exalted that made popular perception of Creation being a crapsack world. Not &quot;not having miracles&quot;. Exalted goes miles in the other direction, going into loving detail about it's crackhead asshole deities.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the record, I still don't grasp why saying belief doesn't have magic power is cynical. I'm not religious, and that doesn't stop me from being optimistic in real life. </div> </div> </div>Like I said. &quot;There are gods, they are assholes, praying to them is giving them free chocolate and only weakling mortal losers would pray, Real Solars just beat people up until they do what they say&quot; isn't &quot;belief has no magic power&quot;, it's outright maltheism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55177#post55177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, a master psychologist who fools people into thinking they're healed <i>until it actually happens</i> is kind of a cool concept. I hope you won't mind if I steal it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I approve. Good luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T21:59:30-08:00","id":55240,"title":"","content":"Exalted has always been maltheistic. While there's a threshold of cynicism on somethings, it doesn't mean that some topics are free from cynical takes. Creation is meant to run on real politik and since early Exalted 1e has generally gone pretty harsh on religions in general. 2e had a lot of other stupid to it in addition to this (mostly through petty malice and incompetence more than realpolitik).<br /> <br /> The Cult of the Illumianted, Immaculate Order, the ancestor cult, and the Hundred Gods Heresy have always been varying range of control mechanism, conspiracy, political exploit or racket. Gods <i>are </i>generally assholes and not to be trusted to do their job for the sake of their job, because gods are people and people can be like that. WHen you're a powerful person and no one is about to tell you no, that becomes more likely the case.<br /> <br /> Prayer has been a boring effect, as a note, so that you don't go around bullying gods for the effect you need as you need it. It would otherwise turn prayer effectively into a form of wishcasting against STs who don't know how to say &quot;no&quot; and kind of undermine what you're supposed to do, whcih is do stuff your damned stuff because you're an Exalt.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T22:07:30-08:00","id":55246,"title":"","content":"So, 31 pages.<br /> <br /> Are y'all even talking about Performance anymore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T22:10:14-08:00","id":55248,"title":"","content":"Surprisingly, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T22:13:29-08:00","id":55249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55121#post55121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*points to the new Sail Charm that means you don't need to favour Athletics to do appropriate Sailor-y athletic stuff*</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is that faith healing is not really a major part of the mythology Exalted draws on. Sure, gods can heal you, but the imagery of a holy man laying his hands on you and declaring you healed in the name of the LORD is heavily associated with two things:<br /> <br /> One, Christian faith-healers in the real world. Exalted doesn't have that faith.<br /> <br /> And two, D&amp;D-style healbot clerics, which Exalted is deliberately trying to get away from.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, in Exalted's setting it <i>is</i> true that a decent sailor is expected to be able to keep his footing on the deck and climb the rigging. Hence, there's a Sail charm to do those things, but there's no Performance-based Faith Healing charm because Faith Healing isn't a major thing in this setting.<br /> <br /> (You could use Presence or Performance to help people with <i>spiritual</i> issues, or psychological ones. Soothing people's souls is part of the purpose of art. But making little Timmy walk again isn't something priests in Exalted's source materials generally do.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T22:19:15-08:00","id":55253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55238#post55238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- <b>The cynical shit that drowned 2e was the endless deconstruction and realpolitik</b>. Guess what? Prayer batteries is part of that. It's one of the aspects of Exalted that made popular perception of Creation being a crapsack world. Not &quot;not having miracles&quot;. Exalted goes miles in the other direction, going into loving detail about it's crackhead asshole deities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> I'll take a moment to object to this. I've been reminded to take another look at the 1e materials that came with the kickstarter, recently, and I've gotta say, they make 2e look cheerful and pollyanna. The kinship to the Old World Of Insufficient Interest is instantly obvious in a way that only the deeply annoying cover copy was in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T22:52:38-08:00","id":55266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55253#post55253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> I'll take a moment to object to this. I've been reminded to take another look at the 1e materials that came with the kickstarter, recently, and I've gotta say, they make 2e look cheerful and pollyanna. The kinship to the Old World Of Insufficient Interest is instantly obvious in a way that only the deeply annoying cover copy was in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. 2e's issue wasn't just the cynicism and realpolitik. Exalted always has had that. It is that it was generally bad at it, undermined what was established before or hamfisted at how it tried to do it (often with a lot of shock value or shitty people being super evil instead of just normally shitty).<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T22:58:30-08:00","id":55268,"title":"","content":"I still try to wrap my head about the differences between Presence and Performance.<br /> One of which is for me:<br /> Performance can be ritualized exchange of words (commoner-priest / priest-god / knight-king / diplomat-diplomat / summoner-demon / actor-audience), where Presence is more spontaneous. A little bit like Melee (you have to prepare a weapon, here it is the ritual) and Brawl (just punch and be good at it).<br /> <br /> I think Performance does not only to make a character very good at this, but also motivates this behavior in other people, the character talks to (giving them appropriate penalties if they don't oblige).<br /> Performance might also help to find the perfect moment to switch from ritual to personal exchange (&quot;Let's talk about this in private&quot;), or make deliberate changes in a ritual (i.e. giving a role in a play the resemblance the king's advisor), which might offset people (feeling honored, or irritated) giving the character appropriate bonuses.<br /> <br /> Charms could help in the localization of plays and rituals (knowing that you shouldn't dress the hero of a play in blue in this region, as it implies weakness) and in the enforcing or breaking of ritualized behavior.<br /> <br /> I know, I know, this might overlap with Socialize or even Occult, but somehow everything overlaps slightly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://owncloud.scaenicus.net/index.php/s/saLcZXhVcOu0j3W/download?path=%2F&amp;files=ScaenicusBacked_big.png&amp;downloadStartSecret=mflqpfu2cd8\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/ScaenicusBacked.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1491-scaenicus","name":"Scaenicus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1491_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T23:13:06-08:00","id":55272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55238#post55238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. Thing is, I've never said that a hypothetical faith healing Charm should be as good as &quot;all of Medicine put together&quot;. If you want to build a doctor, take Medicine, I agree. If I were outlining it's relative restrictions, I'd probably go with &quot;extremely Obvious&quot;, &quot;requires a congregation of faithful [Messianic keyword?]&quot;, probably &quot;extremely high mote cost&quot;, maybe tack on (higher) willpower costs... in many ways, a Sorcery-style counterpart to a Solar Medicine Charm, but not available to other splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sail only gives you very basic Athletics effects (not even as good as basic Graceful Crane Stance). If all you can get with Messianic healing is super basic stuff instead of healing cripples and lepers and stuff, there isn't much point. If you CAN heal cripples and lepers, then apart form Contagion-Curing Touch and Instant Treatment Methodology, it really IS &quot;all of Medicine put together&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> o.0<br /> <br /> All Charms are magic. I assumed a typo. </div> </div> </div>Do I really have to do this? &quot;Magic&quot; defined as Occult-specific stuff like thaumaturgy and sorcery and such, not <i>every single thing about Creation</i>, which, yes, are magic from our point of view, but are just how things work in Exalted. I'm just gonna go ahead and quote you for the sake of completeness:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In short, Occult is the &quot;real magic&quot; skill of the setting, and the priests are left with a &quot;charlatan&quot; badge, because... why? Why do sorcerors get real magic and priests get to be phonies? </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Doesn't? Sure, duh, that's kind of a gimme - this is a &quot;what should be added&quot; thread. Kinda stupid to argue from &quot;how it is&quot;.<br /> <br /> Plus &quot;the way Creation works&quot; gets manhandled by Solar Charms on a regular basis. Love is absolutely breakable... unless the Intimacy is backed by Righteous Lion Defense, in which case no, no power in Creation can stop you loving them.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the strength of your faith (your Conviction in 2e) is absolutely relevant - channel Conviction, and you can do things you otherwise couldn't (bonus to rolls are handy things).<br /> <br /> And Solars turn things up to 11. Except this, and that's something that can be *fixed*. We don't need to attack all proposed changes &quot;because that's not how it currently works&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Oh, I've never said faith isn't something that makes you DO stuff. I'm gonna quote myself because heck, why not, this message is already bursting with quotes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That doesn't mean faith doesn't have power. It doesn't have power in the &quot;make miracles happen&quot; way, but it has power in the &quot;make people act&quot; way. And people have done some pretty cool stuff with religion as a motivation. That is a faith I feel has a place in Creation, even if plenty of people don't have it. And if faithful people can do awesome stuff in our world where (I believe) there are no miracles, then surely they can do the same in a Creation with the miracle of Exaltation, even if there aren't any others? </div> </div> </div>Also, &quot;Love is breakable&quot; isn't &quot;the way Creation works&quot;. Love is just another emotion with no particular power. Solars can protect it like they can protect any of their Intimacies. People can use it as motivation for spending a Virtue channel or a willpower point. Blaque's point when he mentioned Love is that it's not <i>special</i>. Rather like faith. Or, heck, anger. Hating someone really hard lets you channel your Conviction just as much. That doesn't mean anger has particular supernatural significance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Occult does not help you make Prayer Rolls in Exalted, remember? Not everything that involves knowing something is Lore or Occult. </div> </div> </div>My point being that Occult helps you with thaumaturgy, which includes the Art of Warding and... Exorcism. And that you can argue that a catholic priest warding off a demon is using Occult, not Performance, since his ability to do so comes from his knowledge, not his ability to make a good show.<br /> <br /> Since we're being all chummy and talking: did you know the exorcist statblock in the core is a master of the Art of Warding, and yet the Art of Warding isn't in the core? It's in Oadenol's Codex. I think it's amusing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - A character who heals with a touch using Medicine Charms isn't a charlatan. My objection there was that sticking within Zenith caste abilities only made it possible to make a charlatan - because people wanted Performance and religion to only be good for convincing people of things, rather than actually doing something in and of itself. </div> </div> </div>I've already mentioned I consider Favored Abilities to be crucial in refining your character concept, so I'll spare you a rehash.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Cult does show that in Creation in every edition, faith has had power, it's just been a very boring kind of power. So okay, that one I'll defend. </div> </div> </div>Except, again, that it's not the faith that gives the power, it's the prayer. The ritual. Your whole Cult can think you're an asshole but as long as they're saying the words it'll work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - The cynical shit that drowned 2e was the endless deconstruction and realpolitik. Guess what? Prayer batteries is part of that. It's one of the aspects of Exalted that made popular perception of Creation being a crapsack world. Not &quot;not having miracles&quot;. Exalted goes miles in the other direction, going into loving detail about it's crackhead asshole deities. </div> </div> </div>Gods being assholes is kind of a different issue. Given the two relevant chapter fictions we've had so far (a field god sacrificing himself, and a river god hurting mortals out of grief rather than cruelty), I rather think it's not going to be universal in Ex3. Though there are still going to be exploitative asshole gods, just as there are exploitative asshole people in real life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T23:33:02-08:00","id":55289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55240#post55240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted has always been maltheistic. While there's a threshold of cynicism on somethings, it doesn't mean that some topics are free from cynical takes. Creation is meant to run on real politik and since early Exalted 1e has generally gone pretty harsh on religions in general. 2e had a lot of other stupid to it in addition to this (mostly through petty malice and incompetence more than realpolitik).<br /> <br /> The Cult of the Illumianted, Immaculate Order, the ancestor cult, and the Hundred Gods Heresy have always been varying range of control mechanism, conspiracy, political exploit or racket. Gods <i>are </i>generally assholes and not to be trusted to do their job for the sake of their job, because gods are people and people can be like that. WHen you're a powerful person and no one is about to tell you no, that becomes more likely the case.<br /> <br /> Prayer has been a boring effect, as a note, so that you don't go around bullying gods for the effect you need as you need it. It would otherwise turn prayer effectively into a form of wishcasting against STs who don't know how to say &quot;no&quot; and kind of undermine what you're supposed to do, whcih is do stuff your damned stuff because you're an Exalt.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh sod this. Literally from my very first post mentioning faith healing I've been advocating for specific Charms that do specific effects through the power of the Solar, not fucking wishcasting or ANYTHING to do with getting the gods of the setting to do anything. Congratulations, your sheer stubborn refusal to read a damn word I've written has convinced me there's no bloody point continuing to post. Well done, Blaque, well bloody done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T23:40:45-08:00","id":55291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scaenicus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55268#post55268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still try to wrap my head about the differences between Presence and Performance.<br /> One of which is for me:<br /> Performance can be ritualized exchange of words (commoner-priest / priest-god / knight-king / diplomat-diplomat / summoner-demon / actor-audience), where Presence is more spontaneous. A little bit like Melee (you have to prepare a weapon, here it is the ritual) and Brawl (just punch and be good at it).<br /> <br /> I think Performance does not only to make a character very good at this, but also motivates this behavior in other people, the character talks to (giving them appropriate penalties if they don't oblige).<br /> Performance might also help to find the perfect moment to switch from ritual to personal exchange (&quot;Let's talk about this in private&quot;), or make deliberate changes in a ritual (i.e. giving a role in a play the resemblance the king's advisor), which might offset people (feeling honored, or irritated) giving the character appropriate bonuses.<br /> <br /> Charms could help in the localization of plays and rituals (knowing that you shouldn't dress the hero of a play in blue in this region, as it implies weakness) and in the enforcing or breaking of ritualized behavior.<br /> <br /> I know, I know, this might overlap with Socialize or even Occult, but somehow everything overlaps slightly.</div> </div> </div> </div>We actually been having a good discussion about this over at <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/53472-performance-v-presence\">Performance v. Presence</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T02:04:00-08:00","id":55336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55196#post55196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Original application of Contagion-Curing Touch, the way I see it. I'm having a blast thinking up this social Twilight with such a keen insight on people he can do this sort of thing. This just displaced my Eclipse shaman concept as the first character I want to play in Ex3.</div> </div> </div> </div>So basically a practitioner of headology?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T02:44:15-08:00","id":55347,"title":"","content":"I do think the more miracluous effects should fall under Sorcery... though they did mention that Sorcery actions would be about &quot;building up&quot; the mote cost of the spell, instead of using pools, I think.<br /> <br /> In that case a Charm which lets you channel your Cult into a Sorcery mote-building action could be thematic/interesting? Not sure if it would fall under Occult or Performance though... mostly because Performance seems to only cover the Prayer action, rather than faith/religion as a whole. Which again, is an implication that prayer is a show, not (necessarily) an act of faith imho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T05:49:27-08:00","id":55394,"title":"","content":"I consider Performance based faith healing to be custom charm territory.<br /> I'm sure someone could make it work for their character concept but I don't think it's a good idea to put a charm like that in the corebook to shape first-time readers impressions of Solar Exalted and the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T06:23:24-08:00","id":55412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55114#post55114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You probably didn't understand what I said.<br /> <br /> The sheet doesn't have Drive, Firearms, Gardening, or Scrimshaw. These things are not central to how the game is played, or important enough to the play experience that they be there. Some of them are actively inappropriate. So, what is Prayer? Is it inappropriate, or simply not central, or somewhere in between? That is not conjecture, it is a developmental fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I definitely understood what you said. Now you're goalpost shifting by adding comparisons with two abilities that don't exist at all in Exalted because they're covered by Sail/Ride and Archery, respectively, and two that are pretty clearly applications of other Abilities, like scrimshaw with Craft. I think it's you who don't understand what I'm saying, so I'll clarify with as much detail as I find polite.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying prayer should be given as much attention as, say, applications of combat skills. I'm not saying prayer should be given as much attention as the social influence system. I'm not saying it should be its own ability, Prayer, and, in fact, I'm not talking specifically about prayer at all.<br /> <br /> What I'm talking about is having a system somewhere in the setting description portions that talk about how normal religion works in Creation. It's obviously a pretty important point that needs to be addressed, since a number of people in this very thread were making a LOT of false assumptions about it, and I don't expect even 5% of 3e's eventual players to ever read this thread. I'm saying religion, the interaction between deities and mortals, and so forth should have a section somewhere at all.<br /> <br /> If it's even half as long as the literally eight pages that were dedicated to currency exchange rates, banking, investment, and accounting that were the first eight pages of the Panoply chapter of the Core Rulebook in 2e, that should be more than sufficient to give people a pretty good idea of what the average interaction between a farming town and their harvest god entails, what the organized faith of Ahlat looks like, and how the Immaculate Order changes that interaction when it rolls into town.<br /> <br /> So, I'm not saying that prayer needs to be elevated to the level of its own Ability. I'm not, and have never been, saying that prayer should be taking center stage in the Performance Ability. Hell, I haven't even been talking about actual prayer for a while now. I'm talking about religion, and seeing it addressed and described some way in the core book as a general explanation of an element of the setting.<br /> <br /> Do you understand now? Or do I probably still just not understand what you said?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T07:44:28-08:00","id":55437,"title":"","content":"Well they're doing that. They've got Grabowski writing sections on both religion and economics, as I recall. So...you should be pleased with what you're getting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T08:53:56-08:00","id":55480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55437#post55437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well they're doing that. They've got Grabowski writing sections on both religion and economics, as I recall. So...you should be pleased with what you're getting?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying I was displeased, I was just explaining what the point I was actually making was. It was something that really only bore one or two sentences, but after repeated misunderstandings, I thought I should explain in fullest detail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T09:28:57-08:00","id":55503,"title":"","content":"Okay, I've reached out some feelers to one of the players in my game who's been playing a Performance-centric Zenith for years. I'll see if she has any contributions that escape the incredibly dense black hole of Prayer charms that we seem to have found ourselves in.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, what John's said has kind of reframed what I'm thinking and made me think a bit more of what I'd like out of Performance.<br /> <br /> The Solar performer should fascinate.<br /> <br /> Crowds should gather as he plays, and he can form a congregation drumming on an empty wooden tub in the poorest streets of Nexus.It won't be a politically, economically, or even particularly physically powerful congregation, but their awe of him would be genuine.<br /> <br /> She should be able to call others to join in her revels. Her ecstatic dance beckons, and her assembly falls into step with her without meaning to. Even gods might follow, for her power is such that they can recognize their greater in her. She does not command their obedience--that may come after, through more blunt application of personality, or more tangible tools--but she has their attention.<br /> <br /> His touch is narcotic.<br /> <br /> Her words will outlive her by a thousand years or more; some will say that they have lost their power, for surely see how they no longer call the gods to order, and see how a child's rough emulation of her song no longer brings women and men to tears as was written. Yet that boy will pass it down to his sons, as they will their sons after them. Perhaps in time the origins will be forgotten completely, or the lyrics will fall away and an achingly poignant melody remains if only as a whistle or a hum. But it does live on, less changed and far longer than it had any right to.<br /> <br /> It is immortality in a notes; some Wyld Hunts have put villages to the sword after taking down the Anathema; it is not to kill the people, but to stop the music.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T11:15:54-08:00","id":55567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54005#post54005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please note that if you dropped Michael Jackson into the outskirts of Creation and had him dance, the effect would not be &quot;wow cool, he can dance really well.&quot; It would shake the foundations of belief. They would think he was a divine madman, surely touched by the gods. His dancing would provoke mania, fear, rage, awe. The people of Creation have never seen such movements before. They would be provoked by them. They would conclude that he was possessed by demons or by the spirits of the air and sky. If he claimed &quot;I am the representative of X god,&quot; they would be far more inclined to believe him, because he dances as if possessed.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54346#post54346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then, should Solar Performance have a Charm that allows a nearby spirit to possess him as he sings and/or dances?<br /> <br /> The spirit is already present, so &quot;prayers aren't heard&quot; is preserved. In the previous two Editions and presumably the next, most spirits won't have any of the Possession Charms that would let them enter into a willing or unwilling host.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone think this suggestion of mine is a good or bad idea? Any disagreements, or reasons why?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=54544#post54544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'sacrifice' gave way to tithing as the Roman Catholic Church became more powerful and priests figured they may as well enjoy the sacrificed animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, animal sacrifice gave way much sooner than that, given that Jesus Christ's death on the cross made any further blood sacrifices pointless. And even before then, the Jews were expected to tithe to the temple. (Also, most animal sacrifices were <i>scripturally intended</i> to be eaten by the temple priesthood anyway.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 01-22-2014, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T11:37:29-08:00","id":55582,"title":"","content":"I'd kind of prefer spirit possession (in either direction) being Occult. Nothing says you can't Use an Occult Charm before you start dancing. Or during, depending on combo rules and whether you're even using charms on your dance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T11:53:46-08:00","id":55588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drakhan Valane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55582#post55582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd kind of prefer spirit possession (in either direction) being Occult. Nothing says you can't Use an Occult Charm before you start dancing. Or during, depending on combo rules and whether you're even using charms on your dance.</div> </div> </div> </div>A valid point, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Or... hmm. With an Occult Charm, you can allow a spirit to possess you, even if they don't have the Charm to do so, but that doesn't help if they don't want to do it. With a Performance Charm, you can inspire the spirit to accept the invitation of your Occult Charm when otherwise they might not see a reason to go through with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T11:55:59-08:00","id":55592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55588#post55588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A valid point, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Or... hmm. With an Occult Charm, you can allow a spirit to possess you, even if they don't have the Charm to do so, but that doesn't help if they don't want to do it. With a Performance Charm, you can inspire the spirit to accept the invitation of your Occult Charm when otherwise they might not see a reason to go through with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't think you need a specific Performance charm to do that. I'd actually hope that's something you can use a persuasive Presence charm for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T12:07:10-08:00","id":55599,"title":"","content":"I think of Performance Charms as magic that influences emotions and perceptions. Hmm ... what if you use a Performance Charm to inspire your followers to dancing until they achieve a trance state that eases possession by opening up their minds, maybe have them spend a willpower instead of having the spirit spend Essence, etc.? Vodoun rituals?<br /> <br /> I think hypnotizing your audience and otherwise affecting their state of mind is definitely in design space for Performance, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T14:05:43-08:00","id":55678,"title":"","content":"Haven't gone through the giant thread as of yet so I maybe reiterating something. Please forgive me. <br /> <br /> For me, I have little problem with Solar Performance. It works really well though I wish it had more enhancement powers (think super bard) and a little less mind assault (emotional control and memory erase). <br /> <br /> The thing for me is that I am less concerned with Solar charms. I trust you guys on that utterly. I am more concerned with Solars as a whole thematically. For a long time, I didn't like them. I had always from the 2E core book gotten the idea that they were the generic &quot;awesome&quot; splat. After a conversation about the current game I am running. We noticed something. The main book in 2E is really only relevant up until 50 exp or so. We see Solars fighting minor gods and bandits and that is about it. Fast forward to Dreams and suddenly they at 3000+ exp are all douche bags. <br /> <br /> Nothing in those books communicates greatness. It does not have the same resonance as a Heracles or Gilgamesh. <br /> <br /> I think for me, I want the performance charms to reflect what has excited me about Solars as of late. The sheer greatness. The unlimited power that any one of them could be the next superman OR the next doomsday (power level in their relative setting analogy). I want the charms to be something that an effectively cosmological force would have. What does performance look like from the perspective of epic greatness. If it is just neat tricks and powers, that is one thing. But I want the charms to from any ability to excite me about the splat. In this case, communicate the granduer or horror that Solars could be. <br /> <br /> I know that is abstract. Hope it helps. <br /> <br /> Hokyo Joshua","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1613-hokyoroshi","name":"HokyoRoshi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1613_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T14:07:48-08:00","id":55681,"title":"","content":"When did this become about possession, and what does dancing &quot;like a man possessed&quot; have to do with actual possession?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T14:21:35-08:00","id":55691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55681#post55681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When did this become about possession, and what does dancing &quot;like a man possessed&quot; have to do with actual possession?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually being possessed would sure explain dancing like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T14:40:12-08:00","id":55708,"title":"","content":"So, talked to the player, and she is definitely of the &quot;My performance should be able to work miracles&quot; school, specifically citing some of the things Link does with the Ocarina and the Wind Waker. That's been done to death here, so I'm not going to revisit that topic. <br /> <br /> That said, she was much more specific in mentioning another charm that I do wonder about<b></b>: Does Demon-Wracking Glory have a place in this? Can the cry and ululation of the divine madman drive out wicked spirits, and bring unclean souls to their knees in pain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T15:07:31-08:00","id":55728,"title":"","content":"This might be out of place. But I really want to FUS RO DAH some motherfuckers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Might be more of a DB than Solar thing, but still wanna put it out there somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T15:31:25-08:00","id":55745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55708#post55708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, talked to the player, and she is definitely of the &quot;My performance should be able to work miracles&quot; school, specifically citing some of the things Link does with the Ocarina and the Wind Waker. That's been done to death here, so I'm not going to revisit that topic.<br /> <br /> That said, she was much more specific in mentioning another charm that I do wonder about<b></b>: Does Demon-Wracking Glory have a place in this? Can the cry and ululation of the divine madman drive out wicked spirits, and bring unclean souls to their knees in pain?</div> </div> </div> </div>I gotta admit, the book <i>does</i> say that Solars can do things like yell so hard that their opponents burst into flames, yet those kinds of effects were never visited in the charms chapter, for presence or performance anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T15:53:00-08:00","id":55761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55745#post55745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gotta admit, the book <i>does</i> say that Solars can do things like yell so hard that their opponents burst into flames, yet those kinds of effects were never visited in the charms chapter, for presence or performance anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a performance charm (in Abyssals IIRC) that can cause damage to enemies with performance. It was an upgrade from the special effects charm.<br /> <br /> In other non-typical areas, there's also the whole of medicine where you determine your style, which can include yelling at people to man up and thus healing them of injuries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T16:03:06-08:00","id":55770,"title":"","content":"Sharing this without comment...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cI know, too, that death is the only god who comes when you call.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><a href=\"http://www.goodreads.com/author/show/3619.Roger_Zelazny\" target=\"_blank\">Roger Zelazny</a><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, </span></span></span><i><a href=\"http://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/18319\" target=\"_blank\">Frost &amp; Fire</a></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T16:21:52-08:00","id":55786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55728#post55728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might be out of place. But I really want to FUS RO DAH some motherfuckers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Might be more of a DB than Solar thing, but still wanna put it out there somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </di