l effects charm.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, that's the charm Demon-Wracking Glory (not Demon-Wracking Shout) is a Mirror of. Or course the mirror concept is going away, but the charm is a legitimate idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","user":"Mockery","date":". 01-22-2014, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T17:02:31-08:00","id":55813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drakhan Valane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55798#post55798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate Skyrim. &lt;_&lt;</div> </div> </div> </div><i>I will fight you naked</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T17:04:00-08:00","id":55816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55813#post55813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>I will fight you naked</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>I would rather you didn't.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T18:30:05-08:00","id":55877,"title":"","content":"So I guess my question with regards to the &quot;prayer is for chumps&quot; situation is, why should that mean Zeniths are about making prayer more effective? Shouldn't Zeniths, then, be out to enslave the gods and make them into mindless automata like least gods are? Why wouldn't &quot;prayer Charms&quot; be about forcing the god in question to bend to your will and only receive compensation at your mercy? I'm not especially fond of the humans-gods relationship being this bluntly antagonistic, mind you, but if leading the masses in prayer is literally nothing but bad for them, what part of being priests makes Zenith Castes anything but awful for Creation? Making the cults about themselves isn't exactly a step up from this, and no other Caste has such a morally bankrupt presentation about their basic function. I suppose there's the fact that the Solars were created by the Unconquered Sun, so it's entirely possible that Zeniths are in fact just meant to enforce his protection racket, but that's still an indictment against their very existence that none of the other Castes receive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T19:07:57-08:00","id":55893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55877#post55877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I guess my question with regards to the &quot;prayer is for chumps&quot; situation is, why should that mean Zeniths are about making prayer more effective? Shouldn't Zeniths, then, be out to enslave the gods and make them into mindless automata like least gods are? Why wouldn't &quot;prayer Charms&quot; be about forcing the god in question to bend to your will and only receive compensation at your mercy? I'm not especially fond of the humans-gods relationship being this bluntly antagonistic, mind you, but if leading the masses in prayer is literally nothing but bad for them, what part of being priests makes Zenith Castes anything but awful for Creation? Making the cults about themselves isn't exactly a step up from this, and no other Caste has such a morally bankrupt presentation about their basic function. I suppose there's the fact that the Solars were created by the Unconquered Sun, so it's entirely possible that Zeniths are in fact just meant to enforce his protection racket, but that's still an indictment against their very existence that none of the other Castes receive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume because if pushed too hard to logical conclusions (if I want to just get something I'll get the god of randomt ask to do it for me) it turns prayer into an elaborate form of wishcasting, which is bad for the game and against the magic paradigm we have.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T19:31:55-08:00","id":55901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55877#post55877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I guess my question with regards to the &quot;prayer is for chumps&quot; situation is, why should that mean Zeniths are about making prayer more effective? Shouldn't Zeniths, then, be out to enslave the gods and make them into mindless automata like least gods are? Why wouldn't &quot;prayer Charms&quot; be about forcing the god in question to bend to your will and only receive compensation at your mercy? I'm not especially fond of the humans-gods relationship being this bluntly antagonistic, mind you, but if leading the masses in prayer is literally nothing but bad for them, what part of being priests makes Zenith Castes anything but awful for Creation? Making the cults about themselves isn't exactly a step up from this, and no other Caste has such a morally bankrupt presentation about their basic function. I suppose there's the fact that the Solars were created by the Unconquered Sun, so it's entirely possible that Zeniths are in fact just meant to enforce his protection racket, but that's still an indictment against their very existence that none of the other Castes receive.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why we have the difference between Priests--which a Zenith can be--and Prophets, which all Zeniths apparently <i>are.</i><br /> <br /> Prayer to the gods is fine, on a sheer metaphysical level. However, the Gods that are powerful enough to pray to are frequently powerful enough to engage in a nasty game of attrition: they may not go to any particular lengths to make your life better if you pray, but they'll make your life miserable if you don't.<br /> <br /> The Zenith is the Prophet. He brings the word to the people, not the other way around. If he desires to bring the Gods to justice--and he may well--then as previously discussed in this thread, he grabs that god by the collar and punches it or sexes it or pays it off or whatever needs to happen to make that deity do their job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T21:08:03-08:00","id":55923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55877#post55877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I guess my question with regards to the &quot;prayer is for chumps&quot; situation is, why should that mean Zeniths are about making prayer more effective? Shouldn't Zeniths, then, be out to enslave the gods and make them into mindless automata like least gods are? Why wouldn't &quot;prayer Charms&quot; be about forcing the god in question to bend to your will and only receive compensation at your mercy? I'm not especially fond of the humans-gods relationship being this bluntly antagonistic, mind you, but if leading the masses in prayer is literally nothing but bad for them, what part of being priests makes Zenith Castes anything but awful for Creation? Making the cults about themselves isn't exactly a step up from this, and no other Caste has such a morally bankrupt presentation about their basic function. I suppose there's the fact that the Solars were created by the Unconquered Sun, so it's entirely possible that Zeniths are in fact just meant to enforce his protection racket, but that's still an indictment against their very existence that none of the other Castes receive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I can put my finger on it, but those kind of Prayer Charms sound more like how Sidereals would do it. For some reason, I think Zeniths would be more naturally talented at amping up the power, frequency, and fervor of prayers and then holding that as a very tempting bargaining chip in godly negotiations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T21:58:57-08:00","id":55948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55786#post55786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also would love this, but to me this is clearly a Linguistics charm, harnessing the power of words and drawing out their meaning to make the effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, sure, using the magic inherent in the draconic words of power to achieve a variety of effects (of which Fus Ro Dah is only one) is Linguistics. Shouting SO DAMN HARD you kill people isn't Linguistics, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T22:02:01-08:00","id":55950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55901#post55901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is why we have the difference between Priests--which a Zenith can be--and Prophets, which all Zeniths apparently <i>are.</i><br /> <br /> Prayer to the gods is fine, on a sheer metaphysical level. However, the Gods that are powerful enough to pray to are frequently powerful enough to engage in a nasty game of attrition: they may not go to any particular lengths to make your life better if you pray, but they'll make your life miserable if you don't.<br /> <br /> The Zenith is the Prophet. He brings the word to the people, not the other way around. If he desires to bring the Gods to justice--and he may well--then as previously discussed in this thread, he grabs that god by the collar and punches it or sexes it or pays it off or whatever needs to happen to make that deity do their job.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then they should probably not be called Priest-Kings, if they aren't intended to invoke the idea of playing a priest in the minds of prospective players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T22:06:51-08:00","id":55953,"title":"","content":"Priest-King is only one role they can fill. However it is also a valid one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T22:15:15-08:00","id":55956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jorlem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55950#post55950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then they should probably not be called Priest-Kings, if they aren't intended to invoke the idea of playing a priest in the minds of prospective players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except Priest-King sounds neat, so they should totally keep it. And priest-kings are not like simple priests, because they are also kings. And the idea is more &quot;priest of the Unconquered Sun&quot;, which doesn't really involve the same social role as mortal priests because the UCS doesn't have the same relationship with mortals as your average Terrestrial god. Being a mortal priest is being sort of bureaucrat/negotiator. Being a priest of the UCS is, well... There's no negotiation involved because he's not threatening to smite you and you can't bribe him for blessings. He already Exalted you, which is pretty much the extant of what he intends to do. Now it's your duty to use it.<br /> <br /> Basically, priest-king = prophet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","user":"Kazorh","date":". 01-23-2014, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T22:23:07-08:00","id":55958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55956#post55956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, priest-king = prophet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prophet, Leader of Men (and Women, etc.), All Around Badass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T22:45:23-08:00","id":55970,"title":"","content":"I had completely forgotten Demon-Wracking Glory was a thing until people started talking about it here. It <i>does</i> let you do bone-breaking shouts and gouts of holy fire, so I guess that's that for the &quot;things that are in-theme for Solar Charms&quot;. It also lets you kill demons with prayers to the Sun.<br /> <br /> I tend not to search for Solar Charms in the Abyssal book, which I suppose is a failing on my part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T23:54:34-08:00","id":55982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55970#post55970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had completely forgotten Demon-Wracking Glory was a thing until people started talking about it here. It <i>does</i> let you do bone-breaking shouts and gouts of holy fire, so I guess that's that for the &quot;things that are in-theme for Solar Charms&quot;. It also lets you kill demons with prayers to the Sun.<br /> <br /> I tend not to search for Solar Charms in the Abyssal book, which I suppose is a failing on my part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Too bad the charm is way too busy with 3 different effects though, it would be so much better if it's just modeled itself after other Essence-weapon charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T05:08:37-08:00","id":56049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55970#post55970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had completely forgotten Demon-Wracking Glory was a thing until people started talking about it here. It <i>does</i> let you do bone-breaking shouts and gouts of holy fire, so I guess that's that for the &quot;things that are in-theme for Solar Charms&quot;. It also lets you kill demons with prayers to the Sun. I tend not to search for Solar Charms in the Abyssal book, which I suppose is a failing on my part.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>The first place I <b>check</b> for Solar Charms</i> is non-Solar splatbooks!<br /> <br /> So, John, while you might not be an Adventure Time! fan, I found a relevant quote on the show. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goliad</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Princess. Bee cares not for flower. If getting pollen hurt or killed flower, bee would not care. Bee is stronger than flower. Goliad is stronger than bee. Goliad is stronger than all.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T07:45:49-08:00","id":56120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=55956#post55956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, priest-king = prophet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure that no one would actually describe most of, say, the biblical prophets as looking anything like &quot;priest-kings,&quot; so I don't think this is a good summation. (Those being, probably, the guys the majority of the fanbase would think of first when we say &quot;prophet&quot; - first impressions matter here.)<br /> <br /> Let's divorce things from the conversation a little bit: what is a priest-king? He's someone who fulfills two roles, and his fulfillment of these roles is <i>linked</i>. He rules the people; he stands for the people before the gods; he rules the people <i>because</i> he stands for the people before the gods. That's part of the core Zenith identity, as currently presented.<br /> <br /> And hey! Zeniths actually are pretty good at becoming kings, in past editions, because they've got all those crazy &quot;Follow me!&quot; abilities. They're also pretty good being priests, because that's (a) a caste power and (b) at least in 2e, also related to your crazy &quot;Follow me!&quot; abilities. We see this in the signature Zeniths that show up. Panther - for all that Panther is not a good signature character - is distinctly the one on a mission from (a) god. The Hierophant is <i>both</i>: intercessor before the Unconquered Sun, and person of great authority in the Deliberative <i>because</i> of that role.<br /> <br /> I'm not defending these signature characters, but I am saying - look, the game has been pretty clear in its signalling here in the past. That doesn't mean it can't change, but it means if it's going to, we need to recognize that this is a change. Zeniths as &quot;the guys who don't really intercede with the gods, but do go punch them, which... I guess anyone else could also do just as well&quot; is a <i>big change</i> in that identity, and it's one that dumps priest-king as an archetype.<br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> All that said, there is a real problem here with prayer becoming random magic wish-granting. But that problem is inherent in the current structure of how prayer works, and especially for how it works relative to the <i>little</i> gods - the ones you might actually try to bribe with it. And everything else aside, that really, really needs to be fixed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T11:48:03-08:00","id":56261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pretty sure that no one would actually describe most of, say, the biblical prophets as looking anything like &quot;priest-kings,&quot; so I don't think this is a good summation. (Those being, probably, the guys the majority of the fanbase would think of first when we say &quot;prophet&quot; - first impressions matter here.) </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure none of the biblical prophets are Solar Exalted who live in Creation, nor do they live in any sort of pulp fantasy universe where an expression like &quot;priest-king&quot; is appropriate and thematic (rather like sorcerer-king). I'm also pretty sure the Christian God isn't the Unconquered Sun.<br /> <br /> I'm also pretty sure Jesus is actually referred to as the King of the Jews, so even though God doesn't have the same thing with leadership that Sol does, Jesus is still imbued by divine authority over mortals.<br /> <br /> I'm also pretty sure that neither Panther nor the Hierophant act in any way like it's been established that mortal priests do. Panther is out on a mission for God, rather like some sort of... prophet. The Hierophant is an intercessor for the Unconquered Sun, not for the myriad Terrestrial gods (who are generally beneath the notice of an elder Solar and had better do what they're told, because they definitely don't want to get punched by the Hierophant).<br /> <br /> You'll notice that a main point of my previous post was that a Zenith being a priest of the Unconquered Sun is fundamentally different from a mortal being a priest of the local head god, because the local head god has a relationship with the people that is fundamentally different from the relationship the Sun has with the people. In fact, a Zenith who is a priest of the Unconquered Sun is more like a prophet, in the sense of a singular individual imbued with great power and authority from On High to effect change, rather than a member of the temple bureaucracy. The mortal and the Zenith are both priests, but what it means in practice is different, because one of them is a mortal and the other is a Zenith.<br /> <br /> So, if you consider that Panther and the Hierophant are good enough examples of the priest-king, then there is no change at all. This is exactly the same thing that has been going on in previous editions.<br /> <br /> Just in case you want to use that argument: yes, ALL Solars are singular individuals imbued with great power and authority. You'll also notice that all Solars are warriors of the gods created to overthrow the Primordials, and that doesn't stop Dawns from being the warrior caste. The Zenith are those most meant to evoke the particular theme of wielding divine authority, helped along by their caste abilities (like the &quot;Follow me!&quot; Charms, as you mention).<br /> <br /> Putting emphasis on the punching is also misleading: Zenith do have social Charms. The point is that when they intercede with the gods, they don't do so as supplicants. The relationship between the mortal priest and the god is inherently unequal because the god is always more personally powerful than the mortal, even if we're talking about a situation where the mortal has enough political power to get concessions out of the god. A Zenith, however, is mostly going to be equal or superior to any gods he intercedes with on behalf of mortals. Even if he uses diplomacy, the fact that he COULD punch the god changes the relationship.<br /> <br /> tl;dr: I meant both priest-king and prophet as they're being use to describe Zeniths, not in all cases ever.<br /> <br /> Was there anything else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","user":"Kazorh","date":". 01-23-2014, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T12:28:46-08:00","id":56287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding FUS RO DAH:<br /> <br /> Yes, I want to finally see the bone-breaking shout which is mentioned in the 2e core as a 'thematic' ability but never actually used. I don't know if it should actually go in performance, but it might as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's not neglect the &quot;blinding flash of solar light&quot; trick either. I feel that such a thing is a natural advancement from Phantom Conjuring Performance, especially if we still get Demon-Wracking Glory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T13:07:31-08:00","id":56306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=56261#post56261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure none of the biblical prophets are Solar Exalted who live in Creation, nor do they live in any sort of pulp fantasy universe where an expression like &quot;priest-king&quot; is appropriate and thematic (rather like sorcerer-king). I'm also pretty sure the Christian God isn't the Unconquered Sun.<br /> <br /> I'm also pretty sure Jesus is actually referred to as the King of the Jews, so even though God doesn't have the same thing with leadership that Sol does, Jesus is still imbued by divine authority over mortals.<br /> <br /> I'm also pretty sure that neither Panther nor the Hierophant act in any way like it's been established that mortal priests do. Panther is out on a mission for God, rather like some sort of... prophet. The Hierophant is an intercessor for the Unconquered Sun, not for the myriad Terrestrial gods (who are generally beneath the notice of an elder Solar and had better do what they're told, because they definitely don't want to get punched by the Hierophant).<br /> <br /> You'll notice that a main point of my previous post was that a Zenith being a priest of the Unconquered Sun is fundamentally different from a mortal being a priest of the local head god, because the local head god has a relationship with the people that is fundamentally different from the relationship the Sun has with the people. In fact, a Zenith who is a priest of the Unconquered Sun is more like a prophet, in the sense of a singular individual imbued with great power and authority from On High to effect change, rather than a member of the temple bureaucracy. The mortal and the Zenith are both priests, but what it means in practice is different, because one of them is a mortal and the other is a Zenith.<br /> <br /> So, if you consider that Panther and the Hierophant are good enough examples of the priest-king, then there is no change at all. This is exactly the same thing that has been going on in previous editions.<br /> <br /> Just in case you want to use that argument: yes, ALL Solars are singular individuals imbued with great power and authority. You'll also notice that all Solars are warriors of the gods created to overthrow the Primordials, and that doesn't stop Dawns from being the warrior caste. The Zenith are those most meant to evoke the particular theme of wielding divine authority, helped along by their caste abilities (like the &quot;Follow me!&quot; Charms, as you mention).<br /> <br /> Putting emphasis on the punching is also misleading: Zenith do have social Charms. The point is that when they intercede with the gods, they don't do so as supplicants. The relationship between the mortal priest and the god is inherently unequal because the god is always more personally powerful than the mortal, even if we're talking about a situation where the mortal has enough political power to get concessions out of the god. A Zenith, however, is mostly going to be equal or superior to any gods he intercedes with on behalf of mortals. Even if he uses diplomacy, the fact that he COULD punch the god changes the relationship.<br /> <br /> tl;dr: I meant both priest-king and prophet as they're being use to describe Zeniths, not in all cases ever.<br /> <br /> Was there anything else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Zeniths are one of the most miracle-starved Castes. Performance and Presence are social, Resistance's and Integrity's miracles don't help anyone else, and that leaves *Survival* to be their &quot;I perform miracles&quot; Caste Ability.<br /> <br /> If people are picking Castes and mostly sticking to in-Caste Charms, Zeniths suck at being miracle-workers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Panther is a lousy archetypal Zenith, because he's more a Dawn with some Zenith flavouring than a Zenith with some Dawn flavouring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T13:16:10-08:00","id":56316,"title":"","content":"That's an idea worth considering- survival charms as miracles. There is a lot of ideas that can be filled in here- multiplying food, purifying water, creating shelter despite terrible whether conditions, even powerful enviromental hazards like sandstorms. I mean, who is to say that survival has to work just for one person? Technically, even in 2e you could create a social/military unit and use some of the survival charms on whole groups of people... I don't know, I think there is some merit to that.<br /> <br /> If that was a place exclusively occupied by sorcery, I could understand, but in 2e, Infernals of Cecylyne had charms that granted water and food on deserts and caused enviromental hazards (and funnily enough, the second one actually worked off of Cult background). I don't know what the Devs stance on those is, maybe in 3e it IS a sorcery's playing-ground, but I dunno, I think there is a precedence here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T13:33:03-08:00","id":56332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=56120#post56120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure that no one would actually describe most of, say, the biblical prophets as looking anything like &quot;priest-kings,&quot; so I don't think this is a good summation. (Those being, probably, the guys the majority of the fanbase would think of first when we say &quot;prophet&quot; - first impressions matter here.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally would. I'd say Muhammad is as well.<br /> <br /> For the record, I'd totally be right, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T13:47:58-08:00","id":56341,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">So, just putting this out there, but the people in favor of prayer charms and the people against them are still talking about <i><b>entirely different meanings of the word prayer</b></i>.</span><br /> <br /> The people against it are against it because they see it as <i>supplication</i>, <i>submission</i>, and <i>begging</i> for <i>intercession by gods</i>. They think it would either have effects <i>too broad</i> to be well-defined or balanced and would be <i>mismatched with the themes </i>of the Unconquered Sun and being lords of Creation.<br /> <br /> The people in favor of it are in favor of it because they see it as issuing <i>demands</i> and <i>statements of negotiation</i>. They see <i>prayer as a bargaining chip</i> that <i>isn't offered personally</i> but is <i>offered by mortals</i> who are <i>directed by the performer</i>. They see it as a <i>resource</i> to be <i>used personally</i> or <i>offered to a deity</i> as <i>essence, ambrosia, and quintessence</i> to get a bonus in normal <i>social influence</i>. for the <i>offerings/payments</i>. They see it as <i>manipulating and directing cults</i> and using <i>non-prayer-specific Performance through prayer</i> the way you use <i>Linguistics through written letters</i>. They see it as an avenue of <i>economics</i> and <i>communication</i>.<br /> <br /> And neither the people in support of prayer charms nor the people against it seem to have the slightest clue what the other is actually talking about, because they're both talking about fundamentally different things and assuming the others are talking about the same thing.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I apologize in advance if this explanation comes across as condescending or generally dickish. I don't mean it that way at all, I'm just hoping this can take the conversation from a glorified 'yuh huh, nuh uh' to somewhere actually constructive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","user":"Storyteller","date":". 01-23-2014, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1974-jagadaishio","name":"jagadaishio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T14:07:41-08:00","id":56354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagadaishio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=56341#post56341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[COLOR=#B22222][SIZE=20px] The people in favor of it are in favor of it because they see it as issuing <i>demands</i> and <i>statements of negotiation</i>. They see <i>prayer as a bargaining chip</i> that <i>isn't offered personally</i> but is <i>offered by mortals</i> who are <i>directed by the performer</i>. They see it as a <i>resource</i> to be <i>used personally</i> or <i>offered to a deity</i> as <i>essence, ambrosia, and quintessence</i> to get a bonus in normal <i>social influence</i>. for the <i>offerings/payments</i>. They see it as <i>manipulating and directing cults</i> and using <i>non-prayer-specific Performance through prayer</i> the way you use <i>Linguistics through written letters</i>. They see it as an avenue of <i>economics</i> and <i>communication</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is exactly what I think the prayer part of the performance tree should enable the solar to do (in my opinion). Also as FromBeyond said, although slightly unrelated, survival could be a great way to carry out some of Moses and Jesuses miracles <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Also, look at <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Ow3IPUb4QtgMb1y2evMSGlJxE2VmTEOvyhJDu2eMAAo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">the exalted fan collection</a> that we are making.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/80-truemonk","name":"TrueMonk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T15:14:56-08:00","id":56377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=56261#post56261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure none of the biblical prophets are Solar Exalted who live in Creation, nor do they live in any sort of pulp fantasy universe where an expression like &quot;priest-king&quot; is appropriate and thematic (rather like sorcerer-king). I'm also pretty sure the Christian God isn't the Unconquered Sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>And these are good reasons why <i>prophet</i> is not analogous to priest-king: the examples prophet calls to mind are wildly different from what we want for priest-kings.<br /> <br /> Edit: Okay, let me try redoing that more helpfully. Yes, sure, the biblical prophets have some different characteristics relative to the Exalted. But they're still among the more commonly known examples of what the word signifies - I mean, heck, they're the source that John appealed to upthread. Clearly they're close enough for reference's sake.<br /> <br /> But, I mean, priest-king is not a concept totally without referent in real-world human civilization. There's a statue called &quot;The Priest-King&quot; - it is, among other things, a dude who looks kind of like a king and kind of like a priest. Within Christianity, Christ is acknowledged by his followers as their prophet, priest, and king. There's sources for the term - this isn't something that has to go purely other-world for its basis!<br /> <br /> The division I was trying to point to, though, is this: The priest and the king are both leaders of their respective systems - again, see the Hierophant for one example of what that looks like. The priest-king <i>is</i> the system: he's the religious chokepoint and the law-making authority in one go. That... doesn't tend to be a good descriptor of most prophets, who tend to stand outside of/criticize the systems.<br /> <br /> And again, that's a fine Zenith concept. But the guy who is actually part of the system with the gods - who communes amiably with them, appeases them, and returns with their messages to tell to the people who supplicate <i>through</i> him - that's kind of a different thing. The guy who is that, and <i>also</i> your sovereign, is something else still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 01-23-2014, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T15:21:03-08:00","id":56380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=56332#post56332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I totally would. I'd say Muhammad is as well.<br /> <br /> For the record, I'd totally be right, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, all right, I stand corrected: Dayen would say so.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to argue Muhammad - I think that's actually a pretty good example. But I think the case is considerably harder to make for, say, Jeremiah or Micah or Nathan or Elijah, who were a lot of things, but never <i>kings</i>, and for the most part never (in the context of how Judaism defined it) priests, either. And that suggests to me that Muhammad is priest-king as <i>well</i> as prophet, rather than that the two terms are identical.<br /> <br /> I mean, to be clear, I think &quot;prophet&quot; is also a valid Zenith role. I'm just objecting to the folding-up of the idea of priest - and, to be clear here, using that in the sense of &quot;the guy who is the established mode of connection between the people and the gods&quot; - and &quot;king,&quot; in the sense of &quot;temporal ruler,&quot; into prophet. You can be <i>both</i>, but they're not identical categories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 01-23-2014, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T15:39:20-08:00","id":56390,"title":"","content":"I'll shrug mightily at that. You're talking about men who had enough support to gainsay the Temple in Jerusalem and get away with it (with some hiccups for the ones who resisted the duty to prophesy) and continue live well, even if someone else wore the crown. Who are we to say they're not kings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T15:59:22-08:00","id":56403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=56332#post56332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I totally would. I'd say Muhammad is as well.<br /> <br /> For the record, I'd totally be right, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does David count?<br /> <br /> Ramses the Great was a great leader of his time and godhead of his nation.<br /> <br /> Paul Muad'Dib, sans the actual prescience stuff, fit pretty well. He even had a cult more or less dedicated to him being the divine godhead which he built around himself. The Preacher in <i>Children of Dune</i> also would of qualified I think.<br /> <br /> Note quite on the prophet thing at all, but as another example, Blind Kazir in <i>Night's Master</i> has at least some pretty neat heroic wanderer stuff to him, if not prophet. Bringing him up because he feels pretty Zenith to me for somer eason as I think on it for being a generally good and righteous brave dudeman.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T16:24:49-08:00","id":56415,"title":"","content":"Blaque, the Preacher <i>was</i> Paul, sans any of his abilities, except a commanding voice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T22:11:54-08:00","id":56581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=56377#post56377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The division I was trying to point to, though, is this: The priest and the king are both leaders of their respective systems - again, see the Hierophant for one example of what that looks like. The priest-king <i>is</i> the system: he's the religious chokepoint and the law-making authority in one go. That... doesn't tend to be a good descriptor of most prophets, who tend to stand outside of/criticize the systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, I could argue that prophets can totally be priest-kings. I mean, there's some material there. Jesus and Muhammad started outside the system, criticizing it, and then created a new replacement system, thereby filling all your requirements for being part of both categories. (I'll freely admit that I'm less knowledgeable about the Old Testament ones.)<br /> <br /> That's not really the point. Jorlem was saying that if Zeniths are prophets, not priests, then we shouldn't call them priest-kings. I was telling him that when we say Zeniths aren't priests, we're saying they're not like normal mortal priests. Supplication, negotiating with gods from a position of inferiority, all that stuff. And when we say they're priest-kings, we DON'T mean they're like normal mortal priests, because a king priest of the Unconquered Sun isn't going to do that supplication and negotiating stuff. Because he's the king. And there's no point negotiating with Sol Invictus. The Priest-King of the Sun is an individual imbued with divine authority, not just another cog in the temple bureaucracy like a mere priest. And then I made the tie-in with prophets, because when we throw the word prophet around, we mean, in part, that Zeniths are individuals imbued with divine authority, not just another cog in the temple bureaucracy like a mere priest. So i was saying that &quot;priest-king&quot; and &quot;prophet&quot; are different from &quot;priest&quot; in similar ways. Which brings the ultimate point: that &quot;priest-king&quot; is an accurate descriptor of Zeniths even if &quot;priest&quot; isn't necessarily.<br /> <br /> I also wrote &quot;priest-king = prophet&quot; because it made for a catchy sentence and a good end to my argument. So if nothing else I said convinced you, you can tell yourself I'm a horrible, horrible person who spreads lies for the sake of catchy sentences.<br /> <br /> And just to be sure I'm not offending anyone else with less than precise statements: when I say &quot;we mean&quot;, what I'm saying is my own personal interpretation, and not necessarily what anyone else actually means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","user":"Kazorh","date":". 01-24-2014, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T22:29:04-08:00","id":56584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=56415#post56415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blaque, the Preacher <i>was</i> Paul, sans any of his abilities, except a commanding voice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware, just sort of trying to not be spoilery about it. And he did have at least a different role about things in how he was going about being the Preacher compared to when he was the Emperor.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T22:40:48-08:00","id":56587,"title":"","content":"I'm currently reading Children of Dune for the first time. Thanks. &lt;_&lt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T22:48:10-08:00","id":56590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=56390#post56390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll shrug mightily at that. You're talking about men who had enough support to gainsay the Temple in Jerusalem and get away with it (with some hiccups for the ones who resisted the duty to prophesy) and continue live well, even if someone else wore the crown. Who are we to say they're not kings?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because they usually didn't. 'Prophet' was a job that one could be trained in, and usually one 'qualified' for the training in the same way that one qualified for most jobs in those days: by being the son of someone with that job. There were exceptions to this; Amos, for example, explicitly stated that he was not the son of a prophet, but that God had chosen him to deliver the message, when a priest called him out for prophesying against Beit-El.<br /> <br /> Usually, though, they worked more or less alongside the priests, as the other half of the line of communication with God. The priests managed the Temple and the sacrifices, sending the people's prayers to God, so to speak, while the prophets told the people what God wanted them to do.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, unpopular prophets were sometimes jailed or kicked out of cities for unpopular prophecies, and there is a <a href=\"http://www.mechon-mamre.org/p/pt/pt09a18.htm\" target=\"_blank\">story in the Book of Kings </a>where Obadiah saved a group of one hundred prophets (out of a much larger number) from being killed, so they often weren't able to defy the crown.<br /> <br /> <br /> My point is, prophets had a designated place in that society, and often weren't standing outside speaking inward. That said, the times when that did happen are the times that are better remembered, and these are probably the one that Zeniths are meant to reflect. Elijah, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T22:54:50-08:00","id":56593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drakhan Valane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=56587#post56587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently reading Children of Dune for the first time. Thanks. &lt;_&lt;</div> </div> </div> </div>I take no responsibility. I tried damn it!<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T23:06:28-08:00","id":56595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drakhan Valane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=56587#post56587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently reading Children of Dune for the first time. Thanks. &lt;_&lt;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry man, the book's been out for more than thirty years. Hell, almost forty. I read it when I was seven. I was pretty sure it was (semi)-common knowledge, especially with, y'know the mini-series released a few years back, about what happened to Paul. I apologize.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm also going to warn you: THERE ARE NO DUNE BOOKS AFTER GOD-EMPEROR. Just.... treat them like Chapters 1 and 2 of Infernals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T05:41:00-08:00","id":56674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=56390#post56390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll shrug mightily at that. You're talking about men who had enough support to gainsay the Temple in Jerusalem and get away with it (with some hiccups for the ones who resisted the duty to prophesy) and continue live well, even if someone else wore the crown. Who are we to say they're not kings?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, notably, &quot;continue to live well&quot; didn't tend to be true for a lot of them. Jeremiah got thrown into a pit and ultimately dragged off to Egypt. Elijah hid out in caves and ravines and lived off what the ravens brought. Tradition says Isaiah was sawed in half long-ways. This was evidently a regular enough thing that Jesus could refer to the Jerusalem as &quot;the city that kills the prophets&quot; and no one objected.<br /> <br /> So... I would call that a pretty good reason, especially since the people who did this to them were, y'know, kings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=56581#post56581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, I could argue that prophets can totally be priest-kings.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'd agree with you - I argued the same thing at the top of the page.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's not really the point. Jorlem was saying that if Zeniths are prophets, not priests, then we shouldn't call them priest-kings. </div> </div> </div>I agree with this, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was telling him that when we say Zeniths aren't priests, we're saying they're not like normal mortal priests. Supplication, negotiating with gods from a position of inferiority, all that stuff. </div> </div> </div>Then I'd agree with Jorlem: we really shouldn't call them something that invokes what people think of as priests.<br /> <br /> I'd also say that I think supplication/negotiating with the gods is definitely a viable Zenith role! When you're just starting out, you offer the prayers of the city to the local landscape gods, and they bless your crops; when you've built a nation, you offer its prayers to Ahlat, and he gives you victory in battle; when you rule a direction, you sway the Incarnae themselves. This isn't necessarily a position of <i>inferiority</i>, but it is a case where you're leading your people in praise of whomever, inspiring them to worship, speaking with the gods on their behalf, in exchange for whatever awesome thing they agree to provide in return. That, to me, is Zenith priestliness.<br /> <br /> But if that's <i>not</i> a core concept, then yeah, I think we should ditch &quot;priest&quot; as a descriptor for them. &quot;God-Puncher&quot; isn't a bad title, but it's a pretty different one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 01-24-2014, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T06:12:32-08:00","id":56686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=56674#post56674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if that's <i>not</i> a core concept, then yeah, I think we should ditch &quot;priest&quot; as a descriptor for them. &quot;God-Puncher&quot; isn't a bad title, but it's a pretty different one.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, though, from Stephen's description, it seems like &quot;Priest&quot; by itself is not an appropriate moniker for Zeniths. By itself. It's missing the &quot;King&quot; part of it which turns them from priests to <i>theocrats</i>. <i>Solar</i> priests are admittedly not your run of the mill priests in Creation. Solars aren't run of the mill anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T10:07:01-08:00","id":56844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=56674#post56674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then I'd agree with Jorlem: we really shouldn't call them something that invokes what people think of as priests.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, how about<b></b>: Zeniths and mortals are both priests, in the sense of interceding with gods and leading the prayers and all. However, due to the mortal state of one and the Exalted status of the other, in practice, their being priests ends up meaning somewhat different things.<br /> <br /> When &quot;Zeniths are not priests&quot; is said, it is to imply that they do not have some particular implications. These implications are the norm for mortal priests, who are also the majority of priests in Creation. Saying they are not like &quot;normal mortal priests from Creation&quot; is not the same thing as saying they do not possess any qualities at all that can be invoked by the concept of priest in the mind of readers.<br /> <br /> Priest-king, which ditches some of the implications due to the kingliness, does not need the same caveats as &quot;priest&quot; to accurately describe Zeniths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also say that I think supplication/negotiating with the gods is definitely a viable Zenith role! When you're just starting out, you offer the prayers of the city to the local landscape gods, and they bless your crops; when you've built a nation, you offer its prayers to Ahlat, and he gives you victory in battle; when you rule a direction, you sway the Incarnae themselves. This isn't necessarily a position of <i>inferiority</i>, but it is a case where you're leading your people in praise of whomever, inspiring them to worship, speaking with the gods on their behalf, in exchange for whatever awesome thing they agree to provide in return. That, to me, is Zenith priestliness.<br /> <br /> But if that's <i>not</i> a core concept, then yeah, I think we should ditch &quot;priest&quot; as a descriptor for them. &quot;God-Puncher&quot; isn't a bad title, but it's a pretty different one.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Did you actually read my previous messages? Like, for example, this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Putting emphasis on the punching is also misleading: Zenith do have social Charms. The point is that when they intercede with the gods, they don't do so as supplicants. The relationship between the mortal priest and the god is inherently unequal because the god is always more personally powerful than the mortal, even if we're talking about a situation where the mortal has enough political power to get concessions out of the god. A Zenith, however, is mostly going to be equal or superior to any gods he intercedes with on behalf of mortals. Even if he uses diplomacy, the fact that he COULD punch the god changes the relationship. </div> </div> </div>And did you read the passages earlier in the thread that comment that all gods, from lowly Terrestrial terrain features all the way to Celestial powerhouses like Ahlat, should consider the help of a Zenith a boon because they are very good at leading the people in prayer and inspiring them to worship?<br /> <br /> Nobody is saying that the Zenith &quot;core concept&quot; is to punch or, at best, bully every god he comes across. You are totally free to be nice to all gods ever and not punch them. Nothing in my previous posts is meant to say that Zeniths cannot speak with the gods on the behalf of the people. It IS meant to say that a Zenith has an ability to sway the masses to the god or away from the god that no mortal has. When it is positive, the relation between the god and the Zenith will tend to be that of allies, with the understanding that both can feasibly harm or help the other, rather than boss and subordinate.<br /> <br /> I would also note that single-handedly building a nation and then offering its praises to Ahlat, while it is priestly as you yourself comment, is definitely NOT what a normal mortal priest from Creation does. Heck, when a mortal achieves that, then bring on the Priest-King title. They're still not going to have the same sway with gods as a Zenith, but the dude is badass. They earned it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T12:20:07-08:00","id":56924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=56595#post56595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry man, the book's been out for more than thirty years. Hell, almost forty. I read it when I was seven. I was pretty sure it was (semi)-common knowledge, especially with, y'know the mini-series released a few years back, about what happened to Paul. I apologize.<br /> <br /> I'm also going to warn you: THERE ARE NO DUNE BOOKS AFTER GOD-EMPEROR. Just.... treat them like Chapters 1 and 2 of Infernals.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) That's why I didn't go all &quot;SPOILER-ALERT! WHAT THE FUCK, DUDE!?&quot;<br /> 2) What mini-series?<br /> 3) Hah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T12:23:09-08:00","id":56927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://aliendovecote.com/uploads/twine/kesha.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://aliendovecote.com/uploads/twine/kesha.html</a></div> </div> </div> </div>the enlightenment, it burns","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T12:47:44-08:00","id":56943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=56844#post56844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, how about<b></b>: Zeniths and mortals are both priests, in the sense of interceding with gods and leading the prayers and all. However, due to the mortal state of one and the Exalted status of the other, in practice, their being priests ends up meaning somewhat different things.<br /> <br /> When &quot;Zeniths are not priests&quot; is said, it is to imply that they do not have some particular implications. These implications are the norm for mortal priests, who are also the majority of priests in Creation. Saying they are not like &quot;normal mortal priests from Creation&quot; is not the same thing as saying they do not possess any qualities at all that can be invoked by the concept of priest in the mind of readers.<br /> <br /> Priest-king, which ditches some of the implications due to the kingliness, does not need the same caveats as &quot;priest&quot; to accurately describe Zeniths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, all right.<br /> <br /> I mean... again, I was objecting that &quot;priest-king&quot; and &quot;prophet&quot; aren't rocking the same vibe, and the game shouldn't say the former and mean the latter. That was, I thought, about all I said.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T13:14:26-08:00","id":56968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://aliendovecote.com/uploads/twine/kesha.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://aliendovecote.com/uploads/twine/kesha.html</a></div> </div> </div> </div>OH MY STARS AND GARTERS","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T13:43:10-08:00","id":56983,"title":"","content":"Can you provide me with an alternate link? Cus' I get 403 error.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T14:37:24-08:00","id":57013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drakhan Valane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/52328-tell-me-what-you-want-re-solar-performance?p=56924#post56924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) That's why I didn't go all &quot;SPOILER-ALERT! WHAT THE FUCK, DUDE!?&quot;<br /> 2) What 